tate, 2);\\n  state.flailLeft = 0;\\n  const b = pressFlail(state, 2);\\n  state.flailCool = 0;\\n  const c = pressFlail(state, 2);\\n  console.log('cooldown', { a, b, c });\\n}\\nEOF\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Find the flail angle that saves a 3.5 gust\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-e02b04f1-b3fa-4586-8336-f099f2e03482-58.log\",\"total_bytes\":955}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"4cc1384a-840a-4312-9407-d3eb6b0117fc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_36","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The physics matches the plan's table almost exactly.\n\nBalance step tests confirm the physics. Flails save at 30° and 32° but fail early or without flail. Brace and gust angles match the plan. Full lean overshoots then settles. Extra mass raises the peak. Recovery prevents refall. The balance step is ready for the full game.\n\nThe spike test will be replaced by the real test suite. The remaining game code is being planned in large batches across input, events, programme logic, data files, and the director.\n\nThe Standing event base class is being drafted. It will manage tiers, lanes, balance states, dolls, ragdolls, the physics world, and game flags like god mode.\n\nThe Standing base class now includes a physics step size and a NaN guard. It builds the physics world, adds ground, and spawns dolls in each lane. Falling triggers ragdoll creation and disables the doll body. Recovery removes the ragdoll and resets the doll to its saved balance state.\n\nThe Standing base class now includes a `stepCores` method. It advances time, ticks timers in each lane, and triggers recovery once the recover timer expires. For standing dolls it applies disturbance forces and runs the balance step. The physics world steps after all lanes are processed.\n\nThe `stepCores` method now checks each doll's translation for NaN and triggers falls via `checkFall`. The `dispose` method removes all ragdolls, frees the physics world, and clears the dolls array. A timer logic issue was spotted: `tickTimers` decrements both recovery and flail timers, but `checkFall` only sets the recovery timer when a fall occurs.\n\nThe timer logic is confirmed sound. `tickTimers` correctly decrements the recovery counter after a fall, and recovery triggers once it reaches zero.\n\nA new bug was spotted: `stepCores` steps the physics world before calling `checkFall`. This means the world may advance one frame after a doll falls but before the ragdoll is spawned.\n\nThe suspected frame-order bug is harmless. The physics world steps once before the fall check, so the core advances one frame after the angle threshold is crossed. On the next frame the disabled core skips balanceStep, but the ragdoll still receives its own physics step.\n\nRecovery timing is confirmed safe. The disabled core skips balanceStep for one frame, but the physics world still steps once afterward. This single free-fall step is within the 0.35-second grace window, so the doll does not fall again before balanceStep resumes.\n\nFruit attached colliders are removed when a doll falls. The input system will expose a `flailPressed` flag for event handlers to call `pressFlail`. `tickTimers` will be called only inside `stepCores` to prevent double-ticking. Gamepad buttons and axes are mapped, along with keyboard controls for weight using W, A, S, D, arrows, and a sticky balance-mode ring.\n\nKeyboard controls are being mapped for move mode, balance mode, and UI actions. Mouse input will be normalized to a unit disc, with right-drag look and wheel zoom. A `weightSource()` function is being designed to prioritize the last active device, then gamepad sticks, then keyboard, then pointer movement.\n\nThe `weightSource()` priority is now defined. A gamepad last used drives the weight stick. Keyboard keys win while held. The pointer only drives after it has moved since a key press.\n\nThe weight ring persists its last position when keys are released, only switching to the pointer once the pointer moves. A latch mechanism preserves key presses between polling cycles. The foot ramp scales from 0 to 1 over 0.12 seconds. Hopping triggers on cross, space, or both mouse buttons. Create and Options inputs are mutually exclusive.\n\nInput codes will be normalized to single-letter KeyX format. Menu navigation will use dpad, stick, arrows, WASD, and hover, with a separate poll from play so WASD moves focus in menus but weight in balance. The director will set the input mode to menu, balance, move, plates, or air. Plate spins will accumulate half-turn angles from A and D presses. A screen-to-world rotation helper is being drafted.\n\nThe screen-to-world rotation helper is verified. At yaw zero, screen up maps to negative world z and screen right to positive world x.\n\nGamepad stick axes are mapped: axis0 is right and axis1 is down. Pointer input is normalized from the center of the viewport by 0.33 times the height, then clamped to a unit disc.\n\nThe balance-mode weight ring will be stored in screen space as `wishScreenX` and `wishScreenY`. Events will convert these to world coordinates using the current camera yaw via a `worldWish(yaw)` helper.\n\nThe weight ring updates in screen space. Keyboard keys integrate a 1.6-unit-per-second vector and clamp to the unit disc. The pointer snaps directly to its offset. The pad stick maps X to X and negates Y before clamping. Pressing C recentres the ring.\n\nWhen the last device is a pad, the weight wish resets to zero on stick input. This is correct because a resting stick position is the intended target. Keyboard keys remain the sticky exception.\n\nIn move mode, the wish is set directly from key direction, pad stick, or pointer without integration.\n\nIsland look will use the right stick or right mouse drag to accumulate yaw and pitch.\n\nMenu focus will be handled by the director, not input. Input will expose directional edges and confirm, back, and pause. Stick menu navigation triggers once when an axis crosses 0.5 and releases below 0.3. A virtual pad helper for bot.js is being drafted with functions to write stick axes and set button states.\n\nA `makePad` helper is being drafted to create a virtual gamepad with four axes, sixteen buttons, and a no-op vibration actuator. A `balanceWish` function for the bot is also being written: it samples the past position from history, applies gain and noise terms, and computes the next balance wish.\n\nThe balance wish now includes a z component with 0.8 noise scaling, clamped to the disc. The parked bot simply returns the goal as its wish with no correction. A deterministic Box-Muller transform is being added to the RNG stream so rhythm timing can use Gaussian offsets.\n\nEvents will be deterministic and completable by the sharp bot. Event durations will match the test specification. The fruit hat test spans 7200 steps, but with only a few bodies it should run quickly enough; Rapier handled ten bodies in the spike test without issue.\n\nThe full playthrough should take roughly 10 to 20 seconds. Event metadata will live in `src/data/events.js`. A generator file will produce long dialogue arrays to hit the required sentence counts. A preliminary `about.js` and exit interview will be drafted later. Artwork will be built by a scene builder that creates island and event sets from primitives; it only runs when a renderer exists, so headless mode skips it.\n\nA rich island scene will be built in `art/island.js` for the launch test title screen. The director state machine is being designed with twenty-two screens and state fields for attract mode, idle state, day index, step index, and profile.\n\nThe director state now tracks live event data, phase timing, dialogue, medals, stats, marbles, touch-only mode, pause origin, settings, dev mode, group status, session, tutorial progress, god mode, time scale, and the active bot skill. Menu choices are data-driven; focus moves with input, and `choiceList` and `activate` will let the test select options directly.\n\nThe test will drive the director by reading choices and calling `confirm()` directly, rather than using a physics-skipping step helper. It will set the bot skill to 'sharp' during play and advance through screens like question and age using `advanceUntil`. The test loop is being drafted to boot the game, navigate the title and name entry, accept the paint prompt, complete the island tutorial, then proceed to the question screen.\n\nThe test loop now includes the plan screen, intro, and results. The tutorial bot will perform leans during the island tutorial. Check-in runs as an internal event for three tests before advancing to age. Age waits for confirm or auto-advances after eight seconds. Plan shows cards and starts the focused one on confirm.\n\nCheck-in durations are set to 10 seconds for stand, 18 for lean, 16 for step, 15 for quick, and 12 for onefoot. Three tests total about 40 seconds, and five days of events add roughly 700 seconds of simulation time. The full playthrough is estimated at 30 to 60 seconds. A progress log will only appear on failure. If the run is too slow, solver iterations can be reduced for simple events.\n\nSession mode will run in the browser through a `runSession` director path that skips the day flow and uses a simple card stage. Ghosts remain data-only when no renderer is present, letting tests compare body translations directly. I am now writing the files.\n\nI will compose the dialogue data by hand-crafting roughly eighty unique full sentences, then combine openers and closers to reach the required two hundred distinct strings. These will be stored as explicit arrays in a source file.\n\nI will write real arrays rather than generated strings to keep the dialogue distinct and in-character. The data files come first, followed by input, events, director, presentation, and tests. Event tiers will be encoded faithfully, and the step class chart must include full timing so the sharp bot can finish it.\n\nReal judging will replace the 97-point target so the sharp bot can score well. Plate spinners will use mostly kinematic energy numbers with optional shard bodies; the sharp bot cycles bands to earn a high share, while clumsy bots tap slower and less accurately to keep their share below 15 on tier one. The tippy raft must end within ninety seconds, so the shrink radius and swell timing will be tuned for that limit, with bots pushing against the tilt model.\n\nThe tippy raft will use a lightweight kinematic model instead of full Rapier physics. Dolls will walk and push against the tilt rather than standing in place, matching the plan’s specification that everything on the island uses the balance core.\n\nThe tippy raft will use a disc collider and dynamic balls in Rapier for realism, while integrating tilt with the plan’s formula (K 6, C 3.5). Dolls will be modeled as points with velocity, slope push, and shove. A winner is declared when one remains, satisfying the acceptance criteria that every round ends within ninety seconds.\n\nThe tippy raft will use four dynamic bodies with locked rotations, each receiving a linear velocity update per step. Tilt will act as gravity on a fixed disc. Sections that drift beyond the shrinking radius are removed as splashes. The island loop will place a walker on a ring, alternating feet and pacing a band. The walker’s position will be computed analytically while the doll may lean.\n\nThe sharp bot will steer the island ring and maintain cadence to complete two laps. Room service will use foot stepping, glasses as cylinders on a tray collider, and gusts; damping and bracing will be tuned if five glasses are lost. I am starting to write files and test each event. The title and folder checklist item is now marked done.\n\nThe title screen is now marked complete in the plan checklist. I will write the base director, fruit hat, and poses events first, then test them before moving on to the remaining events in batches.\n\nInput, bot, glyphs, base, fruit hat, poses, and score files are now complete. Programme data is also ready. The next step is to write a test for these events and run the fruit hat, poses, and balance tests before continuing with the remaining events.\n\nFruit hat catch logic is now defined. A ball collider is added to the doll body at local offsets for each glass, and the bot steers toward landing in the last 0.95 seconds. The basket reaches up to 0.46 meters with full lean, which clears the 0.45 meter landing radius and the 0.34 meter catch radius.\n\nThe fruit hat bot will aim by comparing the basket position to the landing target rather than the foot position, using a PD controller scaled by reach. The plan’s bot description says to lean to put the basket under the target, but with lag.\n\nThe fruit hat catch radius is set to 0.38 meters to include the basket rim. The bot will clamp its lean wish against the reach limit so the basket arrives near the landing spot without overshooting.\n\nThe fruit hat scoring formula applies a multiplier of 1 plus 0.1 times the number of glasses caught, then adds that value to the score and increments the banked count. The never-bank strategy is viable because each glass adds only about 0.015 kg, so roughly thirteen glasses are needed to tip the doll at rest; catching all sixty would require thirty-seven, which is easily achievable.\n\nThe never-bank bot must reliably fill the hat so the doll tips; a missed catch would stall the fall. Catching is disabled during the one-second bank animation. Flail will shake off the top fruit by removing its collider. Urchins appear on ten percent of catches, applying a brief negative impulse and deducting one point.\n\nUrchins will be reduced to 8% with a 0.8 N·m knock for 0.15 seconds, and tuned if the sharp bot falls too easily. Boots and pineapples are kept at low rates; seven normal fruit is safe, and a pineapple among them should still allow the banking bot to tip. A `src/events/index.js` registry will be added, and the director will be written after the event APIs are finalized.\n\nThe director will call botInput for each lane, then feed the resulting input object into the real input pad so the event’s fixed loop runs through the standard path. Headless tests can still invoke botInput and fixed directly, but using the director is more integrated.\n\nTests will use a `botCommand` helper to write inputs directly into the pad array, then call `input.poll()` and pass the lane-specific input object into `ev.fixed()`. This keeps the event from invoking its own bot logic during the fixed loop; the driver, attract, and director all follow the same single path.\n\nThe input system will detect hop as an edge so held buttons do not re-trigger every frame. Each lane gets its own `createInput()` pad, and bots write to their lane's pad. The spike test file will be removed once the real tests cover it.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The balance step matches the plan: a full lean settles near 18°, a 2 N·m gust peaks at 22°, and a flail timed near 32° saves a fall. Next I’ll build input and the events on that step."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60d7f0b5-6c48-4f7b-be93-786919846b82-59","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/goal/plan.md","old_string":"- [ ] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder.","new_string":"- [x] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60d7f0b5-6c48-4f7b-be93-786919846b82-60","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/bot.js","new_string":"/** Calibrated bots. They write a standard-mapped pad; they do not touch game state. */\n\nexport const SKILLS = {\n  sharp: { delay: 0.16, gain: 1.4, gainLoad: 0.7, noise: 0, reaction: 0.12, speedErr: 0.3, timingSd: 0.028 },\n  average: { delay: 0.26, gain: 1.0, gainLoad: 0.55, noise: 0.03, reaction: 0.28, speedErr: 0.8, timingSd: 0.055 },\n  clumsy: { delay: 0.38, gain: 0.8, gainLoad: 0.45, noise: 0.07, reaction: 0.5, speedErr: 1.4, timingSd: 0.095 },\n};\n\nexport function skillOf(name) {\n  return SKILLS[name] || SKILLS.average;\n}\n\nexport function makePad(connected = true) {\n  return {\n    id: 'virtual',\n    index: 0,\n    connected,\n    mapping: 'standard',\n    axes: [0, 0, 0, 0],\n    buttons: Array.from({ length: 16 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0 })),\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve(); } },\n  };\n}\n\nexport function clearPad(pad) {\n  pad.axes.fill(0);\n  for (const b of pad.buttons) {\n    b.pressed = false;\n    b.value = 0;\n  }\n}\n\n/** Disc-space wish: x right, y up. Written as a stick (axis 1 positive is down). */\nexport function writeWish(pad, x, yUp) {\n  const h = Math.hypot(x, yUp);\n  const s = h > 1 ? 1 / h : 1;\n  pad.axes[0] = x * s;\n  pad.axes[1] = -yUp * s;\n}\n\nexport function writeButton(pad, index, down, value = null) {\n  pad.buttons[index].pressed = !!down;\n  pad.buttons[index].value = value == null ? (down ? 1 : 0) : value;\n}\n\nexport function correctWish(skill, goal, dot, t, loaded, phase = 0) {\n  const g = loaded ? skill.gainLoad : skill.gain;\n  const n = skill.noise * Math.sin(t * 3.1 + phase);\n  const n2 = skill.noise * Math.cos(t * 2.3 + phase * 1.7);\n  let x = goal.x + g * (goal.x - dot.x) + n;\n  let y = goal.y + g * (goal.y - dot.y) + n2;\n  const h = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  if (h > 1) { x /= h; y /= h; }\n  return { x, y };\n}\n\n/** A short history so the bot reacts to where the dot was `delay` seconds ago. */\nexport function remember(history, t, dot, keep = 1.2) {\n  history.push({ t, x: dot.x, y: dot.y });\n  const cut = t - keep;\n  while (history.length && history[0].t < cut) history.shift();\n}\n\nexport function recall(history, t) {\n  if (!history.length) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\n  let best = history[0];\n  for (const sample of history) {\n    if (sample.t <= t) best = sample;\n    else break;\n  }\n  return best;\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-60d7f0b5-6c48-4f7b-be93-786919846b82-61","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/glyphs.js","new_string":"/** Prompt glyphs. Every element the UI draws carries data-glyph. */\n\nconst VERBS = {\n  weight: { pad: 'stick', key: 'wasd', mouse: 'move' },\n  leftFoot: { pad: 'l2', key: 'q', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\n  rightFoot: { pad: 'r2', key: 'e', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\n  hop: { pad: 'cross', key: 'space', mouse: 'mouse-both' },\n  flail: { pad: 'square', key: 'f', mouse: 'mouse-middle' },\n  breathe: { pad: 'r1', key: 'shift', mouse: 'shift' },\n  ask: { pad: 'triangle', key: 't', mouse: 't' },\n  use: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\n  back: { pad: 'circle', key: 'esc', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\n  pause: { pad: 'options', key: 'esc', mouse: 'esc' },\n  look: { pad: 'rstick', key: 'mouse', mouse: 'drag' },\n  confirm: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\n};\n\nconst XBOX = {\n  cross: 'a',\n  circle: 'b',\n  square: 'x',\n  triangle: 'y',\n  l1: 'lb',\n  r1: 'rb',\n  l2: 'lt',\n  r2: 'rt',\n  options: 'menu',\n  create: 'view',\n  stick: 'ls',\n  rstick: 'rs',\n};\n\nexport function glyphFor(verb, device, set = 'playstation') {\n  const row = VERBS[verb] || VERBS.use;\n  if (device === 'mouse') return row.mouse;\n  if (device === 'key') return row.key;\n  const id = row.pad;\n  if (set === 'xbox' && XBOX[id]) return XBOX[id];\n  return id;\n}\n\nexport function promptFor(verbs, device, set = 'playstation') {\n  return verbs.map((verb) => ({\n    verb,\n    glyph: glyphFor(verb, device, set),\n    device,\n    set: device === 'pad' ? set : device,\n  }));\n}\n\n/** Inline SVG. Tests read data-glyph, not the picture. */\nexport function glyphSvg(glyph) {\n  const ink = '#1A1420';\n  const common = `data-glyph=\"${glyph}\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\" viewBox=\"0 0 36 36\"`;\n  const shapes = {\n    cross: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#8fd0ff\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M12 12 L24 24 M24 12 L12 24\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></svg>`,\n    circle: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#ffb4c8\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></svg>`,\n    square: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#ffd0e0\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"11\" y=\"11\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></svg>`,\n    triangle: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#b8f0c8\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M18 10 L26 24 L10 24 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></svg>`,\n    l2: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">L2</text></svg>`,\n    r2: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">R2</text></svg>`,\n    r1: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">R1</text></svg>`,\n    l1: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">L1</text></svg>`,\n    options: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M12 18 H24 M18 14 V22\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/></svg>`,\n    stick: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#efe7da\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"16\" r=\"5\" fill=\"${ink}\"/></svg>`,\n    rstick: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#efe7da\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"18\" r=\"5\" fill=\"${ink}\"/></svg>`,\n    a: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#7dffb3\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">A</text></svg>`,\n    b: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#ff8b8b\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">B</text></svg>`,\n    x: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#8fd0ff\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">X</text></svg>`,\n    y: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#ffe08a\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">Y</text></svg>`,\n    lt: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">LT</text></svg>`,\n    rt: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">RT</text></svg>`,\n    lb: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">LB</text></svg>`,\n    rb: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff6e4\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">RB</text></svg>`,\n    menu: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"6\" y=\"8\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M11 16 H25 M11 21 H25\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg>`,\n    view: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"6\" y=\"8\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"14\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" fill=\"${ink}\"/></svg>`,\n    ls: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#efe7da\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"${ink}\">LS</text></svg>`,\n    rs: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#efe7da\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"${ink}\">RS</text></svg>`,\n  };\n  if (shapes[glyph]) return shapes[glyph];\n  const label = String(glyph).replace('mouse-', '').slice(0, 6);\n  return `<svg ${common}><rect x=\"4\" y=\"6\" width=\"28\" height=\"24\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fffaf2\" stroke=\"${ink}\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Fredoka,sans-serif\" fill=\"${ink}\">${label}</text></svg>`;\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2067,"output_tokens":11364,"cache_read_input_tokens":168576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"9378daef-bec2-46de-8b33-fb233159bf9e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60d7f0b5-6c48-4f7b-be93-786919846b82-59","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"- [ ] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder.\",\"new_string\":\"- [x] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/goal/plan.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/goal/plan.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/goal/plan.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"- [ ] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder.\",\"old_line\":37,\"new_string\":\"- [x] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder.\",\"new_line\":37,\"context_before\":\"Keep age, payouts, tilt, scoring, and the balance torque step pure so tests call them without a canvas. One fixed 1/120 step is shared by the page and the tests. Events take a list of lanes so solo, bots, couch play, ghosts, and attract are the same code. Bundle an IIFE into one HTML file so `file://` works with no module import. A test mode advances sim time without waiting and can skip the renderer. One test command prints only failures and a count; rerun only the part a change touches.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n\",\"context_after\":\"- [ ] Boot a single-file build: Three r180 ink scene, Rapier 0.19.3, unmodified hub client, WebGL2 fallback, and a test advance hook. Confirm `file://` draws.\\n- [ ] Add the balance core, three-device input, Balance Disc, jointed doll, ragdoll recovery, and Fruit Hat. Lock them with tests from a fresh world.\\n- [ ] Add the island ritual (check-in, Wobble Age, jar, tilt) and every other §6 event, each tested from its own start.\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60d7f0b5-6c48-4f7b-be93-786919846b82-60","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/** Calibrated bots. They write a standard-mapped pad; they do not touch game state. */\\n\\nexport const SKILLS = {\\n  sharp: { delay: 0.16, gain: 1.4, gainLoad: 0.7, noise: 0, reaction: 0.12, speedErr: 0.3, timingSd: 0.028 },\\n  average: { delay: 0.26, gain: 1.0, gainLoad: 0.55, noise: 0.03, reaction: 0.28, speedErr: 0.8, timingSd: 0.055 },\\n  clumsy: { delay: 0.38, gain: 0.8, gainLoad: 0.45, noise: 0.07, reaction: 0.5, speedErr: 1.4, timingSd: 0.095 },\\n};\\n\\nexport function skillOf(name) {\\n  return SKILLS[name] || SKILLS.average;\\n}\\n\\nexport function makePad(connected = true) {\\n  return {\\n    id: 'virtual',\\n    index: 0,\\n    connected,\\n    mapping: 'standard',\\n    axes: [0, 0, 0, 0],\\n    buttons: Array.from({ length: 16 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0 })),\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve(); } },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function clearPad(pad) {\\n  pad.axes.fill(0);\\n  for (const b of pad.buttons) {\\n    b.pressed = false;\\n    b.value = 0;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Disc-space wish: x right, y up. Written as a stick (axis 1 positive is down). */\\nexport function writeWish(pad, x, yUp) {\\n  const h = Math.hypot(x, yUp);\\n  const s = h > 1 ? 1 / h : 1;\\n  pad.axes[0] = x * s;\\n  pad.axes[1] = -yUp * s;\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeButton(pad, index, down, value = null) {\\n  pad.buttons[index].pressed = !!down;\\n  pad.buttons[index].value = value == null ? (down ? 1 : 0) : value;\\n}\\n\\nexport function correctWish(skill, goal, dot, t, loaded, phase = 0) {\\n  const g = loaded ? skill.gainLoad : skill.gain;\\n  const n = skill.noise * Math.sin(t * 3.1 + phase);\\n  const n2 = skill.noise * Math.cos(t * 2.3 + phase * 1.7);\\n  let x = goal.x + g * (goal.x - dot.x) + n;\\n  let y = goal.y + g * (goal.y - dot.y) + n2;\\n  const h = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (h > 1) { x /= h; y /= h; }\\n  return { x, y };\\n}\\n\\n/** A short history so the bot reacts to where the dot was `delay` seconds ago. */\\nexport function remember(history, t, dot, keep = 1.2) {\\n  history.push({ t, x: dot.x, y: dot.y });\\n  const cut = t - keep;\\n  while (history.length && history[0].t < cut) history.shift();\\n}\\n\\nexport function recall(history, t) {\\n  if (!history.length) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  let best = history[0];\\n  for (const sample of history) {\\n    if (sample.t <= t) best = sample;\\n    else break;\\n  }\\n  return best;\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/bot.js has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/bot.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/bot.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/** Calibrated bots. They write a standard-mapped pad; they do not touch game state. */\\n\\nexport const SKILLS = {\\n  sharp: { delay: 0.16, gain: 1.4, gainLoad: 0.7, noise: 0, reaction: 0.12, speedErr: 0.3, timingSd: 0.028 },\\n  average: { delay: 0.26, gain: 1.0, gainLoad: 0.55, noise: 0.03, reaction: 0.28, speedErr: 0.8, timingSd: 0.055 },\\n  clumsy: { delay: 0.38, gain: 0.8, gainLoad: 0.45, noise: 0.07, reaction: 0.5, speedErr: 1.4, timingSd: 0.095 },\\n};\\n\\nexport function skillOf(name) {\\n  return SKILLS[name] || SKILLS.average;\\n}\\n\\nexport function makePad(connected = true) {\\n  return {\\n    id: 'virtual',\\n    index: 0,\\n    connected,\\n    mapping: 'standard',\\n    axes: [0, 0, 0, 0],\\n    buttons: Array.from({ length: 16 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0 })),\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve(); } },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function clearPad(pad) {\\n  pad.axes.fill(0);\\n  for (const b of pad.buttons) {\\n    b.pressed = false;\\n    b.value = 0;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** Disc-space wish: x right, y up. Written as a stick (axis 1 positive is down). */\\nexport function writeWish(pad, x, yUp) {\\n  const h = Math.hypot(x, yUp);\\n  const s = h > 1 ? 1 / h : 1;\\n  pad.axes[0] = x * s;\\n  pad.axes[1] = -yUp * s;\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeButton(pad, index, down, value = null) {\\n  pad.buttons[index].pressed = !!down;\\n  pad.buttons[index].value = value == null ? (down ? 1 : 0) : value;\\n}\\n\\nexport function correctWish(skill, goal, dot, t, loaded, phase = 0) {\\n  const g = loaded ? skill.gainLoad : skill.gain;\\n  const n = skill.noise * Math.sin(t * 3.1 + phase);\\n  const n2 = skill.noise * Math.cos(t * 2.3 + phase * 1.7);\\n  let x = goal.x + g * (goal.x - dot.x) + n;\\n  let y = goal.y + g * (goal.y - dot.y) + n2;\\n  const h = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n  if (h > 1) { x /= h; y /= h; }\\n  return { x, y };\\n}\\n\\n/** A short history so the bot reacts to where the dot was `delay` seconds ago. */\\nexport function remember(history, t, dot, keep = 1.2) {\\n  history.push({ t, x: dot.x, y: dot.y });\\n  const cut = t - keep;\\n  while (history.length && history[0].t < cut) history.shift();\\n}\\n\\nexport function recall(history, t) {\\n  if (!history.length) return { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  let best = history[0];\\n  for (const sample of history) {\\n    if (sample.t <= t) best = sample;\\n    else break;\\n  }\\n  return best;\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-60d7f0b5-6c48-4f7b-be93-786919846b82-61","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/** Prompt glyphs. Every element the UI draws carries data-glyph. */\\n\\nconst VERBS = {\\n  weight: { pad: 'stick', key: 'wasd', mouse: 'move' },\\n  leftFoot: { pad: 'l2', key: 'q', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n  rightFoot: { pad: 'r2', key: 'e', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\\n  hop: { pad: 'cross', key: 'space', mouse: 'mouse-both' },\\n  flail: { pad: 'square', key: 'f', mouse: 'mouse-middle' },\\n  breathe: { pad: 'r1', key: 'shift', mouse: 'shift' },\\n  ask: { pad: 'triangle', key: 't', mouse: 't' },\\n  use: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n  back: { pad: 'circle', key: 'esc', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\\n  pause: { pad: 'options', key: 'esc', mouse: 'esc' },\\n  look: { pad: 'rstick', key: 'mouse', mouse: 'drag' },\\n  confirm: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n};\\n\\nconst XBOX = {\\n  cross: 'a',\\n  circle: 'b',\\n  square: 'x',\\n  triangle: 'y',\\n  l1: 'lb',\\n  r1: 'rb',\\n  l2: 'lt',\\n  r2: 'rt',\\n  options: 'menu',\\n  create: 'view',\\n  stick: 'ls',\\n  rstick: 'rs',\\n};\\n\\nexport function glyphFor(verb, device, set = 'playstation') {\\n  const row = VERBS[verb] || VERBS.use;\\n  if (device === 'mouse') return row.mouse;\\n  if (device === 'key') return row.key;\\n  const id = row.pad;\\n  if (set === 'xbox' && XBOX[id]) return XBOX[id];\\n  return id;\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptFor(verbs, device, set = 'playstation') {\\n  return verbs.map((verb) => ({\\n    verb,\\n    glyph: glyphFor(verb, device, set),\\n    device,\\n    set: device === 'pad' ? set : device,\\n  }));\\n}\\n\\n/** Inline SVG. Tests read data-glyph, not the picture. */\\nexport function glyphSvg(glyph) {\\n  const ink = '#1A1420';\\n  const common = `data-glyph=\\\"${glyph}\\\" width=\\\"36\\\" height=\\\"36\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 36 36\\\"`;\\n  const shapes = {\\n    cross: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#8fd0ff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M12 12 L24 24 M24 12 L12 24\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    circle: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ffb4c8\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    square: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ffd0e0\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><rect x=\\\"11\\\" y=\\\"11\\\" width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"14\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    triangle: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#b8f0c8\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M18 10 L26 24 L10 24 Z\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    l2: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">L2</text></svg>`,\\n    r2: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">R2</text></svg>`,\\n    r1: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">R1</text></svg>`,\\n    l1: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">L1</text></svg>`,\\n    options: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#fff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M12 18 H24 M18 14 V22\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    stick: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"16\\\" r=\\\"5\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    rstick: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"20\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"5\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    a: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#7dffb3\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">A</text></svg>`,\\n    b: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ff8b8b\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">B</text></svg>`,\\n    x: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#8fd0ff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">X</text></svg>`,\\n    y: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ffe08a\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">Y</text></svg>`,\\n    lt: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">LT</text></svg>`,\\n    rt: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">RT</text></svg>`,\\n    lb: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">LB</text></svg>`,\\n    rb: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">RB</text></svg>`,\\n    menu: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"6\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"24\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"#fff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M11 16 H25 M11 21 H25\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    view: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"6\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"24\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"#fff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><rect x=\\\"14\\\" y=\\\"14\\\" width=\\\"8\\\" height=\\\"8\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    ls: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">LS</text></svg>`,\\n    rs: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">RS</text></svg>`,\\n  };\\n  if (shapes[glyph]) return shapes[glyph];\\n  const label = String(glyph).replace('mouse-', '').slice(0, 6);\\n  return `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"6\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"24\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fffaf2\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"11\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">${label}</text></svg>`;\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/glyphs.js has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/glyphs.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/glyphs.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/** Prompt glyphs. Every element the UI draws carries data-glyph. */\\n\\nconst VERBS = {\\n  weight: { pad: 'stick', key: 'wasd', mouse: 'move' },\\n  leftFoot: { pad: 'l2', key: 'q', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n  rightFoot: { pad: 'r2', key: 'e', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\\n  hop: { pad: 'cross', key: 'space', mouse: 'mouse-both' },\\n  flail: { pad: 'square', key: 'f', mouse: 'mouse-middle' },\\n  breathe: { pad: 'r1', key: 'shift', mouse: 'shift' },\\n  ask: { pad: 'triangle', key: 't', mouse: 't' },\\n  use: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n  back: { pad: 'circle', key: 'esc', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\\n  pause: { pad: 'options', key: 'esc', mouse: 'esc' },\\n  look: { pad: 'rstick', key: 'mouse', mouse: 'drag' },\\n  confirm: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n};\\n\\nconst XBOX = {\\n  cross: 'a',\\n  circle: 'b',\\n  square: 'x',\\n  triangle: 'y',\\n  l1: 'lb',\\n  r1: 'rb',\\n  l2: 'lt',\\n  r2: 'rt',\\n  options: 'menu',\\n  create: 'view',\\n  stick: 'ls',\\n  rstick: 'rs',\\n};\\n\\nexport function glyphFor(verb, device, set = 'playstation') {\\n  const row = VERBS[verb] || VERBS.use;\\n  if (device === 'mouse') return row.mouse;\\n  if (device === 'key') return row.key;\\n  const id = row.pad;\\n  if (set === 'xbox' && XBOX[id]) return XBOX[id];\\n  return id;\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptFor(verbs, device, set = 'playstation') {\\n  return verbs.map((verb) => ({\\n    verb,\\n    glyph: glyphFor(verb, device, set),\\n    device,\\n    set: device === 'pad' ? set : device,\\n  }));\\n}\\n\\n/** Inline SVG. Tests read data-glyph, not the picture. */\\nexport function glyphSvg(glyph) {\\n  const ink = '#1A1420';\\n  const common = `data-glyph=\\\"${glyph}\\\" width=\\\"36\\\" height=\\\"36\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 36 36\\\"`;\\n  const shapes = {\\n    cross: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#8fd0ff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M12 12 L24 24 M24 12 L12 24\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    circle: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ffb4c8\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    square: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ffd0e0\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><rect x=\\\"11\\\" y=\\\"11\\\" width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"14\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    triangle: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#b8f0c8\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M18 10 L26 24 L10 24 Z\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    l2: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">L2</text></svg>`,\\n    r2: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">R2</text></svg>`,\\n    r1: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">R1</text></svg>`,\\n    l1: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">L1</text></svg>`,\\n    options: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#fff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M12 18 H24 M18 14 V22\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    stick: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"16\\\" r=\\\"5\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    rstick: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"20\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"5\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    a: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#7dffb3\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">A</text></svg>`,\\n    b: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ff8b8b\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">B</text></svg>`,\\n    x: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#8fd0ff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">X</text></svg>`,\\n    y: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#ffe08a\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"24\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"16\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">Y</text></svg>`,\\n    lt: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">LT</text></svg>`,\\n    rt: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">RT</text></svg>`,\\n    lb: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">LB</text></svg>`,\\n    rb: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fff6e4\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">RB</text></svg>`,\\n    menu: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"6\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"24\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"#fff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><path d=\\\"M11 16 H25 M11 21 H25\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"2\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    view: `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"6\\\" y=\\\"8\\\" width=\\\"24\\\" height=\\\"20\\\" rx=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"#fff\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><rect x=\\\"14\\\" y=\\\"14\\\" width=\\\"8\\\" height=\\\"8\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    ls: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">LS</text></svg>`,\\n    rs: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"12\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">RS</text></svg>`,\\n  };\\n  if (shapes[glyph]) return shapes[glyph];\\n  const label = String(glyph).replace('mouse-', '').slice(0, 6);\\n  return `<svg ${common}><rect x=\\\"4\\\" y=\\\"6\\\" width=\\\"28\\\" height=\\\"24\\\" rx=\\\"6\\\" fill=\\\"#fffaf2\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><text x=\\\"18\\\" y=\\\"23\\\" text-anchor=\\\"middle\\\" font-size=\\\"11\\\" font-family=\\\"Fredoka,sans-serif\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\">${label}</text></svg>`;\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"9aa3ac2c-66ad-4994-82b1-49c32416c077"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_37","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Glyph SVG contains font sizes of 11, 12, and 16 inside its text elements.\n\nSmall SVG text would fail the 30px computed style test. I will remove text from SVGs and use paths only. Keycap labels will be large HTML text next to the glyphs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-19c5f100-2ab4-48fa-a295-b49281e9fa41-62","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js","new_string":"/** One player's hands. Stick, keys and pointer share one wish. Last device wins. */\n\nconst WEIGHT_KEYS = new Set(['KeyW', 'KeyA', 'KeyS', 'KeyD', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight']);\n\nexport function normCode(code) {\n  const c = String(code || '');\n  if (/^[a-z]$/.test(c)) return 'Key' + c.toUpperCase();\n  if (/^[A-Z]$/.test(c)) return 'Key' + c;\n  if (c === ' ') return 'Space';\n  return c;\n}\n\nfunction emptyEdges() {\n  return {\n    confirm: false, back: false, pause: false, hop: false, flail: false, ask: false,\n    up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, recenter: false,\n    plateA: false, plateD: false,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function createInput() {\n  const keys = new Set();\n  const latched = new Set();\n  let pointer = { x: 0, y: 0, moved: false, buttons: 0, px: 0, py: 0 };\n  let lastDevice = 'pad';\n  let lastPointer = false;\n  let padSource = () => [];\n  let padIndex = 0;\n  const wish = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n  let feetL = 0;\n  let feetR = 0;\n  let lookX = 0;\n  let lookY = 0;\n  let zoom = 0;\n  let stickMenu = 0;\n  let createHeld = false;\n  let seenPointer = false;\n  const view = { w: 1920, h: 1080 };\n  let rumble = true;\n\n  function edgesOf() {\n    return emptyEdges();\n  }\n  let edges = edgesOf();\n\n  function markDevice(kind) {\n    lastDevice = kind;\n    lastPointer = kind === 'mouse';\n  }\n\n  function keyDown(code) {\n    const c = normCode(code);\n    if (keys.has(c)) return;\n    keys.add(c);\n    latched.add(c);\n    markDevice(c.startsWith('Mouse') ? 'mouse' : 'key');\n  }\n\n  function keyUp(code) {\n    keys.delete(normCode(code));\n  }\n\n  function pointerMove(x, y, buttons) {\n    const dx = x - pointer.px;\n    const dy = y - pointer.py;\n    pointer.px = x;\n    pointer.py = y;\n    pointer.buttons = buttons ?? pointer.buttons;\n    if (Math.hypot(dx, dy) >= 4) {\n      seenPointer = true;\n      markDevice('mouse');\n    }\n    const nx = (x - view.w / 2) / (view.h * 0.33);\n    const ny = (y - view.h / 2) / (view.h * 0.33);\n    const h = Math.hypot(nx, ny);\n    const s = h > 1 ? 1 / h : 1;\n    pointer.x = nx * s;\n    pointer.y = -ny * s;\n    pointer.moved = seenPointer;\n  }\n\n  function pointerButtons(buttons, x, y) {\n    const prev = pointer.buttons;\n    pointer.buttons = buttons;\n    if (x != null) pointerMove(x, y, buttons);\n    if ((buttons & 1) && !(prev & 1)) latched.add('MouseLeft');\n    if ((buttons & 2) && !(prev & 2)) latched.add('MouseRight');\n    if ((buttons & 4) && !(prev & 4)) latched.add('MouseMiddle');\n    if (buttons) markDevice('mouse');\n  }\n\n  function weightKeyDown() {\n    for (const k of WEIGHT_KEYS) if (keys.has(k)) return true;\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  function keyVector() {\n    let x = 0;\n    let y = 0;\n    if (keys.has('KeyA') || keys.has('ArrowLeft')) x -= 1;\n    if (keys.has('KeyD') || keys.has('ArrowRight')) x += 1;\n    if (keys.has('KeyW') || keys.has('ArrowUp')) y += 1;\n    if (keys.has('KeyS') || keys.has('ArrowDown')) y -= 1;\n    const h = Math.hypot(x, y);\n    if (h > 1) { x /= h; y /= h; }\n    return { x, y };\n  }\n\n  function readPad() {\n    const list = padSource() || [];\n    const pad = list[padIndex];\n    if (!pad || pad.connected === false) return null;\n    return pad;\n  }\n\n  function poll(dt, mode = 'menu') {\n    edges = edgesOf();\n    const pad = readPad();\n    let stickX = 0;\n    let stickY = 0;\n    let stickActive = false;\n    createHeld = false;\n    if (pad && pad.mapping === 'standard') {\n      stickX = pad.axes?.[0] || 0;\n      stickY = pad.axes?.[1] || 0;\n      const mag = Math.hypot(stickX, stickY);\n      if (mag > 0.25) {\n        stickActive = true;\n        markDevice('pad');\n      }\n      const btn = (i) => !!(pad.buttons?.[i]?.pressed);\n      const val = (i) => Number(pad.buttons?.[i]?.value || (btn(i) ? 1 : 0));\n      if (btn(0) || btn(1) || btn(2) || btn(3) || btn(9)) markDevice('pad');\n      createHeld = btn(8);\n      if (btn(9) && !createHeld) edges.pause = true;\n      if (btn(0)) edges.confirm = true;\n      if (btn(1)) edges.back = true;\n      if (btn(2)) edges.flail = true;\n      if (btn(3)) edges.ask = true;\n      if (btn(12)) edges.up = true;\n      if (btn(13)) edges.down = true;\n      if (btn(14)) edges.left = true;\n      if (btn(15)) edges.right = true;\n      const targetL = val(6);\n      const targetR = val(7);\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetL - feetL));\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetR - feetR));\n      if (btn(0)) edges.hop = true;\n      lookX = pad.axes?.[2] || 0;\n      lookY = pad.axes?.[3] || 0;\n      if (mag > 0.55) {\n        const dir = Math.abs(stickX) > Math.abs(stickY) ? (stickX > 0 ? 'right' : 'left') : (stickY > 0 ? 'down' : 'up');\n        if (stickMenu !== dir) {\n          edges[dir] = true;\n          stickMenu = dir;\n        }\n      } else if (mag < 0.3) stickMenu = 0;\n      if (rumble && pad.vibrationActuator && edges.flail) {\n        try { pad.vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', { duration: 80, strongMagnitude: 0.4, weakMagnitude: 0.6 }); } catch { /* ignore */ }\n      }\n    } else {\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, (keys.has('KeyQ') || (pointer.buttons & 1) ? 1 : 0) - feetL));\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, (keys.has('KeyE') || (pointer.buttons & 2) ? 1 : 0) - feetR));\n    }\n\n    const pressed = (c) => latched.has(c) || keys.has(c);\n    if (pressed('Enter') || pressed('Space')) edges.confirm = true;\n    if (pressed('Escape') || pressed('Backspace')) {\n      edges.back = true;\n      if (pressed('Escape')) edges.pause = true;\n    }\n    if (pressed('KeyF') || latched.has('MouseMiddle')) edges.flail = true;\n    if (pressed('Space') || ((pointer.buttons & 1) && (pointer.buttons & 2))) edges.hop = true;\n    if (pressed('KeyT')) edges.ask = true;\n    if (pressed('KeyC')) edges.recenter = true;\n    if (latched.has('KeyA')) edges.plateA = true;\n    if (latched.has('KeyD')) edges.plateD = true;\n    if (pressed('ArrowUp') || pressed('KeyW')) edges.up = true;\n    if (pressed('ArrowDown') || pressed('KeyS')) edges.down = true;\n    if (pressed('ArrowLeft') || pressed('KeyA')) edges.left = true;\n    if (pressed('ArrowRight') || pressed('KeyD')) edges.right = true;\n    if (latched.has('MouseLeft')) edges.confirm = true;\n    if (latched.has('MouseRight') && mode === 'menu') edges.back = true;\n\n    // Menu edges from keys should be edges, not levels. A held key repeats via a small gate.\n    // Latched keys are the edge. Levels above also set edges while held, which would scroll menus.\n    // Rebuild menu edges from latches only, then add stick/dpad which are already edged.\n    if (mode === 'menu') {\n      edges.up = latched.has('ArrowUp') || latched.has('KeyW') || edges.up && !keys.has('KeyW') && !keys.has('ArrowUp');\n      edges.down = latched.has('ArrowDown') || latched.has('KeyS') || (stickMenu === 'down');\n      edges.left = latched.has('ArrowLeft') || latched.has('KeyA') || (stickMenu === 'left');\n      edges.right = latched.has('ArrowRight') || latched.has('KeyD') || (stickMenu === 'right');\n      edges.up = latched.has('ArrowUp') || latched.has('KeyW') || stickMenu === 'up';\n      edges.confirm = latched.has('Enter') || latched.has('Space') || latched.has('MouseLeft') || (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed && latched.has('__pad0'));\n    }\n\n    // Pad confirm is level-triggered above. Latch it so a held Cross confirms once.\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) {\n      if (!latched.has('__padCross')) {\n        edges.confirm = true;\n        latched.add('__padCross');\n      } else if (mode === 'menu') edges.confirm = false;\n    } else latched.delete('__padCross');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[1]?.pressed) {\n      if (!latched.has('__padCircle')) { edges.back = true; latched.add('__padCircle'); }\n      else if (mode === 'menu') edges.back = false;\n    } else latched.delete('__padCircle');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[2]?.pressed) {\n      if (!latched.has('__padSquare')) { edges.flail = true; latched.add('__padSquare'); }\n      else edges.flail = false;\n    } else latched.delete('__padSquare');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[9]?.pressed && !createHeld) {\n      if (!latched.has('__padOpt')) { edges.pause = true; latched.add('__padOpt'); }\n      else edges.pause = false;\n    } else latched.delete('__padOpt');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[3]?.pressed) {\n      if (!latched.has('__padTri')) { edges.ask = true; latched.add('__padTri'); }\n      else edges.ask = false;\n    } else latched.delete('__padTri');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) {\n      if (!latched.has('__padHop')) { edges.hop = true; latched.add('__padHop'); }\n      else if (mode !== 'move') edges.hop = false;\n    } else latched.delete('__padHop');\n\n    const source = weightSource(stickActive);\n    if (mode === 'balance' || mode === 'move' || mode === 'air') {\n      if (source === 'key' && mode === 'balance') {\n        const v = keyVector();\n        wish.x += v.x * 1.6 * dt;\n        wish.y += v.y * 1.6 * dt;\n      } else if (source === 'key') {\n        const v = keyVector();\n        wish.x = v.x;\n        wish.y = v.y;\n      } else if (source === 'mouse') {\n        wish.x = pointer.x;\n        wish.y = pointer.y;\n      } else if (source === 'pad') {\n        wish.x = stickX;\n        wish.y = -stickY;\n      }\n      if (edges.recenter || latched.has('KeyC')) { wish.x = 0; wish.y = 0; }\n      const h = Math.hypot(wish.x, wish.y);\n      if (h > 1) { wish.x /= h; wish.y /= h; }\n    }\n\n    // Keyboard feet if no pad was driving them.\n    if (!pad || pad.mapping !== 'standard') {\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\n      const targetL = keys.has('KeyQ') || (pointer.buttons & 1) ? 1 : 0;\n      const targetR = keys.has('KeyE') || (pointer.buttons & 2) ? 1 : 0;\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetL - feetL));\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetR - feetR));\n    }\n\n    const breathe = keys.has('ShiftLeft') || keys.has('ShiftRight') || !!(pad && pad.buttons?.[5]?.pressed);\n    latched.clear();\n    // Keep pad latches that are not real keys. They live in `keys`? I cleared all latches including pad ones.\n    // Pad latches were stored in `latched` and just got cleared. Re-add the held pad markers.\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) latched.add('__padCross');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) latched.add('__padHop');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[1]?.pressed) latched.add('__padCircle');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[2]?.pressed) latched.add('__padSquare');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[3]?.pressed) latched.add('__padTri');\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[9]?.pressed) latched.add('__padOpt');\n\n    return {\n      edges,\n      wish: { x: wish.x, y: wish.y },\n      feetL, feetR, breathe,\n      lookX, lookY, zoom,\n      device: lastDevice,\n      pointer: lastPointer,\n      createHeld,\n      padConnected: !!(pad && pad.connected !== false && pad.mapping === 'standard'),\n      source,\n    };\n  }\n\n  function weightSource(stickActive) {\n    if (lastDevice === 'pad') return 'pad';\n    if (weightKeyDown()) return 'key';\n    if (pointer.moved && lastPointer) return 'mouse';\n    if (stickActive) return 'pad';\n    return lastDevice === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : 'key';\n  }\n\n  function worldWish(yaw = 0) {\n    const c = Math.cos(yaw);\n    const s = Math.sin(yaw);\n    return {\n      x: wish.x * c + wish.y * s,\n      z: wish.x * s - wish.y * c,\n    };\n  }\n\n  function snapshot(yaw = 0) {\n    const w = worldWish(yaw);\n    return {\n      wishX: w.x,\n      wishZ: w.z,\n      screenX: wish.x,\n      screenY: wish.y,\n      feetL,\n      feetR,\n      hop: edges.hop,\n      flail: edges.flail,\n      breathe: keys.has('ShiftLeft') || keys.has('ShiftRight'),\n      use: edges.confirm,\n      ask: edges.ask,\n      device: lastDevice,\n      plateA: edges.plateA,\n      plateD: edges.plateD,\n    };\n  }\n\n  return {\n    keyDown, keyUp, pointerMove, pointerButtons,\n    poll, snapshot, worldWish,\n    setPadSource(fn) { padSource = fn; },\n    setPadIndex(i) { padIndex = i; },\n    setView(w, h) { view.w = w; view.h = h; },\n    setRumble(on) { rumble = !!on; },\n    get edges() { return edges; },\n    get lastDevice() { return lastDevice; },\n    get wish() { return wish; },\n    setDevice(kind) { lastDevice = kind; },\n    consume() { const e = edges; edges = edgesOf(); return e; },\n  };\n}\n\n/** Rotate a screen wish (x right, y up) into the world. */\nexport function screenWishToWorld(x, y, yaw) {\n  const c = Math.cos(yaw);\n  const s = Math.sin(yaw);\n  return { x: x * c + y * s, z: x * s - y * c };\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11657,"output_tokens":4500,"cache_read_input_tokens":170624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"7938c562-7ca6-4b50-aa99-14cf149db8cc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-19c5f100-2ab4-48fa-a295-b49281e9fa41-62","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/** One player's hands. Stick, keys and pointer share one wish. Last device wins. */\\n\\nconst WEIGHT_KEYS = new Set(['KeyW', 'KeyA', 'KeyS', 'KeyD', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight']);\\n\\nexport function normCode(code) {\\n  const c = String(code || '');\\n  if (/^[a-z]$/.test(c)) return 'Key' + c.toUpperCase();\\n  if (/^[A-Z]$/.test(c)) return 'Key' + c;\\n  if (c === ' ') return 'Space';\\n  return c;\\n}\\n\\nfunction emptyEdges() {\\n  return {\\n    confirm: false, back: false, pause: false, hop: false, flail: false, ask: false,\\n    up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, recenter: false,\\n    plateA: false, plateD: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function createInput() {\\n  const keys = new Set();\\n  const latched = new Set();\\n  let pointer = { x: 0, y: 0, moved: false, buttons: 0, px: 0, py: 0 };\\n  let lastDevice = 'pad';\\n  let lastPointer = false;\\n  let padSource = () => [];\\n  let padIndex = 0;\\n  const wish = { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  let feetL = 0;\\n  let feetR = 0;\\n  let lookX = 0;\\n  let lookY = 0;\\n  let zoom = 0;\\n  let stickMenu = 0;\\n  let createHeld = false;\\n  let seenPointer = false;\\n  const view = { w: 1920, h: 1080 };\\n  let rumble = true;\\n\\n  function edgesOf() {\\n    return emptyEdges();\\n  }\\n  let edges = edgesOf();\\n\\n  function markDevice(kind) {\\n    lastDevice = kind;\\n    lastPointer = kind === 'mouse';\\n  }\\n\\n  function keyDown(code) {\\n    const c = normCode(code);\\n    if (keys.has(c)) return;\\n    keys.add(c);\\n    latched.add(c);\\n    markDevice(c.startsWith('Mouse') ? 'mouse' : 'key');\\n  }\\n\\n  function keyUp(code) {\\n    keys.delete(normCode(code));\\n  }\\n\\n  function pointerMove(x, y, buttons) {\\n    const dx = x - pointer.px;\\n    const dy = y - pointer.py;\\n    pointer.px = x;\\n    pointer.py = y;\\n    pointer.buttons = buttons ?? pointer.buttons;\\n    if (Math.hypot(dx, dy) >= 4) {\\n      seenPointer = true;\\n      markDevice('mouse');\\n    }\\n    const nx = (x - view.w / 2) / (view.h * 0.33);\\n    const ny = (y - view.h / 2) / (view.h * 0.33);\\n    const h = Math.hypot(nx, ny);\\n    const s = h > 1 ? 1 / h : 1;\\n    pointer.x = nx * s;\\n    pointer.y = -ny * s;\\n    pointer.moved = seenPointer;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pointerButtons(buttons, x, y) {\\n    const prev = pointer.buttons;\\n    pointer.buttons = buttons;\\n    if (x != null) pointerMove(x, y, buttons);\\n    if ((buttons & 1) && !(prev & 1)) latched.add('MouseLeft');\\n    if ((buttons & 2) && !(prev & 2)) latched.add('MouseRight');\\n    if ((buttons & 4) && !(prev & 4)) latched.add('MouseMiddle');\\n    if (buttons) markDevice('mouse');\\n  }\\n\\n  function weightKeyDown() {\\n    for (const k of WEIGHT_KEYS) if (keys.has(k)) return true;\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function keyVector() {\\n    let x = 0;\\n    let y = 0;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyA') || keys.has('ArrowLeft')) x -= 1;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyD') || keys.has('ArrowRight')) x += 1;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyW') || keys.has('ArrowUp')) y += 1;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyS') || keys.has('ArrowDown')) y -= 1;\\n    const h = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n    if (h > 1) { x /= h; y /= h; }\\n    return { x, y };\\n  }\\n\\n  function readPad() {\\n    const list = padSource() || [];\\n    const pad = list[padIndex];\\n    if (!pad || pad.connected === false) return null;\\n    return pad;\\n  }\\n\\n  function poll(dt, mode = 'menu') {\\n    edges = edgesOf();\\n    const pad = readPad();\\n    let stickX = 0;\\n    let stickY = 0;\\n    let stickActive = false;\\n    createHeld = false;\\n    if (pad && pad.mapping === 'standard') {\\n      stickX = pad.axes?.[0] || 0;\\n      stickY = pad.axes?.[1] || 0;\\n      const mag = Math.hypot(stickX, stickY);\\n      if (mag > 0.25) {\\n        stickActive = true;\\n        markDevice('pad');\\n      }\\n      const btn = (i) => !!(pad.buttons?.[i]?.pressed);\\n      const val = (i) => Number(pad.buttons?.[i]?.value || (btn(i) ? 1 : 0));\\n      if (btn(0) || btn(1) || btn(2) || btn(3) || btn(9)) markDevice('pad');\\n      createHeld = btn(8);\\n      if (btn(9) && !createHeld) edges.pause = true;\\n      if (btn(0)) edges.confirm = true;\\n      if (btn(1)) edges.back = true;\\n      if (btn(2)) edges.flail = true;\\n      if (btn(3)) edges.ask = true;\\n      if (btn(12)) edges.up = true;\\n      if (btn(13)) edges.down = true;\\n      if (btn(14)) edges.left = true;\\n      if (btn(15)) edges.right = true;\\n      const targetL = val(6);\\n      const targetR = val(7);\\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetL - feetL));\\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetR - feetR));\\n      if (btn(0)) edges.hop = true;\\n      lookX = pad.axes?.[2] || 0;\\n      lookY = pad.axes?.[3] || 0;\\n      if (mag > 0.55) {\\n        const dir = Math.abs(stickX) > Math.abs(stickY) ? (stickX > 0 ? 'right' : 'left') : (stickY > 0 ? 'down' : 'up');\\n        if (stickMenu !== dir) {\\n          edges[dir] = true;\\n          stickMenu = dir;\\n        }\\n      } else if (mag < 0.3) stickMenu = 0;\\n      if (rumble && pad.vibrationActuator && edges.flail) {\\n        try { pad.vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', { duration: 80, strongMagnitude: 0.4, weakMagnitude: 0.6 }); } catch { /* ignore */ }\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, (keys.has('KeyQ') || (pointer.buttons & 1) ? 1 : 0) - feetL));\\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, (keys.has('KeyE') || (pointer.buttons & 2) ? 1 : 0) - feetR));\\n    }\\n\\n    const pressed = (c) => latched.has(c) || keys.has(c);\\n    if (pressed('Enter') || pressed('Space')) edges.confirm = true;\\n    if (pressed('Escape') || pressed('Backspace')) {\\n      edges.back = true;\\n      if (pressed('Escape')) edges.pause = true;\\n    }\\n    if (pressed('KeyF') || latched.has('MouseMiddle')) edges.flail = true;\\n    if (pressed('Space') || ((pointer.buttons & 1) && (pointer.buttons & 2))) edges.hop = true;\\n    if (pressed('KeyT')) edges.ask = true;\\n    if (pressed('KeyC')) edges.recenter = true;\\n    if (latched.has('KeyA')) edges.plateA = true;\\n    if (latched.has('KeyD')) edges.plateD = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowUp') || pressed('KeyW')) edges.up = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowDown') || pressed('KeyS')) edges.down = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowLeft') || pressed('KeyA')) edges.left = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowRight') || pressed('KeyD')) edges.right = true;\\n    if (latched.has('MouseLeft')) edges.confirm = true;\\n    if (latched.has('MouseRight') && mode === 'menu') edges.back = true;\\n\\n    // Menu edges from keys should be edges, not levels. A held key repeats via a small gate.\\n    // Latched keys are the edge. Levels above also set edges while held, which would scroll menus.\\n    // Rebuild menu edges from latches only, then add stick/dpad which are already edged.\\n    if (mode === 'menu') {\\n      edges.up = latched.has('ArrowUp') || latched.has('KeyW') || edges.up && !keys.has('KeyW') && !keys.has('ArrowUp');\\n      edges.down = latched.has('ArrowDown') || latched.has('KeyS') || (stickMenu === 'down');\\n      edges.left = latched.has('ArrowLeft') || latched.has('KeyA') || (stickMenu === 'left');\\n      edges.right = latched.has('ArrowRight') || latched.has('KeyD') || (stickMenu === 'right');\\n      edges.up = latched.has('ArrowUp') || latched.has('KeyW') || stickMenu === 'up';\\n      edges.confirm = latched.has('Enter') || latched.has('Space') || latched.has('MouseLeft') || (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed && latched.has('__pad0'));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Pad confirm is level-triggered above. Latch it so a held Cross confirms once.\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padCross')) {\\n        edges.confirm = true;\\n        latched.add('__padCross');\\n      } else if (mode === 'menu') edges.confirm = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padCross');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[1]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padCircle')) { edges.back = true; latched.add('__padCircle'); }\\n      else if (mode === 'menu') edges.back = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padCircle');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[2]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padSquare')) { edges.flail = true; latched.add('__padSquare'); }\\n      else edges.flail = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padSquare');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[9]?.pressed && !createHeld) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padOpt')) { edges.pause = true; latched.add('__padOpt'); }\\n      else edges.pause = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padOpt');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[3]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padTri')) { edges.ask = true; latched.add('__padTri'); }\\n      else edges.ask = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padTri');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padHop')) { edges.hop = true; latched.add('__padHop'); }\\n      else if (mode !== 'move') edges.hop = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padHop');\\n\\n    const source = weightSource(stickActive);\\n    if (mode === 'balance' || mode === 'move' || mode === 'air') {\\n      if (source === 'key' && mode === 'balance') {\\n        const v = keyVector();\\n        wish.x += v.x * 1.6 * dt;\\n        wish.y += v.y * 1.6 * dt;\\n      } else if (source === 'key') {\\n        const v = keyVector();\\n        wish.x = v.x;\\n        wish.y = v.y;\\n      } else if (source === 'mouse') {\\n        wish.x = pointer.x;\\n        wish.y = pointer.y;\\n      } else if (source === 'pad') {\\n        wish.x = stickX;\\n        wish.y = -stickY;\\n      }\\n      if (edges.recenter || latched.has('KeyC')) { wish.x = 0; wish.y = 0; }\\n      const h = Math.hypot(wish.x, wish.y);\\n      if (h > 1) { wish.x /= h; wish.y /= h; }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Keyboard feet if no pad was driving them.\\n    if (!pad || pad.mapping !== 'standard') {\\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\\n      const targetL = keys.has('KeyQ') || (pointer.buttons & 1) ? 1 : 0;\\n      const targetR = keys.has('KeyE') || (pointer.buttons & 2) ? 1 : 0;\\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetL - feetL));\\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetR - feetR));\\n    }\\n\\n    const breathe = keys.has('ShiftLeft') || keys.has('ShiftRight') || !!(pad && pad.buttons?.[5]?.pressed);\\n    latched.clear();\\n    // Keep pad latches that are not real keys. They live in `keys`? I cleared all latches including pad ones.\\n    // Pad latches were stored in `latched` and just got cleared. Re-add the held pad markers.\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) latched.add('__padCross');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) latched.add('__padHop');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[1]?.pressed) latched.add('__padCircle');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[2]?.pressed) latched.add('__padSquare');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[3]?.pressed) latched.add('__padTri');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[9]?.pressed) latched.add('__padOpt');\\n\\n    return {\\n      edges,\\n      wish: { x: wish.x, y: wish.y },\\n      feetL, feetR, breathe,\\n      lookX, lookY, zoom,\\n      device: lastDevice,\\n      pointer: lastPointer,\\n      createHeld,\\n      padConnected: !!(pad && pad.connected !== false && pad.mapping === 'standard'),\\n      source,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function weightSource(stickActive) {\\n    if (lastDevice === 'pad') return 'pad';\\n    if (weightKeyDown()) return 'key';\\n    if (pointer.moved && lastPointer) return 'mouse';\\n    if (stickActive) return 'pad';\\n    return lastDevice === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : 'key';\\n  }\\n\\n  function worldWish(yaw = 0) {\\n    const c = Math.cos(yaw);\\n    const s = Math.sin(yaw);\\n    return {\\n      x: wish.x * c + wish.y * s,\\n      z: wish.x * s - wish.y * c,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function snapshot(yaw = 0) {\\n    const w = worldWish(yaw);\\n    return {\\n      wishX: w.x,\\n      wishZ: w.z,\\n      screenX: wish.x,\\n      screenY: wish.y,\\n      feetL,\\n      feetR,\\n      hop: edges.hop,\\n      flail: edges.flail,\\n      breathe: keys.has('ShiftLeft') || keys.has('ShiftRight'),\\n      use: edges.confirm,\\n      ask: edges.ask,\\n      device: lastDevice,\\n      plateA: edges.plateA,\\n      plateD: edges.plateD,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    keyDown, keyUp, pointerMove, pointerButtons,\\n    poll, snapshot, worldWish,\\n    setPadSource(fn) { padSource = fn; },\\n    setPadIndex(i) { padIndex = i; },\\n    setView(w, h) { view.w = w; view.h = h; },\\n    setRumble(on) { rumble = !!on; },\\n    get edges() { return edges; },\\n    get lastDevice() { return lastDevice; },\\n    get wish() { return wish; },\\n    setDevice(kind) { lastDevice = kind; },\\n    consume() { const e = edges; edges = edgesOf(); return e; },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Rotate a screen wish (x right, y up) into the world. */\\nexport function screenWishToWorld(x, y, yaw) {\\n  const c = Math.cos(yaw);\\n  const s = Math.sin(yaw);\\n  return { x: x * c + y * s, z: x * s - y * c };\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/** One player's hands. Stick, keys and pointer share one wish. Last device wins. */\\n\\nconst WEIGHT_KEYS = new Set(['KeyW', 'KeyA', 'KeyS', 'KeyD', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight']);\\n\\nexport function normCode(code) {\\n  const c = String(code || '');\\n  if (/^[a-z]$/.test(c)) return 'Key' + c.toUpperCase();\\n  if (/^[A-Z]$/.test(c)) return 'Key' + c;\\n  if (c === ' ') return 'Space';\\n  return c;\\n}\\n\\nfunction emptyEdges() {\\n  return {\\n    confirm: false, back: false, pause: false, hop: false, flail: false, ask: false,\\n    up: false, down: false, left: false, right: false, recenter: false,\\n    plateA: false, plateD: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function createInput() {\\n  const keys = new Set();\\n  const latched = new Set();\\n  let pointer = { x: 0, y: 0, moved: false, buttons: 0, px: 0, py: 0 };\\n  let lastDevice = 'pad';\\n  let lastPointer = false;\\n  let padSource = () => [];\\n  let padIndex = 0;\\n  const wish = { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n  let feetL = 0;\\n  let feetR = 0;\\n  let lookX = 0;\\n  let lookY = 0;\\n  let zoom = 0;\\n  let stickMenu = 0;\\n  let createHeld = false;\\n  let seenPointer = false;\\n  const view = { w: 1920, h: 1080 };\\n  let rumble = true;\\n\\n  function edgesOf() {\\n    return emptyEdges();\\n  }\\n  let edges = edgesOf();\\n\\n  function markDevice(kind) {\\n    lastDevice = kind;\\n    lastPointer = kind === 'mouse';\\n  }\\n\\n  function keyDown(code) {\\n    const c = normCode(code);\\n    if (keys.has(c)) return;\\n    keys.add(c);\\n    latched.add(c);\\n    markDevice(c.startsWith('Mouse') ? 'mouse' : 'key');\\n  }\\n\\n  function keyUp(code) {\\n    keys.delete(normCode(code));\\n  }\\n\\n  function pointerMove(x, y, buttons) {\\n    const dx = x - pointer.px;\\n    const dy = y - pointer.py;\\n    pointer.px = x;\\n    pointer.py = y;\\n    pointer.buttons = buttons ?? pointer.buttons;\\n    if (Math.hypot(dx, dy) >= 4) {\\n      seenPointer = true;\\n      markDevice('mouse');\\n    }\\n    const nx = (x - view.w / 2) / (view.h * 0.33);\\n    const ny = (y - view.h / 2) / (view.h * 0.33);\\n    const h = Math.hypot(nx, ny);\\n    const s = h > 1 ? 1 / h : 1;\\n    pointer.x = nx * s;\\n    pointer.y = -ny * s;\\n    pointer.moved = seenPointer;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pointerButtons(buttons, x, y) {\\n    const prev = pointer.buttons;\\n    pointer.buttons = buttons;\\n    if (x != null) pointerMove(x, y, buttons);\\n    if ((buttons & 1) && !(prev & 1)) latched.add('MouseLeft');\\n    if ((buttons & 2) && !(prev & 2)) latched.add('MouseRight');\\n    if ((buttons & 4) && !(prev & 4)) latched.add('MouseMiddle');\\n    if (buttons) markDevice('mouse');\\n  }\\n\\n  function weightKeyDown() {\\n    for (const k of WEIGHT_KEYS) if (keys.has(k)) return true;\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function keyVector() {\\n    let x = 0;\\n    let y = 0;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyA') || keys.has('ArrowLeft')) x -= 1;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyD') || keys.has('ArrowRight')) x += 1;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyW') || keys.has('ArrowUp')) y += 1;\\n    if (keys.has('KeyS') || keys.has('ArrowDown')) y -= 1;\\n    const h = Math.hypot(x, y);\\n    if (h > 1) { x /= h; y /= h; }\\n    return { x, y };\\n  }\\n\\n  function readPad() {\\n    const list = padSource() || [];\\n    const pad = list[padIndex];\\n    if (!pad || pad.connected === false) return null;\\n    return pad;\\n  }\\n\\n  function poll(dt, mode = 'menu') {\\n    edges = edgesOf();\\n    const pad = readPad();\\n    let stickX = 0;\\n    let stickY = 0;\\n    let stickActive = false;\\n    createHeld = false;\\n    if (pad && pad.mapping === 'standard') {\\n      stickX = pad.axes?.[0] || 0;\\n      stickY = pad.axes?.[1] || 0;\\n      const mag = Math.hypot(stickX, stickY);\\n      if (mag > 0.25) {\\n        stickActive = true;\\n        markDevice('pad');\\n      }\\n      const btn = (i) => !!(pad.buttons?.[i]?.pressed);\\n      const val = (i) => Number(pad.buttons?.[i]?.value || (btn(i) ? 1 : 0));\\n      if (btn(0) || btn(1) || btn(2) || btn(3) || btn(9)) markDevice('pad');\\n      createHeld = btn(8);\\n      if (btn(9) && !createHeld) edges.pause = true;\\n      if (btn(0)) edges.confirm = true;\\n      if (btn(1)) edges.back = true;\\n      if (btn(2)) edges.flail = true;\\n      if (btn(3)) edges.ask = true;\\n      if (btn(12)) edges.up = true;\\n      if (btn(13)) edges.down = true;\\n      if (btn(14)) edges.left = true;\\n      if (btn(15)) edges.right = true;\\n      const targetL = val(6);\\n      const targetR = val(7);\\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetL - feetL));\\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetR - feetR));\\n      if (btn(0)) edges.hop = true;\\n      lookX = pad.axes?.[2] || 0;\\n      lookY = pad.axes?.[3] || 0;\\n      if (mag > 0.55) {\\n        const dir = Math.abs(stickX) > Math.abs(stickY) ? (stickX > 0 ? 'right' : 'left') : (stickY > 0 ? 'down' : 'up');\\n        if (stickMenu !== dir) {\\n          edges[dir] = true;\\n          stickMenu = dir;\\n        }\\n      } else if (mag < 0.3) stickMenu = 0;\\n      if (rumble && pad.vibrationActuator && edges.flail) {\\n        try { pad.vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', { duration: 80, strongMagnitude: 0.4, weakMagnitude: 0.6 }); } catch { /* ignore */ }\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, (keys.has('KeyQ') || (pointer.buttons & 1) ? 1 : 0) - feetL));\\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, (keys.has('KeyE') || (pointer.buttons & 2) ? 1 : 0) - feetR));\\n    }\\n\\n    const pressed = (c) => latched.has(c) || keys.has(c);\\n    if (pressed('Enter') || pressed('Space')) edges.confirm = true;\\n    if (pressed('Escape') || pressed('Backspace')) {\\n      edges.back = true;\\n      if (pressed('Escape')) edges.pause = true;\\n    }\\n    if (pressed('KeyF') || latched.has('MouseMiddle')) edges.flail = true;\\n    if (pressed('Space') || ((pointer.buttons & 1) && (pointer.buttons & 2))) edges.hop = true;\\n    if (pressed('KeyT')) edges.ask = true;\\n    if (pressed('KeyC')) edges.recenter = true;\\n    if (latched.has('KeyA')) edges.plateA = true;\\n    if (latched.has('KeyD')) edges.plateD = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowUp') || pressed('KeyW')) edges.up = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowDown') || pressed('KeyS')) edges.down = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowLeft') || pressed('KeyA')) edges.left = true;\\n    if (pressed('ArrowRight') || pressed('KeyD')) edges.right = true;\\n    if (latched.has('MouseLeft')) edges.confirm = true;\\n    if (latched.has('MouseRight') && mode === 'menu') edges.back = true;\\n\\n    // Menu edges from keys should be edges, not levels. A held key repeats via a small gate.\\n    // Latched keys are the edge. Levels above also set edges while held, which would scroll menus.\\n    // Rebuild menu edges from latches only, then add stick/dpad which are already edged.\\n    if (mode === 'menu') {\\n      edges.up = latched.has('ArrowUp') || latched.has('KeyW') || edges.up && !keys.has('KeyW') && !keys.has('ArrowUp');\\n      edges.down = latched.has('ArrowDown') || latched.has('KeyS') || (stickMenu === 'down');\\n      edges.left = latched.has('ArrowLeft') || latched.has('KeyA') || (stickMenu === 'left');\\n      edges.right = latched.has('ArrowRight') || latched.has('KeyD') || (stickMenu === 'right');\\n      edges.up = latched.has('ArrowUp') || latched.has('KeyW') || stickMenu === 'up';\\n      edges.confirm = latched.has('Enter') || latched.has('Space') || latched.has('MouseLeft') || (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed && latched.has('__pad0'));\\n    }\\n\\n    // Pad confirm is level-triggered above. Latch it so a held Cross confirms once.\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padCross')) {\\n        edges.confirm = true;\\n        latched.add('__padCross');\\n      } else if (mode === 'menu') edges.confirm = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padCross');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[1]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padCircle')) { edges.back = true; latched.add('__padCircle'); }\\n      else if (mode === 'menu') edges.back = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padCircle');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[2]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padSquare')) { edges.flail = true; latched.add('__padSquare'); }\\n      else edges.flail = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padSquare');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[9]?.pressed && !createHeld) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padOpt')) { edges.pause = true; latched.add('__padOpt'); }\\n      else edges.pause = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padOpt');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[3]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padTri')) { edges.ask = true; latched.add('__padTri'); }\\n      else edges.ask = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padTri');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) {\\n      if (!latched.has('__padHop')) { edges.hop = true; latched.add('__padHop'); }\\n      else if (mode !== 'move') edges.hop = false;\\n    } else latched.delete('__padHop');\\n\\n    const source = weightSource(stickActive);\\n    if (mode === 'balance' || mode === 'move' || mode === 'air') {\\n      if (source === 'key' && mode === 'balance') {\\n        const v = keyVector();\\n        wish.x += v.x * 1.6 * dt;\\n        wish.y += v.y * 1.6 * dt;\\n      } else if (source === 'key') {\\n        const v = keyVector();\\n        wish.x = v.x;\\n        wish.y = v.y;\\n      } else if (source === 'mouse') {\\n        wish.x = pointer.x;\\n        wish.y = pointer.y;\\n      } else if (source === 'pad') {\\n        wish.x = stickX;\\n        wish.y = -stickY;\\n      }\\n      if (edges.recenter || latched.has('KeyC')) { wish.x = 0; wish.y = 0; }\\n      const h = Math.hypot(wish.x, wish.y);\\n      if (h > 1) { wish.x /= h; wish.y /= h; }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Keyboard feet if no pad was driving them.\\n    if (!pad || pad.mapping !== 'standard') {\\n      const ramp = dt / 0.12;\\n      const targetL = keys.has('KeyQ') || (pointer.buttons & 1) ? 1 : 0;\\n      const targetR = keys.has('KeyE') || (pointer.buttons & 2) ? 1 : 0;\\n      feetL += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetL - feetL));\\n      feetR += Math.max(-ramp, Math.min(ramp, targetR - feetR));\\n    }\\n\\n    const breathe = keys.has('ShiftLeft') || keys.has('ShiftRight') || !!(pad && pad.buttons?.[5]?.pressed);\\n    latched.clear();\\n    // Keep pad latches that are not real keys. They live in `keys`? I cleared all latches including pad ones.\\n    // Pad latches were stored in `latched` and just got cleared. Re-add the held pad markers.\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) latched.add('__padCross');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[0]?.pressed) latched.add('__padHop');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[1]?.pressed) latched.add('__padCircle');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[2]?.pressed) latched.add('__padSquare');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[3]?.pressed) latched.add('__padTri');\\n    if (pad && pad.buttons?.[9]?.pressed) latched.add('__padOpt');\\n\\n    return {\\n      edges,\\n      wish: { x: wish.x, y: wish.y },\\n      feetL, feetR, breathe,\\n      lookX, lookY, zoom,\\n      device: lastDevice,\\n      pointer: lastPointer,\\n      createHeld,\\n      padConnected: !!(pad && pad.connected !== false && pad.mapping === 'standard'),\\n      source,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function weightSource(stickActive) {\\n    if (lastDevice === 'pad') return 'pad';\\n    if (weightKeyDown()) return 'key';\\n    if (pointer.moved && lastPointer) return 'mouse';\\n    if (stickActive) return 'pad';\\n    return lastDevice === 'mouse' ? 'mouse' : 'key';\\n  }\\n\\n  function worldWish(yaw = 0) {\\n    const c = Math.cos(yaw);\\n    const s = Math.sin(yaw);\\n    return {\\n      x: wish.x * c + wish.y * s,\\n      z: wish.x * s - wish.y * c,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function snapshot(yaw = 0) {\\n    const w = worldWish(yaw);\\n    return {\\n      wishX: w.x,\\n      wishZ: w.z,\\n      screenX: wish.x,\\n      screenY: wish.y,\\n      feetL,\\n      feetR,\\n      hop: edges.hop,\\n      flail: edges.flail,\\n      breathe: keys.has('ShiftLeft') || keys.has('ShiftRight'),\\n      use: edges.confirm,\\n      ask: edges.ask,\\n      device: lastDevice,\\n      plateA: edges.plateA,\\n      plateD: edges.plateD,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    keyDown, keyUp, pointerMove, pointerButtons,\\n    poll, snapshot, worldWish,\\n    setPadSource(fn) { padSource = fn; },\\n    setPadIndex(i) { padIndex = i; },\\n    setView(w, h) { view.w = w; view.h = h; },\\n    setRumble(on) { rumble = !!on; },\\n    get edges() { return edges; },\\n    get lastDevice() { return lastDevice; },\\n    get wish() { return wish; },\\n    setDevice(kind) { lastDevice = kind; },\\n    consume() { const e = edges; edges = edgesOf(); return e; },\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/** Rotate a screen wish (x right, y up) into the world. */\\nexport function screenWishToWorld(x, y, yaw) {\\n  const c = Math.cos(yaw);\\n  const s = Math.sin(yaw);\\n  return { x: x * c + y * s, z: x * s - y * c };\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"c54befa4-154d-4e80-9872-78db59fc5e21"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_38","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The input poll function is messy due to menu edges and latched clearing.\n\nThe keyboard confirm edge logic is sound. Menu mode edges are convoluted and need testing later. The snapshot function should store the breathe flag from the poll result instead of reading keys directly.\n\nThe mouse hop is level-triggered on both buttons every frame. It needs to become an edge trigger. The pad breathe flag in snapshot is also broken and needs patching.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a790ef59-0223-45ad-8df3-f4170491ff8f-63","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js","old_string":"  let stickMenu = 0;\n  let createHeld = false;","new_string":"  let stickMenu = 0;\n  let createHeld = false;\n  let breatheHeld = false;\n  let bothMouse = false;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a790ef59-0223-45ad-8df3-f4170491ff8f-64","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js","old_string":"    if (pressed('Space') || ((pointer.buttons & 1) && (pointer.buttons & 2))) edges.hop = true;","new_string":"    const both = (pointer.buttons & 1) && (pointer.buttons & 2);\n    if (pressed('Space') || (both && !bothMouse)) edges.hop = true;\n    bothMouse = both;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a790ef59-0223-45ad-8df3-f4170491ff8f-65","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js","old_string":"    const breathe = keys.has('ShiftLeft') || keys.has('ShiftRight') || !!(pad && pad.buttons?.[5]?.press