completed programme steps, not skill, and is level after The Grand Hold, which cannot be failed. Days, Free Play, and later days continue, and no skill gate blocks the story. A sharp bot finishes each Tier 1 event with no NaN and no physics panic, and disposing the event does not leak bodies.\\n\\n4. Keyboard and mouse play the same screens as a pad. Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox-letter option, and keycaps or mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse. After 10 seconds with no input on the title or main menu, a looping bot demo of real events starts; any input leaves it and is not also acted on. Dev mode opens only from pause and includes the §14 tools plus live sliders for balance, world, events, rewards, and ink that change a running event and reset to defaults. A coarse pointer with no fine pointer shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a working Settings control, has no touch gameplay, and still runs attract mode. Music defaults to 10%. Music, effects, and gibberish voices are synthesized in code, and every spoken line is also on screen. At 1920×1080, gameplay text is at least 30px, a screen has at most six choices, and focus is visible.\\n\\n5. Group Class on one screen seats 1–4 local players on the couch events, and Tippy Raft can end with a winner. An AI Hub session is Protocol v1 ghost mode: the unmodified session client is the first script in `head` after the charset meta; the §12 metas are present (`hub:session` 1, players `1-4`, mode `ghost`, minutes, goal, howto, type Game, source Wii Fit) and `hub:webgpu` required is not set; the game connects and calls ready with no key press, shows its own card, schedules the round on `AIHub.time()`, draws ghost dolls that never affect local physics, reports progress from the start of the clock, sends one result, and on time-up or end stops input and sound. The hub harness passes at 1 player, at 2 players, at 4 players with latency, jitter, and loss, and with the host leaving. Outside a session, Enter and Space on the title leave a drawn frame and no error. Options is ignored while Create is held.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: Add in-repo tests that drive the shipped simulation (the same fixed step the page runs), not a copy of the formulas and not a mock of the unit under test. One command prints only failures and a one-line count, and its full run covers criteria 2–4 from their own start states: balance (parked stick, fall/recover, load, Fruit Hat bank versus never-bank), each §6 event, check-in/age/marbles/tilt, a sim-time playthrough from a fresh profile through the ending and a later day, input verbs and glyphs, attract at 10 seconds with the press swallowed, dev sliders and reset, touch-only copy and Settings, offline audio renders that are finite, non-silent, and not clipped with music gain 0.10, the 1080p UI limits, the exit-interview shape, and the built HTML (no external requests, no audio files, no TODO/placeholder/stub, client immediately after charset). Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/test-full.log`. Pass only if the count shows zero failures.\\n2. gating: Launch the real root HTML from `file://` twice, in Playwright Chromium, with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. Each run must show no page errors, a live WebGPU device (a lost device fails), a canvas whose drawing size matches the requested view, and a pixel readback that is substantially painted (a large painted fraction or a bbox covering most of the surface, with dark ink-like pixels and a spread of other colours — not merely non-zero). The title string on screen equals GameTitle. A stubbed standard pad or a key then changes screen or balance state in a second capture. Both runs must succeed the same way. Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. If the browser cannot start, save that launcher error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.txt` and criterion 1's file checks plus the non-render tests in step 1 are the bar. A readback that succeeds and is blank or nearly blank is a game failure, not this fallback.\\n3. gating: Serve the built HTML and the hub harness on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port, confirm the response is this game, then run the harness to `body[data-complete=\\\"true\\\"]` and `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` for `players=1`, `players=2`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`, and `scenario=host-leave`. Stop only that server, by its PID. Also open the file outside a session and press Enter, Space, Enter, Space: no errors and a drawn frame. Capture `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. evidence: At 1920×1080, with the same rendering flags, capture title, island on day 1 and level, each event mid-play, results, jar, age reveal, four-player Group Class, dev mode, and About into `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. A WebKit load that reports the WebGL2 fallback and no page errors goes to `{SCRATCH}/webkit.log`. Absence of these shots does not fail the goal once steps 1–3 pass.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- FPS targets, optimization, or a performance budget.\\n- A real DualSense, TV, listener, second human, or iOS Safari. Stand-ins in TASK.md are as far as those checks go.\\n- Recreating Wii Fit activities, its balance board, its age/bank product names, Mii avatars, or its white gym look.\\n- Shared-world hub mode, chat, emotes, custom names, or any network besides the hub client.\\n- Typed profile names, or a fail state that stops the days.\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\nOnly this work folder. New sources live in the named dev subfolder; the bundled HTML, `exit-interview.json`, and `PROGRESS.md` land in the work-folder root. Runtime deps are three@0.180.0, @dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3, esbuild, playwright@1.63.0, Fredoka, and the AI Hub session client plus harness (protocol v1, client 1.4.0) from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`. Wii Fit's own activity list was not re-derived: PLAN.md already maps the source's pillars onto original events and forbids copying those activities.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep age, payouts, tilt, scoring, and the balance torque step pure so tests call them without a canvas. One fixed 1/120 step is shared by the page and the tests. Events take a list of lanes so solo, bots, couch play, ghosts, and attract are the same code. Bundle an IIFE into one HTML file so `file://` works with no module import. A test mode advances sim time without waiting and can skip the renderer. One test command prints only failures and a count; rerun only the part a change touches.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder.\\n- [ ] Boot a single-file build: Three r180 ink scene, Rapier 0.19.3, unmodified hub client, WebGL2 fallback, and a test advance hook. Confirm `file://` draws.\\n- [ ] Add the balance core, three-device input, Balance Disc, jointed doll, ragdoll recovery, and Fruit Hat. Lock them with tests from a fresh world.\\n- [ ] Add the island ritual (check-in, Wobble Age, jar, tilt) and every other §6 event, each tested from its own start.\\n- [ ] Add menus, attract, dev sliders, synthesized audio, glyphs, touch-only, Group Class, and the hub ghost session.\\n- [ ] Ship the ending, About/Credits, exit-interview.json, `{SCRATCH}/test-full.log` with zero failures, the two launch captures, and the hub log.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md's three WebGPU flags alone lose the device while the frame counter still climbs. Rendering checks must also pass `--use-vulkan=swiftshader` and `--use-angle=swiftshader`. A lost device, or a readback that succeeds and is blank, is a failure.\\n- Software WebGPU is only a few frames per second here, and extra browsers are killed when memory runs out. Logic tests must not need a renderer; keep at most two browsers open.\\n- PLAN.md §18 lets a short build cut whole events in a fixed order. That does not relax this plan: this computer can run the full demo, so every §6 event is required. A stub, a placeholder, or a cut of a do-not-cut system fails.\\n- The hub rejects an edited `session.js` and checks its hash. If the published client hash differs from the hash written in PLAN.md, use the hash shipped with that client release and fail the build on a mismatch.\\n- A real pad unlocking audio, and whether the music sounds good, cannot be confirmed here. Signal tests, plus the on-screen prompt if audio stays suspended after pad input, are the bar.\\n\",\"total_lines\":49}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6e08751f-3af2-4039-899c-c2409987cc1f-27","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,76,101,118,101,108,32,66,101,115,116,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,47,115,114,99,47,105,110,112,117,116,47,103,108,121,112,104,115,46,106,115,10,53,50,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,103,108,121,112,104,83,118,103,40,103,108,121,112,104,41,32,123,10,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,76,101,118,101,108,32,66,101,115,116,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,47,115,114,99,47,100,97,116,97,47,116,117,110,105,110,103,46,106,115,10,52,50,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,99,108,97,109,112,84,117,110,105,110,103,40,105,100,44,32,118,97,108,117,101,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/glyphs.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"export function glyphSvg(glyph) {\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/tuning.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"export function clampTuning(id, value) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"5972f886-ed1a-48c5-8f8a-dee14462620a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_55","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will now write the bulk of the game.\n\nA node script will generate dialogue. I'll write event physics and a solid director. Separate files are better than one large module for designer tools and architecture tests.\n\nA shared `screenFromLean` utility will be added. The Cairn bot will target center {0,0} with loaded state 0.7. Stone placement colliders use half-extents of r×0.8 by hh by r×0.8.\n\nStones will use mass 0.02, linear damping 0.1, angular damping 0.6, and setCanSleep(false) so they stay active when the doll leans. The slab collider dimensions are being checked against the plan's half-extent notation.\n\nThe slab's 0.55m width is too large for a head piece. It should be half-extents of 0.275m, matching the stone notation.\n\nThe slab will use mass 0.05 and local y 0.95. Stones will have a ±1.5 cm random offset on release. I am also adding logic to count stones placed on the slab.\n\nA stone counts only if it lands within 0.32 m of the doll body, above 0.85 m, and has not fallen below 0.5 m. The first Tier 1 stone spawns at 1.0 s, then every 5.5 s for six stones, followed by an 8 s hold. Sway ramps from sway0 to sway1 across the stacking and hold phases. Breathing follows the poses pattern. The slab's weight creates roughly 0.47 m of margin.\n\nSix stones weigh roughly 1.44 kg, giving a total margin of about 1.9 m. The cairn design relies on stones sliding off the doll rather than tipping it over. The sharp bot will stay level to keep stones in place, while the clumsy bot oscillates and drops some. Tier 2 without breathing will lose stones, so the breath-synced strategy must reduce sway enough to prevent that. If both bots retain all stones, the test will fail.\n\nI will measure the physics before adjusting anything. If the simulation is too stable, I may add a small horizontal velocity on release based on lean rate to make sway matter. I will write all event files and a driver next. I also need to fix the fruit hat driver convention in tests and add a `nanWorld` helper.\n\nI am now writing the files. The director will be a single large module of roughly 1500 lines. I have sketched its state: screen, attract mode, idle timer, active event, profile, day index, and step counter.\n\nThe director will track a phase string such as morning, question, checkin, age, plan, class, results, jar, bed, or ending. It advances time by stepping a fixed substep and then a frame callback. When a test bot is active, it writes the bot’s input commands into the pad before each input poll.\n\nThe bot pad will also write the breathe, left foot, and right foot buttons. Plate bots use stick circles, while key bots tap A and D directly. Multi-lane group classes will give each lane its own input and pad; solo mode uses one. Ghost lanes have no physics.\n\nIn a session, only the local lane simulates physics; ghosts are purely visual and interpolated by the director. Attract mode uses bot lanes, which still simulate in the event but run with god mode enabled. The playthrough test will drive menus through the pad rather than using an internal skip.\n\nThe test will script a deterministic menu playthrough. It will press confirm at the title screen, select the default name, choose Programme, and proceed through island dialogue and check-in. The test must decide whether to enable the sharp bot before check-in or let the programme auto-enable it.\n\nThe test will keep the sharp bot active for the entire playthrough. During menus, the bot will zero out the stick so it does not scroll the menu; only button presses will drive navigation. Bot pad writes will be restricted to play, check-in, and attract screens.\n\nThe test will run full event durations without time scaling. Simulation speed is acceptable: roughly 34 seconds for all events, and about 4.5 seconds for the playthrough alone.\n\nThe room service event will use high damping and friction for the tumblers. A glass is lost if it tilts past 35 degrees or leaves the tray bounds. The physics must stay stable because the plan forbids catching a Rapier panic and continuing. Parenting the tumblers as colliders with mass on the doll is a safer alternative to tracking a stability number from lean rate.\n\nI will try real tumblers with CCD and high damping. If the physics panics, I will fall back to a sensor-and-rule system that removes glasses when the doll tilts too far. The tray sits at local (0, 0.5, 0.3). Each tumbler is a dynamic body with height 0.06 m, radius 0.05 m, and mass 0.012 kg. They start just above the tray.\n\nTumblers will be props so they collide with the doll and ground. They will be placed at the tray top and held still for a few frames before walking begins. The room service event will be coded and tested early.\n\nThe springboard event will keep the standing doll on the board for score tracking, even though pumping does not physically move it. During the \"air\" phase the balance joint is removed, gravity is zeroed, and torque is applied directly to the body while the angle is integrated in script. If physics panics, the body will be disabled and only analytic scoring will continue.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f368064f-aedf-4362-aefb-5ecc4f1ec44d-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"progress|ready\\(|time-up|ghost|__hubCheck|data-complete","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/tools/hub","glob":"*.js","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f368064f-aedf-4362-aefb-5ecc4f1ec44d-29","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function check|pass|progress|ghost|ready","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/tools/hub/harness.html","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7823,"output_tokens":3399,"cache_read_input_tokens":104192,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"b537ec09-1f3d-41b4-8b31-3feb01fbf6b3"}
