{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_84","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There is a large amount of remaining code to complete.\n\nTwelve major components remain: dialogue, director flow, audio engine, renderer, art, UI, session hub, attract mode, dev tools, tests, build, and launch logging. The plan is to write complete modules first, then add tests, then build and run.\n\nReviewing existing APIs and event structures to align the director module with current code. Reading score.js, programme.js, events/index.js, and related files in parallel.\n\nThe hardest test is the full game flow: Title → profile → tutorial → all days through menus with a stubbed pad and bot in every class → ending → credits → Maintenance day → Free Play. Next I will write the core game systems.\n\nThe flow test will run in Node with rendering disabled. It will import the director directly and drive it via `__TEST__.advance()`, `bot()`, and `goto()`. The public test command is `node tools/test.mjs`.\n\nThe director will dynamically import the renderer so it can run in Node without Three.js. The flow test must use the real input system and navigate through menus with a stubbed pad rather than skipping story sections via goto(). Tests must drive shipped code on its natural path.\n\nThe full five-day flow test will require roughly 700 seconds of simulated time plus menus. At 120Hz this equals about 84,000 steps. Node should handle this load because prior smoke tests showed 60-second events finishing in hundreds of milliseconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-181a2375-58c5-4a3a-9935-7f30e3a06186-9","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/input.js","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-181a2375-58c5-4a3a-9935-7f30e3a06186-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":