{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_116","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"takeLine uses Math.floor on a roll value that is passed in.\n\nThe function is in dialogue.js and does not use Math.random. I am now writing the core systems, starting with save.js, script.js, loop.js, and audio files.\n\nA full generator-based script system is unnecessary. A simple beat queue inside the director will handle dialogue and timing instead.\n\nExplicit screen flow replaces generators for reliability. script.js remains for sequences and tests. loop.js is being written with a fixed timestep and requestAnimationFrame fallback.\n\nloop.js now clamps delta time to 0.25 seconds and runs up to 30 fixed timesteps per frame. The audio engine will be a compact synthesizer.\n\nThe offline audio renderer uses a 44100 Hz OfflineAudioContext. It applies a dynamics compressor with aggressive limiting and a low master gain. The render function returns peak amplitude, RMS level, clipping status, and finiteness.\n\nThe audio factory connects music, SFX, and voice gains to the master compressor. It then renders the offline buffer and computes peak amplitude, RMS level, and finiteness from the channel data.\n\nThe audio renderer now flags clipping when peak amplitude reaches 0.999 or higher. Instrument gains will be tuned so a two-second motif stays above an RMS threshold of 0.005. Voice synthesis will schedule blips across the text. Formant frequencies for five vowels are defined, with Trudy's high formants multiplied by 1.3, Stillwater's lower formants mixed with noise, and Bolster using a sawtooth wave. Each voice gain is set to keep peak amplitude near 0.5.\n\nVoice gains are now fixed at 0.22 for Trudy, 0.55 for Stillwater, 0.7 for Bolster, and 0.4 for the guest. Gary's squawk will be handled separately. The `speak` function walks raw text characters to schedule blips, grouping consecutive letters and flushing them on vowel transitions or punctuation.\n\nThe `speak` function now uses a simpler loop over raw characters. Consecutive letters are buffered into syllable groups and scheduled as blips at the voice rate. Non-letter characters trigger noise ticks or pauses. The implementation is being streamlined further while preserving energy.\n\nThe voice scheduler now buffers two-letter groups into blips and pauses on non-letters. The title track is set to 92 BPM with swing at 0.08, using a Dbmaj9 motif and a simple bass line. An island track at 84 BPM is also being defined.\n\nrenderTrack schedules four bars of motif and bass. SFX functions will accept context, destination, and time arguments. The createAudio engine lazily instantiates an AudioContext and resumes it on unlock.\n\nThe audio engine now exposes setGains, setTilt, detune, play, stop, and state methods. The developer is deciding whether state().audio.music should return the stored settings value or the live gain.\n\nThe audio state will expose the live bus gain of 0.10 so tests can read it, while the stored settings value remains 10. The engine will stay silent when the AudioContext is suspended and unlock on the first user gesture. On session end it will close or suspend and disconnect the context and block further note playback. The director script is being written in a single pass.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40cbc71e-0e67-4463-b506-9ffdea7230dc-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/raft.js","offset":160,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40cbc71e-0e67-4463-b506-9ffdea7230dc-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"roundT|rounds","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/raft.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":306,"output_tokens":2563,"cache_read_input_tokens":156032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"4b1fc9bd-b699-49e8-b207-fea5d03727ef"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-40cbc71e-0e67-4463-b506-9ffdea7230dc-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"160→    const clumsy = skill === 'clumsy';\\n    const grip = skill === 'sharp' ? 1.6 : skill === 'average' ? 0.85 : 0.2;\\n    const highX = -Math.sign(this.tx || 0.0001);\\n    const highZ = -Math.sign(this.tz || 0.0001);\\n    let x = clamp(-p.x * grip + highX * (clumsy ? 0.9 : 0.15), -1, 1);\\n    let z = clamp(-p.z * grip + highZ * (clumsy ? 0.9 : 0.15), -1, 1);\\n    let flail = false;\\n    if (!clumsy) {\\n      for (let j = 0; j < this.players.length; j++) {\\n        if (j === i || this.players[j].out) continue;\\n170→        const d = Math.hypot(this.players[j].x - p.x, this.players[j].z - p.z);\\n        if (d < 1.25 && p.cool <= 0) flail = true;\\n      }\\n    } else if (Math.hypot(p.x, p.z) > this.radius * 0.7) {\\n      x = -Math.sign(p.x) * 0.4;\\n      z = -Math.sign(p.z) * 0.4;\\n    }\\n    return { wishX: x, wishZ: z, flail, hop: false };\\n  }\\n\\n180→  result(i = 0) {\\n    const won = this.wins[i] || 0;\\n    const form = clamp(40 + 30 * won, 0, 100);\\n    const winner = this.wins.indexOf(Math.max(...this.wins));\\n    return {\\n      form, raw: won, medal: medalOf(form),\\n      stats: `${won} rounds · seat ${winner + 1} leads`,\\n      falls: 0,\\n      won,\\n      winner,\\n190→    };\\n  }\\n\\n  botInput(i) {\\n    const move = this.botMove(i);\\n    return { x: move.wishX, y: -(move.wishZ || 0), flail: move.flail, hop: false, breathe: false };\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"160→    const clumsy = skill === 'clumsy';\\n    const grip = skill === 'sharp' ? 1.6 : skill === 'average' ? 0.85 : 0.2;\\n    const highX = -Math.sign(this.tx || 0.0001);\\n    const highZ = -Math.sign(this.tz || 0.0001);\\n    let x = clamp(-p.x * grip + highX * (clumsy ? 0.9 : 0.15), -1, 1);\\n    let z = clamp(-p.z * grip + highZ * (clumsy ? 0.9 : 0.15), -1