a\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"14\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n    rs: `<svg ${common}><circle cx=\\\"18\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"15\\\" fill=\\\"#efe7da\\\" stroke=\\\"${ink}\\\" stroke-width=\\\"3\\\"/><circle cx=\\\"22\\\" cy=\\\"18\\\" r=\\\"4\\\" fill=\\\"${ink}\\\"/></svg>`,\\n  };\\n\",\"total_lines\":82}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"3719a294-00df-45fc-84a1-d9bb63c5b92a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_126","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Glyphs are path-only. A fallback exists at the end.\n\nWriting the UI and director now. The director is large. A menu array defines the six main screens. Screen setters update the view and save state. Input handling in fixed() checks a locked flag.\n\nThe fixed() function polls input and routes to attract mode or screen handlers. Title, menu, and touch screens trigger attract mode after ten seconds of idle time. Waking during attract mode exits it. Waking during title resets idle and activates the screen on confirmation.\n\nMenu input uses edge detection. Up and down arrows move focus. Left and right arrows adjust sliders. Confirm activates the selected choice. Back returns to the previous screen.\n\nPlay mode ignores menu edge navigation. Pause opens the pause menu during active play and halts event stepping. Dev builds are restricted to pause. Restart disposes and rebuilds the current event, returning to intro or countdown. Leaving a class disposes it and returns to the island or main menu. Check-in events spawn a CheckIn instance and begin bot play.\n\nCheck-in completion computes age and displays it on the age screen. The age-falls test runs day one and day two check-ins with a sharp bot. Ages should drop because handicap decreases even when the mean stays similar. Programme tests allow any card order. After all classes finish, the bed screen appears with Bed and Free Play choices. Bed stamps and advances to the next morning. Grand hold classes with zero tilt trigger an ending screen before bed.\n\nThe ending screen has two pages. The first shows the middle line. Confirming advances to the second page, which displays the credits roll text. Confirming again stamps the day if it is not already stamped, sets dayIndex to 5, and transitions to the maintenance morning screen. Day indices run from 0 through 4 for the five regular days. After the grand hold class completes at index 4, the ending sequence runs credits before bed and then maintenance.\n\nFree play from the menu contains fourteen events. The grand hold notch is marked complete when the tilt reaches zero, even though the event itself may not yet be done. This early completion can push the step count above the other day-five classes if the grand hold is played last. The plan expects this behavior: the final notch occurs inside the hold, and remaining tildes follow the completed step count.\n\nThe final notch is the last programme step. Tilt only reaches zero when grand hold completes and is the last remaining step, or when that notch fires. If earlier steps are skipped, tilt stays above zero. The story order plays all classes before grand hold.\n\nThe tilt formula is 9° multiplied by one minus completed divided by total. This makes the island level once the final notch fires, even if earlier steps were skipped.\n\nThe last notch will mark every programme step complete. This guarantees the island levels during the grand hold even if earlier steps were skipped. It is a generous interpretation that matches the story's intent to keep the player from getting stuck.\n\nThe intro screen shows can and cant. Confirming starts a three-second countdown before play. Session mode skips the title screen and uses AIHub.time() for its loop. The runSession function sets session state, clears stopped, and listens for card events.\n\nSession mode registers AIHub callbacks for start, time-up, end, leave, and recv. It seeds a deal RNG to pick three cards from the session pool into slots, marks ready, and begins listening for keys.\n\nSession mode avoids Math.random entirely. It uses AIHub.time() in milliseconds, converting to seconds and clamping negative values. The round splits into sixty-two-second slots; once three slots pass, the session waits and sends the result. Progress updates every second and ghost messages every tenth of a second. The local phase is mapped to an intro window, a play window, or a score window.\n\nSession mode handles time jumps by switching to the slot the clock indicates. It disposes the current event and starts the correct one, then advances the event by elapsed play time in capped chunks to prevent desync.\n\nWithin a slot it steps by frame delta. If local play time leads the event by more than half a second it catches up with capped fixed steps.\n\nSlot zero scores zero during its intro. After play the score is the sum of each round multiplied by ten.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b4cc9192-c648-4c2a-aa25-7826e14fdac6-98","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"type: 'welcome'|players:|function connect","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/vendor/session.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2626,"output_tokens":2316,"cache_read_input_tokens":173568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"7e9c5d77-992d-4565-9d6d-62c295fb0b1e"}
