{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-18770f7d-1339-41e1-b223-ec555d716ce2-103","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/vendor/session.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"57765664-e694-413a-bafa-e0199de70973"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_132","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The rate limit allows 20 requests per second with a burst of 40. Ten ghosts per second is safe.\n\nGhosts will be sent every 100ms of AIHub.time, or once per frame if that interval passes. This yields roughly six ghosts per second. The send is skipped before time reaches zero during the countdown and resumes after the intro ends. During the intro, ghosts are still sent with a label such as \"Poses 0\" in 24 characters.\n\nsetSessionMode(true) is called at session start to route rng through AIHub.rng. Card answers are captured via window keydown for Enter and M before the game is ready.\n\nPad triangle is mapped to button 3. Card answers use Enter and M. A second tap target handles \"more\". Enter is blocked from falling through to other handlers.\n\nDuring a session, the pause edge shows a volume overlay instead of pausing. Development tools are disabled.\n\nThe lobby group class has four seats. Pads cross-join each seat. Keyboard input joins as one seat. Once at least one player joins, the menu offers Quick Class, Pick, and Back.\n\nThe lobby menu narrows to three options: Quick Class, Choose Three, and Back. Quick Class selects three couch events at random and runs them with lanes equal to the joined players; the raft event adds bots when fewer than two lanes are present. After each event, players are ranked by form and awarded 4, 3, 2, or 1 points, with a final podium.\n\nFour pads can join Group Class. Each pad controls its own lane by pressing cross on button 0. The test will choose the Tippy Raft event directly, since Quick Class might not select it. During group play, the director creates one input per seat with setPadIndex(i), and the pad source returns all pads. Bots are null, so the test may not drive skillfully.\n\nTippy Raft ends with a winner field rather than a specific seat. Without input, players stand at start positions and are eventually knocked off by swells and shrink. If no one drives, the round ends at 85 seconds with the closest-to-center winner. Three rounds total about 255 seconds of simulation time. The test may use bot('sharp') during group raft, which would write identical pad values to all lanes.\n\nThe test will verify that each pad controls its own lane by setting different stick directions on separate pads and checking that their lean values differ. It will then run the raft event with bot skill to ensure it finishes with a winner.\n\nBot input is applied per lane through botInput(i), so each pad drives its own lane independently.\n\nThe attract mode shows an 18-second event list, then a 5-second title before looping. It tracks visits and skips god mode for the fruit hat event.\n\nDevelopment tools are grouped into pages of four controls plus reset and back buttons.\n\nThe test will open pause during play, enter Dev Mode, adjust the maxLean slider, verify the state tuning reflects the new value, and confirm that reset restores the default. The dev screen is unreachable from the title screen because goto('dev') no-ops and the menu omits it.\n\nSettings are split into four pages: sound, controls, display, and game. Each page holds at most six focusables. Controls use glyphs for left and right cycles, plus rumble, auto breathe, and rhythm. Display settings include UI scale, ink, shake, and fullscreen. Game settings cover difficulty and save reset. Every page uses three sliders plus next and back buttons.\n\nThe sound page holds five items: music, sound, voice sliders, next page, and back. A \"Glyphs\" choice cycles left and right instead of using separate buttons.\n\nAbout pages are eight text screens with previous and next navigation. A minimal about.js will be written by hand to match the JSON, and the build script will overwrite it from exit-interview data.\n\nI will write exit-interview.json and about.js with the final text. Provisional issue counts will be recorded in issues.md now so they stay stable after testing. Three critical bugs are logged: logReps scoring an empty first rep, Plank beginning a fall twice, and Island Loop cadence using a changing modulo that scored 26.\n\nThe exit interview is written before the final test run. Eight issues are logged, five of them critical. The eighth is a one-foot margin applied twice.\n\nA coarse-pointer check will detect touch devices at boot. On touch screens, the game starts directly in the screen instead of the title, while settings and attract mode remain available; key or pad input returns to the title. The Island screen will show a Trudy line with Today's Plan, Bed, and Back to menu choices, using edges.ask for navigation.\n\nPaint and hat choices unlock after earning marbles. The journal shows stamps, an age graph, medals, and totals. The balance disc is a DOM circle with a dot positioned by cob; data-cob-x will let tests verify lean movement. Errors are caught only at main() boot, not inside event steps, so physics panics remain visible.\n\nThe director lets physics panics propagate so tests can see them. createGame will await initRapier() once before returning the API. Node tests will call it with manual and render disabled.\n\nStorage will use opts.storage, memoryStorage, or localStorage. A fresh profile defaults to Maple with coral paint and no hat, zero marbles, and empty progress arrays. The save writes on every screen change. Reloading creates a new game instance that restores the saved state at startup. The goto function blocks the dev screen unless the current screen is pause.\n\nThe `goto` function routes to `startEvent` for the play screen and `setScreen` otherwise. The `bot` helper stores skill and options. `advance` converts seconds into fixed ticks and calls `frame` once at the end. Speech timers use fixed delta time. Rendering is skipped. The dev time scale multiplies in the real loop, but `advance` stays unscaled so tests remain deterministic.\n\nSingle-step advances one fixed tick even while paused. UI scale and glyph set are wired into state.input.glyphSet. Mouse hover is handled by ui.js and keyboard input by main.js; node tests call input methods directly instead of using window listeners. The director polls input from pads. Menu confirm on a pad requires pressing cross, advancing one frame, and releasing. Focus logic in state() suffices for node tests; DOM visibility is verified with Playwright.\n\nI will write the director and UI modules next. The event import graph is safe: checkin imports from game/checkin.js, not director. Solo events use one local lane for the player profile. Attract mode uses one bot lane named Demo with god mode enabled. The fruit hat attract event disables god mode and sets bankAt to 99 so it topples. Session lanes are one local seat.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9ded1924-769b-4107-abed-b3b18e2acdb8-104","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"opts\\.session|this\\.session|duration = 50","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":789,"output_tokens":3052,"cache_read_input_tokens":182400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"0bab2ac2-bc53-4841-a855-5b02edeea526"}
