5,32,112,108,117,115,32,97,32,115,104,111,114,116,32,84,83,76,32,112,97,115,115,32,103,97,118,101,32,116,104,101,32,119,104,111,108,101,32,105,110,107,32,108,111,111,107,32,111,110,32,98,111,116,104,32,98,97,99,107,101,110,100,115,46,34,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":93,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"## 1. The game\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"## 2. Originality rules\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"## 3. Controls\"},{\"line_number\":98,\"content\":\"## 4. The balance model\"},{\"line_number\":174,\"content\":\"**The Balance Disc.** `cob = (leanX, leanZ) / maxLean` is the dot, shown truthfully. Draw it as inline SVG and move it with transforms each frame. It is the game's signature HUD: a large circular dial with rings, a target zone that turns green when you are inside, the solid dot, a faint ring showing where your stick is asking to go, and a short inked trail of the last half second, like a seismograph needle. Diameter is about 22% of screen height, bottom left. Trudy peeks over its rim and reacts. In Group Class each player gets a smaller one (14%) along the bottom edge.\"},{\"line_number\":180,\"content\":\"**Breath.** In Stillness events a breath ring pulses: 4 s growing, 4 s shrinking. Hold Breathe while it grows, release while it shrinks. Over the last full cycle, 70%+ in sync multiplies sway and tremor by 0.6 and form gain by 1.25. Out of sync does nothing bad except miss the bonus. Accessibility toggle: auto-breathe. It is worth a lot ✔: perfectly in sync, Poses Tier 1 goes 95→100 / 66→91 / 54→78, and The Cairn Tier 2 goes from 5.3 / 4.8 / 2 stones of 8 to 8 / 8 / 6.3.\"},{\"line_number\":186,\"content\":\"## 5. Programme and progress\"},{\"line_number\":201,\"content\":\"**A day's flow:** morning line → personal question (Yes/No) → Check-In → Wobble Age reveal → Today's Plan (cards in any order: walk there or pick a card to go directly) → each class → Results → marbles → the island comes up a notch → extra Free Play if wanted → the bed hut. Press Use, the screen inks out, a stamp lands on the calendar, the next dawn. Palettes follow the day's steps (dawn, noon, golden, dusk), unless an event pins its own (Step Class at dusk, The Grand Hold at sunset).\"},{\"line_number\":210,\"content\":\"**Wobble Age.** `age = round(18 + 81 × (1 − mean)^1.3 + handicap)`, clamped to 18..99. The handicap is a comic head start that shrinks each day: +24, +16, +8, +3, then 0. So the number always falls, and that is what makes coming back feel good. With unchanged skill, Day 1 to Day 5 ✔: 56→32 / 66→42 / 86→62. The reveal is the comic set piece: lights dim, drum roll, numbers spin on a wooden counter, sting, Trudy's line from a band of lines by age. Stored per day and drawn as the Journal's graph. It never asks your real age (\\\"I didn't ask how old you are. I asked your knees.\\\").\"},{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"## 6. Events\"},{\"line_number\":234,\"content\":\"**Flow.** Intro Card (name, one sentence, what you can and can't do, one diagram, this device's prompts; Use to begin) → instructor counts 3-2-1 → play → whistle or bell → Results (ink-stamp medal, one big number, one line of stats, a line of dialogue, retry or continue) → marbles in the programme.\"},{\"line_number\":245,\"content\":\"- *Play:* The heron demonstrates, then the target ring glides from centre to the pose's spot on the disc (3 s). Follow it, then hold while the ring shrinks. Breath ring runs throughout.\"},{\"line_number\":259,\"content\":\"- *Play:* Sit on a lily pad for 60 s. Stay in the small calm zone. Calm fills a meter, and creatures arrive at thresholds: dragonfly on your nose, frog on your head, koi circling, turtle, and at full calm Ms. Stillwater tiptoes over and pats your head. Move too much and they scatter. Ripples spread from the pad in proportion to how much you move: this is a beautiful TSL shader on the pond. Distractions: Trudy whispering (\\\"Don't think about your left knee\\\"), a sneeze (telegraphed \\\"Ah... ah...\\\": press Flail to stifle it, or take a big shove).\"},{\"line_number\":266,\"content\":\"- *Play:* A log across your shoulders. A tempo ribbon moves down 2 s, pauses 0.5 s, up 2 s, rests 0.5 s. Squeeze both triggers to sink (depth = average of L2 and R2; on keyboard and mouse, holding both ramps depth down at the tempo's speed and releasing ramps up). Stay in the ribbon's band and keep the dot centred. Fatigue grows each rep: depth shake from .015 to .07, a narrower band (half-width .16→.10), stronger rumble.\"},{\"line_number\":315,\"content\":\"- *Play:* Carry a tray of tumblers along a narrow boardwalk. **Alternate feet to step** (same foot twice is a stumble). Each step rocks you a little. Leaning steers sideways too. Wind gusts are telegraphed for a full second by ink streaks and a rising sound, **and the Balance Disc shows a green zone where to lean.** Gary swoops for a glass on Tier 2+. Wobbly planks on Tier 2+. Off the edge: splash, respawn at the last buoy with one fewer glass. Deliver what is left to the table. The lesson the game teaches: **small early leans keep the glasses, sudden big ones throw them.**\"},{\"line_number\":331,\"content\":\"- *Numbers ✔:* radius 6, losing 1 m every 12 s down to 2. Tilt model K 6, C 3.5, 14° for one doll at the rim, clamped to 26°. Slope push `tilt × 10`. Walk 3 m/s. Swell about every 6 s: adds 2.5 rad/s to the tilt velocity. Shove: within 1.3 m, gives the target 6 m/s, decaying at 3 /s, with a 2 s cooldown. Over 16 rounds with one sharp, two average and one clumsy bot: rounds lasted 10-55 s, 29 s on average; wins 6 / 8 (between two bots) / 2. So skill helps and doesn't decide it. (Without swells and at a slow shrink, rounds never ended: everyone just stands in the middle.)\"},{\"line_number\":337,\"content\":\"- *Play:* Your balance is now tied directly to the island: your lean tips everything below you. Four 20-second phases, each a remix: a Pose with breath; four stones on your head; storm gusts with Gary; a short Step Class in the wind with the class cheering from below. Then the last hold: 15 s, the ring shrinking to the centre, sway fading as you succeed, the final notch coming up.\"},{\"line_number\":361,\"content\":\"## 7. Screens\"},{\"line_number\":363,\"content\":\"**The 10-foot rules.** All UI is a DOM overlay over the canvas. Lowest text size is 30 px at 1080p; body text 36+; titles huge. Keep a 5% safe margin. At most six choices on a screen, not counting a page switcher. Longer lists are split into pages. One idea per screen. No tables, no scrolling lists of data, no small print except on About, which is paged. Every focusable thing has a thick, bouncing, inked focus state, and hover moves that focus. Default font: Fredoka (section 16). UI elements look like paper tags and wooden signs with inked borders, each slightly rotated, never a web form.\"},{\"line_number\":376,\"content\":\"| Journal | Page 1: calendar with stamps. Page 2: the Wobble Age graph, as a big inked line and three big numbers. Page 3+: medals shelf, up to 8 per page. Page last: silly totals (Floor Exercises, Minutes, Marbles) |\"},{\"line_number\":380,\"content\":\"| Settings | Four pages. Sound: Music (default **10**), Sound, Voice. Controls: glyph style, rumble, auto-breathe, rhythm offset. Display: UI scale, ink strength, reduce shake, fullscreen. Game: difficulty, reset save (with an in-game confirm). Sliders move with left and right, drag with mouse |\"},{\"line_number\":385,\"content\":\"Transitions use an ink-blot wipe: add a `wipe` uniform to the post chain, mixing to ink colour where a noise value is below it. Dialogue: a paper speech tag in the lower third with the speaker's name, text typing out in time with the voice. Use to advance, or it auto-advances for barks. Everything spoken is on screen; there is no audio-only line.\"},{\"line_number\":389,\"content\":\"## 8. Cast and writing\"},{\"line_number\":393,\"content\":\"**Trudy, Head of Alignment.** A chunky spirit level on two stubby pegs. Her bubble is her eye: it slides to the high side of the world, and to wherever she is feeling. She has been crooked with the island since she was installed and thinks of this as normal. Fussy aunt energy. Keeps count of everything and insists she isn't. She gets attached to you and would die before saying so.\"},{\"line_number\":406,\"content\":\"**Ms. Stillwater, Stillness.** A tall heron on one leg. Half-closed eyes. A voice like a slow door. She has never blinked on camera. She notices everything and is not bothered by any of it.\"},{\"line_number\":425,\"content\":\"## 9. Art bible\"},{\"line_number\":427,\"content\":\"The look is **sun-bleached Japanese resort postcard meets wooden toy box, drawn in ink.** I rendered this cast and these materials with the recipe below and they read clearly on a TV-sized frame ✔.\"},{\"line_number\":444,\"content\":\"**Materials ✔.** Everything solid is cel-shaded: `MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color, gradientMap })` with a 3-step `DataTexture` ramp `[96, 178, 255]`, `NearestFilter`, `NoColorSpace`. `renderer.toneMapping = THREE.NoToneMapping` keeps the palette true. Sky and sea use `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` with a TSL `colorNode`. Anything that should get a hull outline must be a toon material.\"},{\"line_number\":448,\"content\":\"**The ink recipe ✔** (runs on WebGPU and on the WebGL2 fallback, tested in Chromium and WebKit):\"},{\"line_number\":458,\"content\":\"              grain: uniform(0.02), near: uniform(camera.near), far: uniform(camera.far), ink: uniform(new THREE.Color(INK)) };\"},{\"line_number\":466,\"content\":\"    const wob = hash(floor(time.mul(8)).add(cell.x).add(cell.y.mul(17))).sub(0.5).mul(u.boil);   // hand-drawn line boil\"},{\"line_number\":475,\"content\":\"    const c = mix(colorTex.rgb, u.ink, e);\"},{\"line_number\":477,\"content\":\"    const g = hash(p.x.add(p.y.mul(1571))).sub(0.5).mul(u.grain);\"},{\"line_number\":485,\"content\":\"- TSL `hash()` takes **one float**. Give it a vec2 and you get vertical streaks over the whole image.\"},{\"line_number\":489,\"content\":\"- Glass ✔: **do not use a toon material on glass.** The hull pass draws solid ink back faces behind it and the glass turns smoky grey. Use `MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color: 0xe8fbff, transparent: true, opacity: 0.16, side: DoubleSide, depthWrite: false })`, and draw its outline with thin toon torus rings at the base, shoulder, neck and lip, plus a couple of narrow white highlight strips. It looks like a clean inked glass jar.\"},{\"line_number\":494,\"content\":\"**Sky ✔.** Inverted sphere radius 600, `mix` of the three colours on the view direction's y (`smoothstep(0, .14)` and `smoothstep(.1, .5)`). Add inked toon clouds as flattened spheres that drift.\"},{\"line_number\":498,\"content\":\"- **Peg doll, 1.5 m.** Feet: white flattened spheres r .1 scaled (1, .55, 1.5), at x ±.13. Legs: skin capsules r .08, length .3. Hips at y .46. Shorts: capsule r .2 (scaled 1.05, 1, .85). Shirt: capsule r .21, length .24 (z scale .82). Head: sphere r .23, centre .82 above hips. Headband: torus r .228. Eyes: ink spheres r .024 at (±.08, .85, .205) from hips. Cheeks: pink flattened spheres. Arms: visible darker wooden ball joints r .075 at shoulders (±.26, .5) and r .06 at elbows, skin capsule segments, white mitten spheres r .07. Skin `#F2D3A8`, joints `#D9A86C`, shorts `#2B4A6F`. Vary with paint, hats (visor, beret, bucket hat, perm of spheres, wizard hat, tiny crown), and small height and width changes for guests.\"},{\"line_number\":499,\"content\":\"- **Trudy.** Rounded box (1.1, .42, .26), radius .1, `#F5B700`, on two stubby brown pegs. Dark window (.56, .2, .05) on the face holding a lime `#B9F26B` capsule vial r .075, length .36, lying on its side. Bubble: white flattened sphere with an ink pupil; it slides in the vial. Two ink marks on the vial like a level's centre lines. Round lime end vials at x ±.42 as cheeks. Ink torus arc for a mouth. She hops with squash and stretch. This design is very readable: keep it.\"},{\"line_number\":500,\"content\":\"- **Ms. Stillwater.** One long orange leg (cylinder r .025, height 1.05), the other tucked. Body sphere r .34 scaled (.8, .92, 1.35), `#A9C2D4`. Wings: flattened ellipsoids `#7E9CB4`. S-curve neck: `TubeGeometry` of a Catmull-Rom curve, r .062, `#D6E3EC`, rising to y 2.2. Head sphere r .115. Beak: yellow cone. Ink crest cone. Half-closed eyes as ink torus arcs. A small `#C24D6A` scarf at the base of the neck. For animation, build the neck from 5 joint segments.\"},{\"line_number\":501,\"content\":\"- **Coach Bolster.** Capsule r .72, length .5, scaled (1.06, 1, .9), `#B9806A`. Red sweatband torus at the top. Two pale muzzle spheres, cream cone tusks, tiny ink eyes, flattened flippers `#8D5F4F`, a white lanyard torus and a yellow whistle.\"},{\"line_number\":502,\"content\":\"- **Gary the gull.** White ellipsoid body, grey flattened wings, yellow cone beak, orange peg legs, ink dot eyes and one permanently angry brow.\"},{\"line_number\":504,\"content\":\"- **Island.** Sand disc r 22 over a grass disc r 15 (flush with the sand, or dolls sink into it: all walking surfaces share y = 0), big inverted rock cone below on its one pivot rock. Toy trees: peg trunk plus ball top. Lighthouse: stacked red and cream rings with a lamp and a blue cap. Pavilions: toy-block posts and rounded slab roofs in teal and orange. Sun Deck, Bandstand, Circus Green, Yard, Pier, Jar, Mirror pavilion, Notice Board, Gazebo, Bed Hut at fixed spots around the rim and centre. Every set in section 6 appears here as a landmark, and the class itself runs in its own world (section 16).\"},{\"line_number\":523,\"content\":\"## 10. Animation\"},{\"line_number\":538,\"content\":\"## 11. Audio\"},{\"line_number\":584,\"content\":\"## 12. Multiplayer\"},{\"line_number\":604,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":605,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":606,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"ghost\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":607,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"3\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":608,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Stay balanced through the class: highest score wins\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":609,\"content\":\"<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\\\">\"},{\"line_number\":644,\"content\":\"## 13. Attract mode\"},{\"line_number\":652,\"content\":\"## 14. Dev mode\"},{\"line_number\":656,\"content\":\"**Tools:** jump to any event and tier; jump to any day or step; skip to Results or to the Ending; god mode (no falls); time scale 0.1× to 4×; single-step; free camera; physics debug lines (`world.debugRender()` into a `LineSegments`); stats (fps, step ms, bodies, draw calls); input monitor (both sticks, triggers, last device); force a gust, a fall, a fruit or a stone; play any dialogue line, music track or sting; set Wobble Age; add marbles; unlock all; toggle ink and pick palette; let the bot play; reset save; copy tuning as JSON (to the clipboard, falling back to a large on-screen text so nothing needs a dialog).\"},{\"line_number\":669,\"content\":\"## 15. Touch-only devices\"},{\"line_number\":677,\"content\":\"## 16. Architecture and build\"},{\"line_number\":690,\"content\":\"src/render/    renderer.js  ink.js  palette.js  sky.js  sea.js  cameraRig.js  particles.js  comicText.js\"},{\"line_number\":733,\"content\":\"**Fresh world per event.** Events get a new Rapier world and a new `THREE.Group`, added under one scene that also holds sky, sea and lights. The island is hidden during events, or kept far in the background as scenery where a set wants it. Transitions hide the swap with the ink wipe.\"},{\"line_number\":737,\"content\":\"## 17. Testing\"},{\"line_number\":767,\"content\":\"- **Every test that renders must assert `render.lost` is null.** \\\"Frames rising\\\" proves nothing by itself. Also read the screenshot back as pixels and check it has ink and a range of colours ✔.\"},{\"line_number\":794,\"content\":\"*unit* (Node, no browser): Wobble Age mapping and bounds; marble payouts; tier unlock rules; programme table integrity (every id exists, days still work with a Tier B event removed); charts valid; tuning defaults inside min and max; dialogue ids all exist; save corrupt or old version is handled; rng repeatable; the session client hash; **the exit-interview file**, once it exists: parses, has exactly TASK.md's keys, 4, 6 and 4 feedback answers, no empty value except `series`, `usage` reading `added on import`, 3 to 6 lowercase tags, `genre` from TASK.md's list, `name` equal to the title constant; the built HTML has the metas in `name`, `content` order, the client directly after `<meta charset>`, and no `</script` inside a script. **Source greps:** no `Math.random` outside `src/core/rng.js`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`; no `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`, `window.open`, `WebSocket`, `RTCPeerConnection`; no audio file extensions or `decodeAudioData`; none of the source's nam [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":808,\"content\":\"*ui:* at 1920×1080, walk every screen and assert: no text under 30 px in computed style, nothing outside the viewport or the 5% margin except backgrounds, at most six focusable items, a visible focus. Touch-only: Pixel 7, iPhone and iPad profiles show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and Settings, `page.touchscreen` tap opens Settings, no other controls respond, attract runs, a key or pad clears the state. About shows every Source Information field and the three feedback lists, and matches the exit-interview file.\"},{\"line_number\":810,\"content\":\"**Art pass, by eye, at the end.** `tools/shots.mjs` with `RENDER` at 1920×1080: title, island on Day 1 and Day 5, each event mid-play, results, jar, Age Reveal, Group Class with four dolls, Dev Mode, About. Look for lost legibility at 10 feet, sunk characters, messy ink.\"},{\"line_number\":814,\"content\":\"## 18. Build order and cut order\"},{\"line_number\":820,\"content\":\"| 0 | Skeleton | Build script, single HTML, renderer with ink, sky and sea, Rapier, the loop, hooks, `test.mjs`, session client in place |\"},{\"line_number\":833,\"content\":\"## 19. Done and reporting\"},{\"line_number\":838,\"content\":\"- [ ] WebGPU backend by default, WebGL2 fallback works, cel-shaded with the ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Three R180, Web Audio, Gamepad API\"},{\"line_number\":848,\"content\":\"- [ ] About/Credits, the exit-interview file and your chat reply are all filled in as below\"},{\"line_number\":850,\"content\":\"**Three places, the same content.** TASK.md calls this critical: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback go in **your chat reply** and an **in-game About/Credits screen,** and into **the exit-interview file** beside the HTML. These are your own answers from your own build. Nothing in this plan answers them for you, and section 22 is only an example. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\"},{\"line_number\":854,\"content\":\"2. Write the exit-interview file beside the HTML, using `notes/issues.md` for the counts.\"},{\"line_number\":861,\"content\":\"**The About/Credits screen.** Reached from the main menu. It follows the 10-foot rules: large type, one page at a time, moved with left and right or clicks, never a scrolling wall of text. It is also the one screen where long answers may take several pages: split them rather than shrink them.\"},{\"line_number\":879,\"content\":\"## Source Information\"},{\"line_number\":881,\"content\":\"## Testing Feedback\"},{\"line_number\":883,\"content\":\"## Engine Feedback\"},{\"line_number\":885,\"content\":\"## Prompt Feedback\"},{\"line_number\":897,\"content\":\"| Tech | Three.js R180 on the WebGPU backend (WebGL2 fallback), TSL toon and ink post, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild, Fredoka, plus anything you added, with versions |\"},{\"line_number\":898,\"content\":\"| Art Direction | Cel-shaded ink filter over a wooden-toy resort, all models made in code on Three.js's own materials |\"},{\"line_number\":928,\"content\":\"**The exit-interview file** is one JSON object in TASK.md's exact shape, plain text, every value filled in, and you check that it parses: `sourceInformation` (`date, source, plan, genre, perspective, tech, artDirection, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage`), `testingFeedback`, `engineFeedback`, `promptFeedback` (arrays, answers in order), and `aiHub`:\"},{\"line_number\":940,\"content\":\"| `controls` | The same line as `hub:session-howto` |\"},{\"line_number\":945,\"content\":\"## 20. What was and wasn't verified\"},{\"line_number\":947,\"content\":\"**Tested here on 2026-11-04 (✔ above):** versions exist on npm and jsDelivr; single-file esbuild build from `file://`; WebGPU in Chromium with SwiftShader, and which flags really render; WebGL2 fallback in Chromium and WebKit; `toonOutlinePass` with MRT and the custom ink pass; instanced toon meshes; glass; shadow settings; the look of the cast and all four palettes; client hash; balance model; torque limit; gusts and flail; island tilt; marble pours; ragdoll; Rapier's crash conditions and a soak of every removal path; touch media queries; Fredoka's licence and file names.\"},{\"line_number\":961,\"content\":\"## 21. TASK.md coverage and proof\"},{\"line_number\":963,\"content\":\"Every requirement in TASK.md, in its order: where this plan answers it, and what proves it was met when you build. Test groups are in section 17. Some of what TASK.md asks for can only exist once there is a build: the game itself, its About/Credits screen, the exit-interview file and your final report. This plan covers those by saying exactly what to produce, when, and how it gets checked. Producing them is the build's job, and yours.\"},{\"line_number\":975,\"content\":\"| Stylized cel-shaded / ink filter | Section 9 | `events`: ink pixels in a read-back screenshot ✔. Art pass |\"},{\"line_number\":1026,\"content\":\"## 22. Planning-stage report\"},{\"line_number\":1030,\"content\":\"**Source Information.** Date: 2026-11-04 21:19:05. Source: Wii Fit. Plan: none (this stage wrote it). Genre and Perspective: physics-balance party sports with a daily-ritual progression; third person, with framed stage cameras per event and an orbitable chase camera on the island. Tech: Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0. Art Direction: cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy resort, all models made in code. Animation: `AnimationMixer` clips on jointed rigs, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls (prototyped with test clips). Audio: code-synthesised city-pop and bossa at 10% by default, effects, Animalese and Simlish-style voices (motif, voices and click prototyped). Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 on one screen. Testing: as much headless testing as wanted, with scripts that play and check state; one command printing only failures and a one-l [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":1039,\"content\":\"1. *What did you like most about the engine?* `toonOutlinePass` plus a short TSL pass gave the whole ink look, unchanged on WebGPU and WebGL2.\"},{\"line_number\":1040,\"content\":\"2. *Did you get stuck or guess wrong?* Yes. I took a lost device for 60 fps. `hash()` given a vec2 streaked the image, toon glass turned smoky, and convex-hull stones collapsed on their own.\"},{\"line_number\":1052,\"content\":\"**The exit-interview file's shape,** filled in for this stage. It parses, and its keys match TASK.md's exactly. Replace every value with your own. `name` and `tagline` are \\\"unknown\\\" here only because each builder picks its own title.\"},{\"line_number\":1056,\"content\":\"  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\"},{\"line_number\":1062,\"content\":\"    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":1063,\"content\":\"    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy resort, all models made in code\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":1080,\"content\":\"    \\\"toonOutlinePass plus a short TSL pass gave the whole ink look on both backends.\\\",\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-951a233c-947b-40f4-9018-c965003ea402-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"200→    profile.minutes += (event.t || 0) / 60;\\n    profile.floor += result.falls || 0;\\n    if (eventId !== 'checkin') {\\n      const form = result.form || 0;\\n      const best = profile.best[eventId] || {};\\n      best[tier] = Math.max(best[tier] || 0, form);\\n      profile.best[eventId] = best;\\n      if (!profile.met.includes(eventId)) profile.met.push(eventId);\\n      if (programme.includes(eventId) && !profile.doneSteps.includes(eventId)) profile.doneSteps.push(eventId);\\n      const first = !profile.cleared[eventId];\\n210→      jarPay = marblePayout({\\n        seconds: event.t || 0, form, firstClear: first,\\n        perMin: getTune('marblesPerMin'), medalScale: getTune('medalScale'),\\n      });\\n      profile.cleared[eventId] = true;\\n      profile.medals.push({ id: eventId, tier, form, medal: result.medal });\\n      if (!profile.classDone.includes(eventId)) profile.classDone.push(eventId);\\n    }\\n    event.dispose();\\n    event = null;\\n220→    audio.setTilt(tiltRad());\\n  }\\n\\n  function woke(sample, travel) {\\n    const e = sample.edges;\\n    if (e.confirm || e.back || e.pause || e.hop || e.flail || e.ask || e.up || e.down || e.left || e.right || e.recenter) return true;\\n    if (sample.padConnected && Math.hypot(sample.wish.x, sample.wish.y) > 0.3) return true;\\n    if (travel > 8) return true;\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n230→\\n  function menuMove(sample) {\\n    const list = choicesOf();\\n    const n = list.length || 1;\\n    if (sample.edges.up) focus = (focus - 1 + n) % n;\\n    if (sample.edges.down) focus = (focus + 1) % n;\\n    if (sample.edges.left || sample.edges.right) nudge(list[focus], sample.edges.right ? 1 : -1);\\n    if (sample.edges.confirm) activate(focus);\\n    if (sample.edges.back) back();\\n  }\\n240→\\n  function nudge(choice, dir) {\\n    if (!choice) return;\\n    if (choice.kind === 'slider') {\\n      const def = TUNING_DEFS.find((d) => d.id === choice.id);\\n      if (def) setTune(choice.id, getTune(choice.id) + dir * def.step);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (choice.id === 'music') settings.music = clampNum(settings.music + dir * 5, 0, 100);\\n    if (choice.id === 'sfx') settings.sfx = clampNum(settings.sfx + dir * 5, 0, 100);\\n250→    if (choice.id === 'voice') settings.voice = clampNum(settings.voice + dir * 5, 0, 100);\\n    if (choice.id === 'glyphs') settings.glyphs = settings.glyphs === 'playstation' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n    if (choice.id === 'difficulty') {\\n      const order = ['gentle', 'standard', 'honest'];\\n      const i = order.indexOf(settings.difficulty);\\n      settings.difficulty = order[(i + (dir > 0 ? 1 : 2)) % 3];\\n    }\\n    if (choice.id === 'name') profile.nameIndex = (profile.nameIndex + (dir > 0 ? 1 : NAMES.length - 1)) % NAMES.length;\\n    if (choice.id === 'paint') profile.paintIndex = (profile.paintIndex + (dir > 0 ? 1 : PAINTS.length - 1)) % PAINTS.length;\\n    if (choice.id === 'hat') profile.hatIndex = (profile.hatIndex + (dir > 0 ? 1 : HATS.length - 1)) % HATS.length;\\n260→    if (choice.id === 'page') page = Math.max(0, page + dir);\\n    applySettings();\\n  }\\n\\n  function activate(index) {\\n    const list = choicesOf();\\n    const choice = list[index];\\n    if (!choice || choice.kind === 'slider') return;\\n    focus = index;\\n    audio.unlock();\\n270→    audio.sfx('uiConfirm');\\n    const id = choice.id;\\n    if (screen === 'title') return setScreen(profile.stamps.length || profile.dayIndex > 0 ? 'menu' : 'who');\\n    if (screen === 'touch') return setScreen('settings');\\n    if (screen === 'who' && id === 'begin') {\\n      profile.name = NAMES[profile.nameIndex];\\n      profile.paint = PAINTS[profile.paintIndex].id;\\n      profile.hat = HATS[profile.hatIndex].id;\\n      return setScreen('tutorial');\\n    }\\n280→    if (screen === 'tutorial' && id === 'on') return beginDay();\\n    if (screen === 'menu') {\\n      if (id === 'programme') return profile.classDone.length ? setScreen('plan') : beginDay();\\n      if (id === 'group') { group = { seats: [null, null, null, null], points: [0, 0, 0, 0], playlist: [], cursor: 0 }; return setScreen('group'); }\\n      if (id === 'free') { freePick = true; return setScreen('free'); }\\n      if (id === 'journal') return setScreen('journal');\\n      if (id === 'settings') return setScreen('settings');\\n      if (id === 'about') return setScreen('about');\\n    }\\n    if (screen === 'question') return answerQuestion(id);\\n290→    if (screen === 'reply') { eventId = 'checkin'; beginCountdown(); return; }\\n    if (screen === 'age') return setScreen('plan');\\n    if (screen === 'plan' && eventById(id)) return openIntro(id);\\n    if (screen === 'intro') return beginCountdown();\\n    if (screen === 'results') {\\n      if (id === 'retry') return openIntro(eventId);\\n      return afterResult();\\n    }\\n    if (screen === 'jar') return afterJar();\\n    if (screen === 'bed') {\\n300→      if (id === 'free') { freePick = true; return setScreen('free'); }\\n      return sleepDay();\\n    }\\n    if (screen === 'ending') return setScreen(pageOfEnding());\\n    if (screen === 'credits') { sleepDay(); return setScreen('menu'); }\\n    if (screen === 'pause') return pauseAction(id);\\n    if (screen === 'settings') return settingsAction(id);\\n    if (screen === 'dev') return devAction(id);\\n    if (screen === 'free' && eventById(id)) return openIntro(id);\\n    if (screen === 'group') return groupAction(id);\\n310→    if (screen === 'confirm-reset' && id === 'yes') { resetAll(); return setScreen('title'); }\\n    if (screen === 'confirm-reset') return setScreen('settings');\\n    if (screen === 'island') {\\n      if (id === 'plan') return setScreen('plan');\\n      if (id === 'bed') return setScreen('bed');\\n      if (id === 'menu') return setScreen('menu');\\n    }\\n    paint();\\n  }\\n\\n320→  function pageOfEnding() {\\n    if (screen === 'ending') return 'credits';\\n    return 'credits';\\n  }\\n\\n  function beginDay() {\\n    freePick = false;\\n    profile.classDone = [];\\n    talk('trudy', 'morning');\\n    setScreen('morning');\\n330→  }\\n\\n  function answerQuestion(id) {\\n    const q = QUESTIONS[profile.dayIndex % QUESTIONS.length];\\n    const key = id === 'yes' ? q.yes : id === 'no' ? q.no : id === 'left' ? q.left : q.right;\\n    const line = lookup(key);\\n    speech = { who: 'Trudy', text: line ? line.text : 'Noted.', id: key };\\n    speechLeft = 1.2;\\n    if (line) audio.say(line.text, 'trudy');\\n    setScreen('reply');\\n340→  }\\n\\n  function openIntro(id) {\\n    eventId = id;\\n    tier = tierFor(id);\\n    setScreen('intro');\\n  }\\n\\n  function beginCountdown() {\\n    const plan = today();\\n350→    startEvent(eventId, {\\n      tests: eventId === 'checkin' ? plan.tests : undefined,\\n      god: screen === 'attract',\\n    });\\n    if (eventId === 'checkin') {\\n      screen = 'checkinPlay';\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    countLeft = 3;\\n    setScreen('countdown');\\n360→  }\\n\\n  function afterResult() {\\n    if (eventId === 'checkin') return;\\n    profile.marbles += jarPay;\\n    jarLeft = 2;\\n    audio.sfx('marble');\\n    setScreen('jar');\\n  }\\n\\n370→  function afterJar() {\\n    if (profile.levelled && eventId === 'grandHold') {\\n      sayExact(\\\"Oh. So that's what the middle looks like.\\\");\\n      return setScreen('ending');\\n    }\\n    const plan = today();\\n    const pendingClass = plan.classes.filter((id) => !profile.classDone.includes(id));\\n    if (group && group.playlist) return scoreGroup();\\n    if (pendingClass.length && !freePick) return setScreen('plan');\\n    if (freePick) return setScreen('free');\\n380→    return setScreen('bed');\\n  }\\n\\n  function sleepDay() {\\n    const plan = today();\\n    profile.stamps.push({ day: profile.dayIndex + 1, name: plan.name });\\n    profile.dayIndex += 1;\\n    profile.classDone = [];\\n    palette = 'dawn';\\n    persist();\\n390→  }\\n\\n  function scoreGroup() {\\n    if (!group) return setScreen('menu');\\n    const forms = lastResult && lastResult.forms ? lastResult.forms : group.seats.map((s, i) => (s ? (i === 0 ? lastResult.form : 0) : -1));\\n    const ranked = forms.map((form, i) => ({ i, form })).filter((row) => row.form >= 0).sort((a, b) => b.form - a.form);\\n    const points = [4, 3, 2, 1];\\n    ranked.forEach((row, place) => { group.points[row.i] += points[place] || 1; });\\n    group.cursor += 1;\\n    if (group.cursor >= group.playlist.length) return setScreen('podium');\\n400→    openIntro(group.playlist[group.cursor]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function back() {\\n    if (screen === 'settings' || screen === 'about' || screen === 'journal' || screen === 'free' || screen === 'group' || screen === 'mirror') return setScreen('menu');\\n    if (screen === 'dev') return setScreen('pause');\\n    if (screen === 'pause') { paused = false; return setScreen('play'); }\\n    if (screen === 'plan' || screen === 'island') return setScreen('menu');\\n    if (screen === 'who') return setScreen('title');\\n  }\\n410→\\n  function pauseAction(id) {\\n    if (id === 'resume') { paused = false; return setScreen('play'); }\\n    if (id === 'restart') { openIntro(eventId); return; }\\n    if (id === 'howto') return setScreen('howto');\\n    if (id === 'settings') return setScreen('settings');\\n    if (id === 'dev') { devFromPause = true; return setScreen('dev'); }\\n    if (id === 'leave') {\\n      if (event) event.dispose();\\n      event = null;\\n420→      return setScreen('island');\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function settingsAction(id) {\\n    if (id === 'glyphs') settings.glyphs = settings.glyphs === 'playstation' ? 'xbox' : 'playstation';\\n    if (id === 'rumble') settings.rumble = !settings.rumble;\\n    if (id === 'breathe') settings.autoBreathe = !settings.autoBreathe;\\n    if (id === 'shake') settings.reduceShake = !settings.reduceShake;\\n    if (id === 'full') {\\n430→      const el = doc && doc.documentElement;\\n      if (el && el.requestFullscreen) el.requestFullscreen().catch(() => {});\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'reset') return setScreen('confirm-reset');\\n    if (id === 'next') page = (page + 1) % 4;\\n    if (id === 'prev') page = (page + 3) % 4;\\n    applySettings();\\n    paint();\\n  }\\n\\n440→  function devAction(id) {\\n    if (!devFromPause && screen !== 'dev') return;\\n    if (id === 'reset-tune') resetTuning();\\n    if (id === 'god') god = !god;\\n    if (id === 'faster') timeScale = Math.min(4, timeScale * 2);\\n    if (id === 'slower') timeScale = Math.max(0.1, timeScale / 2);\\n    if (id === 'step' && event) event.fixed(FIXED_DT, [inputs[0].snapshot(0)]);\\n    if (id === 'fall' && event && event.beginFall) event.beginFall(0);\\n    if (id === 'results') { finishEvent(); return setScreen('results'); }\\n    if (id === 'ending') {\\n450→      profile.doneSteps = programme.slice();\\n      profile.levelled = true;\\n      profile.met = eventIds();\\n      sayExact(\\\"Oh. So that's what the middle looks like.\\\");\\n      return setScreen('ending');\\n    }\\n    if (id === 'marbles') profile.marbles += 10;\\n    if (id === 'unlock') profile.met = eventIds();\\n    if (id === 'age') profile.ages.push(41);\\n    if (id === 'bot') botSkill = botSkill ? null : 'sharp';\\n460→    if (id === 'copy') copyText = JSON.stringify(tuningSnapshot());\\n    if (id === 'wipe') return setScreen('confirm-reset');\\n    if (id === 'next') page += 1;\\n    if (id === 'prev') page = Math.max(0, page - 1);\\n    if (id.startsWith('jump-')) {\\n      devFromPause = true;\\n      return openIntro(id.slice(5));\\n    }\\n    paint();\\n  }\\n470→\\n  function groupAction(id) {\\n    if (id === 'quick' || id === 'raft' || eventById(id)) {\\n      const couch = eventIds().filter((eid) => eventById(eid).couch);\\n      const playlist = id === 'quick' ? pickSome(couch, 3) : [id === 'raft' ? 'raft' : id];\\n      group.playlist = playlist;\\n      group.cursor = 0;\\n      const lanes = group.seats.map((seat, i) => seat ? ({\\n        id: i, kind: 'local', name: seat.name, colour: SEAT_COLOURS[i],\\n      }) : null).filter(Boolean);\",\"content_concise\":\"200→    profile.minutes += (event.t || 0) / 60;\\n    profile.floor += result.falls || 0;\\n    if (eventId !== 'checkin') {\\n      const form = result.form || 0;\\n      const best = profile.best[eventId] || {};\\n      best[tier] = Math.max(best[tier] || 0, form);\\n      profile.best[eventId] = best;\\n      if (!profile.met.includes(eventId)) profile.met.push(eventId);\\n      if (programme.includes(eventId) && !profile.doneSteps.includes(eventId)) profile.doneSteps.push(eventId);\\n      const first = !profile.cleared[eventId];\\n210→      jarPay = marblePayout({\\n        seconds: event.t || 0, form, firstClear: first,\\n        perMin: getTune('marblesPerMin'), medalScale: getTune('medalScale'),\\n      });\\n      profile.cleared[eventId] = true;\\n      profile.medals.push({ id: eventId, tier, form, medal: result.medal });\\n      if (!profile.