1,115,58,32,116,104,105,115,46,115,99,111,114,101,115,46,115,108,105,99,101,40,41,44,32,109,101,97,110,58,32,116,104,105,115,46,109,101,97,110,83,99,111,114,101,40,41,44,32,116,101,115,116,115,58,32,116,104,105,115,46,116,101,115,116,115,46,115,108,105,99,101,40,41,32,125,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/checkin.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":4,\"content\":\"import { mean } from './score.js';\"},{\"line_number\":125,\"content\":\"  meanScore() {\"},{\"line_number\":126,\"content\":\"    return mean(this.scores);\"},{\"line_number\":129,\"content\":\"  result() {\"},{\"line_number\":130,\"content\":\"    return { scores: this.scores.slice(), mean: this.meanScore(), tests: this.tests.slice() };\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"2df4045a-be4a-4c05-a8d9-7df56fcbe990"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_144","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The spike uses readLean exported from balancer.\n\nBalance tests should use the shipped balanceStep or Standing events rather than reimplementing the torque formula. The spike's flailWhen threshold is 28 degrees, which aligns with the no-retuning requirement.\n\nThe spike's 28-degree flail threshold may fire too early against the measured 30-34 degree window. The port will assert known good values with tolerance: full stick peaks near 23° and settles near 18°, a 3.5 gust without flail causes a fall, early flails fall, timed flails around 30-34° save, extra mass at y=1.15 falls while lighter mass at y=1.3 raises peak, and recovery has one fall with no instant refall.\n\nA shared drive helper in test/drive.mjs will use real input and bot via pads, not a reimplementation of physics. Flow tests will use createGame. I need to verify the readLean export and pressFlail function. Three.js imports require checking for correct renderer API usage. The art modules will be src/render/ink.js, src/render/materials.js, and src/render/doll.js.\n\nThe art module list now includes src/render/cast.js for simplified characters, src/render/island.js for environment, src/render/stage.js for scene syncing, and src/render/renderer.js using WebGPU with a WebGL2 fallback. src/anim/clips.js will hold idle AnimationMixer clips, and src/main.js is the entry point. The renderer design uses THREE.WebGPURenderer with antialiasing.\n\nThe renderer will catch initialization failures and fall back to a WebGL2 renderer. I need to verify the correct Three.js r180 API for detecting the backend type and handling device loss events.\n\nCanvas sizing will use innerWidth multiplied by the minimum of devicePixelRatio and 2. The renderer needs preserveDrawingBuffer enabled so Playwright can read back pixels via screenshot or toDataURL without blank output. I am checking the Three.js WebGPURenderer constructor options for this setting.\n\nThe renderer will set `preserveDrawingBuffer: true` for the WebGL fallback. The title screen must paint the sky, sea, island, and doll onto the canvas while keeping the DOM title \"Level Best\". Session mode will use a 512 shadow map and a pixel ratio of 1. Ghost dolls will be read from the game session and exposed through state() so the renderer can draw them.\n\nstate() will expose the last eight session ghosts and the group winner from finishEvent's lastResult. The scoreGroup logic needs to call event.result before disposal so each raft lane can report its correct form.\n\nfinishEvent will now capture each lane's form before disposal by mapping event.result(i) into lastResult.forms. The dev page controls are trimmed to six items: three tools plus previous, next, and reset. The Who screen lists Begin first, followed by name, paint, and hat. Attract order and session card pad polling are also being fixed. In sessionFixed mode, Triangle and Cross inputs will be polled before the game starts when the current time is not finite.\n\nProgress updates are coalesced to 1000 ms and the game throttles to 1 s. Ghosts send every 0.1 s with a rate limit of 20 per second and a burst of 40, so 10 per second is fine. In sessionFixed mode, events do not start when fewer than six local players are present, but ghosts still report lean 0 at score zero. Input polling will be moved after snapshot when play begins. Progress fires immediately at t=0 because lastProgress starts at -1. The hub harness will signal ready within 20 seconds without a key press.\n\nThe card shown flag requires both ownsCard and readySent to be true. The game's own card replaces the splash screen once the hub client signals readiness. The HTML must keep the card element in the DOM so mountUi can paint it. main.js will check AIHub.active and connect as a ghost with seats [1, 4] before running the session; otherwise it falls back to standalone mode. The vendor API for AIHub.active and connect still needs verification.\n\nOptions are ignored while the Create button is held. Touch detection matches coarse media queries and ignores fine pointers; main.js sets coarse mode, and tests can override it with setCoarse(true). The attract screen uses wall-clock time via createGame without a manual starts loop, so a ten-second test takes ten real seconds; advance(10) advances simulation time and should start attract immediately. Tests will verify both behaviors. The dev screen cannot be reached from the title pause state.\n\nTuning slider changes will propagate to running events because events call getTune() each step. UI tests will run in Playwright against the built HTML with a ?test=1 flag that exposes __TEST__. The tools/test.mjs runner accepts an optional group argument defaulting to 'full'.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-818d2c47-c6ca-4a64-9559-2b6e803573ac-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/tools/hub/harness.html","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-818d2c47-c6ca-4a64-9559-2b6e803573ac-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"playMs|__hubCheck|data-complete|players|scenario","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/tools/hub","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-818d2c47-c6ca-4a64-9559-2b6e803573ac-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/physics/balancer.js","offset":1,"limit":140}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-818d2c47-c6ca-4a64-9559-2b6e803573ac-33","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/ui/ui.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-818d2c47-c6ca-4a64-9559-2b6e803573ac-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/vendor/session.js","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3936,"output_tokens":2566,"cache_read_input_tokens":83072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"aaad3a0f-ab77-4473-894f-06eb13de05f9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-818d2c47-c6ca-4a64-9559-2b6e803573ac-30","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\\\">\\n<style>\\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\\n10→  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\\n  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\\n  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\\n  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\\n  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\\n  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\\n  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\\n  input.game { width: 300px; }\\n  button { cursor: pointer; }\\n20→  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\\n  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\\n  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\\n  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\\n  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\\n  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\\n  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\\n  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\\n  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\\n  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\\n30→  aside section { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\\n  aside h2 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 6px; }\\n  #checks li { list-style: none; }\\n  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\\n  .ok::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }\\n  .bad::before { content: '✗ '; color: var(--bad); }\\n  .wait::before { content: '… '; color: var(--warn); }\\n  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\\n  #round { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }\\n  .hint { color: var(--dim); }\\n40→</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<header>\\n  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\\n  <label>Game <input class=\\\"game\\\" id=\\\"game\\\" placeholder=\\\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\\\"></label>\\n  <label>Players <select id=\\\"players\\\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\\n  <label>Latency <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"latency\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" value=\\\"60\\\"> ms</label>\\n  <label>Jitter <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"jitter\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" value=\\\"20\\\"> ms</label>\\n  <label>Loss <input type=\\\"number\\\" id=\\\"loss\\\" min=\\\"0\\\" max=\\\"50\\\" value=\\\"0\\\"> %</label>\\n50→  <button id=\\\"restart\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">New round</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"release\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" title=\\\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\\\">Start now</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"timeup\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">Time up</button>\\n  <label>Remove <select id=\\\"who\\\"></select></label>\\n  <button id=\\\"remove\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">Remove player</button>\\n  <button id=\\\"hide\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" aria-pressed=\\\"false\\\">Hide host tab</button>\\n</header>\\n<main>\\n  <div id=\\\"grid\\\"><p class=\\\"hint\\\" style=\\\"padding:16px\\\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\\n  <aside>\\n60→    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\\\"round\\\" class=\\\"hint\\\">No round yet.</div></section>\\n    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\\n    <pre id=\\\"log\\\" aria-live=\\\"off\\\"></pre>\\n  </aside>\\n</main>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\\n\\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\\n70→const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\\n\\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\\n80→  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\\n<meta name=\\\"description\\\" content=\\\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\\\">\\n<style>\\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\\n10→  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\\n  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\\n  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\\n  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\\n  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\\n  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\\n  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\\n  input.game { width: 300px; }\\n  button { cursor: pointer; }\\n20→  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\\n  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\\n  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\\n  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\\n  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\\n  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\\n  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\\n  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\\n  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\\n  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px soli