{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_147","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Grand Hold sequence has five phases: pose, stones, gust, step, and hold.\n\nThe full Grand Hold flow spans roughly 700 seconds of physics. At 10 milliseconds per second that is about 9 seconds of simulation time, which is acceptable for a full test. Daily check-ins add another ~200 seconds of overhead. The director flow begins with the plan screen, then the intro, then a three-second countdown.\n\nThe director flow continues through play, results, and jar screens before returning to the plan or bed. Bots are initialized with game.bot('sharp') before play begins. During the countdown phase, the event does not step forward, so bots remain idle until the play screen starts.\n\nThe attract mode now correctly sets the bot skill to sharp and switches the screen to play. The title flow begins with the Who screen, where Begin is the default choice; confirming creates a profile, then the tutorial and day one begin. A flow test will use manual game creation with memory storage, advancing time or pressing Enter to progress through the screens.\n\nThe menu input system uses keyDown, advance, and keyUp to properly latch presses. The Who screen now defaults to Begin after the fix. activate(index) is exposed for direct choice selection. Settings pages are capped at six items; the dev page will be trimmed. About pages are paged and split into long answers, with model choices sliced to six.\n\nAbout pages will be split into many short arrays of lines to prevent overflow. The page label currently hardcodes \"of 8\" and must be updated to use the dynamic page count instead. A UI test at 1920 by 1080 viewport will verify computed font sizes are at least 30 pixels, that no more than six elements are focusable, and that focus is visible. CSS minimum font size rules will be applied to all text.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4c5