{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_150","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found: `latched.clear()` clears pad markers and then re-adds them.\n\nMenu confirm only checks latched keys, so held Enter won't repeat. Attract mode swallows the press because latched clears during its poll; on the next frame the key is still held but menu confirm ignores it.\n\nPresses released during the attract frame are also swallowed. The renderer will use simple geometry with one doll, island, sky, sea, and props. Dolls rotate by leanX and leanZ during events. Up to four dolls can appear in multiple lanes. Ghost dolls render at ghost message coordinates with opacity and no physics. Session ghost payloads include timestamp, angle, position, lean, color, flags, and state.\n\nGhost dolls will be visually offset by player ID since x and z are zero in the sent data. A small bob animation clip will be added to the AnimationMixer for the doll's arm joints using QuaternionKeyframeTrack. Imports will come from three/webgpu and three/tsl exactly as planned. A potential issue with TSL uniform Color handling was noted.\n\n`post.render()` will run each frame. The camera sits at (0, 4, 12) aimed at the island and moves closer during play. The sea disc has radius 590 and sits near y = -0.05. The sky is an inverted sphere of radius 600 using BackSide and MeshBasicNodeMaterial with a TSL shader that blends low, mid, and top colors based on vertical view angle.\n\nThe sea shader uses a radial sine wave with time and position offsets to create bands, blending sea colors and fading into sky low near the horizon. Both shaders will be colorNodes on MeshBasicNodeMaterial.\n\nClouds will be flattened spheres using a toon material and drift with time in JavaScript. The island will use a sand disc of radius 22 and a grass disc of radius 15 at y=0, with trees, a lighthouse, and huts kept to a modest count so four WebGPU iframes do not run out of memory. The doll will follow the recipe but stay low-poly; CapsuleGeometry is available in three r180 and RoundedBox for Trudy. Doll parts will be parented to a \"hips\" group that rotates as a whole by lean. During events, the scene will show a simple stage floor and the doll, with event-specific props as simple meshes updated from state.\n\nA screenshot of a leaning doll on a stage with event-colored props will suffice if the canvas shows varied colors. The launch test paints the title screen with sky blue, teal sea, sand and green island, dark ink pixels, and \"Level Best\" text before switching screens. `main.js` exposes `window.__RENDER__` every frame containing backend, lost, frames, width, and height. Test mode sets `window.__TEST__` to the game API via `?test=1`. The `?render=0` flag skips the renderer entirely, which is needed for Node tests but UI tests still require the DOM.\n\nUI font tests will run in Chromium without WebGPU to save memory, while launch tests keep WebGPU enabled. The hub scene will use a light setup with pixel ratio 1 and smaller shadows to avoid OOM across four iframes; shadow resolution may drop to 256 in session mode, with further simplification as a fallback.\n\nThe harness waits 20 seconds for `ready()`, so it must fire before every shader finishes compiling. In the main entry point, `createGame` runs first, then `createStage` with `session: true` starts the renderer immediately after initialization. The stage syncs game state on each frame. This keeps WebGPU startup under the timeout even if SwiftShader shaders are slow.\n\nThe main entry point awaits `AIHub.connect()` before calling `game.runSession(info)`, which triggers `ready()`. This is acceptable because the client waits for the hub welcome message first, and the harness only requires `ready()` within 20 seconds of load. Standalone mode skips the hub and calls `game.runStandalone()` directly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2ccf2613-f26b-4356-a906-6630f3d4dea5-48","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function connect|hub.connect|ready: function|function ready","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/vendor/session.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3118,"output_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":105728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"369fa377-6e0c-49e8-afcd-e88c6d765668"}
