{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_155","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ghost mode requires every copy to be sent, except for the single copy where it is optional.\n\nGhost messages are sent every 0.1 seconds during the play window, starting after the countdown ends. Progress reports are sent every second, yielding roughly five updates per six-second game. The time-up event triggers sendResult.\n\nThe score of 0 is finite and valid. The end event locks the game and stops audio and input. Math.random is not replaced; the client seeds it. No alerts or prompts are used, and uncaught exceptions must be avoided. WebGPU initialization may hang, so a timeout or WebGL fallback is being considered.\n\nWebGPU initialization should finish within the 20-second ready deadline. The scene is small with a 256 shadow map and no heavy post-processing. Ghosts are self-reported, so the host flag stays false and copies still send results after time-up.\n\nThe single-player case still requires progress and result messages. The outside-session launch test will be included in the hub test or launch script. The HTML meta tag order is being checked against the plan.\n\nThe session client script must appear immediately after the charset meta tag. The hub:webgpu required attribute must not be set. The page title is Level Best, and the font is embedded inline as base64 woff2. The build process reads exit-interview.json into src/data/about.js, then bundles main.js with esbuild, base64-encodes the fredoka woff2 files, and assembles the HTML. Because director imports about.js, the build must write that file before running esbuild so that node tests can import it.\n\nThe about.js and exit-interview.json files will be written now with the final content. Issue counts may be updated after testing and require a rebuild. The known bugs are:\n\n- logReps lastRep undefined phantom first rep\n- plank double ragdoll\n- island loop cadence / gravity NaN\n- plates bot band\n- room tray half-extents and loss rule\n- raft skill/grip\n- check-in lean sign\n- check-in double margin\n\nFive issues are critical: room tray and spills, island score, plates score, check-in lean age, and plank panic. The remaining three are minor. I will write notes/issues.md before generating the JSON. Any new bugs found during testing will be added to that file and the JSON updated before the final rebuild.\n\nThe about.js export will use a named constant. The UI test will walk every screen via __TEST__.goto and verify font, focusables, and margins. Screens include title, who, tutorial, menu, settings, about, journal, free, group, pause, dev, and touch. Navigation from title to dev fails but works from pause; touch mode is set from title.\n\nTests will default coarse to false. For audio verification, the test harness needs access to renderProbe from the bundled IIFE. Since the module is not directly importable, the plan is to expose it on __TEST__ so the test page can call it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dd4e2152-70fb-4d36-b4b2-788ba489ecfe-54","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function detuneCents|function restTiltRad","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/physics/island.js","-A":8}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2065,"output_tokens":1571,"cache_read_input_tokens":113408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"28750a48-07c7-4b85-814e-dabffcc223ee"}
