{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_180","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"three.tsl.js imports TSL from three/webgpu.\n\nChecking whether three.tsl.js re-exports Color from the TSL namespace or defines its own, since Color bindings may differ.\n\nT.Color and W.Color are different bindings. three.tsl.js likely re-exports a TSL color node as Color. The import still resolves to the same module via Node's cache.\n\nTSL and PostProcessing share the same module instance. esbuild will deduplicate three/webgpu imports. I will write all files now, focusing on visual quality and animation clips. I will patch director fixed() cleanly.\n\nDrafting about.js exit interview content now. Issue counts will be 8 and 5. Notes/issues.md will capture findings. The testing feedback lists eight bugs: a phantom first log rep, double ragdoll on the plank, Island Loop cadence scoring 26, plate bots leaving the band, a Room Service tray that was the wrong size, a raft ignoring skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\n\nFive of the eight issues were critical. The plank could panic physics. Room Service could not deliver. Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure. The check-in lean sign published the wrong Wobble Age.\n\nThe most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading the event's own result.\n\nThe least helpful test counted renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\n\nA fixed step and ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and look on both backends.\n\nRapier cuboids use half-extents. A tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as intended. Removing two colliders in one step panics WASM. TSL hash() takes a single float.\n\nThe ankle torque step, fourteen events, synthesised voices, and the ink scene are all included.\n\nA Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page. The software WebGPU device stays lost without extra swiftshader flags.\n\nNone of Three.js, Rapier, or the hub client were changed.\n\nThe prompt must signal actual drawing, not just frame requests. TASK.md needs the correct WebGPU flags and a note that cuboids use half-extents. The director will keep one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events. Metadata fields are set: usage \"added on import\", players \"1–4\", source Wii Fit, genre Sports, and six lowercase tags. Now writing director patches and files.\n\nRemoving measure() from the engine to avoid looking unfinished. world.js init will accept wasm bytes directly. Director patches include sessionFixed rewrite, Who screen first, aboutPages, devModel, state winner, finishEvent forms, pageLabel, an attract bug fix, and card polling for pad. When session time is not finite, the code polls for confirm or ask. A visual state field will hold lean and ghosts so the renderer does not depend on private session data.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cbcafece-f5fc-4bdf-ad34-97e2f9fea088-86","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"botInput","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/checkin.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":709,"output_tokens":1363,"cache_read_input_tokens":137984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"23a2c5c7-50b9-4798-8f28-0cd83f89dfcf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cbcafece-f5fc-4bdf-ad34-97e2f9fea088-86","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,76,101,118,101,108,32,66,101,115,116,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,47,115,114,99,47,103,97,109,101,47,99,104,101,99,107,105,110,46,106,115,10,49,51,51,58,32,32,98,111,116,73,110,112,117,116,40,105,44,32,115,107,105,108,108,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/checkin.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":133,\"content\":\"  botInput(i, skill) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"66da2969-9799-4e26-8fc5-07b04d5d261a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_181","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CheckIn has botInput. When checkin finishes, fixed() sees the event.\n\nThe bot branch returns before checking event.done. This prevents normal play with bot() from finishing the event and showing results. The fix adds an !attract guard to the bot branch.\n\nThe bot branch now checks event.done after stepEvent. It calls finishEvent and revealsAge for checkin, or sets the results screen otherwise. Human, attract, and session paths already handle this correctly.\n\nA safety timeout will be added to the flow test. Events that never end will fail clearly. Flow advances in chunks until a screen change, capped at roughly 120 seconds.\n\nA playClass helper will automate bot testing. It sets the bot, confirms the intro and countdown, then advances until results with a 180-second cap. The check-in helper handles both the age screen and the results screen.\n\nThe day flow steps are:\n- title activate → who\n- who activate 0 begin → tutorial\n- tutorial activate → morning\n- advance until speech question\n- activate yes → reply\n- activate → checkinPlay\n- bot sharp → advance until age\n- activate → plan\n\nThe full day flow runs through each class in sequence: activate the choice, intro, begin, countdown, play until results, continue, jar, continue. Then bed sleep and repeat until ending.\n\nThe grand hold jar triggers the ending when afterJar sees both levelled and grandHold. noteNotch sets levelled at step 14. The remaining 13 steps are added in finishEvent as each class ends. On day five the order is raft, tug, then grandHold. During play, grandHold may notch while doneSteps already holds the previous 13 plus grandHold, so finishEvent skips adding it again.\n\nThe test assumes classes are played in order. If grandHold is completed before the others, levelled stays false and the day continues normally rather than ending. The tilt state is zeroed when all fourteen steps finish.\n\nThe test will verify marbles rise after the first class. Save and resume will be tested by writing a save, starting a new game with the same storage, and confirming the day continues. Attract mode starts from the title screen and returns to title on keypress. A wall-clock test will advance ten frames without manual input to reach attract. The dev screen is reachable from title.\n\nThe test suite now includes a class pause, dev screen slider change, and reset. Touch input tests set coarse mode and verify the touch screen shows controller or keyboard requirements. Unit tests will grep source files. The full test runner builds HTML before running all groups. UI glyph text uses textContent to avoid unsafe SVG innerHTML issues. The renderer sync is being implemented in createStage.\n\nThe stage object now exposes render, resize, info, sync, and dispose. The main loop runs fixed steps first, then calls the stage renderer, then paints. The renderer syncs doll states from the event and reports backend status. setRender updates the backend for the next state call.\n\nThe launch test will verify __RENDER__ after a few seconds, confirming frames are positive, lost is null, and the backend is webgpu. setRender runs every frame so the next state() call stays current.\n\nCanvas drawing buffer size will be set via renderer.setSize to match the requested viewport. The test expects the canvas drawing size to match the requested view.\n\nThe canvas drawing buffer will be set to window.innerWidth and innerHeight multiplied by the pixel ratio. The launch viewport will use 1280x720 or 960x540 for faster software webgpu rendering. The test waits for at least two frames with a twenty-second timeout. The title screen text must read \"Level Best\".\n\nA stubbed gamepad will let the launch test trigger screen changes. The script will expose a pad array on window and override navigator.getGamepads so the game polls it. Writing to that array will feed input directly into the bot and external pad sources.\n\nA real page launch will use Enter to leave the title screen. The plan also requires pressing Enter, Space, Enter, Space outside a session and capturing hub.log.\n\nError listeners will be added to the test harness. The director patches will be written first, followed by parallel file batches. The no-op measure function and dialogueApi will be removed after verifying they are unused. pageLabel and about.js will be updated so the ABOUT import resolves before any test runs.\n\nThe `aboutPages` function is being drafted to build the About screen content. It assembles a page array from the resort title and tagline, source information, testing feedback, engine feedback, prompt feedback, and AI hub details.\n\nThe About screen will list the AI hub name, tagline, description, type, genre, source, player count, controls, and tags. Credits will cite Fredoka, Three.js R180, and Rapier 0.19.3. Each sentence will be placed on its own page to prevent vertical overflow.\n\nAbout page feedback will be kept to three short lines or fewer. A `chunks` helper will split long text into roughly seventy-character segments so each line fits within the viewport.\n\nThe `chunks` helper splits long text into roughly seventy-character segments. Each chunk becomes one page of up to four lines. If a source field exceeds that, it spans multiple pages with the same label. The test will concatenate all page texts to verify the target string appears somewhere in the About screen.\n\nThe About screen will carry a data-about attribute so tests can target it directly. The renderer will be reasonably complete. Island tilt will be drawn by rotating the island group around the X axis using state().tilt in radians, making the first day look crooked and later days look flat. The state() function will also expose a palette field.\n\nThe palette will advance through dawn, noon, golden, and dusk as the day progresses. A `paletteNow()` helper will return 'dusk' during class steps and grandHold events.\n\nThe palette will advance through dawn, noon, golden, and dusk based on the number of completed steps. A dev palette override can be set for testing. Ink strength from settings will be passed to the renderer uniforms. The world.js initialization also needs updating.\n\nBanned words and phrases will be avoided in the new source. A bug was found where goto('play') overwrites the countdown screen with play, skipping the countdown phase entirely.\n\nThe countdown path via activate is the intended flow. The public goto function is a test hook that skips the countdown screen. During countdown the event exists but does not step, and play steps begin at time zero once the screen switches. Bots will be set before the class starts so they drive the game when play begins. Setting bots during countdown is harmless because the bot branch is only reached on the play screen.\n\nA `press` helper will activate a pad index, and an `until` helper will step the game forward in fixed 1/120-second increments until a predicate passes or a timeout occurs. The author notes that calling `advance(1/120)` repeatedly triggers one frame per step, which is wasteful; advancing by larger chunks would be more efficient.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-79adf950-6c30-4f9b-a992-6dab8576dae9-87","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gravity","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/islandLoop.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-79adf950-6c30-4f9b-a992-6dab8576dae9-88","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"cuboid\\(0\\.3","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/roomService.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1582,"output_tokens":3594,"cache_read_input_tokens":138624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"6dbadcbb-6c5a-4010-8da1-85edaf5ade95"}
