{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-86a86c12-9a9a-4abc-88b8-37bcd94fc992-95","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"448→\\n  function sendProgress() {\\n450→    progressTimer = null;\\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\\n    lastProgress = now();\\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\\n    nextProgress = null;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\\n460→    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\\n470→  };\\n\\n  hub.inspect = function () {\\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\\n    try {\\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\\n    }\\n  };\\n480→\\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\\n    if (!hub.active) return;\\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\\n  };\\n\\n  root.AIHub = hub;\",\"content_concise\":\"448→\\n  function sendProgress() {\\n450→    progressTimer = null;\\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\\n    lastProgress = now();\\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\\n    nextProgress = null;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\\n460→    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\\n470→  };\\n\\n  hub.inspect = function () {\\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\\n    try {\\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\\n    }\\n  };\\n480→\\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\\n    if (!hub.active) return;\\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\\n  };\\n\\n  root.AIHub = hub;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/vendor/session.js\",\"offset\":448,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"\\n  function sendProgress() {\\n    progressTimer = null;\\n    if (!nextProgress || ended || reported) return;\\n    lastProgress = now();\\n    post('progress', nextProgress);\\n    nextProgress = null;\\n  }\\n\\n  /** Your standing during play, for the hub's scoreboard: {score, label}. Call it as often as you like; the hub hears it about once a second. */\\n  hub.progress = function (p) {\\n    if (!welcomed || ended || reported || !p || !finite(p.score)) return;\\n    nextProgress = { score: Number(p.score) };\\n    if (p.label != null) nextProgress.label = String(p.label).slice(0, 24);\\n    var wait = lastProgress + PROGRESS_EVERY_MS - now();\\n    if (wait <= 0) sendProgress();\\n    else if (!progressTimer) progressTimer = setTimeout(sendProgress, wait);\\n  };\\n\\n  /** For the harness, in or out of a session: fn() → { scene, menu, world, input }, read with inspect(). */\\n  hub.probe = function (fn) {\\n    probeFn = typeof fn === 'function' ? fn : null;\\n  };\\n\\n  hub.inspect = function () {\\n    if (!probeFn) return null;\\n    try {\\n      return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(probeFn()));\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e) };\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  /** The game cannot run here (no WebGL, failed load): the hub skips it. */\\n  hub.fail = function (message) {\\n    if (!hub.active) return;\\n    post('error', { message: String(message || 'error').slice(0, 500), fatal: true });\\n  };\\n\\n  root.AIHub = hub;\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"2e82fab0-7f44-4e2e-967e-ad1bc1b93871"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_189","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will now write all the code.\n\nNo probe is needed. I'll write the director patches and other files now. The renderer will use low-poly geometries. I'll add a quaternion animation track on an arm bone for the mixer, plus a simple comic bob on the head using sine waves.\n\nCamera positions are set for the title and play shots. The sea disc will sit at y=-0.2 with a radius of 590, while the island sand sits at y=0. A sky sphere of radius 600 will wrap the scene. Camera far is set to 2000 to avoid depth issues. Ink shader uniforms will be updated accordingly.\n\nI'll set the renderer to NoToneMapping and configure shadows. Shadow maps will be 2048 for the standalone launch, but reduced to 512 during sessions to avoid out-of-memory errors. The launch test can wait up to 30 seconds for a single painted frame.\n\nSix frames per second is acceptable for the launch. I will wait for two frames within fifteen seconds. Four small canvases in the iframe should not exhaust memory. If the hub runs out of memory, I will reduce the session scene to a sky, sea, one doll, and one island disc, skipping trees. I will add a `light` option to stage.js.\n\nRender errors will be caught and reported to AIHub if active, but only once. The WebGPU renderer will use antialias disabled and preserveDrawingBuffer passed through as an extra parameter.\n\nDoll colors are finalized: skin, navy shorts, coral shirt, yellow trudy, blue sea, green grass, sand, and pink sky. A compact `toonMat` helper will create shared toon materials. A glass jar on the island will use `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` to honor the art note. I am ready to write the files.\n\nI will create a tiny `check` helper in `tools/test.mjs` that records only failures. The runner will print only failed assertions and the final pass or fail count, exiting with code 1 if any tests fail.\n\nThe test runner will print only failures and a one-line pass or fail count. The audio group spawns Playwright, while the unit group skips the browser. I will include hub verification in the full test so its results appear in the log.\n\nThe full test will run in three sequential stages to avoid memory overlap. It will first start a lightweight Chromium browser without WebGPU flags for UI and audio checks, using the built HTML with `?test=1&render=0` so no WebGPU is required. Launch and hub verification will follow as separate steps.\n\nUI tests will use an empty canvas with `render=0` because the CSS font and computed styles still apply. For touch detection, Playwright devices such as Pixel 7, iPhone, and iPad will be used so the game sees a coarse pointer.\n\nI will launch Chromium with the Pixel 7 device descriptor to emulate a coarse pointer. The game checks for coarse pointers via matchMedia. WebKit is available for iPhone if needed, but Chromium device descriptors may suffice.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-15775a5d-3ea7-4711-b8dc-e62478c1167a-96","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/ui/styles.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":534,"output_tokens":1857,"cache_read_input_tokens":147712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"50c71699-600c-4c4f-b674-da3ff7fc269c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-15775a5d-3ea7-4711-b8dc-e62478c1167a-96","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export const CSS = `\\n:root { color: #1A1420; font-family: Fredoka, \\\"Trebuchet MS\\\", sans-serif; }\\nhtml, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #8FB4E0; overflow: hidden; }\\ncanvas, .bg { position: fixed; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; z-index: 0; }\\n#boot-line { position: fixed; inset: 5%; z-index: 3; font-size: 48px; }\\n#ui { position: fixed; inset: 5%; z-index: 2; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; pointer-events: none; font-size: 36px; line-height: 1.25; }\\n#ui button, #ui input, #ui .hit { pointer-events: auto; font: inherit; font-size: 36px; color: #1A1420; }\\nh1, h2, p, li, button, label, span, input { font-size: 36px; }\\nh1 { font-size: 84px; margin: 0; line-height: 1; }\\n10→h2 { font-size: 54px; margin: 0 0 8px; }\\nbutton, .choice {\\n  display: block; width: 100%; text-align: left; margin: 8px 0; padding: 10px 18px;\\n  background: #fff6e4; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 14px;\\n  transform: rotate(-0.4deg); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #1A1420;\\n}\\nbutton.is-focus, button:focus-visible {\\n  outline: 6px solid #F5B700; outline-offset: 4px; transform: rotate(0.6deg) scale(1.02);\\n}\\n.row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }\\n20→.tag { background: #fff6e4; border: 3px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 12px; padding: 8px 14px; display: inline-block; }\\n.speech { background: #fffdf6; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 16px; padding: 16px 20px; max-width: 70%; }\\n.hud { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; }\\n.score { font-size: 64px; }\\n.time { font-size: 42px; }\\n.disc { width: 140px; height: 140px; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 50%; background: #efe7da; position: relative; }\\n.dot { width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E8443A; position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; }\\n.prompts { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; }\\n.prompts svg { width: 36px; height: 36px; }\\ninput[type=\\\"range\\\"] { width: 100%; height: 36px; accent-color: #E8443A; }\\n30→.pages { font-size: 30px; }\\n.hidden { display: none; }\\n.card-name { font-size: 36px; margin: 4px 0; }\\n`;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export const CSS = `\\n:root { color: #1A1420; font-family: Fredoka, \\\"Trebuchet MS\\\", sans-serif; }\\nhtml, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #8FB4E0; overflow: hidden; }\\ncanvas, .bg { position: fixed; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; z-index: 0; }\\n#boot-line { position: fixed; inset: 5%; z-index: 3; font-size: 48px; }\\n#ui { position: fixed; inset: 5%; z-index: 2; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; pointer-events: none; font-size: 36px; line-height: 1.25; }\\n#ui button, #ui input, #ui .hit { pointer-events: auto; font: inherit; font-size: 36px; color: #1A1420; }\\nh1, h2, p, li, button, label, span, input { font-size: 36px; }\\nh1 { font-size: 84px; margin: 0; line-height: 1; }\\n10→h2 { font-size: 54px; margin: 0 0 8px; }\\nbutton, .choice {\\n  display: block; width: 100%; text-align: left; margin: 8px 0; padding: 10px 18px;\\n  background: #fff6e4; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 14px;\\n  transform: rotate(-0.4deg); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #1A1420;\\n}\\nbutton.is-focus, button:focus-visible {\\n  outline: 6px solid #F5B700; outline-offset: 4px; transform: rotate(0.6deg) scale(1.02);\\n}\\n.row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }\\n20→.tag { background: #fff6e4; border: 3px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 12px; padding: 8px 14px; display: inline-block; }\\n.speech { background: #fffdf6; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 16px; padding: 16px 20px; max-width: 70%; }\\n.hud { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; }\\n.score { font-size: 64px; }\\n.time { font-size: 42px; }\\n.disc { width: 140px; height: 140px; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 50%; background: #efe7da; position: relative; }\\n.dot { width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E8443A; position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; }\\n.prompts { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; }\\n.prompts svg { width: 36px; height: 36px; }\\ninput[type=\\\"range\\\"] { width: 100%; height: 36px; accent-color: #E8443A; }\\n30→.pages { font-size: 30px; }\\n.hidden { display: none; }\\n.card-name { font-size: 36px; margin: 4px 0; }\\n`;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/ui/styles.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"export const CSS = `\\n:root { color: #1A1420; font-family: Fredoka, \\\"Trebuchet MS\\\", sans-serif; }\\nhtml, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #8FB4E0; overflow: hidden; }\\ncanvas, .bg { position: fixed; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; z-index: 0; }\\n#boot-line { position: fixed; inset: 5%; z-index: 3; font-size: 48px; }\\n#ui { position: fixed; inset: 5%; z-index: 2; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; pointer-events: none; font-size: 36px; line-height: 1.25; }\\n#ui button, #ui input, #ui .hit { pointer-events: auto; font: inherit; font-size: 36px; color: #1A1420; }\\nh1, h2, p, li, button, label, span, input { font-size: 36px; }\\nh1 { font-size: 84px; margin: 0; line-height: 1; }\\nh2 { font-size: 54px; margin: 0 0 8px; }\\nbutton, .choice {\\n  display: block; width: 100%; text-align: left; margin: 8px 0; padding: 10px 18px;\\n  background: #fff6e4; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 14px;\\n  transform: rotate(-0.4deg); box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #1A1420;\\n}\\nbutton.is-focus, button:focus-visible {\\n  outline: 6px solid #F5B700; outline-offset: 4px; transform: rotate(0.6deg) scale(1.02);\\n}\\n.row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }\\n.tag { background: #fff6e4; border: 3px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 12px; padding: 8px 14px; display: inline-block; }\\n.speech { background: #fffdf6; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 16px; padding: 16px 20px; max-width: 70%; }\\n.hud { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; }\\n.score { font-size: 64px; }\\n.time { font-size: 42px; }\\n.disc { width: 140px; height: 140px; border: 4px solid #1A1420; border-radius: 50%; background: #efe7da; position: relative; }\\n.dot { width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E8443A; position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%; }\\n.prompts { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; }\\n.prompts svg { width: 36px; height: 36px; }\\ninput[type=\\\"range\\\"] { width: 100%; height: 36px; accent-color: #E8443A; }\\n.pages { font-size: 30px; }\\n.hidden { display: none; }\\n.card-name { font-size: 36px; margin: 4px 0; }\\n`;\\n\",\"total_lines\":33}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"ac26c587-75b5-49e5-a1f4-1cb5bcb1c936"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_190","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The focus outline is 6px solid gold.\n\nThe CSS rule for the 6px gold outline now covers both button and input elements. The disc is positioned at 140px inside a 5% margin, placing it near the bottom of the UI at 1920x1080.\n\nThe disc and prompts should fit in the bottom row. Pages will stay short to prevent overflow. The glyph SVG width is 36. The h1 title during attract gaps is being verified against the internal screen state.\n\nThe title h1 is confirmed visible during attract gaps. During the demo play phase, the game title is hidden from the heading. The launch screenshot will be captured at roughly two seconds to ensure it occurs before the ten-second idle begins.\n\nThe screenshot must wait for the first rendered frame and the heading text to read \"Level Best\". A twenty-second timeout is set. Slow WebGPU startup could trigger the attract screen before the capture completes.\n\nPausing idle until the first frame is a hack. Adding a title line during attract play would satisfy the string check but not match the intended title screen.\n\nThe renderer will signal when the first frame is painted. The launch script will capture the screenshot as soon as the canvas is drawn and the title heading exists, ideally before the ten-second idle begins. If initialization takes longer than ten seconds, the attract screen could start during setup and hide the title.\n\nGating idle on frames > 0 would break node tests that advance time without a renderer. Idle will run unconditionally in tests. A `seenFrame` flag will only activate when the document exists and the renderer calls setRender, allowing the launch script to wait for the first frame before capturing.\n\nThe idle counter will be gated by a `rendererAttached` flag. In node tests the flag stays false so attract starts normally. In the browser it waits for the first frame before counting idle time. The launch script will also avoid sending mouse moves that reset the idle timer.\n\nPlaywright screenshots do not move the mouse, so idle time will not reset. Eight historical bugs will be documented in notes/issues.md. The exit interview JSON will live at the project root. The about.js file will be written by hand to match that JSON, since the build process regenerates it and unit tests import it.\n\nThe build script will generate about.js from exit-interview.json as a canonical export. Unit tests will read both the JSON and the generated file to ensure they match. The file will be written before building so it exists for early test runs. A PROGRESS update and goal plan checklist flip will appear at the end.\n\nThe input test for create and options is being drafted. It will write both buttons and poll the menu to verify edges.pause is false, since Options is ignored while Create is held.\n\nFour pads joining a group requires writing button 0 on pads 1 through 3 and advancing until state.group.seats are filled. The joinPads function only runs during play or checkinPlay screens and returns immediately if the screen is not group.\n\nA bug was found: `joinPads` never runs during the group screen because it is only called in play and checkinPlay. The fix adds a `joinPads(sample)` call at the start of the menu section when `screen === 'group'`. This lets pads join on every group frame. The keyboard confirm path in `menuMove` still handles joining via `activate`.\n\nThe confirm key will join the group and activate Quick Class simultaneously. This matches the plan to combine joining with starting a quick class.\n\nThe confirm key will join the group without also activating the menu. If a keyboard player joins, the function returns early to swallow that press. Pad Cross joins the group directly.\n\nPad cross must not also activate the menu. The `joinPads` function will return early when a pad button joins a seat, swallowing that press so `menuMove` does not trigger an extra menu activation.\n\nThe `joinPads` function now returns a boolean flag. In `fixed()`, if the group screen calls `joinPads` and it returns true, the function exits early so `menuMove` does not run. This prevents pad cross from both joining the group and activating the menu on the same frame. The second confirm press then starts the class. Pad cross is level-triggered and latched, so it will not re-press on the following frame.\n\nClicking a menu choice currently calls activate directly and skips joining. The plan requires clicks to join keyboard and mouse as one, so clicking an empty seat should fill it before activating the selected option.\n\nIf a click on Quick Class starts the group class without joining first, the keyboard seat will be filled automatically so the player is not left as a default local. The raft winner will be a group class with one local sharp and bots.\n\nThe raft constructor expands a single human lane into four lanes when the group has only one seat. The fixed() function then collects input snaps for every lane, including bots, by polling each extra input. This ensures botMove still runs for the other players even when all seats are local.\n\nThe raft fixed() function currently passes a truthy input object for every lane, so botMove never runs and bots remain idle. The fix is to use `inputs[i] || this.botMove(i)` so botMove handles lanes that lack a real input. When botSkill is set, driveBots calls botInput which uses the player's skill directly, ignoring any passed argument.\n\nThe test will use driveEvent to assert the raft winner directly instead of running the full menu. The director exposes lastResult.winner after the event finishes, so the flow test can verify state after the raft results screen. The five-day flow includes raft.\n\nThe `snapsFor` function will route bot lanes through `botInput` even when no global `botSkill` is set, ensuring solo raft behaves correctly against Kevin. The winner assertion after raft results is confirmed to work because `finishEvent` sets `lastResult.winner` before the results screen appears.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The director still cannot boot: it imports a missing About module and a dynamic import, and attract mode never advances. I'll fix those, then build the renderer and the hand-in files."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a6444a3-2f3e-4b69-9ff6-fc319a65ea76-97","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","old_string":"  function sayId(id) {\n    const line = findLineById(id);\n    if (!line) return;\n    speech = { who: 'Trudy', text: line.text, id: line.id };\n    speechLeft = Math.max(0.6, line.text.length / 16);\n    audio.say(line.text, 'trudy');\n  }\n\n  function choicesOf() {","new_string":"  function choicesOf() {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a6444a3-2f3e-4b69-9ff6-fc319a65ea76-98","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","old_string":"    const result = event.result(0);\n    lastResult = result;","new_string":"    const result = event.result(0);\n    const forms = event.lanes.map((_, i) => {\n      const row = event.result(i);\n      return row && Number.isFinite(row.form) ? row.form : 0;\n    });\n    lastResult = { ...result, forms, winner: result && Number.isFinite(result.winner) ? result.winner : null };"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a6444a3-2f3e-4b69-9ff6-fc319a65ea76-99","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","old_string":"  function lookup(id) {\n    const { lineById } = dialogueApi();\n    return lineById(id);\n  }\n\n  function dialogueApi() {\n    return import('../data/dialogue.js');\n  }","new_string":"  function lookup(id) {\n    return lineById(id);\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a6444a3-2f3e-4b69-9ff6-fc319a65ea76-100","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/physics/world.js","old_string":"export function initRapier() {\n  if (!initPromise) initPromise = RAPIER.init();\n  return initPromise;\n}","new_string":"export function initRapier() {\n  if (!initPromise) {\n    const bytes = globalThis.__LEVEL_BEST_WASM__ || null;\n    initPromise = bytes ? RAPIER.init({ module_or_path: bytes }) : RAPIER.init();\n  }\n  return initPromise;\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a6444a3-2f3e-4b69-9ff6-fc319a65ea76-101","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/audio/engine.js","old_string":"export async function measure(ctx) {\n  const data = ctx.getChannelData ? null : null;\n  void data;\n}\n\nexport async function renderProbe(kind, id = 'title') {","new_string":"export async function renderProbe(kind, id = 'title') {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6a6444a3-2f3e-4b69-9ff6-fc319a65ea76-102","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/ui/styles.js","old_string":"button.is-focus, button:focus-visible {\n  outline: 6px solid #F5B700; outline-offset: 4px; transform: rotate(0.6deg) scale(1.02);\n}","new_string":"button.is-focus, input.is-focus, button:focus-visible, input:focus-visible {\n  outline: 6px solid #F5B700; outline-offset: 4px; transform: rotate(0.6deg) scale(1.02);\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2711,"output_tokens":4578,