holder \\\"ready for the upload, it uses default texture data for as a placeholder.\\\\n\\\\t *\\\\n\\\\t * @param {Texture} te\\\"\\n--- placeholder \\\"ult texture for the given texture that can be used\\\\n\\\\t * as a placeholder until the actual texture is \\\"\\n(node:23834) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317\\\" && node --input-type=module -e \\\"\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'fs';\\nconst t = readFileSync('node_modules/three/build/three.webgpu.js','utf8');\\nfunction show(w) {\\n  let from = 0, c = 0;\\n  while (c < 3) {\\n    const i = t.indexOf(w, from);\\n    if (i < 0) break;\\n    console.log('---', w, JSON.stringify(t.slice(i-60, i+40)));\\n    from = i + w.length; c++;\\n  }\\n}\\nshow('TODO');\\nshow('placeholder');\\n\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"See whether TODO strings are comments or code\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-769b3e4a-f869-46b7-a193-e734fe475d84-136.log\",\"total_bytes\":895}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"2e704569-e429-4e7a-b228-d3da81c42fe9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_207","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ESBuild's `legalComments: 'none'` setting should strip comments during bundling.\n\nConfirmed the prebuilt file contains comments that will be stripped during bundling. Proceeding with the build.\n\nRapier and three.tsl.js are clean of banned words. I will write the renderer and supporting files next, avoiding placeholder references. After writing, I will check src for banned words and grep the built HTML output. I am also considering how esbuild handles Three.js `import.meta.url` in the prebuilt file.\n\nRapier's `import.meta.url` is only used when `init()` loads WASM from a URL. Since the browser passes bytes directly, that code path is skipped. Still, esbuild may try to resolve the WASM file or fail when it encounters the import.\n\nAn esbuild plugin is being drafted to intercept rapier.mjs and replace its `import.meta.url` reference with a direct WASM import, preventing the bundler from failing on that expression.\n\nThe plugin will swap the `new URL(..., import.meta.url)` expression for `globalThis.__LEVEL_BEST_WASM__`. Even though the browser passes bytes and the URL is never evaluated, esbuild still parses that expression and may attempt to bundle the WASM asset.\n\nThe esbuild plugin will prevent the bundler from emitting a separate WASM file. The global variable fallback ensures RAPIER.init() still receives the bytes even if called without arguments. Node tests will import the original package directly, since the replacement only affects the bundled build.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The shell can import once About exists. Next I’ll add the ink scene, the boot file, and the tests that drive the shipped step."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-14428724-9f32-4531-b977-2096ad230f93-137","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json","content":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 23:13:17\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\",\n    \"tech\": \"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\",\n    \"animation\": \"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\",\n    \"research\": \"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\",\n    \"environment\": \"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\",\n    \"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\",\n    \"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\",\n    \"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\",\n    \"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\",\n    \"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\",\n    \"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\",\n    \"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\",\n    \"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\",\n    \"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\",\n    \"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Level Best\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\",\n    \"description\": \"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"comedy\", \"third-person\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"co-op\"]\n  }\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-14428724-9f32-4531-b977-2096ad230f93-138","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/about.js","content":"/** Filled from exit-interview.json by the build. Keep the two copies the same. */\nexport const ABOUT = {\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 23:13:17\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\",\n    \"tech\": \"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\",\n    \"animation\": \"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\",\n    \"research\": \"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\",\n    \"environment\": \"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\",\n    \"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\",\n    \"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\",\n    \"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\",\n    \"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\",\n    \"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\",\n    \"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\",\n    \"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\",\n    \"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\",\n    \"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\",\n    \"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Level Best\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\",\n    \"description\": \"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"comedy\", \"third-person\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"co-op\"]\n  }\n};\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-14428724-9f32-4531-b977-2096ad230f93-139","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/render/ink.js","content":"import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\nimport {\n  mrt, output, normalView, toonOutlinePass, color, float, vec2, vec4, uv, screenSize, Fn, abs, max,\n  smoothstep, mix, uniform, perspectiveDepthToViewZ, time, length, hash, floor, oneMinus,\n} from 'three/tsl';\n\nexport function makeInk(renderer, scene, camera) {\n  const INK = 0x1a1420;\n  const u = {\n    hull: uniform(0.0028), width: uniform(1.4), boil: uniform(0.5), fadeNear: uniform(30), fadeFar: uniform(90),\n    grain: uniform(0.02), near: uniform(camera.near), far: uniform(camera.far), ink: uniform(new THREE.Color(INK)),\n  };\n  const scenePass = toonOutlinePass(scene, camera, color(INK), u.hull, float(1));\n  scenePass.setMRT(mrt({ output, normal: normalView }));\n  const colorTex = scenePass.getTextureNode('output');\n  const normalTex = scenePass.getTextureNode('normal');\n  const depthTex = scenePass.getTextureNode('depth');\n  const post = new THREE.PostProcessing(renderer);\n  post.outputNode = Fn(() => {\n    const cell = floor(uv().mul(vec2(40, 23)));\n    const wob = hash(floor(time.mul(8)).add(cell.x).add(cell.y.mul(17))).sub(0.5).mul(u.boil);\n    const px = u.width.add(wob).div(screenSize);\n    const viewZ = (o) => perspectiveDepthToViewZ(depthTex.sample(uv().add(o)).r, u.near, u.far);\n    const n = (o) => normalTex.sample(uv().add(o)).xyz;\n    const dx = vec2(px.x, 0);\n    const dy = vec2(0, px.y);\n    const z0 = viewZ(vec2(0, 0)).abs();\n    const dz = max(abs(viewZ(dx).sub(viewZ(dx.negate()))), abs(viewZ(dy).sub(viewZ(dy.negate())))).div(z0.max(0.5));\n    const dn = max(length(n(dx).sub(n(dx.negate()))), length(n(dy).sub(n(dy.negate()))));\n    const e = max(smoothstep(0.05, 0.12, dz), smoothstep(0.7, 1.1, dn)).mul(oneMinus(smoothstep(u.fadeNear, u.fadeFar, z0)));\n    const c = mix(colorTex.rgb, u.ink, e);\n    const p = floor(uv().mul(screenSize));\n    const g = hash(p.x.add(p.y.mul(1571))).sub(0.5).mul(u.grain);\n    return vec4(c.add(g).mul(oneMinus(length(uv().sub(0.5)).mul(0.62).pow(2.2))), 1);\n  })();\n  return { post, u };\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-14428724-9f32-4531-b977-2096ad230f93-140","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/anim/clips.js","content":"import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\n\n/** A short idle on a named arm joint. The mixer owns the clip. */\nexport function armIdle(mixer, name = 'arm') {\n  const times = [0, 0.5, 1];\n  const axis = new THREE.Vector3(1, 0, 0);\n  const q = new THREE.Quaternion();\n  const values = [];\n  for (const angle of [0.35, -0.2, 0.35]) {\n    q.setFromAxisAngle(axis, angle);\n    values.push(q.x, q.y, q.z, q.w);\n  }\n  const track = new THREE.QuaternionKeyframeTrack(`${name}.quaternion`, times, values);\n  const clip = new THREE.AnimationClip('idle', 1, [track]);\n  const action = mixer.clipAction(clip);\n  action.setLoop(THREE.LoopRepeat, Infinity);\n  action.play();\n  return action;\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":612,"output_tokens":4198,"cache_read_input_tokens":180224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"a0271f89-2399-4dc0-9436-1ff6ef34f1fe"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-14428724-9f32-4531-b977-2096ad230f93-137","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n    \\\"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\\\",\\n    \\\"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\\\",\\n    \\\"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\\\",\\n    \\\"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Level Best\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"co-op\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 player