{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_210","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"rendererAttached might now be unused and trigger a lint warning.\n\nrendererAttached will remain since unused variables don't cause errors in JavaScript. Next steps are writing build.mjs and tests, then running a quick import of createGame to catch syntax errors before the full test suite.\n\nRoundedBoxGeometry path mapping is confirmed. The devModel choice count is verified at six items, matching the slice limit. A single comprehensive test runner will be written next, along with notes/issues.md and a final source check for banned words.\n\nThe flow test needs careful handling of speech auto-advance. The morning state advances when speechLeft reaches zero or on confirmation, so advancing three times should clear it.\n\nBot placement is also being verified. Setting bot('sharp') at the start of the day is safe because menus never trigger bot output; driveBots only runs during play, check-in, and attract.\n\nBot input is ignored during play when botSkill is active, which is the desired behavior for the flow test. Each test runs in a separate game instance, so attract tests do not inherit a leftover botSkill from earlier tests. Countdown screens remain unaffected because they are not in play mode.\n\nThe play-day flow is being mapped out. After the countdown, pads clear and bots repopulate them on the next frame. The sequence runs through class selection, a three-second countdown, play until results, then continue or jar choices before bed. A `playDay` helper will loop through this cycle. One issue was spotted: `sleepDay` increments the day index but never sets the screen back to bed.\n\nThe bed screen bug is confirmed: `sleepDay` never changes the screen, so pressing sleep again would increment the day index repeatedly. The fix is to route to the next morning or menu after sleep, matching the planned \"screen inks out, stamp lands\" transition.\n\n`sleepDay` will call `beginDay` to return the player to the morning screen. The credits path is safe because `setScreen('menu')` runs immediately after `sleepDay`, overriding any morning transition.\n\nThe credits path is confirmed safe. `sleepDay` increments the day index once, then `setScreen('menu')` replaces the morning screen. The next Continue will check `profile.classDone.length` to decide whether to begin a new day or return to the menu.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-19b1feab-3c2e-4f73-ac16-f4845832c6e5-148","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","old_string":"  function sleepDay() {\n    const plan = today();\n    profile.stamps.push({ day: profile.dayIndex + 1, name: plan.name });\n    profile.dayIndex += 1;\n    profile.classDone = [];\n    palette = 'dawn';\n    persist();\n  }","new_string":"  function sleepDay() {\n    const plan = today();\n    profile.stamps.push({ day: profile.dayIndex + 1, name: plan.name });\n    profile.dayIndex += 1;\n    profile.classDone = [];\n    paletteHold = null;\n    persist();\n    beginDay();\n  }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3212,"output_tokens":1454,"cache_read_input_tokens":192768,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"15bd2a36-c515-445f-8d28-ada15d860515"}
