ivate: (index) => activate(index),\"},{\"line_number\":240,\"content\":\"    if (sample.edges.confirm) activate(focus);\"},{\"line_number\":267,\"content\":\"  function activate(index) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"52021a7e-1de9-446d-a96d-43254c21041c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_229","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`activate` is used internally but not returned from `createGame`.\n\n`activate` must be added to the `createGame` return because `main.js` references it. The fruit hat logic is sound: falls increment correctly, and the never-bank case properly banks zero after at least one fall.\n\n`writeSave` adds a version field, but `readSave` expects it. This mismatch breaks resume and flow-test reloads. `sleepDay` triggers `beginDay`, which sets the morning screen. The menu Continue button may then call `beginDay` again if no classes are done.\n\nThe Continue button routes to `beginDay` when no classes are done, which correctly advances the maintenance day after credits. The Grand Hold notch is handled by pushing `grandHold` into `doneSteps` during play and again in `finishEvent`, zeroing tilt and triggering the ending when `afterJar` detects a levelled state with that event ID.\n\nThe plan screen lists every class, including stamped ones. Focus resets to zero after each class, so the first class is always replayed. Confirming that entry replays the already-completed first class instead of the next pending one.\n\nThe test must manually move focus down to the next unstamped class before confirming, since the plan screen always highlights the first entry. Restricting the plan to pending classes would fix this, but the design intentionally shows all classes.\n\nThe plan screen will auto-focus the first pending class instead of the first entry. A `focusNextClass` helper will locate the next unstamped class when entering the plan screen.\n\n`setScreen` will accept a `keepFocus` flag. When entering the plan screen, it will locate the first unstamped class and set focus there, overriding the usual reset to zero.\n\nFree Play lists all 14 events after the story. The test will verify this by checking `profile.met` and paging through the free play screen, since `state().choices` only shows the current page.\n\nThe maintenance day after credits has three random classes. The test will proceed through morning, question, and check-in, then verify the plan screen lists those three classes.\n\nFor the attract mode, `createGame` without manual input runs a loop that waits eleven seconds. Node `requestAnimationFrame` uses `setTimeout`, so `loop.js` needs inspection. The hold attract path is simpler: it waits for idle time, then calls `advance(10)` to start.\n\nThe wall-clock attract mode waits eleven seconds of real time. This is acceptable but adds time.\n\nFor the dev-tuning test, poses will be played and `maxLean` set to ten. The tuning module must reflect this live value, and resetting it should restore eighteen. Because the game does not expose event internals, the test will verify the change by reading the tuning state directly.\n\nThe dev-tuning test will also verify that the event continues running after a step, not crashing.\n\nFor the group class, four pads join and each controls its own lane. The first confirm joins a pad, and the second confirm starts the event because `joinPads` returns true when it claims a seat.\n\nThe second confirm in the group screen skips the key-device join block because a key device already occupies a seat. It then activates the menu choice at focus zero, which is Quick Class rather than raft. To start raft instead, the test must move focus down to index one or activate that choice directly. The test will write button zero on pads zero through three, advance one tick so they claim seats, and then confirm to begin the event.\n\nWhen all four pads are pressed, `joinPads` sees no empty seats and returns false, so the keyboard confirm falls through to menu activation. The pad cross edge sets `confirm` before the menu-mode latch logic resets it, ensuring the pad press registers as a single confirmation.\n\nThe held pad cross registers as a single confirmation on the first frame, then latches to prevent auto-start. The test will tap Enter to activate Quick Class at focus zero; for the raft variant, it must move focus down first.\n\nTippy Raft will be played until completion. The winner will be finite. All lanes are driven by the same bot skill, ignoring lane kind.\n\nThe input-verbs test will verify that pad, keyboard, and mouse all produce the same positive leanX on a fresh balance event. A new game with no bot will be advanced with the right stick, then the same test repeated with keys and mouse. Prompts are not included in state.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aaf002ca-26e6-4695-be43-14ea88b7ddd4-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/input/glyphs.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aaf002ca-26e6-4695-be43-14ea88b7ddd4-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/ui/ui.js","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aaf002ca-26e6-4695-be43-14ea88b7ddd4-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/core/loop.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aaf002ca-26e6-4695-be43-14ea88b7ddd4-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","offset":1260,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4946,"output_tokens":2517,"cache_read_input_tokens":99200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"16d736b0-81d2-451c-96d1-22aa1ec17482"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aaf002ca-26e6-4695-be43-14ea88b7ddd4-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Prompt glyphs. Every element the UI draws carries data-glyph. */\\n\\nconst VERBS = {\\n  weight: { pad: 'stick', key: 'wasd', mouse: 'move' },\\n  leftFoot: { pad: 'l2', key: 'q', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n  rightFoot: { pad: 'r2', key: 'e', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\\n  hop: { pad: 'cross', key: 'space', mouse: 'mouse-both' },\\n  flail: { pad: 'square', key: 'f', mouse: 'mouse-middle' },\\n  breathe: { pad: 'r1', key: 'shift', mouse: 'shift' },\\n10→  ask: { pad: 'triangle', key: 't', mouse: 't' },\\n  use: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n  back: { pad: 'circle', key: 'esc', mouse: 'mouse-right' },\\n  pause: { pad: 'options', key: 'esc', mouse: 'esc' },\\n  look: { pad: 'rstick', key: 'mouse', mouse: 'drag' },\\n  confirm: { pad: 'cross', key: 'enter', mouse: 'mouse-left' },\\n};\\n\\nconst XBOX = {\\n  cross: 'a',\\n20→  circle: 'b',\\n  square: 'x',\\n  triangle: 'y',\\n  l1: 'lb',\\n  r1: 'rb',\\n  l2: 'lt',\\n  r2: 'rt',\\n  options: 'menu',\\n  create: 'view',\\n  stick: 'ls',\\n30→  rstick: 'rs',\\n};\\n\\nexport function glyphFor(verb, device, set = 'playstation') {\\n  const row = VERBS[verb] || VERBS.use;\\n  if (device === 'mouse') return row.mouse;\\n  if (device === 'key') return row.key;\\n  const id = row.pad;\\n  if (set === 'xbox' && XBOX[id]) return XBOX[id];\\n  return id;\\n40→}\\n\\nexport function promptFor(verbs, device, set = 'playstation') {\\n  return verbs.map((verb) => ({\\n    verb,\\n    glyph: glyphFor(verb, device, set),\\n    device,\\n    set: device === 'pad' ? set : device,\\n  }));\\n}\\n50→\\n/** Inline SVG. Tests read data-glyph, not the picture. */\\nexport function glyphSvg(glyph) {\\n  const ink = '#1A1420';\\n  const common = `data-glyph=\\\"${glyph}\\\" width=\\\"36\\\" height=\\\"36\\\" viewBox=\\\