116,32,111,102,32,116,104,105,115,46,104,97,116,115,91,105,93,41,32,116,104,105,115,46,119,111,114,108,100,46,114,101,109,111,118,101,67,111,108,108,105,100,101,114,40,102,114,117,105,116,46,99,111,108,44,32,116,114,117,101,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":7,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/physics/ragdoll.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":94,\"content\":\"    try { world.removeRigidBody(body); } catch { /* already gone */ }\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/grandHold.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":93,\"content\":\"        this.world.removeRigidBody(body);\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/fruitHat.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":161,\"content\":\"      this.world.removeRigidBody(fruit.body);\"},{\"line_number\":167,\"content\":\"      this.world.removeRigidBody(fruit.body);\"},{\"line_number\":178,\"content\":\"      this.world.removeRigidBody(fruit.body);\"},{\"line_number\":198,\"content\":\"    this.world.removeCollider(top.col, true);\"},{\"line_number\":202,\"content\":\"    for (const fruit of this.hats[i]) this.world.removeCollider(fruit.col, true);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"3935af2f-8e68-45ec-b73c-b7a4023a1f6b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_231","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The previous smoke test passed. Sharp banks at 7 caused clearHat to remove 7 colliders at once.\n\nThe panic likely involves removeRigidBody on two colliders in contact, not clearHat. I'll smoke createGame and a short event first while writing tests, then patch the director minimally.\n\nAdding a `pendingStart` object to pass seed, tier, and lanes into `gotoPlay`. The director will focus the next unfinished class in the plan and prompt on state. Tier resolution will use `extra.tier` when provided. The intro-to-play transition is verified: the god check runs while the screen is still 'intro', then switches to play.\n\n`beginCountdown` now consumes `pendingStart`, merging it into the `startEvent` call. The `goto` handler stores arguments in `pendingStart` before opening the intro and starting the countdown. `setScreen` resets focus unless `keepFocus` is true.\n\nThe `setScreen` patch now focuses the first unfinished class when entering the plan screen. State output now includes prompt glyphs. I'm writing tests next, starting with a `fresh()` helper that resets RNG and tuning before creating a manual game with in-memory storage. The group class raft winner test may span three rounds.\n\nHelper functions `tap`, `press`, and `playUntil` are being added to the test suite. `playUntil` advances the game in half-second chunks until a predicate matches or a cap is reached. The bot should be set at the start of classes, not during menus.\n\nBot('sharp') is set at the start of the flow. Menus remain unaffected because the bot only drives during play.\n\nThe check-in sequence runs as follows: checkinPlay with bot driving, revealAge, tap to plan, tap to intro, begin countdown, play with bot, tap continue, and jar auto or tap. Repeat.\n\nMorning speechLeft is roughly two seconds. Tapping confirm opens the question immediately.\n\nDay zero questions are yes/no. DayIndex modulo four determines left or right.\n\nDay 3 is \"A Little Damp\". The test taps yes or left based on choices.\n\nAfter the day 5 grand hold, the flow runs ending, tap, credits, tap, menu. Day index should be 5 and tilt should be zero.\n\nAges must be between 18 and 99. The same bot skill means age should fall as handicap drops. The test asserts that each day's age is at least as high as the next, or the final age is lower than the first.\n\nMarbles must rise from day one to day five. The save-resume test will snapshot storage after the first day, then create a new game with that same storage object. The restored game should show day two and one stamp.\n\nFree play will be reached from the menu after the story. The test will use both keyboard and mouse paths: tapping ArrowDown twice then Enter to select free play, or using activate(2). Free play pages collect event IDs.\n\nFree play page choices use left and right arrows instead of activate. After the game is levelled, the test will open free play and walk through pages to collect event IDs until all 14 classes are seen or no pages remain. The attract and dev tests will be separate games.\n\nTouch mode will be tested separately. It can be enabled at creation or set after startup, and it shows a title screen with a message and settings choice but no gameplay options.\n\nThe pause menu test verifies six choices appear when Escape is pressed during an event.\n\nPressing Escape during play pauses the game and opens the pause menu. The main menu shows six choices once the tutorial is complete or after one sleep; returning from the title screen to the menu is also valid for counting. The wall-clock attract timer will be tested in isolation to avoid timer conflicts. An input test will verify three devices leaning.\n\nThe input test will use a short custom event instead of the bot. It pushes pad input by writing a rightward stick command to the pad device, then advances two seconds and reads the lean value. Keyboard input will be tested by pressing KeyD; the lastDevice becomes key and the weight ramps up over two seconds, so leanX should be positive.\n\nMouse input will be tested by moving the pointer past a four-pixel threshold to set lastDevice to mouse, then advancing. Flail will be verified by checking that pressing the flail edge sets snapshot.flail and leaves flailLeft or flailCool positive. Feet input will be checked via snapshot after polling, since holding Q or E during a step class would be too complex.\n\nThe input test will verify that pad, keyboard, and mouse produce the same game effect, not just the same snapshot state. Lean direction will be compared across devices to confirm consistent weight. Flail will be tested by pressing once on a standing event and checking that flailCool is positive for all three inputs. For hop, the test will read a public result field after one step from each device instead of relying on fragile edge detection.\n\nThe springboard test is time-boxed. The input test will assert that all three devices produce a positive leanX after a rightward lean command. Flail will be verified by reading a side effect on the event result rather than checking internal state fields.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-28b2ee5b-46bb-49ca-96af-091b5cb89cbb-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"flail","glob":"**/src/events/poses.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-28b2ee5b-46bb-49ca-96af-091b5cb89cbb-52","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/dialogue.js","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-28b2ee5b-46bb-49ca-96af-091b5cb89cbb-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/tuning.js","limit":45}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-28b2ee5b-46bb-49ca-96af-091b5cb89cbb-54","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function (takeLine|lineById|counts)","glob":"**/src/data/dialogue.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4083,"output_tokens":2752,"cache_read_input_tokens":111104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"db8f7958-b94f-47ff-97da-d65a243f8e5d"}
