32,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,76,101,118,101,108,32,66,101,115,116,45,87,105,105,32,70,105,116,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,47,115,114,99,47,100,97,116,97,47,100,105,97,108,111,103,117,101,46,106,115,10,50,53,55,53,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,108,105,110,101,66,121,73,100,40,105,100,41,32,123,10,50,53,57,51,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,116,97,107,101,76,105,110,101,40,115,112,101,97,107,101,114,44,32,98,117,99,107,101,116,44,32,114,111,108,108,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/dialogue.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2575,\"content\":\"export function lineById(id) {\"},{\"line_number\":2593,\"content\":\"export function takeLine(speaker, bucket, roll) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"bb3fb489-e2df-44fd-9ccc-f6eccc2d5bfa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_232","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a plan. I will check the hub harness completion and how to run it. Then I will build.\n\nWriting the test harness now. Each test group will live in its own file and be imported dynamically by tools/test.mjs. Starting with the balance core test.\n\nThe balance core test imports balancer and tuning utilities. It initializes Rapier, resets tuning, and builds a tune object from stored parameters. A world helper function is being defined.\n\nThe world helper creates a physics world with ground and a doll body, then returns the world, body, and fresh balance state. The run function steps through time by calling an optional callback, updating timers, applying balance control, stepping the physics engine, checking for falls, and reading lean angles.\n\nThe run function now computes peak tilt, final tilt, fall count, and a finite check before freeing the world. A full-stick test asserts zero falls, a peak tilt between 20 and 28 degrees, and a settled tilt near 18 degrees.\n\nA `gustFlail` test helper is being written. It applies a 3.5 horizontal force from 0.3 to 0.8 seconds and triggers a flail when the doll's lean crosses a specified threshold after 0.8 seconds. The run stops immediately if the doll falls.\n\nFlail timing is now pinned down. Triggering at 20 or 26 degrees causes a fall. Triggering at 30–34 degrees saves the balance. Triggering at 36 degrees or later falls. An early flail at t=0.1 also fails.\n\nExtra mass will be added via world.createCollider to test how it affects the peak tilt.\n\nRecovery testing will use the Standing class to force a fall, then verify that recovery resets the fall counter and prevents a second fall. The test applies a 3.5 N·m gust until the doll collapses, waits for the 2.2 s recovery window, and confirms the body settles near zero lean without another fall.\n\nThe recovery test will step the Standing class until the doll falls, then continue until the 2.2 s recovery window passes, and assert exactly one fall with a small finite lean.\n\nParked poses will be tested by running a sharp bot with `parked: true` and advancing until results, expecting a form score below 85.\n\nFruit tests will compare two bots: one with infinite bank and one with bank at 7, checking that the latter achieves a form of at least 65 with zero falls.\n\nPlate tests will run sharp and clumsy bots side by side, requiring their gaps to differ by at least 0.15, with keys enabled.\n\nCairn T2 tests will compare synced and unsynced breathing. The bot option `breath: false` disables breathing, and the test asserts that stones are higher with synced breathing.\n\nClumsy form must be below 70 and sharp form must be at least 85.\n\nRoom braced glasses must equal five; unbraced glasses must be fewer than five. The option `brace: false` is used for the unbraced run.\n\nRaft round times must each be under ninety seconds, and the winning time must be finite.\n\nA dispose test will verify that every event tier sharp leaves no lingering world. The director path handles scoring, while a direct event path checks that the world is null after dispose and that a second event does not panic. A `runEvent` helper is being drafted to reset RNG and tuning before each run.\n\nThe `runEvent` helper is being implemented. It creates a manual game with in-memory storage, spawns the bot, and advances the simulation in half-second steps until the screen reaches results or age. It guards against infinite loops and throws if any lane lean becomes non-finite. After finishing, it returns the final state.\n\nThe direct dispose test will instantiate an event, run it briefly, call `dispose()`, assert the world is null, and then create a second event to confirm no panic. A forced fall ragdoll and recover test will be added to the events group; it will use `beginFall` on a `Poses` or `Standing` instance, step until recovery, and assert exactly one fall with finite lean.\n\nI will run the forced fall test as a standalone pre-run before each event to avoid altering scores. I am checking whether `beginFall` sets the ragdoll state and recovery timer correctly, since some events like raft override the normal fall logic.\n\n`beginFall` spawns the ragdoll but does not set `state.fallen` or `recoverLeft`. Without those flags, `stepCores` skips recovery because it only checks `fallen` before calling `beginFall`. The forced fall test must manually set `state.fallen` and `recoverLeft` so the ragdoll actually recovers.\n\nThe forced fall test will set `fallen`, `falls`, and `recoverLeft` before calling `beginFall`. `stepCores` then recovers once the timer expires.\n\nA NaN check on lane lean angles will run during sharp bot runs.\n\nEach event has a time cap to prevent hangs: 180 for poses, 220 for grand, 280 for raft, 120 for island, 90 for fruit, plates, still, tug, room, log, step, cairn, spring, and plank. The loop stops early if results arrive first.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7d5777e9-1398-485c-bc1b-5ddb790d0964-55","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"iframe|gameUrl|src =","glob":"**/tools/hub/harness.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7d5777e9-1398-485c-bc1b-5ddb790d0964-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/ui/styles.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7d5777e9-1398-485c-bc1b-5ddb790d0964-57","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hub:session|meta name","glob":"**/src/main.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5429,"output_tokens":2920,"cache_read_input_tokens":115072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"3656946d-c17d-4c61-87f9-994ae3e14587"}
