{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_246","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"If ink throws an error, the code falls back to renderer.render and sets a lost flag.\n\nA permanent `lost` flag would trap the renderer in a broken state if ink throws repeatedly. I'll leave this as-is and handle it at launch time.\n\nI need to fix the ink graph rather than swallow its errors. The hash() call uses a single float, which is correct. I'll patch the director and write tests next. The dialogue flow looks sound: beginCountdown switches screens without clearing focus, then revealAge restores it properly. Tapping speechLeft on morning will open the question.\n\nThe Who screen's Begin option is index 0, so tapping Enter activates it correctly. Name changes are unnecessary. The flow sets the bot skill at startup, but the attract test runs in a separate game instance, so it won't interfere.\n\nIdle detection resets during countdown and play, so attract mode won't interrupt the flow. The jar auto-advances because the player taps it manually. Bot control ends on the results screen once the event finishes. Check-in flow is confirmed correct: the bot drives checkinPlay, then the event completes and reveals age.\n\nMarbles rise correctly because revealAge adds one and jarPay adds more later in afterResult. The class focus logic works: finishEvent marks classes done, so focus advances to the next unfinished one starting at index zero. During bed, the free pick option is skipped because sleep is selected instead. Tapping Listen on the ending screen shows credits; tapping Same time tomorrow triggers sleepDay before incrementing the day. I noticed a potential issue where sleepDay calls today() before incrementing the day.\n\nThe sleepDay sequence is confirmed correct. It stamps the current day, increments the index, and calls beginDay for the next morning. The menu screen overwrites the new morning state, so no double beginDay occurs between days. Day one starts with the tutorial and no prior stamp.\n\nAfter bed, the Arrival stamp is added and day index becomes 1. The credits screen shows five stamps total: four from days 1–4 plus one from the credits sleep. Five check-ins are recorded.\n\nIf the player continues maintenance from the menu, sleepDay clears classDone and overwrites the first beginDay with a second morning. The player sees that second morning instead. Only one maintenance morning occurs, and the plan contains three classes.\n\nI'll verify the maintenance day plan contains three classes and that the first one can be started. I may play all three if the bench is fast, but the test only needs to run once.\n\nI'll navigate from the maintenance plan back to the menu using Escape, then enter free play. I need to verify that Escape correctly triggers menu back() and returns to the menu screen.\n\nA save-and-resume test will run a short prefix of the flow: complete day one, sleep, then start a new game from the same storage. The resumed game will read the saved day index and stamp, but it always starts at the title screen because createGame resets to title.\n\nThe resume test will assert day 2, one stamp, and the Arrival name. Both the full playthrough and the short save-and-resume game are required. The attract-mode test will advance 72 seconds to observe four events.\n\nThe attract-mode test needs roughly 64 seconds of simulation to see four vignettes, which translates to about 0.6 seconds wall-clock time at ten-millisecond physics steps. The Fruit Hat Without God entry is 18 seconds long, not the full 60. A separate wall-clock test will wait 11 seconds without manual input. I also need to verify whether the dev and pause shortcuts can be triggered from the title screen.\n\nThe dev shortcut works from the title screen. Tuning during an event updates maxLean to 10 and the event reads that value via getTune. I will add state().prompts to the test assertions. Input coverage will include keyboard, pad, and mouse navigation.\n\nNode tests lack a DOM, so pointer hover cannot move focus. Clicking a button still activates it by latching the mouse button. A UI test can hover a button to verify focus moves, then click to confirm activation.\n\nNode input tests will cover pad and keyboard menu navigation, plus mouse click confirmation. All three devices will be verified to lean the same way. Hovering a button will be tested in the UI browser test instead.\n\nFor Xbox glyphs, the plan is to set the glyph style to xbox, then check that menu prompts display the correct glyphs. The lastDevice state updates when a stick is polled slightly or when settings are checked. A single menu frame advance after writeWish will set lastDevice to pad and update the prompts in the same frame.\n\nThe test suite will be split into eight focused files: director patches, lib helpers, unit tests, balance checks, event tests, flow tests, input tests, and a final combined runner. The director patch will be kept small with only three edits.\n\nThe test suite will also include a browser UI test, a runner script, and a launch script. I will run a quick smoke balance and one event before the full playthrough. The events file will group all tiers together. Shared game creation loads WASM once via initRapier. I will reset the RNG between events so fruit patterns stay consistent. Each event receives a seed built from its ID and day index.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8fda1b13-ff2c-472d-97cd-852822644ec1-77","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"opts\\.seed|this\\.label|rng\\(","glob":"**/src/events/*.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1459,"output_tokens":2616,"cache_read_input_tokens":144896,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"54d545d1-104a-4a74-8d0d-ccfbbeae6b1e"}
