{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_247","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Director always sets labels to `${id}-${dayIndex}`, so the seed does not change the stream.\n\nresetRng(seed) before each run changes the baseSeed, so the same label produces a different stream. No seed needs to be passed to individual events. Do not reset RNG mid-event. createGame calls rng during talk() when beginDay.\n\nIsolated event goto play avoids talk() calls, so fruit spawn streams remain independent. Flow and group use separate labels and must not reset RNG mid-event. I will add finishEvent safety, plan focus, and prompts, plus a pendingStart tier override.\n\nopenIntro now reads tier from pendingStart when available. beginCountdown pulls seed, tier, lanes, god, tests, and skill from pendingStart before launching the event. The goto handler for play stores arguments in pendingStart, opens the intro, and immediately begins countdown.\n\nsetScreen will trigger plan focus once focus reaches zero. State prompts will map to verb and glyph objects. finishEvent sets profile.levelled to true once doneSteps reaches the programme length. The grand hold phase advance logic is correct. The plates sharp versus clumsy event may fail and needs fixing, but balance defaults will not be retuned.\n\nI will check if a clumsy score below 70 is plausible for logReps. If the test fails, I will adjust the event scoring or bot rather than the ankle defaults.\n\nI am ready to code. I will patch the director and write large test files. I will update the todos.\n\nThe test runner will show only failures and a final summary line. It will exit with code 1 if any tests fail. Async tests will be awaited individually.\n\nGroup selection will run via `node tools/test.mjs unit flow`. The full suite runs with no arguments.\n\nThe full test suite will run after the build, since unit tests check for missing HTML files. During iteration, balance tests will run first to fail fast. Browser tests are included in full but are slow and memory-intensive; they will be executed sequentially with one browser per scenario and contexts closed between runs to prevent out-of-memory errors.\n\nThe browser harness will use a 960x540 viewport to save memory. If that causes out-of-memory errors, the four-player hub scenario will be retried alone.\n\nHub tests will not run during the first iteration until the node suite passes.\n\nUnit tests will scan built HTML for leftover TODO, FIXME, placeholder, or stub strings after the build.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-caeec6f2-4a15-4d61-a9f2-09db1d3ba27c-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json","offset":39}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3507,"output_tokens":1145,"cache_read_input_tokens":146304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"1a2a253e-3ed9-4427-8810-23a7a0147f0b"}
