{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_287","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Direct Cairn stepping with bot input mapped to wishX and wishZ correctly stacks stones.\n\nThe director's driveBots path through pad and snapshot corrupts the cairn bot's wish. This explains why all stones are lost in the playBot flow. The direct step path works correctly.\n\nThe director path likely fails because the input snapshot lacks wishX, or because the bot is not driving during a countdown, god mode is active, or yaw and lastDevice interfere. The inverted wish may also cause the doll to lean into the sway.\n\nI will inspect the goto('play') event construction and the snapshot Cairn receives during playBot. I plan to sample the event state mid-run using fresh() and goto, since playBot does not expose internal state easily. I also verified that driveBots calls botInput before poll and snapshot, and Cairn.botInput reads the lean correctly.\n\nThe snapshot transformation is not the issue. At zero yaw, worldWish preserves wishX and negates wishZ, matching the debug setup. The mismatch likely comes from writeWish mapping cmd.x and cmd.y to pad axes differently than poll reads them.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8e45f9b6-d12c-459f-8a12-b2d68d505e9c-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function goto|function bot\\(|pendingStart|startEvent|openIntro|beginCountdown|setDevice","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3882,"output_tokens":928,"cache_read_input_tokens":82048,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"571e4938-97b0-4f8d-b051-542515ff2018"}
