5 76% spinning · 9 crashes\\nplates average keys=true share=0.860 form=72.0 86% spinning · 5 crashes\\nplates clumsy keys=true share=0.766 form=53.3 77% spinning · 7 crashes\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer && node recheck.mjs\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Re-run plate and cairn balance checks\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-b0d75b92-2c57-47ed-b745-5684a767ea85-49.log\",\"total_bytes\":865}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"95f83232-fa7f-4d9d-bf05-02a6be67ee03"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_297","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sharp 1 works perfectly.\n\nKeys results are broken. Sharp keys share is 0.757 instead of ~1.0. Clumsy keys is 0.766, matching the stick share. Sharp omega is nearly constant at ~4.25 then jumps to 7.25 and 10.25. The keys path fails to reproduce the target steady omega.\n\nThe keys path fails because the 0.5-second detection window captures almost no taps at steady omega ~4.25. Taps arrive roughly every 0.74 seconds, so the window often sees zero presses and triggers decay instead of rate calculation.\n\nA single missed-tap decay sets the sensed rate to 6.28, which is the M band rather than the L band. The keys path is a special case that bypasses the normal weight-vector measurement and instead uses a 0.5-second press window.\n\nThe 0.5-second window assumes evenly spaced taps, so a single tap yields a rate of 2 Hz and an angular velocity of 6.28 rad/s. That sits in the dead zone between L and M bands, which is why sharp keys registers as dead-zone speed rather than L band. For the S band, about 1.6 taps fall inside the same window.\n\nThe M band also fails. One tap yields 6.28 rad/s, just below the M low threshold of 6.5, while two taps yield 12.57 rad/s, far above the S band. The 0.5-second window is too short and quantized for these bands.\n\nThe fix should measure the time between individual presses rather than counting taps in a fixed bucket. Each new press would instantly yield ω = π / dt_between_presses, smoothed with τ = 0.12 s.\n\nThe keys path is a separate scheme from the stick measurement. The L band is mathematically unreachable with the current 0.5-second window because one tap already yields 6.28 rad/s, which exceeds the L band ceiling of 5 rad/s.\n\nThe plan explicitly listed \"Plate Spinners unreachable on keys\" as a critical bug that the half-turn design was supposed to fix. The current 0.5-second window reintroduces it. The fix will measure the exact interval between individual presses instead of counting taps in a fixed bucket.\n\nThe fix should update the sensed angular velocity only when a new press occurs, using the interval between presses. Between presses the speed must hold steady rather than decay immediately. Decay should only begin once taps stop.\n\nThe fix uses a 0.12-second smoothing window on the interval between presses, with a 0.8-second idle timeout before decay begins. A steady L-band tap every 0.739 seconds now holds the speed constant between presses and converges to the correct angular velocity.\n\nThe 0.8-second decay threshold is too short. At the slowest L-band speed of 3.5 rad/s, the tap interval is 0.90 seconds, so decay would begin before the next press arrives. A longer hold time is needed.\n\nThe idle timeout is set to 1.05 seconds. This safely covers the slowest L-band gap of 0.90 seconds while still allowing decay when tapping stops.\n\nThe first press has no previous interval, so the speed starts at zero and converges after roughly one gap.\n\nSticky key interference from alternating A and D presses cancels out because the wish vector integrates over each single-frame tap.\n\nThe key path keeps magnitude below 0.5, so the stick measurement is bypassed. The phase accumulator alternates strictly between A and D, keeping the wish vector small and stable. KeyDown returns early if a key is already held, but keyUp happens after polling, so each tap registers cleanly. Clumsy keys matching the stick share at 0.766 may be a coincidence.\n\nThe 0.5-second window produced the similar clumsy share by chance, since tap gaps vary widely. After switching to interval-based measurement, clumsy keys will track the stick omega and share. Sharp keys should reach roughly 1.0. The hoop eases toward the smoothed speed each frame while the raw value holds between taps.\n\nThe old 0.5-second press window will be removed to prevent competing models. The lastPress timestamp should initialize to null rather than zero, since the simulation starts at time zero and a value of zero would wrongly indicate an immediate prior press.\n\nThe lastPress array is initialized to -1. The smoothing blend uses a = 1 - exp(-gap/0.12), so a 0.74-second gap almost fully adopts the new interval and a 0.1-second gap adopts about half. This strong blend is more accurate than the continuous stick's τ=0.12 for keys. Negative angular velocity from clumsy wandering still produces taps because floor(spin/π) keeps decreasing.\n\nThe phase accumulator uses signed angular velocity, so the time between floor crossings is π divided by the absolute speed. This keeps the key path consistent with the stick measurement.\n\nWhen angular velocity crosses zero, taps pause and the gap between presses grows. A subsequent tap after a long idle period reads as a very small angular velocity, which can dip the smoothed sensed rate.\n\nA bug was found in the phase accumulator. For negative angular velocity, JavaScript's modulo operator returns a negative remainder, so `turn % 2` is -1 instead of 1. This causes the plate A tap condition to fail while plate D still triggers, meaning negative turns may only hit plate D or neither plate.\n\nThe negative-turn bug halves the tap rate during clumsy wandering. The fix replaces the modulo check with an absolute crossing count so that odd and even turns always trigger the correct plate. A single step that exceeds one half-turn will still produce only one tap.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Stick play now separates the bots. Keys still cannot reach the slow plate band, because one tap inside a half-second window is read as a faster spin. I'll measure speed from the gap between taps."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ecf4d6f3-6592-4670-8e2e-697228b83be6-50","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/plates.js","old_string":"    this.presses = this.lanes.map(() => []);\n    this.crashes = this.lanes.map(() => 0);","new_string":"    this.lastPress = this.lanes.map(() => -1);\n    this.crashes = this.lanes.map(() => 0);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ecf4d6f3-6592-4670-8e2e-697228b83be6-51","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/plates.js","old_string":"      let omega = 0;\n      if (input.plateA || input.plateD) this.presses[i].push(this.t);\n      this.presses[i] = this.presses[i].filter((t) => this.t - t < 0.5);\n      if (mag > 0.5) {\n        const ang = Math.atan2(sy, sx);\n        if (this.hasAng[i]) {\n          let d = ang - this.prevAng[i];\n          while (d > Math.PI) d -= Math.PI * 2;\n          while (d < -Math.PI) d += Math.PI * 2;\n          omega = d / dt;\n        }\n        this.prevAng[i] = ang;\n        this.hasAng[i] = true;\n        const a = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / 0.12);\n        this.sensed[i] += (omega - this.sensed[i]) * a;\n      } else if (this.presses[i].length) {\n        const rate = this.presses[i].length / 0.5;\n        this.sensed[i] = rate * Math.PI;\n        this.hasAng[i] = false;\n      } else {\n        this.sensed[i] *= Math.exp(-3 * dt);\n        this.hasAng[i] = false;\n      }","new_string":"      let omega = 0;\n      const tapped = !!(input.plateA || input.plateD);\n      if (mag > 0.5) {\n        const ang = Math.atan2(sy, sx);\n        if (this.hasAng[i]) {\n          let d = ang - this.prevAng[i];\n          while (d > Math.PI) d -= Math.PI * 2;\n          while (d < -Math.PI) d += Math.PI * 2;\n          omega = d / dt;\n        }\n        this.prevAng[i] = ang;\n        this.hasAng[i] = true;\n        const a = 1 - Math.exp(-dt / 0.12);\n        this.sensed[i] += (omega - this.sensed[i]) * a;\n      } else if (tapped) {\n        const prev = this.lastPress[i];\n        if (prev >= 0) {\n          const gap = this.t - prev;\n          // Each press is half a turn, so the gap is the hoop speed. The slow band is one tap every ~0.7 s.\n          if (gap >= dt && gap <= 1.2) {\n            const instant = Math.PI / gap;\n            const a = 1 - Math.exp(-gap / 0.12);\n            this.sensed[i] += (instant - this.sensed[i]) * a;\n          }\n        }\n        this.lastPress[i] = this.t;\n        this.hasAng[i] = false;\n      } else if (this.lastPress[i] < 0 || this.t - this.lastPress[i] > 1.05) {\n        this.sensed[i] *= Math.exp(-3 * dt);\n        this.hasAng[i] = false;\n      }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ecf4d6f3-6592-4670-8e2e-697228b83be6-52","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/plates.js","old_string":"      const prev = this.spin[i];\n      this.spin[i] += omega * (1 / 120);\n      const turn = Math.floor(this.spin[i] / Math.PI);\n      const tap = turn !== Math.floor(prev / Math.PI);\n      return { x: 0, y: 0, plateA: tap && turn % 2 === 1, plateD: tap && turn % 2 === 0, flail: false, hop: false };","new_string":"      const prev = this.spin[i];\n      this.spin[i] += omega * (1 / 120);\n      const turn = Math.floor(this.spin[i] / Math.PI);\n      const tap = turn !== Math.floor(prev / Math.PI);\n      const which = Math.abs(turn);\n      return { x: 0, y: 0, plateA: tap && which % 2 === 1, plateD: tap && which % 2 === 0, flail: false, hop: false };"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":555,"output_tokens":4960,"cache_read_input_tokens":109440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"a57d47cc-0ef2-4300-bd92-672f02e971a4"}
