0,57,52,57,58,42,42,69,118,101,114,121,32,101,118,101,110,116,39,115,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,115,32,119,101,114,101,32,115,105,109,117,108,97,116,101,100,32,119,105,116,104,32,116,104,101,32,98,111,116,115,44,42,42,32,111,110,32,114,101,97,108,32,82,97,112,105,101,114,32,119,104,101,114,101,32,112,104,121,115,105,99,115,32,109,97,116,116,101,114,58,32,70,114,117,105,116,32,72,97,116,44,32,80,111,115,101,115,44,32,84,104,101,32,67,97,105,114,110,44,32,83,116,105,108,108,32,87,97,116,101,114,44,32,76,111,103,32,82,101,112,115,44,32,80,108,97,110,107,32,38,32,80,101,114,99,104,44,32,84,117,103,32,111,102,32,80,101,97,99,101,44,32,82,111,111,109,32,83,101,114,118,105,99,101,44,32,83,112,114,105,110,103,98,111,97,114,100,44,32,73,115,108,97,110,100,32,76,111,111,112,44,32,84,104,101,32,71,114,97,110,100,32,72,111,108,100,32,97,110,100,32,83,116,101,112,32,67,108,97,115,115,32,111,110,32,116,104,101,32,114,101,97,108,32,98,97,108,97,110,99,101,32,99,111,114,101,44,32,84,105,112,112,121,32,82,97,102,116,44,32,80,108,97,116,101,32,83,112,105,110,110,101,114,115,32,102,114,111,109,32,97,32,109,111,118,105,110,103,32,115,116,105,99,107,32,118,101,99,116,111,114,44,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,67,104,101,99,107,45,73,110,46,32,75,101,121,115,32,119,101,114,101,32,115,105,109,117,108,97,116,101,100,32,97,103,97,105,110,115,116,32,116,104,101,32,115,116,105,99,107,32,102,111,114,32,80,111,115,101,115,44,32,83,116,105,108,108,32,87,97,116,101,114,44,32,70,114,117,105,116,32,72,97,116,44,32,82,111,111,109,32,83,101,114,118,105,99,101,32,97,110,100,32,80,108,97,116,101,32,83,112,105,110,110,101,114,115,46,32,84,104,105,115,32,111,118,101,114,116,117,114,110,101,100,32,109,121,32,102,105,114,115,116,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,115,32,102,111,114,32,80,108,97,116,101,32,83,112,105,110,110,101,114,115,44,32,84,117,103,32,111,102,32,80,101,97,99,101,44,32,76,111,103,32,82,101,112,115,44,32,80,108,97,110,107,32,38,32,80,101,114,99,104,44,32,82,111,111,109,32,83,101,114,118,105,99,101,44,32,84,105,112,112,121,32,82,97,102,116,44,32,76,101,97,110,32,77,97,116,99,104,44,32,84,104,101,32,67,97,105,114,110,39,115,32,116,111,112,32,116,105,101,114,44,32,83,116,101,112,32,67,108,97,115,115,39,115,32,108,101,97,110,32,110,111,116,101,115,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,107,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,32,109,111,100,101,108,46,32,69,120,112,101,99,116,32,116,104,101,32,115,97,109,101,32,119,104,101,110,32,121,111,117,32,98,117,105,108,100,58,32,42,42,109,101,97,115,117,114,101,32,98,101,102,111,114,101,32,121,111,117,32,116,114,117,115,116,32,97,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,46,42,42,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":14,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"- **Keys in balance events ✔: they move the asking ring, and it stays where you leave it.** Holding a key moves the ring at 1.6 units/s; releasing leaves it there, and C recentres. The ring must be clearly visible on the Balance Disc, because a player steering by keys watches the ring, not the dot. I tested three models with a person-like bot. Keys that spring back on release needed 9.6 presses a second just to hold a pose. A tap-then-accelerate model scored worst (Poses Tier 1: 68 / 75 / 38). This one holds up against the stick: Poses Tier 1 98 / 62 / 54 (stick 100 / 76 / 63), Tier 2 86 / 58 / 34 (90 / 64 / 53), Still Water Tier 1 100 / 85 / 28 (100 / 93 / 24), Fruit Hat Tier 1 21 / 22 / 20 banked with no falls (28 / 33 / 28), Room Service Tier 1 all five glasses. Use a move speed of about 1.6 and don't add acceleration.\"},{\"line_number\":195,\"content\":\"| 4 | A Little Damp | Quick Lean, One-Foot Hold, Stand Still | Springboard, Still Water, Island Loop | Air control. Group Class invitation |\"},{\"line_number\":240,\"content\":\"**Non-standing poses reuse the balance core:** in Plank & Perch, Still Water and Tug of Peace the core stays upright and invisible, and the visible doll plays the pose and rocks with it. Nothing in the rules knows the difference.\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"**Still Water** (Lily Pond; high three-quarter camera over the water)\"},{\"line_number\":259,\"content\":\"- *Play:* Sit on a lily pad for 60 s. Stay in the small calm zone. Calm fills a meter, and creatures arrive at thresholds: dragonfly on your nose, frog on your head, koi circling, turtle, and at full calm Ms. Stillwater tiptoes over and pats your head. Move too much and they scatter. Ripples spread from the pad in proportion to how much you move: this is a beautiful TSL shader on the pond. Distractions: Trudy whispering (\\\"Don't think about your left knee\\\"), a sneeze (telegraphed \\\"Ah... ah...\\\": press Flail to stifle it, or take a big shove).\"},{\"line_number\":260,\"content\":\"- *Tiers ✔, 60 s:* calm zone r .15, .12, .10; sway .07→.18, .1→.22, .12→.26; tremor .05; 2, 3, 4 sneezes (1.2 s warning; a missed one is a 2.2 N·m shove for .3 s). Calm rises 1/30 per s in the zone and falls 1/8 per s outside it, and creatures arrive at .2, .4, .6, .8, 1. Time in zone: Tier 1 100% / 95% / 80% (peak calm 1 / 1 / .67), Tier 2 86 / 71 / 48, Tier 3 62 / 49 / 31.\"},{\"line_number\":261,\"content\":\"- *Scoring:* form = mean of (share of time in the zone, calm at the end) ✔ Tier 1 100 / 89 / 48. *Bot:* hold centre, stifle sneezes.\"},{\"line_number\":391,\"content\":\"**Writing style.** Short sentences. Polite. Second person. Chirpy and calm, with something slightly off. Instructions are plain and exact, then a small, sincere, odd aside. Praise is mild and specific. Every failure gets a line that makes it fine. The joke is the straight face. Write at least 200 Trudy lines, 60 for each instructor, 60 for guests, in `src/data/dialogue.js`, by situation, picked without repeats.\"},{\"line_number\":513,\"content\":\"| Lily Pond | −13, 7 | Still Water | Notice Board | 1, 9 | Today's Plan, Journal |\"},{\"line_number\":554,\"content\":\"| Stillness | Poses, Cairn, Still Water | 60 BPM, free; pad, bells on the breath cycle, flute | Dmaj9 Emaj9/D, slowly, Lydian |\"},{\"line_number\":634,\"content\":\"5. **Scoring.** Each slot gives `round(form × 10)`. Call `AIHub.progress({ score, label: 'Fruit Hat 420' })` every second **from the moment time reaches 0, with score 0 during the first intro.** The harness checks for ghost traffic and progress about 4 seconds into play, well before the first class starts, and fails the game if there is none. `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once at the end, for example stats `{ 'Floor Exercises': 2, 'Best medal': 'Pleasant', 'Wobble Age': 41 }`, and an award from a small list (\\\"Suspiciously Still\\\"). Then a calm \\\"waiting for the others\\\" with Trudy.\"},{\"line_number\":826,\"content\":\"| 6 | Tier B events, in this order | Still Water, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace, Island Loop |\"},{\"line_number\":829,\"content\":\"**Cut order if you run short. Cut whole things, never stub them, and leave no trace (TASK.md: no stubs, no placeholders).** First Island Loop, then Tug of Peace, then Plank & Perch, then Still Water, then Tier 3 of each event (leaving a two-tier ladder), then Tier 2. Do not cut: Fruit Hat, Poses, Check-In, Trudy, the tilting island, the jar, the finale, Attract, Dev Mode, Group Class, the hub session, glyphs, audio. The day table builds from the registry, so cutting an event needs no other change.\"},{\"line_number\":949,\"content\":\"**Every event's numbers were simulated with the bots,** on real Rapier where physics matter: Fruit Hat, Poses, The Cairn, Still Water, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace, Room Service, Springboard, Island Loop, The Grand Hold and Step Class on the real balance core, Tippy Raft, Plate Spinners from a moving stick vector, and the Check-In. Keys were simulated against the stick for Poses, Still Water, Fruit Hat, Room Service and Plate Spinners. This overturned my first numbers for Plate Spinners, Tug of Peace, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Room Service, Tippy Raft, Lean Match, The Cairn's top tier, Step Class's lean notes and the keyboard model. Expect the same when you build: **measure before you trust a number.**\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-893efe4a-8b94-42a2-b135-55243b6ac987-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { DEG } from '../physics/balancer.js';\\n\\nexport function screenOf(state, maxDeg) {\\n  const m = Math.max(1e-4, maxDeg) * DEG;\\n  return { x: state.leanX / m, y: -state.leanZ / m };\\n}\\n\\nexport function clamp(n, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, n));\\n10→}\\n\\nexport function lerp(a, b, u) {\\n  return a + (b - a) * clamp(u, 0, 1);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { DEG } from '../physics/balancer.js';\\n\\nexport function screenOf(state, maxDeg) {\\n  const m = Math.max(1e-4, maxDeg) * DEG;\\n  return { x: state.leanX / m, y: -state.leanZ / m };\\n}\\n\\nexport function clamp(n, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, n));\\n10→}\\n\\nexport function lerp(a, b, u) {\\n  return a + (b - a) * clamp(u, 0, 1);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/lean.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"import { DEG } from '../physics/balancer.js';\\n\\nexport function screenOf(state, maxDeg) {\\n  const m = Math.max(1e-4, maxDeg) * DEG;\\n  return { x: state.leanX / m, y: -state.leanZ / m };\\n}\\n\\nexport function clamp(n, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, n));\\n}\\n\\nexport function lerp(a, b, u) {\\n  return a + (b - a) * clamp(u, 0, 1);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":14}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-893efe4a-8b94-42a2-b135-55243b6ac987-72","content":"{\"type\":\"BackgroundTaskStarted\",\"task_id\":\"2ce081f7-234c-4c84-a88b-765b11585d81\",\"task_type\":\"bash\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-893efe4a-8b94-42a2-b135-55243b6ac987-72.log\",\"status\":\"running\",\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer && node matrix.mjs\",\"summary\":\"Background task 2ce081f7-234c-4c84-a88b-765b11585d81 started\",\"retrieval_hint\":\"Use get_command_or_subagent_output with task_ids=[\\\"2ce081f7-234c-4c84-a88b-765b11585d81\\\"] when you need the output.\",\"pid\":137779}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"5a97cb42-79ad-4927-a6f0-21c8bcb6ed99"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_306","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The PLAN specifies Still Water Tier 1 metrics: 100% / 95% / 80% in zone and 100 / 89 / 48 form.\n\nThe clumsy bot's form is only 14.6, far below the planned 48. The correct skills are in place, so the issue likely lies in the balance controller or noisy lean readings.\n\nSneeze shoves knock clumsy out of the zone, and calm drops too slowly outside to recover. Sharp still water is at least 85, so the controller can hold the zone when the bot is good. Clumsy is simply too sloppy for a 0.15 zone.\n\nThe plan's clumsy bot actually stayed in the zone 80% of the time with form 48. The current clumsy bot is far worse. The correction formula is a proportional controller on the delayed dot: x = -g * dot.x + noise. With g=0.8 and a dot of 0.2, the wish is -0.16, but the actual lean is only 3.6°. That weak correction explains why clumsy cannot hold the zone.\n\nThe 1.26° noise wobble is larger than the 2.7° zone, so delay and noise likely push clumsy outside often. Our physics or bot may differ from the plan's. Sway might fight the controller and cause oscillation beyond the zone. I will measure still water in-zone share directly for each skill and record peak cob.\n\nThe plan's still water form is mean(share, calm)*100, not formOf(raw, par). The par does not scale the score; form is the performance itself. To reach the planned 48, clumsy must hold the zone about 80% of the time with end calm near 0.67 and a mean near 0.48. The balance core may respond differently than the plan's simulation, so tuning the bot for this event rather than global skills might be necessary.\n\nThe plan's stated form 48 implies end calm near 0.16, not the peak 0.67. The mean of 0.80 and 0.16 equals 0.48. This suggests clumsy exits the zone late and drains calm. The current 14.6 form means clumsy is barely inside at all.\n\nThe 0.38-second delay is not the main problem; the 7-second sway period makes it small relative to the zone. The ±0.07 wish noise is the larger issue, but it still fits inside the 0.15 zone. If the physics tracks the wish accurately, the bot should be able to stay inside. The real cause of clumsy's poor performance must lie elsewhere.\n\nThe physics may not track small wishes quickly enough, so sway could push the lean past the zone while the delayed correction overshoots. I will wait for the heavy matrix run to finish before adding a debug measurement. I will also check plank, tug, island, step, springboard, and grand hold bots to see how their result formulas can be fixed.\n\nPoses likely passes because its targets are larger and more forgiving. The still water failure probably stems from the `correctWish` function itself.\n\nA short measurement script will run after the matrix completes. The still water bot might use gainLoad to avoid overshoot, though the plan only warns against high gain under load and this event is not loaded.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed7e9111-3123-4a21-8438-6af779367bd8-73","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"formOf|botInput|par:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ed7e9111-3123-4a21-8438-6af779367bd8-74","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["2ce081f7-234c-4c84-a88b-765b11585d81"],"timeout_ms":60000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2910,"output_tokens":1880,"cache_read_input_tokens":134528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"4d68b087-c29f-47b4-9bf2-cb12d9a8438c"}
