y no delay        form 94.6 93% calm time · 4 visitors calm 0.96 falls 0 out 7% peak 0.18\\nclumsy gain 0.35       form 34.1 67% calm time · 0 visitors calm 0.01 falls 0 out 33% peak 0.28\\nclumsy cap 0.12        form 35.0 70% calm time · 0 visitors calm 0.00 falls 0 out 30% peak 0.28\\navg plain              form 98.1 98% calm time · 4 visitors calm 0.98 falls 0 out 2% peak 0.17\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer && node still-probe.mjs\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Probe why Still Water clumsy scores low\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-770f3cce-7782-466b-8416-8880579638fa-81.log\",\"total_bytes\":932}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"9a83e194-3330-457d-9e84-be4f2def695e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_312","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The smoking gun is a \"clumsy no noise\" form 99.\n\n0.07 noise destroys still water. Delay alone scores 94.6. The correctWish noise model adds 0.07 amplitude to the wish within a 0.15 zone. Average noise of 0.03 scores 98.\n\nThe 0.07 noise is tiny compared to the 0.46 wobble. The controller amplifies it into a 0.46 oscillation via feedback gain 0.8 and delay 0.38. No-noise clumsy stays stable at 0.17. Zeroing the noise makes clumsy score 99, which is Exemplary and bypasses the skill test.\n\nScoring 99 passes the matrix but makes clumsy and sharp identical, which kills the skill gradient. The plan targets form 48. A better outcome would be clumsy around 45-60, sharp at 100, and average near 90. The challenge is making noise push them out of the zone about 20-40% of the time without the 71% resonant blow-up.\n\nThe plan's 80% zone time and form 48 only work because the event ends with calm at 0.16, not the peak calm of 0.67. If the bot simply tracked a noisy wish without amplifying it, the noise would stay near 0.07 and keep the bot inside the zone almost all the time, scoring roughly 100 instead of 48.\n\nThe original 80% zone time and 48 form were possible because calm drained at the end. The current blow-up is 71% outside and only scores 15. Damping the bot would kill the resonant wobble, but clumsy would then score 99 instead of the planned ~48. The question is whether a 99 score for clumsy is acceptable.\n\nThe still water test does not require clumsy to score below 70, so 99 passes the matrix. The real problem is that perfect clumsy would make skill irrelevant. The plan should aim for form 48 without retuning global skills. The noise is injected inside the feedback loop, which causes the delayed controller to resonate. Filtering the noise so it moves the target slowly within and slightly beyond the zone would bypass that feedback loop.\n\nThe noise should be a slow wander of the goal rather than a high-frequency kick. The current correctWish already adds noise at 3.1 rad/s and 2.3 rad/s, which is not super fast. The 0.46 blow-up means the loop gain is too high.\n\nDamping the correction gain to 0.35 cut the peak wobble from 0.46 to 0.28 and outside time from 71% to 33%. Form fell to 34 because calm drained to 0.01 at the end. The next probes are gain 0.5 and 0.55, or a low-passed wish.\n\nThe simplest fix is to low-pass the still water bot's wish output instead of changing correctWish globally. Poses already scores 52, so the global noise model should stay untouched. The probe will apply a 0.08 low-pass filter to the raw correction to prevent noisy delayed feedback from yanking the bot out of the zone.\n\nThe low-pass filter will use a 0.08 smoothing factor on the raw correction. Gain probes will run at 0.5 and 0.6, and noise will be halved to 0.035. The goal is to kill the resonant wobble while keeping the slow sway.\n\nSteady-state calm is 0 when the bot spends 79% of the time inside the zone. Below that, calm drains to zero and form equals half the zone share. The 67% in-time case therefore yields a form near 33.5.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-61871b7d-a2eb-4946-a732-d0cce0c8c681-82","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer/still-probe.mjs","old_string":"run('clumsy gain 0.35', 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => correctWish({ ...skill, gain: 0.35 }, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7));\nrun('clumsy cap 0.12', 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => {\n  const w = correctWish(skill, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7);\n  const h = Math.hypot(w.x, w.y) || 1;\n  const s = Math.min(1, 0.12 / h);\n  return { x: w.x * s, y: w.y * s };\n});\nrun('avg plain', 'average', plain);","new_string":"let prev = { x: 0, y: 0 };\nfunction lp(a, skill, cob, past, t) {\n  const w = correctWish(skill, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7);\n  prev = { x: prev.x + (w.x - prev.x) * a, y: prev.y + (w.y - prev.y) * a };\n  return prev;\n}\nfor (const a of [0.04, 0.08, 0.15, 0.25]) {\n  prev = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n  run(`clumsy lp ${a}`, 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => lp(a, skill, cob, past, t));\n}\nfor (const g of [0.45, 0.55, 0.65]) {\n  run(`clumsy gain ${g}`, 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => correctWish({ ...skill, gain: g }, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7));\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":548,"output_tokens":2494,"cache_read_input_tokens":158208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"8c7c7bdf-2079-425d-a25a-eaae5474b8ec"}
