lumsy gain 0.65       form 17.6 35% calm time · 0 visitors calm 0.00 falls 0 out 65% peak 0.40\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer && node still-probe.mjs\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Probe damped Still Water clumsy bots\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-c4ce4b98-eb23-41d1-9942-29c4b66307e6-83.log\",\"total_bytes\":1319}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"de5b4f8b-6949-4a02-8027-11870ba96e28"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_314","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Low-pass filtering worsened the bot's sway because it cannot correct itself.\n\nLower gain still leaves the bot under 40 and drains calm. The 3.1 rad/s noise is the oscillator feedback. A slow goal wander near the zone edge with stable correction could replace noise. Amplitude scales with skill.noise / 0.07 so clumsy bots wander more.\n\nCorrection will use a shorter delay or the current cob without fast noise inside the loop. Sharp bots stay at zero with perfect form. Average bots wander about 0.05, remaining safely inside. Clumsy bots reach roughly 0.12, often near the edge; the amplitude must be tuned so they are inside about 82–88% of the time. A pure sine goal path means the bot is always inside if the amplitude stays below 0.15, so the path must occasionally exceed that limit to allow occasional outside excursions.\n\nA pure circular goal path with amplitude 0.16 would keep the bot permanently outside, draining calm and destroying form. A linear path instead allows the bot to spend a calculable fraction of its time inside the zone. For an amplitude of 0.22, the sine stays within the 0.15 radius for about 68% of each half-period.\n\nAn amplitude of 0.154 yields an 85% inside rate, with brief outside excursions at the peaks. Net calm rises by about 0.01 per second, so calm reaches its cap and form averages 92. This exceeds the required 48.\n\nTo hit the exact 48 target, calm must end low. This requires either brief final excursions or an overall outside rate above 79%. At an 82% inside rate, calm ends near 0.3 and form is about 56. At 80%, it is roughly 45. At 83%, it is about 61.\n\nA sine wander with amplitude 0.156 yields the exact 82% inside rate, but this is a very narrow and fragile tuning. Small tracking errors would shift the effective amplitude away from that target. A better approach may be to stop fighting the physics: add a slow position bias that the stable controller tracks directly, with amplitude chosen by measurement rather than by formula.\n\nThe implementation uses a sine-cosine goal with amplitude 0.154, driven by slow frequencies of 0.35 and 0.23. The stable controller corrects toward this wandering target without the fast noise term. Sharp bots stay at zero with perfect form. Average bots reach amplitude 0.066, remaining safely inside the zone. Clumsy bots hit the 0.154 limit, which is borderline.\n\nA two-axis lissajous path is too complex because its distance from the origin varies unpredictably. A single-axis sine wander is cleaner. The amplitude will be tuned by probing values of 0.15, 0.16, 0.17, 0.18, and 0.20.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-08b8fc32-73e2-4690-975c-24d968c324f3-84","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer/still-probe.mjs","old_string":"let prev = { x: 0, y: 0 };\nfunction lp(a, skill, cob, past, t) {\n  const w = correctWish(skill, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7);\n  prev = { x: prev.x + (w.x - prev.x) * a, y: prev.y + (w.y - prev.y) * a };\n  return prev;\n}\nfor (const a of [0.04, 0.08, 0.15, 0.25]) {\n  prev = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n  run(`clumsy lp ${a}`, 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => lp(a, skill, cob, past, t));\n}\nfor (const g of [0.45, 0.55, 0.65]) {\n  run(`clumsy gain ${g}`, 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => correctWish({ ...skill, gain: g }, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7));\n}","new_string":"for (const amp of [0.15, 0.17, 0.19, 0.22, 0.26]) {\n  run(`clumsy wander ${amp}`, 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => {\n    const goal = { x: amp * Math.sin(t * 0.45 + 0.7), y: amp * 0.35 * Math.sin(t * 0.31) };\n    return correctWish({ ...skill, noise: 0 }, goal, past, t, false, 0.7);\n  });\n}\nrun('avg wander 0.08', 'average', (skill, cob, past, t) => {\n  const goal = { x: 0.08 * Math.sin(t * 0.45 + 0.7), y: 0.028 * Math.sin(t * 0.31) };\n  return correctWish({ ...skill, noise: 0 }, goal, past, t, false, 0.7);\n});\nrun('sharp wander 0', 'sharp', (skill, cob, past, t) => correctWish({ ...skill, noise: 0 }, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7));"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":818,"output_tokens":2382,"cache_read_input_tokens":161280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"e4c02bce-c4dd-4375-8773-0a04c1b3c878"}
