{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_316","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A wander of 0 is interesting.\n\nThe controller overshoots the goal. Peak motion is roughly twice the amplitude. I will try smaller amplitudes: 0.06, 0.08, 0.10, and 0.12. The relationship may not be linear due to resonance. The y component also adds to the radius.\n\nThe overshoot likely comes from the PD-like correctWish formula with gain 0.8. I will try a smaller gain of 0.4 paired with amplitude 0.12. I also plan to replace the wander loop and skip the first test runs to save time.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f6903995-e020-4201-88fd-f3be00c36854-86","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer/still-probe.mjs","old_string":"for (const amp of [0.15, 0.17, 0.19, 0.22, 0.26]) {\n  run(`clumsy wander ${amp}`, 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => {\n    const goal = { x: amp * Math.sin(t * 0.45 + 0.7), y: amp * 0.35 * Math.sin(t * 0.31) };\n    return correctWish({ ...skill, noise: 0 }, goal, past, t, false, 0.7);\n  });\n}\nrun('avg wander 0.08', 'average', (skill, cob, past, t) => {\n  const goal = { x: 0.08 * Math.sin(t * 0.45 + 0.7), y: 0.028 * Math.sin(t * 0.31) };\n  return correctWish({ ...skill, noise: 0 }, goal, past, t, false, 0.7);\n});\nrun('sharp wander 0', 'sharp', (skill, cob, past, t) => correctWish({ ...skill, noise: 0 }, { x: 0, y: 0 }, past, t, false, 0.7));","new_string":"for (const amp of [0.04, 0.06, 0.08, 0.1, 0.12]) {\n  run(`x ${amp}`, 'clumsy', (skill, cob, past, t) => {\n    const goal = { x: amp * Math.sin(t * 0.5 + 0.7), y: amp * 0.6 * Math.sin(t * 0.37 + 1.2) };\n    return correctWish({ ...skill, noise: 0, gain: 0.55 }, goal, past, t, false, 0.7);\n  });\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":696,"output_tokens":963,"cache_read