{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_327","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I am carefully examining each failure.\n\nThe \"Attract seen < 4\" failure points to stepAttract around lines 680-740. The mouse flail bug is in the director's pointer() method: when down=false, it calls pointer(960, 540, 0), but because buttons is zero, pointerButtons never fires and the middle button stays stuck.\n\nThe flail edge is generated by pointerButtons when the middle button transitions from up to down. Because pointerMove sets the button state to zero before pointerButtons runs, the press-to-release transition never registers.\n\nThe test API calls pointerButtons before pointerMove, so the previous state is already stale. The fix is to call pointerButtons first in director's pointer() method.\n\npointerButtons already calls pointerMove internally when coordinates are provided. Because it sets the button state before invoking pointerMove, the rising edge is detected correctly. Calling pointerButtons alone in director's pointer() method fixes the flail detection.\n\nThe mouse title leave failure at line 71 is the same bug. The pad and key title leaves pass, but the mouse fails because pointerMove consumes the button change before pointerButtons can detect the edge.\n\nThe prompts test at line 106 also fails. After a key press, lastDevice is still \"pad\" instead of \"key\". keyDown marks the device as key, but advance polling appears to overwrite it.\n\nThe pad axes were never cleared after the previous test step. When keyDown set lastDevice to key, the next poll still found stick magnitude above 0.25 and marked the device as pad again. The test expects a key press to override an active pad.\n\nThe plan says \"last device wins.\" A held stick is still current input, so the pad should override a key press. The test failure is therefore correct.\n\nThe prompts test expects a key press to override the pad even while the stick is still deflected. The plan says keys win while a weight key is down, but the test name suggests prompts should switch to key glyphs immediately after KeyA. This suggests the test may be wrong, or the rules need clarification.\n\nThe fix is to change the poll order so that a weight key overrides a held pad. When KeyA is down, the poll should mark the device as key instead of letting the stick magnitude override it. The summary's weightSource rule already says to use pad only when lastDevice is pad; otherwise weight keys win.\n\nThe current `weightSource` logic is backwards. It returns 'pad' whenever `lastDevice` is pad, even if a weight key is currently down. Because `markDevice('pad')` runs every poll while stick magnitude exceeds 0.25, the device can never remain 'key' while a stick is deflected. The test expects a key press to override the pad immediately after KeyA, so the rules need to be reversed.\n\nA better approach is to mark the pad only when the stick changes, not every frame it is held. The poll should compare current stick axes against a stored `lastStick` value and call `markDevice('pad')` only if the deflection moved or the device was not already pad. This lets a key press override a held stick without requiring the stick to move.\n\nThe change-detection approach is confirmed. A stick deflection from zero to 0.6 correctly marks the device as pad on the first poll. Once a key press sets lastDevice to key, subsequent polls with the same deflection do not overwrite it. This lets prompts switch to key glyphs immediately after KeyA.\n\nThe prompt test only checks glyph appearance, so a key-driven wish integration is acceptable. I need to verify how prompts are built in model() after the fix. The four pads test shows lane0 lean at zero after joining the raft and advancing 1.2 seconds; I am investigating possible causes.\n\nThe four pads test failure may stem from the group raft using bot lanes instead of human pads. The first confirm might start the event before seats are read. The raft could also use a balance event that bypasses normal wish integration. Another possibility is that pressChoice set lane 0 to key input, preventing the stick from overriding it.\n\nThe four pads test failure is now clear. pressChoice and tap set lastDevice to key on input 0, and Enter is released before writeWish runs. Because weightSource only returns pad when lastDevice is pad, the source falls back to key with no active keys, so the wish stays at zero and lane0 lean remains zero.\n\nThe four pads failure may be caused by the raft using bot lanes instead of human pads. The test does not set botSkill, so the human path should apply the pad stick to lane 0. I need to check whether the join logic actually assigns pad 0 as a playing lane or if the raft uses a different control such as boat steering that does not affect leanX.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ec515bbf-7ec1-4875-960b-ddc2bae65f55-107","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","offset":660,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ec515bbf-7ec1-4875-960b-ddc2bae65f55-108","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function joinPads|groupAction|lanes","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ec515bbf-7ec1-4875-960b-ddc2bae65f55-109","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/raft.js","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3932,"output_tokens":2975,"cache_read_input_tokens":185856,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"f5f00fc9-962b-4b11-814b-b0386e57ebdd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ec515bbf-7ec1-4875-960b-ddc2bae65f55-107","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"660→        snaps.push(inputs[i].snapshot(0));\\n      }\\n    }\\n    return snaps;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sampleToSnap(sample, input) {\\n    return input.snapshot(0);\\n  }\\n\\n670→  function stepEvent(dt, snaps) {\\n    if (!event || paused) return;\\n    event.fixed(dt, snaps || []);\\n    if (event.frame) event.frame(dt);\\n  }\\n\\n  function noteNotch() {\\n    if (event && event.notch && !profile.doneSteps.includes('grandHold')) {\\n      profile.doneSteps.push('grandHold');\\n      profile.levelled = profile.doneSteps.length >= programme.length;\\n680→      if (!profile.met.includes('grandHold')) profile.met.push('grandHold');\\n      audio.sfx('creak');\\n    }\\n    if (profile.doneSteps.length >= programme.length) profile.levelled = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function revealAge() {\\n    const mean = lastResult.mean || 0;\\n    const age = wobbleAge(mean, Math.min(4, profile.dayIndex));\\n    profile.ages.push(age);\\n690→    profile.marbles += 1;\\n    sayExact(`Your Wobble Age is ${age}.`);\\n    setScreen('age');\\n  }\\n\\n  function openQuestion() {\\n    setScreen('question');\\n  }\\n\\n  function startAttract() {\\n700→    attract = { index: 0, left: 18, between: 0, seen: [] };\\n    idle = 0;\\n    botSkill = 'sharp';\\n    launchAttract();\\n  }\\n\\n  function launchAttract() {\\n    const id = ATTRACT[attract.index % ATTRACT.length];\\n    if (!attract.seen.includes(id)) attract.seen.push(id);\\n    startEvent(id, { god: id !== 'fruitHat', lanes: [{ id: 0, kind: 'bot', name: 'Demo', colour: SEAT_COLOURS[1] }] });\\n710→    botOpt = id === 'fruitHat' ? { bankAt: 99 } : {};\\n    screen = 'play';\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepAttract(dt) {\\n    if (!attract) return;\\n    if (attract.between > 0) {\\n      attract.between -= dt;\\n      screen = 'title';\\n      if (attract.between <= 0) launchAttract();\\n720→      return;\\n    }\\n    const snaps = driveBots(dt);\\n    if (event) stepEvent(dt, snaps);\\n    attract.left -= dt;\\n    if (!event || event.done || attract.left <= 0) {\\n      if (event) { event.dispose(); event = null; }\\n      attract.index += 1;\\n      attract.left = 18;\\n      if (attract.index % ATTRACT.length === 0) {\\n730→        attract.between = 5;\\n        screen = 'title';\\n        botSkill = null;\\n      } else launchAttract();\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stopAttract(swallow) {\\n    if (event) { event.dispose(); event = null; }\\n    attract = null;\",\"content_concise\":\"660→        snaps.push(inputs[i].snapshot(0));\\n      }\\n    }\\n    return snaps;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sampleToSnap(sample, input) {\\n    return input.snapshot(0);\\n  }\\n\\n670→  function stepEvent(dt, snaps) {\\n    if (!event || paused) return;\\n    event.fixed(dt, snaps || []);\\n    if (event.frame) event.frame(dt);\\n  }\\n\\n  function noteNotch() {\\n    if (event && event.notch && !profile.doneSteps.includes('grandHold')) {\\n      profile.doneSteps.push('grandHold');\\n      profile.levelled = profile.doneSteps.length >= programme.length;\\n680→      if (!profile.met.includes('grandHold')) profile.met.push('grandHold');\\n      audio.sfx('creak');\\n    }\\n    if (profile.doneSteps.length >= programme.length) profile.levelled = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function revealAge() {\\n    const mean = lastResult.mean || 0;\\n    const age = wobbleAge(mean, Math.min(4, profile.dayIndex));\\n    profile.ages.push(age);\\n690→    profile.marbles += 1;\\n    sayExact(`Your Wobble Age is ${age}.`);\\n    setScreen('age');\\n  }\\n\\n  function openQuestion() {\\n    setScreen('question');\\n  }\\n\\n  function startAttract() {\\n700→    attract = { index: 0, left: 18, between: 0, seen: [] };\\n    idle = 0;\\n    botSkill = 'sharp';\\n    launchAttract();\\n  }\\n\\n  function launchAttract() {\\n    const id = ATT