{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_330","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ragdoll has 10 bodies. Fruit might spawn one during recovery.\n\nThe 5 extra bodies are build-time props, not a leak. The correct check compares body counts before and after the fall, then asserts the ragdoll is removed.\n\nThe simplest check is to snapshot the body count right before beginFall. After recovery, the ragdoll's 10 bodies must be gone, so the final count should not exceed that snapshot plus any props spawned during the wait.\n\nThe proposed check fails if fruit spawns during recovery. Adding one body makes the count exceed the ragdoll-removed threshold. A loose buffer is possible but imprecise.\n\nThe exact body count assertion is dropped. The test will instead verify that the ragdoll is fully removed and the world frees its bodies on dispose. A simpler check compares the post-fall body count to the pre-fall snapshot.\n\nThe proposed `len() < spiked` check is sound. The ragdoll contributes 10 bodies to the post-fall count, so any removal leaves a gap of at least one body. Fruit spawns during recovery are rare and small enough to not break this threshold.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-109d5606-c78a-429b-8629-6640179e9f2a-116","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"prompts|lastDevice|glyph","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3817,"output_tokens":979,"cache_read_input_tokens":199296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"771d17ef-01dc-44bf-a9f0-8c6acb01dece"}
