{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_342","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical issue was found with the attract wake test.\n\nThe Enter key wakes the attract screen and consumes the latch, so the title screen stays stable. The key is also issued after pads are cleared, preventing driveBots from interfering.\n\nMenu wish updates correctly during attract. The menu poll sees a cleared pad and no wish, so it does not trigger a wake. The Enter key is latched and consumed by the menu poll, which sets confirm and clears the latch. The menu wish copy appears necessary.\n\nZeroing the menu wish when the pad stick is inactive is correct for wake detection. Balance polls are only interrupted by attract, so a previous balance wish will not persist into the next poll. The menu wish should be placed just before the balance wish block or after the stick state is known.\n\nThe menu wish block will not overwrite the balance wish. A standard pad in menu mode copies stickX and negated stickY into wish.x and wish.y. The stickActive threshold is 0.25, while the wake threshold is 0.3, so small resting values will not trigger a wake.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40374259-9316-48ae-bd71-c66f9b27156a-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"fruitInterval","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-40374259-9316-48ae-bd71-c66f9b27156a-38","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"spawn\\(|createRigidBody","glob":"**/roomService.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1642,"output_tokens":1765,"cache_read_input_tokens":71808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"28f3242a-89e3-4cb9-954f-9a2251171f0a"}
