,99,116,32,102,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,103,101,110,114,101,46,32,84,104,101,32,109,111,117,115,101,32,97,105,109,115,44,32,108,111,111,107,115,44,32,97,110,100,32,99,108,105,99,107,115,32,109,101,110,117,32,105,116,101,109,115,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,105,110,103,115,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,119,111,114,108,100,32,40,104,111,118,101,114,32,109,111,118,101,115,32,116,104,101,32,102,111,99,117,115,41,32,119,104,101,114,101,118,101,114,32,116,104,101,32,103,101,110,114,101,32,117,115,101,115,32,105,116,46,32,79,110,45,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,112,114,111,109,112,116,115,32,102,111,108,108,111,119,32,116,104,101,32,105,110,112,117,116,32,117,115,101,100,32,108,97,115,116,58,32,80,108,97,121,83,116,97,116,105,111,110,32,103,108,121,112,104,115,32,102,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,99,111,110,116,114,111,108,108,101,114,32,40,119,105,116,104,32,97,32,83,101,116,116,105,110,103,115,32,111,112,116,105,111,110,32,116,111,32,115,104,111,119,32,88,98,111,120,32,103,108,121,112,104,115,44,32,65,32,66,32,88,32,89,44,32,105,110,115,116,101,97,100,41,44,32,107,101,121,115,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,117,115,101,32,98,117,116,116,111,110,115,32,102,111,114,32,107,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,32,97,110,100,32,109,111,117,115,101,46,10,49,48,57,58,69,120,105,116,32,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,58,32,98,101,102,111,114,101,32,121,111,117,32,102,105,110,105,115,104,44,32,97,108,115,111,32,115,97,118,101,32,116,104,101,115,101,32,97,110,115,119,101,114,115,32,97,115,32,101,120,105,116,45,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,106,115,111,110,32,105,110,32,116,104,105,115,32,102,111,108,100,101,114,39,115,32,114,111,111,116,44,32,98,101,115,105,100,101,32,116,104,101,32,103,97,109,101,39,115,32,46,104,116,109,108,58,32,111,110,101,32,74,83,79,78,32,111,98,106,101,99,116,32,105,110,32,101,120,97,99,116,108,121,32,116,104,101,32,115,104,97,112,101,32,98,101,108,111,119,44,32,101,118,101,114,121,32,118,97,108,117,101,32,102,105,108,108,101,100,32,105,110,32,40,34,117,110,107,110,111,119,110,34,32,102,111,114,32,97,110,121,116,104,105,110,103,32,121,111,117,32,99,97,110,39,116,32,99,111,110,102,105,114,109,41,46,32,84,111,111,108,115,32,114,101,97,100,32,105,116,32,40,116,104,101,32,103,97,109,101,39,115,32,114,117,110,32,114,101,99,111,114,100,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,65,73,32,72,117,98,32,99,97,116,97,108,111,103,117,101,41,44,32,115,111,32,119,114,105,116,101,32,112,108,97,105,110,32,116,101,120,116,44,32,97,110,100,32,99,104,101,99,107,32,116,104,97,116,32,116,104,101,32,102,105,108,101,32,112,97,114,115,101,115,32,97,115,32,74,83,79,78,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":30,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"Design for a PS5 DualSense, or any pad the browser reports with `mapping === 'standard'`, on a TV at 10 feet. Keyboard and mouse play the same game on the same screens, with no separate desktop layout, and they should feel native rather than like stand-ins. Weight comes from a stick on a controller and from the pointer with a mouse. Both are analog. **Stick and mouse are always screen-relative:** up is away from the camera, right is screen right. Rotate the input by the camera's yaw before using it.\"},{\"line_number\":87,\"content\":\"- **Hover means the pointer moved ✔.** Move focus only on a `pointermove` whose coordinates changed. A browser also fires `pointerenter` when a menu appears under a parked mouse, and that made focus jump by itself under a controller player.\"},{\"line_number\":94,\"content\":\"- **Audio on a controller ✔.** Call `AudioContext.resume()` on pad input too, not only on keys and clicks. My first wiring left a controller-only player in silence. I can't confirm here that every browser accepts a gamepad press as the gesture that unlocks audio, so if the context is still suspended a few seconds after pad input, show a small tag asking for a key or click.\"},{\"line_number\":321,\"content\":\"- *Play:* Pump the board by squeezing both feet as it goes down. Press Hop near the top to launch. In the air the stick rotates you, holding Hop tucks and spins you faster. Hit the water. **Two ways to win:** a clean entry (head or feet down within 12°) makes barely a ripple and earns Grace. A perfect belly flop (front flat within 20°) sends up a giant column of water, knocks Gary out of the sky, and earns Splash. Score is the better of the two times height. Anything else is \\\"Technically a Dive.\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":324,\"content\":\"- *Whole run ✔,* pump then launch then a real spinning body, over 40 dives each: launch speed 5.4 / 3.8 / 3 m/s, height from a 5 m tower 6.5 / 5.7 / 5.5 m. Belly flop hit rate 43% / 35% / 13% at full stick, 85 / 68 / 45 at half stick. Head first 35 / 20 / 5 at full stick. **Half stick is too slow to get head first from the 5 m tower** (0% for everyone); it works from 9 m (40 / 0 / 0). Letting go, the spin coasts on for about 22° at full stick, so release early.\"},{\"line_number\":681,\"content\":\"**Stack.** `three@0.180.0` (import only from `three/webgpu` and `three/tsl`; addons from `three/addons/...` work ✔), `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3`, `esbuild`, `playwright@1.63.0`, `@fontsource/fredoka` (SIL OFL; put its name and licence in the credits). Web Audio and the Gamepad API directly. `npm i` these in the dev folder ✔; Playwright finds the browsers already here.\"},{\"line_number\":743,\"content\":\"- Keep to one or two browsers at once and close them when done. \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers rather than retrying.\"},{\"line_number\":744,\"content\":\"- Don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`: the browsers are already here. `npm i playwright@1.63.0` finds them ✔. `PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE` is already set; keep it if a script spawns a browser with a clean environment. If you want a Python tool, use `uv run --with ...`; this plan's tools are all Node.\"},{\"line_number\":747,\"content\":\"- There is no display. A headed browser needs `xvfb-run`, and you shouldn't need one.\"},{\"line_number\":756,\"content\":\"| Second player | TASK.md suggests two browser pages. The hub's harness is that test, built for this: it plays 2-4 copies at once, in frames of one page, on a simulated network. Add four stubbed pads for Group Class |\"},{\"line_number\":794,\"content\":\"*unit* (Node, no browser): Wobble Age mapping and bounds; marble payouts; tier unlock rules; programme table integrity (every id exists, days still work with a Tier B event removed); charts valid; tuning defaults inside min and max; dialogue ids all exist; save corrupt or old version is handled; rng repeatable; the session client hash; **the exit-interview file**, once it exists: parses, has exactly TASK.md's keys, 4, 6 and 4 feedback answers, no empty value except `series`, `usage` reading `added on import`, 3 to 6 lowercase tags, `genre` from TASK.md's list, `name` equal to the title constant; the built HTML has the metas in `name`, `content` order, the client directly after `<meta charset>`, and no `</script` inside a script. **Source greps:** no `Math.random` outside `src/core/rng.js`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`; no `alert(`, `confirm(`, `prompt(`, `window.open`, `WebSocket`, `RTCPeerConnection`; no audio file extensions or `decodeAudioData`; none of the source's nam [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":808,\"content\":\"*ui:* at 1920×1080, walk every screen and assert: no text under 30 px in computed style, nothing outside the viewport or the 5% margin except backgrounds, at most six focusable items, a visible focus. Touch-only: Pixel 7, iPhone and iPad profiles show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and Settings, `page.touchscreen` tap opens Settings, no other controls respond, attract runs, a key or pad clears the state. About shows every Source Information field and the three feedback lists, and matches the exit-interview file.\"},{\"line_number\":848,\"content\":\"- [ ] About/Credits, the exit-interview file and your chat reply are all filled in as below\"},{\"line_number\":850,\"content\":\"**Three places, the same content.** TASK.md calls this critical: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback go in **your chat reply** and an **in-game About/Credits screen,** and into **the exit-interview file** beside the HTML. These are your own answers from your own build. Nothing in this plan answers them for you, and section 22 is only an example. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\"},{\"line_number\":854,\"content\":\"2. Write the exit-interview file beside the HTML, using `notes/issues.md` for the counts.\"},{\"line_number\":928,\"content\":\"**The exit-interview file** is one JSON object in TASK.md's exact shape, plain text, every value filled in, and you check that it parses: `sourceInformation` (`date, source, plan, genre, perspective, tech, artDirection, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage`), `testingFeedback`, `engineFeedback`, `promptFeedback` (arrays, answers in order), and `aiHub`:\"},{\"line_number\":954,\"content\":\"- **Real hardware.** Nobody has played this with a real controller on a real TV. I can't confirm that every browser accepts a gamepad press as the gesture that unlocks audio (section 3 gives the fallback).\"},{\"line_number\":963,\"content\":\"Every requirement in TASK.md, in its order: where this plan answers it, and what proves it was met when you build. Test groups are in section 17. Some of what TASK.md asks for can only exist once there is a build: the game itself, its About/Credits screen, the exit-interview file and your final report. This plan covers those by saying exactly what to produce, when, and how it gets checked. Producing them is the build's job, and yours.\"},{\"line_number\":996,\"content\":\"| This computer: tools, browsers, WebGPU flags and secure pages | Sections 16 and 17, Browser flags | `events`: `render.lost` null ✔ |\"},{\"line_number\":1000,\"content\":\"| Sharing: browsers, `/tmp`, `playwright install`, system Python and `uv` | Section 17, Sharing this computer | Your practice |\"},{\"line_number\":1052,\"content\":\"**The exit-interview file's shape,** filled in for this stage. It parses, and its keys match TASK.md's exactly. Replace every value with your own. `name` and `tagline` are \\\"unknown\\\" here only because each builder picks its own title.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/TASK.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\"},{\"line_number\":40,\"content\":\"  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\"},{\"line_number\":55,\"content\":\"- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\"},{\"line_number\":63,\"content\":\"- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\"},{\"line_number\":64,\"content\":\"- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\"},{\"line_number\":83,\"content\":\"Design the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\"},{\"line_number\":109,\"content\":\"Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a9b41fb1-2757-44ad-baa5-1235d5148722-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ListDir\",\"Content\":{\"content\":\"- /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/\\n  - node_modules/\\n    - @dimforge/\\n      - rapier3d-compat/\\n        - coarena.d.ts\\n        - control/\\n          - character_controller.d.ts\\n          - index.d.ts\\n          - pid_controller.d.ts\\n          - ray_cast_vehicle_controller.d.ts\\n        - dynamics/\\n          - ccd_solver.d.ts\\n          - coefficient_combine_rule.d.ts\\n          - impulse_joint.d.ts\\n          - impulse_joint_set.d.ts\\n          - index.d.ts\\n          - integration_paramete