med dev subfolder; the bundled HTML, `exit-interview.json`, and `PROGRESS.md` land in the work-folder root. Runtime deps are three@0.180.0, @dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3, esbuild, playwright@1.63.0, Fredoka, and the AI Hub session client plus harness (protocol v1, client 1.4.0) from `https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`. Wii Fit's own activity list was not re-derived: PLAN.md already maps the source's pillars onto original events and forbids copying those activities.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep age, payouts, tilt, scoring, and the balance torque step pure so tests call them without a canvas. One fixed 1/120 step is shared by the page and the tests. Events take a list of lanes so solo, bots, couch play, ghosts, and attract are the same code. Bundle an IIFE into one HTML file so `file://` works with no module import. A test mode advances sim time without waiting and can skip the renderer. One test command prints only failures and a count; rerun only the part a change touches.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick GameTitle with a real RNG after brainstorming riffs, record it in PROGRESS.md, and create the matching dev subfolder.\\n- [ ] Boot a single-file build: Three r180 ink scene, Rapier 0.19.3, unmodified hub client, WebGL2 fallback, and a test advance hook. Confirm `file://` draws.\\n- [ ] Add the balance core, three-device input, Balance Disc, jointed doll, ragdoll recovery, and Fruit Hat. Lock them with tests from a fresh world.\\n- [ ] Add the island ritual (check-in, Wobble Age, jar, tilt) and every other §6 event, each tested from its own start.\\n- [ ] Add menus, attract, dev sliders, synthesized audio, glyphs, touch-only, Group Class, and the hub ghost session.\\n- [ ] Ship the ending, About/Credits, exit-interview.json, `{SCRATCH}/test-full.log` with zero failures, the two launch captures, and the hub log.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md's three WebGPU flags alone lose the device while the frame counter still climbs. Rendering checks must also pass `--use-vulkan=swiftshader` and `--use-angle=swiftshader`. A lost device, or a readback that succeeds and is blank, is a failure.\\n- Software WebGPU is only a few frames per second here, and extra browsers are killed when memory runs out. Logic tests must not need a renderer; keep at most two browsers open.\\n- PLAN.md §18 lets a short build cut whole events in a fixed order. That does not relax this plan: this computer can run the full demo, so every §6 event is required. A stub, a placeholder, or a cut of a do-not-cut system fails.\\n- The hub rejects an edited `session.js` and checks its hash. If the published client hash differs from the hash written in PLAN.md, use the hash shipped with that client release and fail the build on a mismatch.\\n- A real pad unlocking audio, and whether the music sounds good, cannot be confirmed here. Signal tests, plus the on-screen prompt if audio stays suspended after pad input, are the bar.\\n\",\"total_lines\":49}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"58059607-eb96-40c1-b0ec-e9b85a2a6cd6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_352","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A large remaining task is present.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5f7c267-ccf3-4dbb-a4b4-fcc5cc59f5d9-58","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5f7c267-ccf3-4dbb-a4b4-fcc5cc59f5d9-59","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5f7c267-ccf3-4dbb-a4b4-fcc5cc59f5d9-60","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"built page|exit-interview|TODO|session client|function unitTests","glob":"**/test/unit.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d5f7c267-ccf3-4dbb-a4b4-fcc5cc59f5d9-61","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/tools/build.mjs","limit":200}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10056,"output_tokens":652,"cache_read_input_tokens":92288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"6763ae44-ef25-48bd-bafc-f04c92c4af51"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d5f7c267-ccf3-4dbb-a4b4-fcc5cc59f5d9-58","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Issues caught while building Level Best\\n\\n1. Log Reps counted a phantom first rep because `lastRep` was undefined. Critical: no. The score started a rep early.\\n2. Plank & Perch could spawn a second ragdoll for one fall. Critical: yes. A second removal in the same step panics Rapier for the whole page.\\n3. Island Loop scored cadence from `t % period` and wrote tilted gravity into the world. Critical: yes. A sharp jog scored 26, and the gravity write produced NaN.\\n4. Plate Spinners' bot left the band it was supposed to hold. Critical: yes. A sharp bot scored about 47 instead of a full spin.\\n5. Room Service built the tray with full extents and lost glasses that were still on it. Critical: yes. The order could not be delivered.\\n6. Tippy Raft ignored the lane's skill and the grip that keeps a sharp player near the middle. Critical: no. Rounds still ended, but skill did not matter.\\n7. Check-in leaned the doll toward the wrong side of the target. Critical: yes. The Wobble Age came out of the wrong mean.\\n10→8. Check-in applied the calm margin twice. Critical: no. The stand test was stricter than the written one, but the day still finished.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Issues caught while building Level Best\\n\\n1. Log Reps counted a phantom first rep because `lastRep` was undefined. Critical: no. The score started a rep early.\\n2. Plank & Perch could spawn a second ragdoll for one fall. Critical: yes. A second removal in the same step panics Rapier for the whole page.\\n3. Island Loop scored cadence from `t % period` and wrote tilted gravity into the world. Critical: yes. A sharp jog scored 26, and the gravity write produced NaN.\\n4. Plate Spinners' bot left the band it was supposed to hold. Critical: yes. A sharp bot scored about 47 instead of a full spin.\\n5. Room Service built the tray with full extents and lost glasses that were still on it. Critical: yes. The order could not be delivered.\\n6. Tippy Raft ignored the lane's skill and the grip that keeps a sharp player near the middle. Critical: no. Rounds still ended, but skill did not matter.\\n7. Check-in leaned the doll toward the wrong side of the target. Critical: yes. The Wobble Age came out of the wrong mean.\\n10→8. Check-in applied the calm margin twice. Critical: no. The stand test was stricter than the written one, but the day still finished.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Issues caught while building Level Best\\n\\n1. Log Reps counted a phantom first rep because `lastRep` was undefined. Critical: no. The score started a rep early.\\n2. Plank & Perch could spawn a second ragdoll for one fall. Critical: yes. A second removal in the same step panics Rapier for the whole page.\\n3. Island Loop scored cadence from `t % period` and wrote tilted gravity into the world. Critical: yes. A sharp jog scored 26, and the gravity write produced NaN.\\n4. Plate Spinners' bot left the band it was supposed to hold. Critical: yes. A sharp bot scored about 47 instead of a full spin.\\n5. Room Service built the tray with full extents and lost glasses that were still on it. Critical: yes. The order could not be delivered.\\n6. Tippy Raft ignored the lane's skill and the grip that keeps a sharp player near the middle. Critical: no. Rounds still ended, but skill did not matter.\\n7. Check-in leaned the doll toward the wrong side of the target. Critical: yes. The Wobble Age came out of the wrong mean.\\n8. Check-in applied the calm margin twice. Critical: no. The stand test was stricter than the written one, but the day still finished.\\n\",\"total_lines\":10}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d5f7c267-ccf3-4dbb-a4b4-fcc5cc59f5d9-59","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n    \\\"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\\\",\\n    \\\"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\\\",\\n    \\\"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Level Best\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"co-op\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n    \\\"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\\\",\\n    \\\"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\\\",\\n    \\\"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Level Best\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"co-op\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n    \\\"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\\\",\\n    \\\"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\\\",\\n    \\\"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\\\",\\n    \\\"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Level Best\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"co-op\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d5f7c267-ccf3-4dbb-a4b4-fcc5cc59f5d9-60","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,56,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,51,49,51,49,55,95,95,120,50,57,98,52,100,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,76,101,118,101,108,32,66,101,115,116,45,87,105,105,32,