{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_359","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand model() to identify existing screens and understand how pages work.\n\nThe goto function restricts navigation to most screens. It blocks dev unless the current screen is pause or dev, and it handles play specially when an id argument is provided.\n\ngoto('play') without an id simply calls setScreen('play'), which is acceptable for UI audit if model handles it.\n\nI will check model() for screens with more than six choices or small text. Dev pages, About pages, and Menu all have six choices.\n\nThe 5% margin is the safe area inside #ui. Focus outlines and button shadows may extend slightly outside #ui into that margin.\n\nFocus rings might exceed the 5% margin. At 1080p, a 6px outline plus 4px offset places the ring 10px outside #ui. I will write an audit that allows this small overflow.\n\nThe audit will flag text smaller than 30 pixels, focusable elements exceeding six, and missing focus outlines. Interactive controls must sit within the 5% inset with a small tolerance for outline overflow. The About page test will cycle through entries using ArrowRight, collect displayed text, and verify each sourceInformation value and feedback line.\n\nI need to verify how About paging works with left and right nudges.\n\nThe touch screen test loads a device, checks for the required controller prompt and one Settings button, taps Settings, and confirms the settings screen appears.\n\nFor attract mode, the director resets idle time on wake and starts attract after ten seconds when no session is active. I should confirm whether this idle logic applies to touch screens.\n\nWith render=0, the stage never initializes and setRender is never called. holdAttract stays true forever, so idle time never accumulates and attract mode never starts. The flow test runs in Node without a document, so holdAttract is false and attract works normally.\n\nThe sim attract test uses fresh(), which likely omits the document argument. For a browser UI test of touch attract mode, either render=1 is needed to trigger setRender, or holdAttract must be cleared another way. setRender is not exposed on __TEST__; it lives internally on the game object. With manual=1 the main loop never starts, so advance() calls frame() once. I need to check whether that single frame invocation actually triggers setRender.\n\nframe() does not trigger setRender because onFrame listeners only publish when a stage exists. Exposing setRender on __TEST__ is the cleanest fix for the browser attract test.\n\nI will clear the attract hold in main.js when render=0. Calling setRender with a dummy backend and zero frames releases holdAttract, allowing attract mode to start during manual browser tests.\n\nsetRender is already exposed on the returned game object, so main.js can call it directly when render=0. This fixes the attract hold without exposing internal methods. The boot screen will still clear normally because onFrame removes it once the screen changes.\n\nThe boot screen clears automatically once the frame loop runs, but holdAttract remains true until setRender fires. Calling setRender before the loop starts releases the hold immediately so idle time counts from the first frame. The node flow test does not use this path. I should be careful because setRender also sets backend and lost.\n\nThe main.js change will require a rebuild because the build may have already snapshotted that file. For the touch attract test, manual mode and advance() are used to avoid a race with the real frame loop. The test will load the Pixel 7 device context with ?test=1&render=0&manual=1, wait for __TEST__, assert the controller prompt is present, verify the Settings button exists, tap it, and confirm the settings screen appears.\n\nTapping a corner on the touch screen should leave it unchanged, since only Settings is interactive. After entering attract mode, pressing Enter will exit it and return to the coarse title or touch screen.\n\nThe pad source falls back to game.pads when window.__pads is empty, so the test can use __TEST__.key('Enter', true) to exit attract mode and advance.\n\nTapping the body at 10,10 on a touch screen should leave the screen unchanged, since only Settings is interactive. Touchscreen taps generate touch events that become click events, so tapping the Settings button will trigger activation correctly. If matchMedia does not report coarse pointer support, the screen may remain on title instead of touch, so a quick post-build playwright script will verify this behavior.\n\nI need to inspect model() to identify every screen and gather About text for the audit. SVG glyphs are 36px, but if they are path-only shapes without text nodes, the audit must account for that. The pager page indicator is 30px, which satisfies the size requirement. The boot line is 48px, so it may exceed the 5% inset margin; with manual mode, it persists until advance or frame removes it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6847355-e03b-4cb0-925c-0433b6d1ddbe-85","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function model|screen === 'about'|pages","glob":"**/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6847355-e03b-4cb0-925c-0433b6d1ddbe-86","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","offset":850,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2461,"output_tokens":2481,"cache_read_input_tokens":122240,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"42091c12-5d3e-4386-85c1-7b31ce0ff970"}
