{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_365","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A file might be one long line, causing grep path issues.\n\nThe workspace grep tool ignores node_modules. That explains why it missed the BoxGeometry import visible in the file read. The export list starts with AdditiveAnimationBlendMode.\n\nA Node ESM script will verify whether BoxGeometry is exported from three/webgpu. If it is missing, aliasing 'three' to the webgpu bundle would break RoundedBoxGeometry. Alternative fixes include using esbuild's alias or a plugin banner.\n\nThe esbuild alias should only redirect the exact 'three' import when the importer is the addon. If three and three/webgpu are separate module instances, RoundedBoxGeometry extending BoxGeometry from core while the renderer uses webgpu's BoxGeometry could cause instanceof checks to fail.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4576b161-f465-4754-9bc1-a34f60c51e3e-99","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node --input-type=module -e \"import * as T from 'three/webgpu'; console.log('rev', T.REVISION, 'box', typeof T.BoxGeometry, 'vec', typeof T.Vector3, 'color', typeof T.Color);\"","description":"Check three/webgpu exports BoxGeometry"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":386,"output_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":141952,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"f54092e8-b3d6-40c5-a50f-af6eeda2bfaf"}
