in.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/main.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"boot().catch((err) => {\\n  errors.push(String((err && err.message) || err));\\n});\",\"old_line\":119,\"new_string\":\"start().catch((err) => {\\n  errors.push(String((err && err.message) || err));\\n});\",\"new_line\":119,\"context_before\":\"fit();\\n}\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"34a311e7-eb4d-49de-9312-e5c41fa14ce2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_370","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Moving setRender before __TEST__ is visible.\n\nsetRender runs synchronously after createGame resolves. No await occurs during this path, so the browser never yields to the test's waitForFunction.\n\nThe test's waitForFunction polls on a timer, so it sees __TEST__ after setRender has already run. Rebuilding now.\n\nWriting browser tests and the launch script in parallel with the build. The launch script will use Playwright to render the HTML file and capture a pixel-accurate screenshot.\n\nThe launch script configures a 1920×1080 headless Chromium instance with sandbox disabled. It captures page and console errors, navigates to the HTML file, and waits for the canvas and title element to appear.\n\nThe waitForFunction now checks that the title reads \"Level Best\", __RENDER__ exists, and at least one frame has rendered. It then validates that the backend is WebGPU and that no context was lost. Pixel data will be captured by screenshotting the canvas element directly, since WebGPU canvases may not be readable via 2D context.\n\nThe launch script will screenshot the canvas element directly via Playwright. It must then decode the resulting PNG buffer to analyze pixels. A lightweight PNG decoder is needed, since Playwright does not include one. Options under consideration are pngjs, sharp, or a minimal custom parser.\n\nWebGPU canvases cannot be read via 2D getImageData unless preserveDrawingBuffer is enabled, so Playwright's screenshot is the correct approach. Node.js has no built-in PNG decoder, so the plan is to check for pngjs or sharp globally, or fall back to Python PIL via uv.\n\npngjs is not installed, so a Node-based PNG decoder is not viable. A JPEG screenshot was considered but rejected as too weak. The current idea is to read back pixels directly from the WebGPU canvas via WebGL2 context, though that may fail if WebGPU owns the canvas.\n\nChecking renderer.js for preserveDrawingBuffer settings. Adding a test-only readback to the renderer is extra scope. A small PNG decoder could handle Playwright's screenshot output. Python3 without PIL cannot decode PNG, but `uv run --with pillow` is permitted.\n\nA custom PNG decoder will be written directly in Node.js inside launch.mjs. It will parse the signature, inflate zlib data, and unfilter RGBA pixels using zlib.inflateSync. This avoids external dependencies like pngjs or Python tools while keeping verification as a single command.\n\nThe pixel analysis will look for dark ink and sky-blue colors, a spread of at least eight quantized colors, and a non-background bounding box. The title must read \"Level Best\". Two sequential runs will verify the screen changes after a key press. A 1280×720 viewport may be faster for software WebGPU.\n\nViewport is set to 1280×720 with deviceScaleFactor 1. Canvas width and height will be checked against the viewport multiplied by DPR. The wait for the title and first frames now uses a 45-second timeout to allow for SwiftShader shader compilation.\n\nA 1-second recheck for device loss after the first frame is needed, since bad flags lose the context at 0.2 seconds while good flags keep it alive. Page errors will be captured and saved to launch.log.\n\nThe hub test belongs in a separate file, not the launch script. A timing issue was spotted: the attract screen starts after 10 seconds, so waiting 45 seconds for GPU compilation could cause the title h1 to disappear before the screenshot is taken.\n\nThe screenshot will be taken as soon as the title appears and the first frames render, before the attract screen can start. A key press will then advance the view from title to who.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a07a7025-f9dc-46aa-be9d-51e4bc3e886d-107","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"addEventListener|keydown|pointermove","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null