{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9d69840a-a089-47fc-8f3b-d806fba0853b-129","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"330→    sun.color.setHex(pal.sun);\\n    sun.intensity = pal.sunIntensity;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sync(state) {\\n    if (!state) return;\\n    shown = state.screen;\\n    applyPalette(state.palette || 'dawn');\\n    const playing = state.screen === 'play' || state.screen === 'checkinPlay' || state.screen === 'attract';\\n    island.visible = !playing || state.screen === 'attract';\\n340→    island.rotation.z = -(state.tilt || 0);\\n    const lanes = (state.event && state.event.lanes) || [];\\n    dolls.forEach((doll, i) => {\\n      const lane = lanes[i];\\n      const show = playing ? !!lane : i === 0;\\n      doll.visible = show;\\n      if (!show) return;\\n      const x = (i - (lanes.length - 1) / 2) * (playing ? LANE_GAP * 0.35 : 0);\\n      doll.position.set(x, lane && lane.fallen ? 0.2 : 0, 0);\\n      const cob = lane && lane.cob ? lane.cob : { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n350→      doll.rotation.z = -(cob.x || 0) * 0.45;\\n      doll.rotation.x = (cob.y || 0) * 0.45;\\n      if (lane && lane.fallen) doll.rotation.z = -1.1;\\n    });\\n    const ghostList = state.ghosts || [];\\n    ghosts.forEach((doll, i) => {\\n      const g = ghostList[i];\\n      doll.visible = !!g;\\n      if (!g) return;\\n      doll.rotation.z = -(g.lx || 0) * 0.02;\\n360→      doll.rotation.x = (g.lz || 0) * 0.02;\\n      if (g.f) doll.rotation.z = -1.1;\\n    });\\n    if (state.freeCam) camera.position.set(16, 10, 20);\\n    else if (playing && state.screen !== 'attract') camera.position.set(0.2, 3.4, 8.5);\\n    else camera.position.set(9, 6.5, 16);\\n    camera.lookAt(0, playing && state.screen !== 'attract' ? 1.1 : 1.2, 0);\\n    if (trudy.userData.bubble) {\\n      trudy.userData.bubble.position.x = Math.sin(frames * 0.05) * 0.12;\\n    }\\n370→  }\\n\\n  function render(useInk = true) {\\n    const dt = Math.min(0.05, clock.getDelta());\\n    for (const doll of dolls) doll.userData.mixer.update(dt);\\n    const drift = clock.elapsedTime;\\n    clouds.forEach((cloud, i) => { cloud.position.x = -10 + ((i * 7 + drift * 0.4) % 28); });\\n    gary.position.x = Math.sin(drift * 0.3) * 3;\\n    try {\\n      if (useInk) ink.post.render();\\n380→      else renderer.render(scene, camera);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      lost = lost || (err && err.message) || 'render failed';\\n      try { renderer.render(scene, camera); } catch { /* the device is already gone */ }\\n    }\\n    frames += 1;\\n  }\\n\\n  resize(canvas.clientWidth || 1280, canvas.clientHeight || 720, 1);\\n  render(true);\\n390→\\n  return {\\n    resize, sync, render, applyPalette,\\n    info() { return { backend, lost, frames, width, height }; },\\n    setInk(on) { ink.u.boil.value = on ? 0.5 : 0; ink.u.width.value = on ? 1.4 : 0.2; },\\n    shown() { return shown; },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"330→    sun.color.setHex(pal.sun);\\n    sun.intensity = pal.sunIntensity;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sync(state) {\\n    if (!state) return;\\n    shown = state.screen;\\n    applyPalette(state.palette || 'dawn');\\n    const playing = state.screen === 'play' || state.screen === 'checkinPlay' || state.screen === 'attract';\\n    island.visible = !playing || state.screen === 'attract';\\n340→    island.rotation.z = -(state.tilt || 0);\\n    const lanes = (state.event && state.event.lanes) || [];\\n    dolls.forEach((doll, i) => {\\n      const lane = lanes[i];\\n      const show = playing ? !!lane : i === 0;\\n      doll.visible = show;\\n      if (!show) return;\\n      const x = (i - (lanes.length - 1) / 2) * (playing ? LANE_GAP * 0.35 : 0);\\n      doll.position.set(x, lane && lane.fallen ? 0.2 : 0, 0);\\n      const cob = lane && lane.cob ? lane.cob : { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n350→      doll.rotation.z = -(cob.x || 0) * 0.45;\\n      doll.rotation.x = (cob.y || 0) * 0.45;\\n      if (lane && lane.fallen) doll.rotation.z = -1.1;\\n    });\\n    const ghostList = state.ghosts || [];\\n    ghosts.forEach((doll, i) => {\\n      const g = ghostList[i];\\n      doll.visible = !!g;\\n      if (!g) return;\\n      doll.rotation.z = -(g.lx || 0) * 0.02;\\n360→      doll.rotation.x = (g.lz || 0) * 0.02;\\n      if (g.f) doll.rotation.z = -1.1;\\n    });\\n    if (state.freeCam) camera.position.set(16, 10, 20);\\n    else if (playing && state.screen !== 'attract') camera.position.set(0.2, 3.4, 8.5);\\n    else camera.position.set(9, 6.5, 16);\\n    camera.lookAt(0, playing && state.screen !== 'attract' ? 1.1 : 1.2, 0);\\n    if (trudy.userData.bubble) {\\n      trudy.userData.bubble.position.x = Math.sin(frames * 0.05) * 0.12;\\n    }\\n370→  }\\n\\n  function render(useInk = true) {\\n    const dt = Math.min(0.05, clock.getDelta());\\n    for (const doll of dolls) doll.userData.mixer.update(dt);\\n    const drift = clock.elapsedTime;\\n    clouds.forEach((cloud, i) => { cloud.position.x = -10 + ((i * 7 + drift * 0.4) % 28); });\\n    gary.position.x = Math.sin(drift * 0.3) * 3;\\n    try {\\n      if (useInk) ink.post.render();\\n380→      else renderer.render(scene, camera);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      lost = lost || (err && err.message) || 'render failed';\\n      try { renderer.render(scene, camera); } catch { /* the device is already gone */ }\\n    }\\n    frames += 1;\\n  }\\n\\n  resize(canvas.clientWidth || 1280, canvas.clientHeight || 720, 1);\\n  render(true);\\n390→\\n  return {\\n    resize, sync, render, applyPalette,\\n    info() { return { backend, lost, frames, width, height }; },\\n    setInk(on) { ink.u.boil.value = on ? 0.5 : 0; ink.u.width.value = on ? 1.4 : 0.2; },\\n    shown() { return shown; },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/render/renderer.js\",\"offset\":330,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"    sun.color.setHex(pal.sun);\\n    sun.intensity = pal.sunIntensity;\\n  }\\n\\n  function sync(state) {\\n    if (!state) return;\\n    shown = state.screen;\\n    applyPalette(state.palette || 'dawn');\\n    const playing = state.screen === 'play' || state.screen === 'checkinPlay' || state.screen === 'attract';\\n    island.visible = !playing || state.screen === 'attract';\\n    island.rotation.z = -(state.tilt || 0);\\n    const lanes = (state.event && state.event.lanes) || [];\\n    dolls.forEach((doll, i) => {\\n      const lane = lanes[i];\\n      const show = playing ? !!lane : i === 0;\\n      doll.visible = show;\\n      if (!show) return;\\n      const x = (i - (lanes.length - 1) / 2) * (playing ? LANE_GAP * 0.35 : 0);\\n      doll.position.set(x, lane && lane.fallen ? 0.2 : 0, 0);\\n      const cob = lane && lane.cob ? lane.cob : { x: 0, y: 0 };\\n      doll.rotation.z = -(cob.x || 0) * 0.45;\\n      doll.rotation.x = (cob.y || 0) * 0.45;\\n      if (lane && lane.fallen) doll.rotation.z = -1.1;\\n    });\\n    const ghostList = state.ghosts || [];\\n    ghosts.forEach((doll, i) => {\\n      const g = ghostList[i];\\n      doll.visible = !!g;\\n      if (!g) return;\\n      doll.rotation.z = -(g.lx || 0) * 0.02;\\n      doll.rotation.x = (g.lz || 0) * 0.02;\\n      if (g.f) doll.rotation.z = -1.1;\\n    });\\n    if (state.freeCam) camera.position.set(16, 10, 20);\\n    else if (playing && state.screen !== 'attract') camera.position.set(0.2, 3.4, 8.5);\\n    else camera.position.set(9, 6.5, 16);\\n    camera.lookAt(0, playing && state.screen !== 'attract' ? 1.1 : 1.2, 0);\\n    if (trudy.userData.bubble) {\\n      trudy.userData.bubble.position.x = Math.sin(frames * 0.05) * 0.12;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function render(useInk = true) {\\n    const dt = Math.min(0.05, clock.getDelta());\\n    for (const doll of dolls) doll.userData.mixer.update(dt);\\n    const drift = clock.elapsedTime;\\n    clouds.forEach((cloud, i) => { cloud.position.x = -10 + ((i * 7 + drift * 0.4) % 28); });\\n    gary.position.x = Math.sin(drift * 0.3) * 3;\\n    try {\\n      if (useInk) ink.post.render();\\n      else renderer.render(scene, camera);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      lost = lost || (err && err.message) || 'render failed';\\n      try { renderer.render(scene, camera); } catch { /* the device is already gone */ }\\n    }\\n    frames += 1;\\n  }\\n\\n  resize(canvas.clientWidth || 1280, canvas.clientHeight || 720, 1);\\n  render(true);\\n\\n  return {\\n    resize, sync, render, applyPalette,\\n    info() { return { backend, lost, frames, width, height }; },\\n    setInk(on) { ink.u.boil.value = on ? 0.5 : 0; ink.u.width.value = on ? 1.4 : 0.2; },\\n    shown() { return shown; },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":397}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"1e1f1e9f-4d85-46e0-9d34-2683b9825b82"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_390","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"createStage calls render once at the end, so frames is already at least 1 when info() is first published, even before the loop begins.\n\nIf the first render throws, lost is set and the launch fails. holdAttract clears after publish sets render on the first stage info, which happens after createStage returns. The game loop runs during createStage because runStandalone starts before awaiting the stage promise.\n\nThe title stays protected during GPU initialization while holdAttract remains active. Launch captures the frame as soon as __RENDER__ appears. Now writing files and building. Browser audio imports from source are acceptable.\n\nlaunch.mjs will be runnable directly as `node tools/launch.mjs` and export runLaunches for reuse. The hub test writes hub.log to scratch so the four scenario results are captured even when run via test.mjs.\n\nThe scratch path will be hardcoded at the top of browser.mjs and launch.mjs so proof files land in the correct run directory regardless of the runner's working directory. Failing checks will be appended to hub.log.\n\nA lightweight PNG decoder is being implemented using node:zlib to parse image headers and extract dimensions.\n\nThe PNG decoder now extracts width, height, bit depth, and color type from the IHDR chunk. It concatenates IDAT chunks and inflates them with zlib. The code allocates a 32-bit output buffer and begins scanning raw scanlines to apply PNG filters.\n\nThe decoder now applies PNG filter types 1 through 4 to each scanline. It reconstructs pixel values from the raw buffer using left, upper, and upper-left neighbors for adaptive filtering.\n\nThe decoder now implements the Paeth predictor for PNG filter type 4. It correctly reads the left neighbor from already-unfiltered bytes while scanning left to right.\n\nThe PNG decoder now copies filtered scanlines into the output buffer. A bug was found in the Paeth predictor: the absolute differences were computed incorrectly. The standard formula is being applied instead.\n\nA `paintStats` helper is being written to analyze captured images. It counts colored, dark, and bright pixels, records unique color buckets, and computes pixel spread.\n\nThe paintStats helper now counts colored, dark, and bright pixels. It computes bounding box dimensions from the painted region. The pass criteria require at least six distinct color buckets, more than thirty percent colored pixels, over fifty dark and bright pixels each, and a bounding box covering more than half the image width and height.\n\nThe hub test will press Enter and wait for the body dataset screen attribute to change from title or attract. This confirms the game loop is running and the key press is being processed.\n\nThe next frame poll should see the Enter key press and activate Begin, switching the screen to who with a fresh profile. The data-screen attribute updates during paint within 100 ms. The capture happens before the ten-second attract timeout, so the screen should still be title. Page errors will also be checked; Rapier deprecation warnings are console.warn, but WebGPU warnings may appear as errors.\n\nPage errors and console errors will be collected. Page errors and Device Lost messages count as failures. Other console errors are logged unless they look like exceptions. Canvas width and height must match the viewport scaled by DPR. The renderer stores these values, and publish copies them from stage.info().\n\nThe canvas may report zero width before layout completes, so the resize fallback defaults to 1280. After the stage promise resolves, main.js calls fit() to set the drawing size from innerWidth.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dbc9757a-7dcc-4dcf-883a-4f37ec951cd7-130","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function resize|width =","glob":"**/renderer.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1279,"output_tokens":2654,"cache_read_input_tokens":167936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"4b082289-4d9e-4c60-95f9-4e5718c0c175"}
