{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_406","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Burst uses noise filtered through a filter.","signature":"Ggnb9LikIFMFNXsG3iibyftJr+u49pl5SNVqIBX23GN4x486VhE5cqaliAniyc1P0F0QuCRfE6mMFube3iZXldoXIsw6s3tO5SMx+YkiEHC6DYhhUMcqAUuYuXwqj797igTeAXfH6Lc/c6+M8BPmxoY2IIAp1isGQppmgEp+TRNGkZPgpMPasaSYr6xrFJUs5zK00o4"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1eeae09b-440e-48d9-9d3b-ce73d2af97c6-155","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/audio/sfx.js","offset":1,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":548,"output_tokens":120,"cache_read_input_tokens":193280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"9c91ba7a-9f31-41ff-b430-b787bb3ba96d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1eeae09b-440e-48d9-9d3b-ce73d2af97c6-155","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Short effects. Variation comes from the caller. */\\n\\nimport { woodblock } from './instruments.js';\\n\\nfunction noise(ctx, seconds) {\\n  const buffer = ctx.createBuffer(1, Math.max(1, Math.floor(ctx.sampleRate * seconds)), ctx.sampleRate);\\n  const data = buffer.getChannelData(0);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) data[i] = Math.sin(i * 0.37 + (i % 13)) * ((i * 17) % 9) / 9;\\n  const src = ctx.createBufferSource();\\n10→  src.buffer = buffer;\\n  return src;\\n}\\n\\nfunction burst(ctx, dest, t, seconds, freq, amp, type = 'bandpass') {\\n  const src = noise(ctx, seconds);\\n  const filter = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n  filter.type = type;\\n  filter.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq, t);\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n20→  g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(amp, t + 0.01);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + seconds);\\n  src.connect(filter); filter.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  src.start(t); src.stop(t + seconds + 0.02);\\n}\\n\\nexport function woodClack(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.4) {\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.08, 1400, amp);\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t + 0.03, 0.06, 900, amp * 0.5);\\n30→  burst(ctx, dest, t + 0.05, 0.05, 1800, amp * 0.3);\\n}\\n\\nexport function toySpring(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.3) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.type = 'sine';\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(220, t);\\n  o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(880, t + 0.25);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(amp, t);\\n40→  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.3);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.32);\\n}\\n\\nexport function splash(ctx, dest, t, big = false) {\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t, big ? 0.6 : 0.25, big ? 500 : 1400, big ? 0.55 : 0.3, 'lowpass');\\n}\\n\\nexport function marble(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.25) {\\n50→  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.type = 'sine';\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(1400 + (t * 100) % 400, t);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(amp, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.12);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.14);\\n}\\n\\n60→export function plateHum(ctx, dest, t, speed = 6) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(180 + speed * 40, t);\\n  g.gain.value = 0.08;\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.4);\\n}\\n\\nexport function plateCrash(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.35, 2200, 0.45); }\\n70→export function fruitThud(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.12, 180, 0.4, 'lowpass'); }\\nexport function urchin(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.1, 2400, 0.35); }\\nexport function whistle(ctx, dest, t) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(1400, t);\\n  o.frequency.linearRampToValueAtTime(1800, t + 0.15);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.2, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.3);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n80→  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.32);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Short effects. Variation comes from the caller. */\\n\\nimport { woodblock } from './instruments.js';\\n\\nfunction noise(ctx, seconds) {\\n  const buffer = ctx.createBuffer(1, Math.max(1, Math.floor(ctx.sampleRate * seconds)), ctx.sampleRate);\\n  const data = buffer.getChannelData(0);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) data[i] = Math.sin(i * 0.37 + (i % 13)) * ((i * 17) % 9) / 9;\\n  const src = ctx.createBufferSource();\\n10→  src.buffer = buffer;\\n  return src;\\n}\\n\\nfunction burst(ctx, dest, t, seconds, freq, amp, type = 'bandpass') {\\n  const src = noise(ctx, seconds);\\n  const filter = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n  filter.type = type;\\n  filter.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq, t);\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n20→  g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(amp, t + 0.01);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + seconds);\\n  src.connect(filter); filter.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  src.start(t); src.stop(t + seconds + 0.02);\\n}\\n\\nexport function woodClack(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.4) {\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.08, 1400, amp);\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t + 0.03, 0.06, 900, amp * 0.5);\\n30→  burst(ctx, dest, t + 0.05, 0.05, 1800, amp * 0.3);\\n}\\n\\nexport function toySpring(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.3) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.type = 'sine';\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(220, t);\\n  o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(880, t + 0.25);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(amp, t);\\n40→  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.3);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.32);\\n}\\n\\nexport function splash(ctx, dest, t, big = false) {\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t, big ? 0.6 : 0.25, big ? 500 : 1400, big ? 0.55 : 0.3, 'lowpass');\\n}\\n\\nexport function marble(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.25) {\\n50→  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.type = 'sine';\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(1400 + (t * 100) % 400, t);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(amp, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.12);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.14);\\n}\\n\\n60→export function plateHum(ctx, dest, t, speed = 6) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(180 + speed * 40, t);\\n  g.gain.value = 0.08;\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.4);\\n}\\n\\nexport function plateCrash(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.35, 2200, 0.45); }\\n70→export function fruitThud(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.12, 180, 0.4, 'lowpass'); }\\nexport function urchin(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.1, 2400, 0.35); }\\nexport function whistle(ctx, dest, t) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(1400, t);\\n  o.frequency.linearRampToValueAtTime(1800, t + 0.15);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.2, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.3);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n80→  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.32);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/audio/sfx.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/** Short effects. Variation comes from the caller. */\\n\\nimport { woodblock } from './instruments.js';\\n\\nfunction noise(ctx, seconds) {\\n  const buffer = ctx.createBuffer(1, Math.max(1, Math.floor(ctx.sampleRate * seconds)), ctx.sampleRate);\\n  const data = buffer.getChannelData(0);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) data[i] = Math.sin(i * 0.37 + (i % 13)) * ((i * 17) % 9) / 9;\\n  const src = ctx.createBufferSource();\\n  src.buffer = buffer;\\n  return src;\\n}\\n\\nfunction burst(ctx, dest, t, seconds, freq, amp, type = 'bandpass') {\\n  const src = noise(ctx, seconds);\\n  const filter = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n  filter.type = type;\\n  filter.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq, t);\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(amp, t + 0.01);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + seconds);\\n  src.connect(filter); filter.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  src.start(t); src.stop(t + seconds + 0.02);\\n}\\n\\nexport function woodClack(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.4) {\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.08, 1400, amp);\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t + 0.03, 0.06, 900, amp * 0.5);\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t + 0.05, 0.05, 1800, amp * 0.3);\\n}\\n\\nexport function toySpring(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.3) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.type = 'sine';\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(220, t);\\n  o.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(880, t + 0.25);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(amp, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.3);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.32);\\n}\\n\\nexport function splash(ctx, dest, t, big = false) {\\n  burst(ctx, dest, t, big ? 0.6 : 0.25, big ? 500 : 1400, big ? 0.55 : 0.3, 'lowpass');\\n}\\n\\nexport function marble(ctx, dest, t, amp = 0.25) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.type = 'sine';\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(1400 + (t * 100) % 400, t);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(amp, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.12);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.14);\\n}\\n\\nexport function plateHum(ctx, dest, t, speed = 6) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(180 + speed * 40, t);\\n  g.gain.value = 0.08;\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.4);\\n}\\n\\nexport function plateCrash(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.35, 2200, 0.45); }\\nexport function fruitThud(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.12, 180, 0.4, 'lowpass'); }\\nexport function urchin(ctx, dest, t) { burst(ctx, dest, t, 0.1, 2400, 0.35); }\\nexport function whistle(ctx, dest, t) {\\n  const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n  const g = ctx.createGain();\\n  o.frequency.setValueAtTime(1400, t);\\n  o.frequency.linearRampToValueAtTime(1800, t + 0.15);\\n  g.gain.setValueAtTime(0.2, t);\\n  g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.3);\\n  o.connect(g); g.connect(dest);\\n  o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.32);\\n\",\"total_lines\":122}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"b617019d-d8c9-4de3-a95e-479985747bd1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_407","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The noise samples are roughly between -1 and 1.\n\nThe 180Hz lowpass filter kills most of the high-frequency noise energy. This leaves only a tiny residual and explains the near-zero peak. The fix is to mix in slower low-frequency sine waves so the filtered thud remains audible.\n\nA 0.02 rad/sample sine wave at roughly 140 Hz will pass the 180 Hz lowpass cleanly. The new noise mix uses a 0.65 amplitude slow sine plus the original high-frequency noise at 0.35. This should produce a peak near 0.4 after the 0.4 gain amp.\n\nThe RMS estimate is roughly 0.12, well above the 0.0008 floor. The biquad lowpass has a default Q of 1, so clipping should be avoided. Splash passed because its 1400 Hz cutoff lets more high-frequency energy through than the 180 Hz thud filter. Adding a slow sine to all noise samples might affect woodClack bandpass levels.\n\nThe slow sine is rejected by the 1400 Hz bandpass, so woodClack is unaffected. Splash and plateCrash are also safe because their filters block the low frequency. The RMS floor will be lowered to 0.001.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-70e8cfef-6303-416f-8e13-3567a45343a6-156","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/audio/sfx.js","old_string":"  for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) data[i] = Math.sin(i * 0.37 + (i % 13)) * ((i * 17) % 9) / 9;","new_string":"  for (let i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {\n    const low = Math.sin(i * 0.02) * 0.55;\n    const grit = Math.sin(i * 0.37 + (i % 13)) * 0.35;\n    data[i] = low + grit;\n  }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1270,"output_tokens":1104,"cache_read_input_tokens":193792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"c76fee6d-3ca9-4f1c-8fc5-a3509b61d79f"}
