{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_438","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title screen looks good. It features a wooden toy island, ink outlines, the Level Best title, a tagline, a Begin button with a focus ring, and PlayStation glyphs.\n\nBoth launches match. The lighthouse and character look odd but are acceptable. Hub tests will run alone to avoid CPU contention with node simulations. The hub needs a long blocking run for four scenarios.\n\nHub will run in the background with block_until_ms set to zero. I'll draft the exit interview and review requirements while it runs. The interview counts depend on the full test results.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/test/browser.mjs","offset":1,"limit":160}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-42","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-43","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317\" && node tools/test.mjs hub","description":"Run hub harness scenarios","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3454,"output_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":83456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"e96514e7-78a4-4846-bb16-9432ce8c0157"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { chromium, devices } from 'playwright';\\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync, mkdirSync, existsSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport { TRACKS, STINGS } from '../src/audio/tracks.js';\\nimport { SFX } from '../src/audio/sfx.js';\\nimport { VOICES } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\n\\n10→const root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\\nconst work = path.resolve(root, '..');\\nconst htmlName = 'Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317.html';\\nconst htmlPath = path.join(work, htmlName);\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer';\\nconst RENDER = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n20→  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n  '--no-sandbox',\\n  '--disable-dev-shm-usage',\\n  '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required',\\n];\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, message) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(message || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n\\n30→function fileUrl(query) {\\n  return `file://${htmlPath}${query || ''}`;\\n}\\n\\nasync function openLogic(browser, query, contextOptions = {}) {\\n  const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1, ...contextOptions });\\n  const page = await context.newPage();\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err.message || err)));\\n  await page.goto(fileUrl(query));\\n40→  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__TEST__, null, { timeout: 30000 });\\n  return { context, page, errors };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function audioTests() {\\n  const tests = [];\\n  tests.push(['music bus is 0.10 and offline renders stay finite', async () => {\\n    assert(existsSync(htmlPath), 'built HTML is missing');\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-dev-shm-usage', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'] });\\n    try {\\n50→      const { context, page, errors } = await openLogic(browser, '?test=1&render=0&manual=1');\\n      const state = await page.evaluate(() => window.__TEST__.state());\\n      assert(Math.abs(state.audio.music - 0.1) < 0.001, `music ${state.audio.music}`);\\n      assert(state.detune === 0, `detune ${state.detune}`);\\n      const jobs = [\\n        ...Object.keys(TRACKS).map((id) => ['track', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(STINGS).map((id) => ['sting', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(SFX).map((id) => ['sfx', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(VOICES).map((id) => ['voice', id]),\\n      ];\\n60→      const failed = [];\\n      for (const [kind, id] of jobs) {\\n        const probe = await page.evaluate(([k, name]) => window.__TEST__.probe(k, name), [kind, id]);\\n        if (!probe.finite || probe.clipped || !(probe.rms > 0.0008)) failed.push(`${kind}:${id} peak=${probe.peak} rms=${probe.rms}`);\\n      }\\n      assert(failed.length === 0, failed.join('; '));\\n      assert(errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\\n      await context.close();\\n    } finally {\\n      await browser.close();\\n70→    }\\n  }]);\\n  return tests;\\n}\\n\\nfunction serveWork() {\\n  const server = createServer((req, res) => {\\n    const url = new URL(req.url, 'http://127.0.0.1');\\n    const rel = decodeURIComponent(url.pathname);\\n    const file = path.resolve(work, `.${rel}`);\\n80→    if (!file.startsWith(work)) {\\n      res.writeHead(403);\\n      res.end('no');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      const data = readFileSync(file);\\n      const ext = path.extname(file);\\n      const type = ext === '.html' ? 'text/html; charset=utf-8'\\n        : ext === '.js' || ext === '.mjs' ? 'text/javascript; charset=utf-8'\\n90→          : 'application/octet-stream';\\n      res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': type, 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\\n      res.end(data);\\n    } catch {\\n      res.writeHead(404);\\n      res.end('missing');\\n    }\\n  });\\n  return new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => resolve(server)));\\n}\\n100→\\nasync function hubScenario(browser, origin, query) {\\n  const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n  const page = await context.newPage();\\n  const folder = 'Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317';\\n  const game = `/${htmlName}`;\\n  const harness = `/${folder}/tools/hub/harness.html?game=${encodeURIComponent(game)}&auto=1&${query}`;\\n  await page.goto(`${origin}${harness}`);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\\n  const report = await page.evaluate(() => window.__hubCheck);\\n110→  await context.close();\\n  return report;\\n}\\n\\nexport async function hubTests() {\\n  const tests = [];\\n  tests.push(['hub harness passes 1, 2, 4 and host-leave, and the page plays alone', async () => {\\n    assert(existsSync(htmlPath), 'built HTML is missing');\\n    const server = await serveWork();\\n    const address = server.address();\\n120→    const origin = `http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}`;\\n    mkdirSync(scratch, { recursive: true });\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: RENDER });\\n    const log = [];\\n    try {\\n      const probe = await fetch(`${origin}/${htmlName}`);\\n      const text = await probe.text();\\n      assert(text.includes('Level Best'), 'served page is not the game');\\n      assert(text.includes('hub:session'), 'served page has no hub meta');\\n      const scenarios = ['players=1', 'players=2', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave'];\\n130→      for (const query of scenarios) {\\n        const report = await hubScenario(browser, origin, query);\\n        const bad = (report.checks || []).filter((check) => !check.pass);\\n        log.push(`${query} pass=${report.pass} ${bad.map((check) => `${check.name}: ${check.detail}`).join(' | ')}`);\\n        assert(report.pass === true, `${query} ${bad.map((check) => check.name + ' ' + check.detail).join('; ')}`);\\n      }\\n      const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n      const page = await context.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err.message || err)));\\n140→      await page.goto(fileUrl(''));\\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__RENDER__ && window.__RENDER__.frames > 0 && !window.__RENDER__.lost, null, { timeout: 90000 });\\n      for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\\n        await page.keyboard.press(key);\\n        await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n      }\\n      const drawn = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const render = window.__RENDER__;\\n        return { screen: document.body.dataset.screen, frames: render.frames, lost: render.lost, active: !!(window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active) };\\n      });\\n150→      assert(drawn.frames > 0 && !drawn.lost, `not drawn ${JSON.stringify(drawn)}`);\\n      assert(drawn.active === false, 'session active outside the hub');\\n      assert(errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\\n      log.push(`solo ${JSON.stringify(drawn)} errors=${errors.length}`);\\n      await context.close();\\n    } finally {\\n      writeFileSync(path.join(scratch, 'hub.log'), log.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n');\\n      await browser.close();\\n      await new Promise((resolve) => server.close(resolve));\\n    }\\n160→  }]);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { chromium, devices } from 'playwright';\\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync, mkdirSync, existsSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport { TRACKS, STINGS } from '../src/audio/tracks.js';\\nimport { SFX } from '../src/audio/sfx.js';\\nimport { VOICES } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\n\\n10→const root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\\nconst work = path.resolve(root, '..');\\nconst htmlName = 'Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317.html';\\nconst htmlPath = path.join(work, htmlName);\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer';\\nconst RENDER = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n20→  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n  '--no-sandbox',\\n  '--disable-dev-shm-usage',\\n  '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required',\\n];\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, message) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(message || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n\\n30→function fileUrl(query) {\\n  return `file://${htmlPath}${query || ''}`;\\n}\\n\\nasync function openLogic(browser, query, contextOptions = {}) {\\n  const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1, ...contextOptions });\\n  const page = await context.newPage();\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err.message || err)));\\n  await page.goto(fileUrl(query));\\n40→  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__TEST__, null, { timeout: 30000 });\\n  return { context, page, errors };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function audioTests() {\\n  const tests = [];\\n  tests.push(['music bus is 0.10 and offline renders stay finite', async () => {\\n    assert(existsSync(htmlPath), 'built HTML is missing');\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-dev-shm-usage', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'] });\\n    try {\\n50→      const { context, page, errors } = await openLogic(browser, '?test=1&render=0&manual=1');\\n      const state = await page.evaluate(() => window.__TEST__.state());\\n      assert(Math.abs(state.audio.music - 0.1) < 0.001, `music ${state.audio.music}`);\\n      assert(state.detune === 0, `detune ${state.detune}`);\\n      const jobs = [\\n        ...Object.keys(TRACKS).map((id) => ['track', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(STINGS).map((id) => ['sting', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(SFX).map((id) => ['sfx', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(VOICES).map((id) => ['voice', id]),\\n      ];\\n60→      const failed = [];\\n      for (const [kind, id] of jobs) {\\n        const probe = await page.evaluate(([k, name]) => window.__TEST__.probe(k, name), [kind, id]);\\n        if (!probe.finite || probe.clipped || !(probe.rms > 0.0008)) failed.push(`${kind}:${id} peak=${probe.peak} rms=${probe.rms}`);\\n      }\\n      assert(failed.length === 0, failed.join('; '));\\n      assert(errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\\n      await context.close();\\n    } finally {\\n      await browser.close();\\n70→    }\\n  }]);\\n  return tests;\\n}\\n\\nfunction serveWork() {\\n  const server = createServer((req, res) => {\\n    const url = new URL(req.url, 'http://127.0.0.1');\\n    const rel = decodeURIComponent(url.pathname);\\n    const file = path.resolve(work, `.${rel}`);\\n80→    if (!file.startsWith(work)) {\\n      res.writeHead(403);\\n      res.end('no');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      const data = readFileSync(file);\\n      const ext = path.extname(file);\\n      const type = ext === '.html' ? 'text/html; charset=utf-8'\\n        : ext === '.js' || ext === '.mjs' ? 'text/javascript; charset=utf-8'\\n90→          : 'application/octet-stream';\\n      res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': type, 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\\n      res.end(data);\\n    } catch {\\n      res.writeHead(404);\\n      res.end('missing');\\n    }\\n  });\\n  return new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => resolve(server)));\\n}\\n100→\\nasync function hubScenario(browser, origin, query) {\\n  const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n  const page = await context.newPage();\\n  const folder = 'Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317';\\n  const game = `/${htmlName}`;\\n  const harness = `/${folder}/tools/hub/harness.html?game=${encodeURIComponent(game)}&auto=1&${query}`;\\n  await page.goto(`${origin}${harness}`);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\\n  const report = await page.evaluate(() => window.__hubCheck);\\n110→  await context.close();\\n  return report;\\n}\\n\\nexport async function hubTests() {\\n  const tests = [];\\n  tests.push(['hub harness passes 1, 2, 4 and host-leave, and the page plays alone', async () => {\\n    assert(existsSync(htmlPath), 'built HTML is missing');\\n    const server = await serveWork();\\n    const address = server.address();\\n120→    const origin = `http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}`;\\n    mkdirSync(scratch, { recursive: true });\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: RENDER });\\n    const log = [];\\n    try {\\n      const probe = await fetch(`${origin}/${htmlName}`);\\n      const text = await probe.text();\\n      assert(text.includes('Level Best'), 'served page is not the game');\\n      assert(text.includes('hub:session'), 'served page has no hub meta');\\n      const scenarios = ['players=1', 'players=2', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave'];\\n130→      for (const query of scenarios) {\\n        const report = await hubScenario(browser, origin, query);\\n        const bad = (report.checks || []).filter((check) => !check.pass);\\n        log.push(`${query} pass=${report.pass} ${bad.map((check) => `${check.name}: ${check.detail}`).join(' | ')}`);\\n        assert(report.pass === true, `${query} ${bad.map((check) => check.name + ' ' + check.detail).join('; ')}`);\\n      }\\n      const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n      const page = await context.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err.message || err)));\\n140→      await page.goto(fileUrl(''));\\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__RENDER__ && window.__RENDER__.frames > 0 && !window.__RENDER__.lost, null, { timeout: 90000 });\\n      for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\\n        await page.keyboard.press(key);\\n        await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n      }\\n      const drawn = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const render = window.__RENDER__;\\n        return { screen: document.body.dataset.screen, frames: render.frames, lost: render.lost, active: !!(window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active) };\\n      });\\n150→      assert(drawn.frames > 0 && !drawn.lost, `not drawn ${JSON.stringify(drawn)}`);\\n      assert(drawn.active === false, 'session active outside the hub');\\n      assert(errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\\n      log.push(`solo ${JSON.stringify(drawn)} errors=${errors.length}`);\\n      await context.close();\\n    } finally {\\n      writeFileSync(path.join(scratch, 'hub.log'), log.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n');\\n      await browser.close();\\n      await new Promise((resolve) => server.close(resolve));\\n    }\\n160→  }]);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/test/browser.mjs\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"import { chromium, devices } from 'playwright';\\nimport { createServer } from 'node:http';\\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync, mkdirSync, existsSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport { TRACKS, STINGS } from '../src/audio/tracks.js';\\nimport { SFX } from '../src/audio/sfx.js';\\nimport { VOICES } from '../src/audio/voice.js';\\n\\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\\nconst work = path.resolve(root, '..');\\nconst htmlName = 'Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317.html';\\nconst htmlPath = path.join(work, htmlName);\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer';\\nconst RENDER = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n  '--no-sandbox',\\n  '--disable-dev-shm-usage',\\n  '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required',\\n];\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, message) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(message || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n\\nfunction fileUrl(query) {\\n  return `file://${htmlPath}${query || ''}`;\\n}\\n\\nasync function openLogic(browser, query, contextOptions = {}) {\\n  const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1, ...contextOptions });\\n  const page = await context.newPage();\\n  const errors = [];\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err.message || err)));\\n  await page.goto(fileUrl(query));\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__TEST__, null, { timeout: 30000 });\\n  return { context, page, errors };\\n}\\n\\nexport async function audioTests() {\\n  const tests = [];\\n  tests.push(['music bus is 0.10 and offline renders stay finite', async () => {\\n    assert(existsSync(htmlPath), 'built HTML is missing');\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: ['--no-sandbox', '--disable-dev-shm-usage', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'] });\\n    try {\\n      const { context, page, errors } = await openLogic(browser, '?test=1&render=0&manual=1');\\n      const state = await page.evaluate(() => window.__TEST__.state());\\n      assert(Math.abs(state.audio.music - 0.1) < 0.001, `music ${state.audio.music}`);\\n      assert(state.detune === 0, `detune ${state.detune}`);\\n      const jobs = [\\n        ...Object.keys(TRACKS).map((id) => ['track', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(STINGS).map((id) => ['sting', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(SFX).map((id) => ['sfx', id]),\\n        ...Object.keys(VOICES).map((id) => ['voice', id]),\\n      ];\\n      const failed = [];\\n      for (const [kind, id] of jobs) {\\n        const probe = await page.evaluate(([k, name]) => window.__TEST__.probe(k, name), [kind, id]);\\n        if (!probe.finite || probe.clipped || !(probe.rms > 0.0008)) failed.push(`${kind}:${id} peak=${probe.peak} rms=${probe.rms}`);\\n      }\\n      assert(failed.length === 0, failed.join('; '));\\n      assert(errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\\n      await context.close();\\n    } finally {\\n      await browser.close();\\n    }\\n  }]);\\n  return tests;\\n}\\n\\nfunction serveWork() {\\n  const server = createServer((req, res) => {\\n    const url = new URL(req.url, 'http://127.0.0.1');\\n    const rel = decodeURIComponent(url.pathname);\\n    const file = path.resolve(work, `.${rel}`);\\n    if (!file.startsWith(work)) {\\n      res.writeHead(403);\\n      res.end('no');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      const data = readFileSync(file);\\n      const ext = path.extname(file);\\n      const type = ext === '.html' ? 'text/html; charset=utf-8'\\n        : ext === '.js' || ext === '.mjs' ? 'text/javascript; charset=utf-8'\\n          : 'application/octet-stream';\\n      res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': type, 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\\n      res.end(data);\\n    } catch {\\n      res.writeHead(404);\\n      res.end('missing');\\n    }\\n  });\\n  return new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => resolve(server)));\\n}\\n\\nasync function hubScenario(browser, origin, query) {\\n  const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n  const page = await context.newPage();\\n  const folder = 'Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317';\\n  const game = `/${htmlName}`;\\n  const harness = `/${folder}/tools/hub/harness.html?game=${encodeURIComponent(game)}&auto=1&${query}`;\\n  await page.goto(`${origin}${harness}`);\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 180000 });\\n  const report = await page.evaluate(() => window.__hubCheck);\\n  await context.close();\\n  return report;\\n}\\n\\nexport async function hubTests() {\\n  const tests = [];\\n  tests.push(['hub harness passes 1, 2, 4 and host-leave, and the page plays alone', async () => {\\n    assert(existsSync(htmlPath), 'built HTML is missing');\\n    const server = await serveWork();\\n    const address = server.address();\\n    const origin = `http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}`;\\n    mkdirSync(scratch, { recursive: true });\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: RENDER });\\n    const log = [];\\n    try {\\n      const probe = await fetch(`${origin}/${htmlName}`);\\n      const text = await probe.text();\\n      assert(text.includes('Level Best'), 'served page is not the game');\\n      assert(text.includes('hub:session'), 'served page has no hub meta');\\n      const scenarios = ['players=1', 'players=2', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave'];\\n      for (const query of scenarios) {\\n        const report = await hubScenario(browser, origin, query);\\n        const bad = (report.checks || []).filter((check) => !check.pass);\\n        log.push(`${query} pass=${report.pass} ${bad.map((check) => `${check.name}: ${check.detail}`).join(' | ')}`);\\n        assert(report.pass === true, `${query} ${bad.map((check) => check.name + ' ' + check.detail).join('; ')}`);\\n      }\\n      const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 }, deviceScaleFactor: 1 });\\n      const page = await context.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err.message || err)));\\n      await page.goto(fileUrl(''));\\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__RENDER__ && window.__RENDER__.frames > 0 && !window.__RENDER__.lost, null, { timeout: 90000 });\\n      for (const key of ['Enter', 'Space', 'Enter', 'Space']) {\\n        await page.keyboard.press(key);\\n        await page.waitForTimeout(200);\\n      }\\n      const drawn = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const render = window.__RENDER__;\\n        return { screen: document.body.dataset.screen, frames: render.frames, lost: render.lost, active: !!(window.AIHub && window.AIHub.active) };\\n      });\\n      assert(drawn.frames > 0 && !drawn.lost, `not drawn ${JSON.stringify(drawn)}`);\\n      assert(drawn.active === false, 'session active outside the hub');\\n      assert(errors.length === 0, errors.join('; '));\\n      log.push(`solo ${JSON.stringify(drawn)} errors=${errors.length}`);\\n      await context.close();\\n    } finally {\\n      writeFileSync(path.join(scratch, 'hub.log'), log.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n');\\n      await browser.close();\\n      await new Promise((resolve) => server.close(resolve));\\n    }\\n  }]);\\n\",\"total_lines\":290}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-42","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Issues caught while building Level Best\\n\\n1. Log Reps counted a phantom first rep because `lastRep` was undefined. Critical: no. The score started a rep early.\\n2. Plank & Perch could spawn a second ragdoll for one fall. Critical: yes. A second removal in the same step panics Rapier for the whole page.\\n3. Island Loop scored cadence from `t % period` and wrote tilted gravity into the world. Critical: yes. A sharp jog scored 26, and the gravity write produced NaN.\\n4. Plate Spinners' bot left the band it was supposed to hold. Critical: yes. A sharp bot scored about 47 instead of a full spin.\\n5. Room Service built the tray with full extents and lost glasses that were still on it. Critical: yes. The order could not be delivered.\\n6. Tippy Raft ignored the lane's skill and the grip that keeps a sharp player near the middle. Critical: no. Rounds still ended, but skill did not matter.\\n7. Check-in leaned the doll toward the wrong side of the target. Critical: yes. The Wobble Age came out of the wrong mean.\\n10→8. Check-in applied the calm margin twice. Critical: no. The stand test was stricter than the written one, but the day still finished.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Issues caught while building Level Best\\n\\n1. Log Reps counted a phantom first rep because `lastRep` was undefined. Critical: no. The score started a rep early.\\n2. Plank & Perch could spawn a second ragdoll for one fall. Critical: yes. A second removal in the same step panics Rapier for the whole page.\\n3. Island Loop scored cadence from `t % period` and wrote tilted gravity into the world. Critical: yes. A sharp jog scored 26, and the gravity write produced NaN.\\n4. Plate Spinners' bot left the band it was supposed to hold. Critical: yes. A sharp bot scored about 47 instead of a full spin.\\n5. Room Service built the tray with full extents and lost glasses that were still on it. Critical: yes. The order could not be delivered.\\n6. Tippy Raft ignored the lane's skill and the grip that keeps a sharp player near the middle. Critical: no. Rounds still ended, but skill did not matter.\\n7. Check-in leaned the doll toward the wrong side of the target. Critical: yes. The Wobble Age came out of the wrong mean.\\n10→8. Check-in applied the calm margin twice. Critical: no. The stand test was stricter than the written one, but the day still finished.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Issues caught while building Level Best\\n\\n1. Log Reps counted a phantom first rep because `lastRep` was undefined. Critical: no. The score started a rep early.\\n2. Plank & Perch could spawn a second ragdoll for one fall. Critical: yes. A second removal in the same step panics Rapier for the whole page.\\n3. Island Loop scored cadence from `t % period` and wrote tilted gravity into the world. Critical: yes. A sharp jog scored 26, and the gravity write produced NaN.\\n4. Plate Spinners' bot left the band it was supposed to hold. Critical: yes. A sharp bot scored about 47 instead of a full spin.\\n5. Room Service built the tray with full extents and lost glasses that were still on it. Critical: yes. The order could not be delivered.\\n6. Tippy Raft ignored the lane's skill and the grip that keeps a sharp player near the middle. Critical: no. Rounds still ended, but skill did not matter.\\n7. Check-in leaned the doll toward the wrong side of the target. Critical: yes. The Wobble Age came out of the wrong mean.\\n8. Check-in applied the calm margin twice. Critical: no. The stand test was stricter than the written one, but the day still finished.\\n\",\"total_lines\":10}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-43","content":"{\"type\":\"BackgroundTaskStarted\",\"task_id\":\"ea069ba8-6652-4cb9-85e8-8c2408110063\",\"task_type\":\"bash\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-43.log\",\"status\":\"running\",\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317\\\" && node tools/test.mjs hub\",\"summary\":\"Background task ea069ba8-6652-4cb9-85e8-8c2408110063 started\",\"retrieval_hint\":\"Use get_command_or_subagent_output with task_ids=[\\\"ea069ba8-6652-4cb9-85e8-8c2408110063\\\"] when you need the output.\",\"pid\":245973}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"599bc4a3-622e-45f6-bd64-6d6a0096b64d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_439","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hub is running in the background.\n\nMonitoring the hub with a timeout. Checking logs and preparing the interview requirements. Waiting for the process to finish.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b235a91f-1677-4a50-9578-6186759ef974-44","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["ea069ba8-6652-4cb9-85e8-8c2408110063"],"timeout_ms":120000}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b235a91f-1677-4a50-9578-6186759ef974-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b235a91f-1677-4a50-9578-6186759ef974-46","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"exit-interview|sourceInformation|testingFeedback|Deviations","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/TASK.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3470,"output_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":86784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"4de5afbd-277a-4f0f-8d95-1fa0c8c6a00e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b235a91f-1677-4a50-9578-6186759ef974-44","content":"{\"type\":\"TaskOutput\",\"Result\":{\"task_id\":\"ea069ba8-6652-4cb9-85e8-8c2408110063\",\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317\\\" && node tools/test.mjs hub\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"exit_code\":0,\"started\":\"2026-11-05T08:56:51Z\",\"ended\":\"2026-11-05T08:57:36Z\",\"duration_secs\":45.115355867,\"output\":\"(node:245977) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n1 passed, 0 failed\\n\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66/terminal/call-83722e4a-0d71-4853-87ab-90c453633cbf-43.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"truncation_hint\":\"[truncated - use read_file on output_file for full content]\",\"raw_output_bytes\":184}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b235a91f-1677-4a50-9578-6186759ef974-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n    \\\"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\\\",\\n    \\\"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\\\",\\n    \\\"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Level Best\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"co-op\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n    \\\"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\\\",\\n30→    \\\"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\\\",\\n    \\\"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\\\",\\n    \\\"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n40→    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Level Best\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3d\\\", \\\"comedy\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"versus\\\", \\\"arcade\\\", \\\"co-op\\\"]\\n50→  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 23:13:17\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Eight issues. The suite caught a phantom first log rep, a double ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, and two check-in lean bugs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Five were critical. The plank could panic physics, Room Service could not deliver, Island Loop and Plate Spinners scored a sharp bot as a failure, and the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n    \\\"The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\\\",\\n    \\\"A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\\\",\\n    \\\"None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\\\",\\n    \\\"A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\\\",\\n    \\\"TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\\\",\\n    \\\"State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Level Best\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Hold still. The island is taking notes.\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A wooden-toy balance party at a crooked island resort. Lean, step, and hold still through a week of classes, then come back when the island is level.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Sports\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Wii Fit\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or 