ild-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer/test-full.log\\\"\",\"summary\":\"Background task 1c0067ab-5eb2-416b-9060-63b0736dacb3 started\",\"retrieval_hint\":\"Use get_command_or_subagent_output with task_ids=[\\\"1c0067ab-5eb2-416b-9060-63b0736dacb3\\\"] when you need the output.\",\"pid\":248339}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"d4924be4-9851-49ce-8ca2-36af065d0ac9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_441","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hub log is complete and green. Full suite is running.\n\nEvents tests may take a while. I'm preparing the issues text to submit immediately upon full suite completion. I'm also auditing the original eight reported bugs to determine which are actually critical.\n\nFour more real game bugs were found by tests. The Cairn latched stone count on first live score read. Plate Spinners counted key taps inside a 0.5s window and blocked the slow band. The Clumsy plate bot wander stayed inside every band so the event could not be lost. Still Water delayed correction with fast noise caused a clumsy form of ~15, though the day still finished.\n\nLog Reps depth error outside the band was zero, so clumsy form was ~30 and not critical. Mouse edges were lost because pointerMove set buttons before pointerButtons read previous state; this is a control failure and likely critical if mouse verbs failed to register. Held stick re-marked the last device every poll, which broke later key sticking but still allowed input.\n\nThe bot stick staying on the pad kept Attract self-woke from staying up, which is a required behavior. Tippy Raft moved but never copied the wish onto its balance state, so the shared core never leaned; this is critical because the balance joint is the game's point. Lowpass thuds were silent because the noise lacked low frequency, though the game remained playable.\n\nThe About screen could not be paged because next, previous, and left or right buttons failed to change pages. This is critical because the required source fields could not be read.\n\nPointer hover repainted and ate the click, so the touch Settings control never opened. This is critical because it was the only touch input.\n\nBundled shader comments contained URLs. This is a build leak, not a play break, so it is not critical.\n\nFruit Hat and Room Service body leaks were test artifacts, not game bugs. The unit draw helper RNG bug was also a test issue.\n\nCritical count from items 9 through 21 is now being tallied.\n\nThe audit is complete. New issues are 8 critical and 5 non-critical. Original issues are 5 critical and 3 non-critical. The total is 21 issues.\n\nThe critical count is 13. I am re-checking the summary list to avoid inventing bugs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f556a326-b8a1-49cd-a815-f7e3025cdaae-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/TASK.md","offset":90,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f556a326-b8a1-49cd-a815-f7e3025cdaae-50","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["1c0067ab-5eb2-416b-9060-63b0736dacb3"],"timeout_ms":180000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1635,"output_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":92288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"020d1156-b6d6-4c27-bd6c-c5574cb020e8"}
