ice, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, and shader comment URLs left in the bundle.\\\",\\n    \\\"Thirteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, and the only touch control did not open.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\",\"new_line\":19,\"context_before\":\"    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n\",\"context_after\":\"  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\\\",\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fdfc683e-6dc5-4b95-a0ab-871f6633ce03-65","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    const pages = [[TITLE, TAGLINE], ['About', 'Level Best Retreat']];\\n    for (const key of Object.keys(info)) pages.push([labels[key] || key, ...chunkText(info[key])]);\\n    pages.push(['Testing']);\\n    for (const line of ABOUT.testingFeedback) pages.push(ch