{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_449","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Twelve unit tests passed. One UI test failed. The total is thirteen passed and one failed.\n\nThe about text test failed. The blob is missing the first feedback line. Four possible causes are being checked: the 80-page limit, unvisited pages, overflow clipping, or insufficient paging.\n\nThe 80-page limit is likely the cause. The source info section contains 14 entries, each about one page. The testing feedback page probably sits beyond that limit.\n\nThe first feedback page starts around page 17, so the 80-page limit is not the cause. The missing text may be clipped by overflow:hidden.\n\nArrowRight paging works for early content, so the key event mechanism is not broken. The missing text likely stems from the long feedback section itself.\n\nThe full feedback line is missing from the blob entirely. It is not merely truncated or split across pages. The root cause is now clear.\n\nThe feedback is split into 7-line pages. The blob joins them with newlines and normalizes whitespace. The full line must be a contiguous substring after that collapse. If every page is visited in order, the text should reconstruct correctly.\n\nThe blob joins pages with newlines, but each page's innerText also contains UI chrome like buttons, page labels, and prompts. That extra text breaks the feedback line into fragments, so the full string is no longer a contiguous substring.\n\nPreviously each feedback line fit on one page. The DOM placed text lines before buttons, so whitespace normalization reconstructed the full sentence correctly. Now the feedback is split across multiple pages, and UI chrome between them breaks that reconstruction.\n\nThe DOM places text lines before buttons, page labels, and prompts on each page. When the answer was one page, the full sentence sat cleanly at the start of that innerText and survived whitespace normalization. Now the answer spans multiple pages, so no single page or concatenated blob contains the complete sentence without UI chrome breaking it. The next step is to list fix options.\n\nThe best fix is to stop splitting the feedback and keep it on one page. The test only checks that the full line exists in the joined blob, so a single page would satisfy it even if overflow clips the text visually. Changing the test to check individual pages is unnecessary.\n\nChecking whether overflow:hidden clips text from innerText. The spec says innerText returns rendered text, but clipped content might be excluded. MDN suggests hidden elements are skipped. Uncertainty remains about whether clipped overflow text is included.\n\nOverflow-clipped text is usually still included in innerText, since the nodes are laid out even when painted off-screen. The failure is caused by splitting the feedback across pages, which breaks the full string into fragments. Reverting that split and keeping each answer on one page should fix the test, provided innerText includes all lines even when they overflow.\n\nThe about section needs roughly fifteen lines. At the current 36px font and 1.25 line-height, that totals about 815 pixels including buttons. The page height is 916 pixels, so the text fits vertically. The main remaining concern is whether the font can shrink enough to keep the lines under 30px.\n\nA precise pixel count shows the feedback section would need roughly 900 pixels. The available content box is about 916 pixels. That leaves almost no margin for error. The last line would likely overflow and get clipped. If that clipped text is excluded from innerText, the includes check fails. The next step is to decide between two fixes.\n\nThe test should strip UI chrome before checking innerText. The requirement is that the About screen shows every field and feedback list, so paging is correct. The full line appearing across pages is valid.\n\nStripping UI chrome with a regex is too fragile. The better fix is to change the test itself. It should collect only paragraph and heading text from the about section, ignoring buttons and page labels entirely.\n\nPage labels are paragraph elements with class `.pages`. They appear between chunks and break the contiguous feedback string. The test should exclude them when collecting about text.\n\nThe test selector will use `p:not(.pages)` to exclude page labels. The \"Testing\" header page is not a paragraph, so it will not insert the word \"Testing\" into the feedback blob.\n\nThe \"Testing\" header sits on a separate page before the feedback, so it does not break the feedback blob. The engine header appears after all testing feedback lines, keeping them contiguous. Only page labels between chunks would insert extra text into the blob.\n\nThe test collector will be updated to exclude page labels and buttons. The addPaged logic stays so pages fit. Eighty arrow presses should visit every page, but the loop may be raised to 120 for safety.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-401dd43a-be67-4450-a9fe-44a37b1ed708-72","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nconst j = JSON.parse(readFileSync(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json\",\"utf8\"));\nfunction chunk(text, width=64) {\n  const words = String(text).split(\" \");\n  const lines = []; let cur=\"\";\n  for (const word of words) {\n    const next = cur ? cur+\" \"+word : word;\n    if (next.length > width && cur) { lines.push(cur); cur = word; } else cur = next;\n  }\n  if (cur) lines.push(cur);\n  return lines.length ? lines : [\"\"];\n}\nfunction pagesOf(lines){ return Math.ceil(lines.length/7); }\nlet n = 2;\nfor (const v of Object.values(j.sourceInformation)) n += pagesOf([v, ...chunk(v)]);\nn += 1;\nfor (const line of j.testingFeedback) { const c = chunk(line); console.log(\"test\", c.length, \"pages\", pagesOf(c)); n += pagesOf(c); }\nn += 1;\nfor (const line of j.engineFeedback) n += pagesOf(chunk(line));\nn += 1;\nfor (const line of j.promptFeedback) n += pagesOf(chunk(line));\nn += 1; // catalogue\nn += pagesOf(chunk(j.aiHub.description));\nn += 3; // type, controls, credits\nconsole.log(\"total pages\", n);\n'","description":"Count About pages after splitting"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":679,"output_tokens":3157,"cache_read_input_tokens":117248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"9ba3d6b4-5f80-43cd-9de3-827fae3b95d0"}
