{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-39370c67-d36d-4103-86ad-aedb44f4da16-87","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { RoundedBoxGeometry } from 'three/addons/geometries/RoundedBoxGeometry.js';\\nimport {\\n  color, mix, smoothstep, positionWorld, cameraPosition, normalize, sub, length, sin, time, step, uniform,\\n} from 'three/tsl';\\nimport { PALETTES } from '../data/palettes.js';\\nimport { INK, LANE_GAP } from '../data/config.js';\\nimport { makeInk } from './ink.js';\\nimport { armIdle } from '../anim/clips.js';\\n10→\\nconst SEATS = [0xe8443a, 0x3b82f6, 0x22c55e, 0xf5b700];\\n\\nfunction rampTexture() {\\n  const data = new Uint8Array([96, 178, 255]);\\n  const tex = new THREE.DataTexture(data, 3, 1);\\n  tex.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\\n  tex.minFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\\n  tex.needsUpdate = true;\\n20→  return tex;\\n}\\n\\nfunction toon(hex, ramp) {\\n  return new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color: hex, gradientMap: ramp });\\n}\\n\\nfunction mesh(geo, mat, parent, x, y, z) {\\n  const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\\n  m.position.set(x, y, z);\\n30→  m.castShadow = true;\\n  m.receiveShadow = true;\\n  parent.add(m);\\n  return m;\\n}\\n\\nfunction makeDoll(ramp, tint) {\\n  const root = new THREE.Group();\\n  const skin = toon(0xf2d3a8, ramp);\\n  const joint = toon(0xd9a86c, ramp);\\n40→  const cloth = toon(tint, ramp);\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { RoundedBoxGeometry } from 'three/addons/geometries/RoundedBoxGeometry.js';\\nimport {\\n  color, mix, smoothstep, positionWorld, cameraPosition, normalize, sub, length, sin, time, step, uniform,\\n} from 'three/tsl';\\nimport { PALETTES } from '../data/palettes.js';\\nimport { INK, LANE_GAP } from '../data/config.js';\\nimport { makeInk } from './ink.js';\\nimport { armIdle } from '../anim/clips.js';\\n10→\\nconst SEATS = [0xe8443a, 0x3b82f6, 0x22c55e, 0xf5b700];\\n\\nfunction rampTexture() {\\n  const data = new Uint8Array([96, 178, 255]);\\n  const tex = new THREE.DataTexture(data, 3, 1);\\n  tex.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\\n  tex.minFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\\n  tex.needsUpdate = true;\\n20→  return tex;\\n}\\n\\nfunction toon(hex, ramp) {\\n  return new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color: hex, gradientMap: ramp });\\n}\\n\\nfunction mesh(geo, mat, parent, x, y, z) {\\n  const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\\n  m.position.set(x, y, z);\\n30→  m.castShadow = true;\\n  m.receiveShadow = true;\\n  parent.add(m);\\n  return m;\\n}\\n\\nfunction makeDoll(ramp, tint) {\\n  const root = new THREE.Group();\\n  const skin = toon(0xf2d3a8, ramp);\\n  const joint = toon(0xd9a86c, ramp);\\n40→  const cloth = toon(tint, ramp);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/render/renderer.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"import * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { RoundedBoxGeometry } from 'three/addons/geometries/RoundedBoxGeometry.js';\\nimport {\\n  color, mix, smoothstep, positionWorld, cameraPosition, normalize, sub, length, sin, time, step, uniform,\\n} from 'three/tsl';\\nimport { PALETTES } from '../data/palettes.js';\\nimport { INK, LANE_GAP } from '../data/config.js';\\nimport { makeInk } from './ink.js';\\nimport { armIdle } from '../anim/clips.js';\\n\\nconst SEATS = [0xe8443a, 0x3b82f6, 0x22c55e, 0xf5b700];\\n\\nfunction rampTexture() {\\n  const data = new Uint8Array([96, 178, 255]);\\n  const tex = new THREE.DataTexture(data, 3, 1);\\n  tex.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\\n  tex.minFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\\n  tex.needsUpdate = true;\\n  return tex;\\n}\\n\\nfunction toon(hex, ramp) {\\n  return new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color: hex, gradientMap: ramp });\\n}\\n\\nfunction mesh(geo, mat, parent, x, y, z) {\\n  const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\\n  m.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  m.castShadow = true;\\n  m.receiveShadow = true;\\n  parent.add(m);\\n  return m;\\n}\\n\\nfunction makeDoll(ramp, tint) {\\n  const root = new THREE.Group();\\n  const skin = toon(0xf2d3a8, ramp);\\n  const joint = toon(0xd9a86c, ramp);\\n  const cloth = toon(tint, ramp);\\n\",\"total_lines\":397}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"7e2a1574-e2b2-4cc6-8dc9-babecb5359ef"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_459","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ramp is a 3x1 texture with 3 bytes.\n\nThe texSubImage error occurs because Three.js DataTexture defaults to RGBAFormat, requiring 12 bytes for three pixels but only receiving 3. The fix is to use RGBA format or RedFormat/Luminance.\n\nThe WebGL2 fallback is broken because WebGL enforces exact buffer sizes, unlike WebGPU. The plan requires this fallback to still draw.\n\nWebKit reported two frames drawn, so the fallback rendered something. The toon materials likely defaulted to black because the texture failed. I will fix the texture buffer size and rebuild. The WebGPU path may also need adjustment since it might have been masking the same bug.\n\nThe island looked properly colored in the WebGPU launch screenshots, so that path likely tolerates the bad ramp or ignores it. I will rebuild and relaunch to verify the fix, since the launch checks pixels for kinds, ink, and sky. The full suite does not depend on the ramp texture.\n\nThe shipped HTML must match the launch-tested version. The ramp will be fixed to a 3x1 RGBA texture with three grayscale stops and alpha. After rebuilding, I will verify WebKit has no console errors, relaunch to capture frames, and rerun unit tests since the HTML content changed.\n\nThe full test suite and relaunch will be rerun to keep the final HTML evidence aligned. The 3-byte texture fix does not change physics behavior, but running both is the right thing to do.\n\nThe texture will use nearest-neighbor filtering, clamp-to-edge wrapping, and no color space or mipmaps. Each ramp stop is duplicated across the red, green, and blue channels to form a grayscale gradient that standard toon shaders sample correctly.\n\nRedFormat with three bytes would still fail because WebGL requires four-byte row alignment. The RGBA buffer is the only safe fix.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"WebKit is on the WebGL2 fallback and the title draws, but the toon ramp is a 3-byte texture in an RGBA slot, so the upload is rejected. I'll give it a 4-byte-aligned ramp and check the fallback again."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-03f4cb80-59cf-431b-b537-98210e41e6cb-88","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/render/renderer.js","old_string":"function rampTexture() {\n  const data = new Uint8Array([96, 178, 255]);\n  const tex = new THREE.DataTexture(data, 3, 1);\n  tex.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\n  tex.minFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\n  tex.needsUpdate = true;\n  return tex;\n}","new_string":"function rampTexture() {\n  const stops = [96, 178, 255];\n  const data = new Uint8Array(stops.length * 4);\n  for (let i = 0; i < stops.length; i++) {\n    data[i * 4] = stops[i];\n    data[i * 4 + 1] = stops[i];\n    data[i * 4 + 2] = stops[i];\n    data[i * 4 + 3] = 255;\n  }\n  const tex = new THREE.DataTexture(data, stops.length, 1);\n  tex.format = THREE.RGBAFormat;\n  tex.magFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\n  tex.minFilter = THREE.NearestFilter;\n  tex.generateMipmaps = false;\n  tex.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\n  tex.needsUpdate = true;\n  return tex;\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":699,"output_tokens":1937,"cache_read_input_tokens":128512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"76c8c105-c47d-4b36-9220-ad40963f8374"}
