7-xhigh-20261104-231317/tools/hub/harness.html\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":204,\"content\":\"    if (env.m?.type !== 'vis') log(`${from} → hub: ${env.m?.type}${env.m?.type === 'result' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify({ time: env.m.time, score: env.m.score }) : ''}${env.m?.type === 'finish' ? ' ' + JSON.stringify(env.m.standings) : ''}`);\"},{\"line_number\":224,\"content\":\"    const cell = { ...p, el, label, frame, endpoint, violations: [], instrumented: true, gone: false, progress: [], cardSent: '' };\"},{\"line_number\":238,\"content\":\"      // The scoreboard's feed: this cell's own progress, as its bridge passes it on.\"},{\"line_number\":241,\"content\":\"        cell.progress.push({ at: performance.now(), ...report });\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"        state.coordinator.progress(id, report.score);\"},{\"line_number\":343,\"content\":\"    const last = cell.progress.at(-1);\"},{\"line_number\":344,\"content\":\"    if (last && !p.result) bits.push(`progress ${last.score}${last.label ? ` (${last.label})` : ''}`);\"},{\"line_number\":469,\"content\":\"    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\"},{\"line_number\":489,\"content\":\"      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\"},{\"line_number\":490,\"content\":\"        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key}: ${c.progress.length} report${c.progress.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`).join(', '));\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"0aefd037-130c-4207-aa0f-3994fdc3dac0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_486","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"hub.rng returns a generator function.\n\ndeal() works. hub.time() returns the current time. The session scoring bug triggers when fixed loop steps repeat while hub.time() stays in a narrow window, or when an event ends early. I will reproduce this with a node script after checking createLoop for step count. Without a bot, sessionFixed uses idle player input.\n\nSpringboard auto-launches after 8 seconds of pump if no hop occurs. Three dives plus air time total roughly 24 seconds, so the event ends early. The reproduction script will use deterministic time and RNG to freeze the game state.\n\nThe reproduction script mocks the AIHub with a deterministic clock and captures progress updates. It initializes a manual game session and freezes time at zero to reproduce the bug where hub.time() stays constant across multiple fixed loop steps.\n\nA hidden tab jump into the play window near the end would trigger an immediate one-tick score. The slot logic uses absolute clock time rather than accumulated event time, so a sudden jump starts the event and scores it instantly on the first step.\n\nA mid-event jump would score a partial result. The real bug is repeated scoring. I will simulate smooth clock advancement from zero to seventy seconds and count how many times the progress score increases. The [55.9, 56) window spans about twelve fixed steps. Each step after the first adds another part.\n\nPoses ends at 33 seconds of play. That triggers one score. Then a new event runs until 55.9 seconds and scores again. The bug produces twelve spam scores during slot zero instead of one. I will run the reproduction in the game folder. I need to check the createGame window option and rapier initialization. Progress is called every second or when lastProgress is negative.\n\nProgress reports fire once per second of hub time, not after every part push. The score at each report therefore includes all spam additions that occurred during that one-second window. Comparing scores at t=40 and t=56 will reveal the multiple additions. Monkeypatching to inspect individual parts is not possible.\n\nI will detect repeated scoring by watching for event timer resets to near zero while the progress score jumps. A single slot should reach at most 1000 points, so a final score above that threshold proves the bug.\n\nA score above 1000 at t=62 confirms multiple parts were added. The first two poses alone could reach roughly 1600 points. Twelve one-tick pose spam events would push the total past 10000. Even a zero-form pose can score about 100 points if the player remains inside the ring.\n\nSpringboard events score zero points, so they are invisible. Poses events likely score non-zero. The script will print progress scores directly. A score above 1000 before the spam window indicates an early-restart bug, while a jump at t=56 indicates window spam. I am deciding whether to include a bot in the reproduction.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-567748a2-778b-4b91-a5f2-c3161fb321f6-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-567748a2-778b-4b91-a5f2-c3161fb321f6-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/core/loop.js","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1344,"output_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":131328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"405789ab-12d9-43bf-8ba2-80b13f3b9611"}
