{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_493","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The minified line contains 55.9.\n\nThe bug is in the shipped HTML. Early events finish before the 50-second play window ends. The session then restarts on the next tick because the event was nulled while local time remained below 56. The fix is to score each slot only once, hold the results screen until local reaches at least 56, and prevent duplicate event starts within the same slot.\n\nThe slot closes only when local reaches 56. Scoring must happen once on transition, not repeatedly while local is between 55.9 and 56. The bug is in director.js at lines 815-837. Two findings would cover the early restart and the repeated world scoring, but they share one root cause.\n\nA single bug finding is cleaner than two. The hub test only checks harness pass, so it misses score inflation. I should ask them to add a test that a session slot contributes exactly one part.\n\nThe findings array will be the implementer's action item. The bug is confirmed at director.js lines 812-837. The test gap should require a sim-time test that one slot contributes exactly one part and the reported score stays at or below 1000 until the next slot.\n\nThe score calculation confirms the bug. Slot 0 forces Poses, and local time advances from 0 to 70 seconds. Progress reaches 257 at t=39, then jumps to 11576 at t=56. The extra ~17 seconds of a 33-second event produces roughly eleven extra full-form parts. The initial 257 score is low because idle does not follow the ring.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The hub slot scorer banks a class more than once. I confirmed that against the shipped director with a clock-driven session."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ee4177e-4706-4d1d-be63-eeb7cb60a162-72","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-verdict-cfc5772a1498-1-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js:812\",\n      \"detail\": \"A hub slot scores and disposes the event while local time is still under 56s, then the next fixed step sees event===null and starts a new one. Poses (33s), Cairn (~42s), Log Reps (40s) and Springboard (3 dives) finish inside the 50s play window and are scored again; once local is in [55.9, 56) every 1/120 step starts a fresh world and pushes another round(form*10). Latch one part per slot and hold results until local>=56. A sim-time session with AIHub.time() must show one part and score<=1000 at the end of slot 0.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"sessionFixed replay, rng deal=0 (slot 0 = Poses): progress score 0 at t=0, 257 at t=39, 11576 at t=56 (one slot must be a single round(form*10), at most 1000). Same 55.9 latch is in the built HTML.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Hub session scoring restarts the class and banks it many times.\\n\\n`sessionFixed` in `src/game/director.js` treats `local < 56` as \\\"still playing\\\". When the event sets `done`, or when `local >= 55.9`, it pushes `round(form*10)`, disposes the world, and sets `event = null`. The next `fixed` step is still inside that window, so `if (!event) startEvent(...)` builds a new world and the same branch scores it again.\\n\\nPLAN.md §12 says each of the three slots is 6s intro, 50s play, 6s results, and contributes one `round(form × 10)`. Several session events end early: Poses tier 1 is `3 * (3 + 8) = 33s`, Cairn tier 1 is about `1.2 + 6*5.5 + 8 = 42s`, Log Reps is `8 * 5 = 40s` at the default tempo, and Springboard sets `done` after three dives. Those completions fall while `local < 56`.\\n\\nSpot-check: manual `createGame`, `runSession`, `AIHub.rng` returning 0 so slot 0 is Poses, clock advanced `1/120` s per fixed step. Progress score was 0 at t=0, 257 at t=39 (first Poses ended), then 11576 at t=56. One slot cannot exceed 1000. The same `55.9` latch is in the bundled HTML. The harness still passes because it does not check the score magnitude.\\n\\nFix: record a slot's part once, and do not call `startEvent` again until `session.slot` changes. Keep the results screen until `local >= 56`. Add a sim-time test that slot 0 contributes one part and the reported score stays ≤ 1000 until the next slot.\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ee4177e-4706-4d1d-be63-eeb7cb60a162-73","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-classifier-cfc5772a1498-1-skeptic-0.md","content":"Hub session scoring restarts the class and banks it many times.\n\n`sessionFixed` in `src/game/director.js` treats `local < 56` as \"still playing\". When the event sets `done`, or when `local >= 55.9`, it pushes `round(form*10)`, disposes the world, and sets `event = null`. The next `fixed` step is still inside that window, so `if (!event) startEvent(...)` builds a new world and the same branch scores it again.\n\nPLAN.md §12 says each of the three slots is 6s intro, 50s play, 6s results, and contributes one `round(form × 10)`. Several session events end early: Poses tier 1 is `3 * (3 + 8) = 33s`, Cairn tier 1 is about `1.2 + 6*5.5 + 8 = 42s`, Log Reps is `8 * 5 = 40s` at the default tempo, and Springboard sets `done` after three dives. Those completions fall while `local < 56`.\n\nSpot-check: manual `createGame`, `runSession`, `AIHub.rng` returning 0 so slot 0 is Poses, clock advanced `1/120` s per fixed step. Progress score was 0 at t=0, 257 at t=39 (first Poses ended), then 11576 at t=56. One slot cannot exceed 1000. The same `55.9` latch is in the bundled HTML. The harness still passes because it does not check the score magnitude.\n\nFix: record a slot's part once, and do not call `startEvent` again until `session.slot` changes. Keep the results screen until `local >= 56`. Add a sim-time test that slot 0 contributes one part and the reported score stays ≤ 1000 until the next slot.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1347,"output_tokens":2284,"cache_read_input_tokens":139264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"5a720973-e3d1-43c0-9ae2-68a6e5188053"}
