{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_497","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand how advance() works and whether I can mock AIHub.\n\nThe test needs a fake AIHub with controllable time(). The sessionFixed logic reads AIHub.time() directly rather than accumulated play time. This creates a mismatch with advance(), which uses real fixed step deltas.\n\nI will mock AIHub.time() to advance in sync with the fixed steps. The bug should appear as multiple parts if time is not aligned. I need a short event from SESSION_SET, because long events finish before 56 seconds and may only score once.\n\nThe restart bug triggers whenever local time falls in the [55.9, 56) window. Every event enters this range, so even a long event can restart. I will run slot 0 to completion and assert exactly one part with score <= 1000.\n\nThe loop restarts the world every 1/120 second during the 0.1-second window from 55.9 to 56 seconds, producing roughly twelve extra scores. A fresh event at t=0 may have zero form, so its score could be zero and mask the bug.\n\nThe test must verify exactly one part, not merely a total score under 1000. A short event like poses can finish twice within slot 0 because its 33-second duration plus the 6-second intro fits inside the 50-second window.\n\nSpringboard could score repeatedly and exceed 1000. I will add a `session.partLatched` flag per slot to ensure only one part is pushed.\n\nThe slot change resets `playT` and clears the event. A new event starts only when none is active and `session.latched` is false. Once the event finishes or local time reaches 55.9 seconds, the score is recorded and `latched` is set to true, preventing any further parts from being pushed.\n\nThe latched flag prevents any new event from starting once the first part is recorded. The results screen stays active until local time reaches 56 seconds, matching the requirement to hold results until then.\n\nThe latched flag prevents any input or world-starting after the first part is recorded. The same step that starts an event can immediately score and latch it, so no double-count occurs. The test will need to access the parts array directly.\n\nstate() does not currently expose session.parts. The test can read the score and part count through hub.progress or hub.result callbacks instead, since the result is only sent after all slots finish.\n\nI will expose session.parts and session.total through state() so the test reads the real game state. The test must drive the shipped advance() function and keep AIHub.time() moving forward; a single jump to 61.9 would not reproduce the bug, because the restart issue requires many steps while time remains inside the [55.9, 56) window or moves through a short event.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0be1982-75f2-40b6-99e5-2d3eca622ee6-107","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"SESSION_SET","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0be1982-75f2-40b6-99e5-2d3eca622ee6-108","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/test/flow.mjs","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d0be1982-75f2-40b6-99e5-2d3eca622ee6-109","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","offset":1195,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2071,"output_tokens":2226,"cache_read_input_tokens":144640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"17aff151-c9eb-4e04-918e-1ffe56e84933"}
