{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_511","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Flow tests passed, including the new hub slot test. Eight tests ran.\n\nThe flow test passed against source, not the built HTML. The hub harness only plays six seconds, so it missed this bug. Rebuilding is required to include the fix in the HTML. Then I will rerun the full suite and relaunch. Interview counts will be updated to twenty-three issues with fourteen critical, plus the hub slot clause.\n\nThe first sentence will list twenty-three issues. The critical sentence will note fourteen critical items plus the hub slot scoring the same class twice. I will update notes, interview, and progress next. Then I will rebuild, run the full suite, and relaunch.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beece87f-8fcf-4fe2-bdfc-ac21a5e5d046-134","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md","old_string":"22. The toon ramp was three bytes in an RGBA texture, so WebGL rejected the upload. Critical: no. The title still drew. The stops are now four-byte pixels.","new_string":"22. The toon ramp was three bytes in an RGBA texture, so WebGL rejected the upload. Critical: no. The title still drew. The stops are now four-byte pixels.\n23. A hub slot scored a finished class and then started it again while the minute was still open. Critical: yes. The same class was scored more than once, and the last tenth of a second built a new world every step."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beece87f-8fcf-4fe2-bdfc-ac21a5e5d046-135","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json","old_string":"    \"Twenty-two issues. Testing caught a phantom first log rep, a second ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a key window that made the slow plate band unreachable, a clumsy plate wander that could not drop a plate, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, a raft whose balance wish never reached the joint, two check-in lean bugs, The Cairn latching zero stones, a Still Water guest stuck outside the calm, a log depth score that ignored near misses, mouse edges dropped before they were read, a parked stick that kept the last device, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, shader comment URLs left in the bundle, and a toon ramp whose three stops were too short for an RGBA upload.\",\n    \"Thirteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, and the only touch control did not open.\",","new_string":"    \"Twenty-three issues. Testing caught a phantom first log rep, a second ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a key window that made the slow plate band unreachable, a clumsy plate wander that could not drop a plate, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, a raft whose balance wish never reached the joint, two check-in lean bugs, The Cairn latching zero stones, a Still Water guest stuck outside the calm, a log depth score that ignored near misses, mouse edges dropped before they were read, a parked stick that kept the last device, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, shader comment URLs left in the bundle, a toon ramp whose three stops were too short for an RGBA upload, and a hub slot that scored a finished class and then started it again.\",\n    \"Fourteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, the only touch control did not open, and a hub slot scored the same class more than once.\","}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beece87f-8fcf-4fe2-bdfc-ac21a5e5d046-136","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PROGRESS.md","old_string":"Issues found while building are in `notes/issues.md`. Twenty-two in all, thirteen of them critical. The About screen and exit-interview.json use that count.","new_string":"Issues found while building are in `notes/issues.md`. Twenty-three in all, fourteen of them critical. The About screen and exit-interview.json use that count."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":391,"output_tokens":1352,"cache_read_input_tokens":173312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"0b231087-d935-4e4d-98dc-c7b5e0dfecb2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-beece87f-8fcf-4fe2-bdfc-ac21a5e5d046-134","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"22. The toon ramp was three bytes in an RGBA texture, so WebGL rejected the upload. Critical: no. The title still drew. The stops are now four-byte pixels.\",\"new_string\":\"22. The toon ramp was three bytes in an RGBA texture, so WebGL rejected the upload. Critical: no. The title still drew. The stops are now four-byte pixels.\\n23. A hub slot scored a finished class and then started it again while the minute was still open. Critical: yes. The same class was scored more than once, and the last tenth of a second built a new world every step.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/notes/issues.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"22. The toon ramp was three bytes in an RGBA texture, so WebGL rejected the upload. Critical: no. The title still drew. The stops are now four-byte pixels.\",\"old_line\":24,\"new_string\":\"22. The toon ramp was three bytes in an RGBA texture, so WebGL rejected the upload. Critical: no. The title still drew. The stops are now four-byte pixels.\\n23. A hub slot scored a finished class and then started it again while the minute was still open. Critical: yes. The same class was scored more than once, and the last tenth of a second built a new world every step.\",\"new_line\":24,\"context_before\":\"19. About and the journal ignored next, previous, and left and right, so the page stayed on the title. Critical: yes. The credits could not be read.\\n20. Hovering a choice rebuilt the button, so the click never landed. Critical: yes. Touch Settings did not open.\\n21. The bundled shader comments still contained web URLs. Critical: no. The page ran, and the unit check rejected the strings.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-beece87f-8fcf-4fe2-bdfc-ac21a5e5d046-135","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    \\\"Twenty-two issues. Testing caught a phantom first log rep, a second ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a key window that made the slow plate band unreachable, a clumsy plate wander that could not drop a plate, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, a raft whose balance wish never reached the joint, two check-in lean bugs, The Cairn latching zero stones, a Still Water guest stuck outside the calm, a log depth score that ignored near misses, mouse edges dropped before they were read, a parked stick that kept the last device, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, shader comment URLs left in the bundle, and a toon ramp whose three stops were too short for an RGBA upload.\\\",\\n    \\\"Thirteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, and the only touch control did not open.\\\",\",\"new_string\":\"    \\\"Twenty-three issues. Testing caught a phantom first log rep, a second ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a key window that made the slow plate band unreachable, a clumsy plate wander that could not drop a plate, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, a raft whose balance wish never reached the joint, two check-in lean bugs, The Cairn latching zero stones, a Still Water guest stuck outside the calm, a log depth score that ignored near misses, mouse edges dropped before they were read, a parked stick that kept the last device, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, shader comment URLs left in the bundle, a toon ramp whose three stops were too short for an RGBA upload, and a hub slot that scored a finished class and then started it again.\\\",\\n    \\\"Fourteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, the only touch control did not open, and a hub slot scored the same class more than once.\\\",\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/exit-interview.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"    \\\"Twenty-two issues. Testing caught a phantom first log rep, a second ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a key window that made the slow plate band unreachable, a clumsy plate wander that could not drop a plate, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, a raft whose balance wish never reached the joint, two check-in lean bugs, The Cairn latching zero stones, a Still Water guest stuck outside the calm, a log depth score that ignored near misses, mouse edges dropped before they were read, a parked stick that kept the last device, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, shader comment URLs left in the bundle, and a toon ramp whose three stops were too short for an RGBA upload.\\\",\\n    \\\"Thirteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, and the only touch control did not open.\\\",\",\"old_line\":20,\"new_string\":\"    \\\"Twenty-three issues. Testing caught a phantom first log rep, a second ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a key window that made the slow plate band unreachable, a clumsy plate wander that could not drop a plate, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, a raft whose balance wish never reached the joint, two check-in lean bugs, The Cairn latching zero stones, a Still Water guest stuck outside the calm, a log depth score that ignored near misses, mouse edges dropped before they were read, a parked stick that kept the last device, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, shader comment URLs left in the bundle, a toon ramp whose three stops were too short for an RGBA upload, and a hub slot that scored a finished class and then started it again.\\\",\\n    \\\"Fourteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, the only touch control did not open, and a hub slot scored the same class more than once.\\\",\",\"new_line\":20,\"context_before\":\"    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n\",\"context_after\":\"    \\\"The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\\\"\\n  ],\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-beece87f-8fcf-4fe2-bdfc-ac21a5e5d046-136","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"Issues found while building are in `notes/issues.md`. Twenty-two in all, thirteen of them critical. The About screen and exit-interview.json use that count.\",\"new_string\":\"Issues found while building are in `notes/issues.md`. Twenty-three in all, fourteen of them critical. The About screen and exit-interview.json use that count.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"Issues found while building are in `notes/issues.md`. Twenty-two in all, thirteen of them critical. The About screen and exit-interview.json use that count.\",\"old_line\":17,\"new_string\":\"Issues found while building are in `notes/issues.md`. Twenty-three in all, fourteen of them critical. The About screen and exit-interview.json use that count.\",\"new_line\":17,\"context_before\":\"\\n`node tools/test.mjs full` printed `102 passed, 0 failed`. Two file:// launches drew the WebGPU title and left it on Enter. The hub harness passed for 1 player, 2 players, 4 players with latency, jitter and loss, and a host leaving. Outside a session, Enter and Space leave a drawn frame.\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"416bd209-5e28-4616-bf91-37f830644559"}
