{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d9ea03f1-f512-46c1-acdc-1964165b3e34-144","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"`node tools/test.mjs full` printed `102 passed, 0 failed`.\",\"new_string\":\"`node tools/test.mjs full` printed `103 passed, 0 failed`.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"`node tools/test.mjs full` printed `102 passed, 0 failed`.\",\"old_line\":15,\"new_string\":\"`node tools/test.mjs full` printed `103 passed, 0 failed`.\",\"new_line\":15,\"context_before\":\"\\nThe game is built. The work-folder root holds the single HTML file, this note, and exit-interview.json. The dev folder holds the modules and the test command.\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\nIssues found while building are in `notes/issues.md`. Twenty-three in all, fourteen of them critical. The About screen and exit-interview.json use that count.\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"11587fc4-3a89-4cb2-aef4-4837630bdfbe"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_517","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A hub slot now keeps one score. When a class finishes, or the play clock reaches 55.9 seconds, that result stays up until the slot ends. The next step does not start the class again.\n\nA sim-time session on `AIHub.time()` plays Springboard through the end of slot 0 and records one part, at 1000 points or under. The full suite printed `103 passed, 0 failed`. Both file:// launches still draw the WebGPU title.\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-04 23:13:17\n- Source: Wii Fit\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: Physics-balance party sports with a daily ritual\n- Perspective: Third person, with a framed stage camera in class and a chase camera on the island\n- Tech: Three.js R180 (WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink), Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0\n- Art Direction: Cel-shaded ink over a wooden-toy island resort, models built in code\n- Animation: AnimationMixer clips on jointed peg dolls, physics-driven lean, Rapier ragdolls on a fall\n- Audio: Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa, effects, and gibberish voices. Music defaults to 10 percent. Every spoken line is also on screen\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen\n- Testing: Headless Playwright and one Node command that prints only failures. Simulated pads. No physical controller\n- Research: PLAN.md, the installed Rapier 0.19 package, and the Three r180 TSL ink recipe\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- Twenty-three issues. Testing caught a phantom first log rep, a second ragdoll on the plank, an Island Loop cadence that scored 26, plate bots that left the band, a key window that made the slow plate band unreachable, a clumsy plate wander that could not drop a plate, a Room Service tray at the wrong size, a raft that ignored skill, a raft whose balance wish never reached the joint, two check-in lean bugs, The Cairn latching zero stones, a Still Water guest stuck outside the calm, a log depth score that ignored near misses, mouse edges dropped before they were read, a parked stick that kept the last device, an attract demo that woke itself, fruit and stamp effects with no low end, About pages that did not turn, a hover that rebuilt the button under the pointer, shader comment URLs left in the bundle, a toon ramp whose three stops were too short for an RGBA upload, and a hub slot that scored a finished class and then started it again.\n- Fourteen were critical. The plank could panic physics, Island Loop and the sharp plate bot scored as a failure, keys could not reach the slow band, plates could not be lost, Room Service could not deliver, the raft joint stayed at rest, The Cairn always reported zero stones, the check-in lean sign would publish the wrong Wobble Age, mouse confirm never fired, attract mode would not stay up, About could not leave its first page, the only touch control did not open, and a hub slot scored the same class more than once.\n- The most helpful test was a sharp bot driving each event through the real pad path and reading that event's own result.\n- The least helpful test was counting renderer frames without reading pixels. A lost device still increments the frame counter.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- One fixed step and one ball joint, plus the TSL ink pass, gave every event the same body and the same look on both backends.\n- Yes. Rapier cuboids are half-extents, so a tray written as cuboid 0.3 was twice as wide as it looked. Removing two colliders in one step panics the wasm. TSL hash() takes one float.\n- The ankle torque step, the fourteen events, the synthesised voices, and the ink scene.\n- A Rapier panic is unrecoverable for the page, and the software WebGPU device stays lost unless the extra swiftshader flags are set.\n- None. I did not change Three, Rapier, or the hub client.\n- A signal that the device is actually drawing, not only that frames were requested.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- The measured numbers, and the instruction not to retune them.\n- TASK.md's three WebGPU flags lose the device, and cuboid sizes look like full extents.\n- Keeping one bot, one stick, and one joint honest across fourteen events.\n- State that cuboids are half-extents, and put the working WebGPU flags in TASK.md."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":172,"output_tokens":1098,"cache_read_input_tokens":177920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"4e023075-de5a-4d8a-a9d2-dfc03de9cb48"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_518","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Re-verifying the previous gap about hub session scoring.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The last round failed because a hub slot scored a class more than once. I’ll re-read the session scorer and the new test, then replay that clock."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9f6105e5-bb82-42e9-8874-2aaf639d9d78-74","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"sessionFixed|scored|parts\\.push|55\\.9|slotScore|one part","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9f6105e5-bb82-42e9-8874-2aaf639d9d78-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"session|slot 0|11576|parts","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/test","glob":"*.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9f6105e5-bb82-42e9-8874-2aaf639d9d78-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/implementer/test-full.log"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":152953,"output_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":1792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"e801943b-53d8-4965-b527-524f1f6c4fce"}
