{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_527","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand the 50s classes.\n\nEvent durations are 50 seconds. The play window is local 6 to 56. Scoring triggers at 55.9. A hub time jump from 55.8 to 56.0 would skip the 55.9 frame entirely.\n\nA time jump past the play window skips scoring entirely. The event remains live but is never stepped or scored, and parts stays empty. A slot change also disposes the event without scoring. The skeptic requires scoring the live event once on any exit from the play window, including local>=56 and slot changes.\n\nScoring must be a single one-time action. It triggers when the slot ends or local reaches 56, but only while the event is live and unlatched. Once scored, no new event starts and no further scoring occurs. If local crosses 56 before the frame steps the event, its current result is scored immediately.\n\nThe score must be strictly positive and at most 1000. A 50s class needs to produce a score greater than zero even with idle input, or a bot is required. Each slot of a 50s class must contain one part with total in that range.\n\nThe test will use a 50-second session class such as plates, fruitHat, or stepClass. It can call game.bot('sharp') before advancing to ensure the event scores above zero. The test must advance AIHub.time() in roughly one-sixth second frames, keeping that interval constant across each frame's steps.\n\nThe test will use a constant millisecond counter that advances by one-sixth second after each batch of 20 fixed steps. The run will cover the full slot from zero to past 56 seconds. Because stepping stops once local reaches 56, an event that finishes at exactly 50 seconds may never reach its done state if the clock jumps over the 55.9 scoring threshold.\n\nThe exact frame boundary at t=56 falls on a 1/6-second mark. When local reaches 56, the current code immediately switches to results without scoring the event. This confirms the bug: the play window ends at exactly 56 seconds, so the event never scores.\n\nA sharp bot on plates should produce a form value above zero, yielding a total score of up to 1000. Idle input would likely score zero, so the test must use a bot to satisfy the positive-score requirement.\n\nI should verify the bot is actually wired into session mode, because an unwired bot would score zero and break the test.\n\nThe \"one part\" requirement means I must latch the event immediately after scoring so no extra parts are added later. When the slot changes at t=62, latched resets to false, but the previous part must remain in the parts array.\n\nI will sample the parts array while slot 0 is still active, after the play window closes but before the slot changes. This ensures the array contains exactly one part, satisfying the test requirement.\n\nI will implement both scoring paths: when local reaches 56 and when the slot changes. I drafted a `latchResult` helper that pushes the rounded form score into the session parts array and updates the total.\n\nThe `latchResult` helper now sets `session.best`, marks the session as latched, disposes the event, and switches to the results screen. The slot-change logic checks for an unlatched live event before resetting the slot counter, play timer, and latched flag. The main loop branches into intro, play, or exit based on local time.\n\nThe slot-change scoring path must call `latchResult` before the session resets its state, because the helper already disposes the event and clears the latched flag. When the session ends entirely, the live event should also be scored if it remains unlatched.\n\nThe session-end path now calls `latchResult` before `sendResult` when the slot index exceeds the available slots. This handles any remaining live event that was never scored.\n\nFor the local>=56 exit, the event has already been stepped on prior frames, so its current form value reflects the play time up to that point. The score can be taken directly without requiring an extra step at the boundary.\n\nThe accumulated event state is the final score. No extra step or new class should be started at the boundary.\n\nA sharp bot on plates should score 100 form, yielding a total of 1000. The test requires a positive score, so I need to verify that session mode actually applies the bot skill and that the 50-second class duration is correct.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-287a8854-6a6e-4f4d-8204-7d791366407e-148","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"opts\\.session \\? 50","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-287a8854-6a6e-4f4d-8204-7d791366407e-149","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/plates.js","offset":100,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-287a8854-6a6e-4f4d-8204-7d791366407e-150","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/test/flow.mjs","offset":198,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2602,"output_tokens":2987,"cache_read_input_tokens":179072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"7ed7f7aa-05f0-4fdb-9974-95aa66dd09ca"}
