{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_531","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"driveBots returns snaps. bot('sharp') sets botSkill.\n\nI'll set the test configuration. I'll implement latchSlot and update the control flow, then extend the test. I may check chart session length. I'll also update issues.md to document this related bug where a class not yet finished gets zero when the clock jumps past its scoring window.\n\nI'll record this as issue 24 and update the interview counts so About stays honest. I'll rebuild and rerun the full suite plus launch because HTML changes require it. I'm also checking whether a class could score zero if the clock jumps past its scoring window before it finishes.\n\nI checked the edge case where the clock jumps past local>=56 before the event starts. The event never began, so scoring correctly returns zero. I also confirmed that a class already in progress scores properly when the clock crosses the boundary.\n\nThe test starts at local 0, so the event always exists. A jump from intro to local 56 correctly scores nothing. I also verified that a slot change during the intro does not trigger scoring.\n\nI confirmed the remaining 19 steps after latch correctly score one part and route to the results screen. I also verified that medalLabel handles undefined medals safely. I'm now writing the code and checking the test timing: 20 steps of 1/6 second each equal exactly 20 frames, so the clock advances precisely by 56 seconds.\n\nI switched the test clock to exact frame-based assignment to avoid floating-point drift. Frame 336 lands exactly at 56 seconds, while frame 335 stays below the 55.9-second threshold, confirming the scoring boundary is clean.\n\nThe test will assert slot 0, event id 'plates', one part, a total between 0 and 1000, results screen, and no active event. If the score is zero, the cause may be weak bot driving, low share clamping form to zero, or a crash from short session duration. The sharp bot should still hold the band at roughly 99% form.\n\nI'll run the single test first to iterate quickly, then run the full flow suite. The tests aren't individually exported, so I'll need a small scratch runner.\n\nI'll run the 6fps test via a one-off Node module import to iterate quickly. The official flow suite and full test run will follow.\n\nThe scoring path will be generic so it handles any live event, not just plates. The test uses plates as the 50-second class. A double-score guard ensures the latch fires only once at local>=56.\n\nI noticed a bug in the progress report: it displays session.total, which stays zero until the event is latched at local>=56. During the first six seconds of play, the user sees no score at all. I am now examining the progress code to fix this.\n\nThe zero-score display during the first six seconds is intentional: the system scores the final result rather than live form. After latching at local 56, progress updates once a second elapses and the total becomes positive. I am now checking whether that progress event fires on the exact frame where the latch occurs.\n\nProgress updates correctly on the exact frame where the latch occurs. The springboard test remains unaffected by this change. Even a slightly imperfect bot still produces a positive score within the required bounds.\n\nI confirmed the plates bot input works without special options. I will add issue 24 as critical and update the interview counts to twenty-four total issues, fifteen critical, after the tests pass. The About page text change requires a full rebuild.\n\nI weighed whether to step the event once more at local>=56 so a class ending exactly at 50 seconds gets its final moments. The result() function already returns earned form without that extra step, and stepping outside the play window would be invalid.\n\nI decided against adding a comment about the 6fps clock skipping the final tenth of a class, since the function name `latchSlot` is clear enough. I also confirmed that `latchSlot` safely no-ops when called before any event exists, so the slot-change guard can fire without issue.\n\nI confirmed that `bot('sharp')` sets the skill correctly even during an active session, and that `runSession` does not reset it. The test will use a fixed-frame clock rather than an incrementing one.\n\nThe deal RNG is stable because it uses the hub directly. A constant 0.5 seed should not break plates wobble. The test will restore session mode and the AIHub after finishing, and any leaked world state is acceptable.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a6beb6f1-18ac-410a-8424-02a38f497f83-159","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/charts.js","offset":55,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3600,"output_tokens":3006,"cache_read_input_tokens":188416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"bb6b8a17-29a2-4680-81d9-5638eb62b07e"}
