{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_541","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to read the full new test carefully.\n\nThe test advances the game by 1/6-second frames while keeping `ms` constant, matching the request. The `latchSlot` logic scores events correctly when they exist and the slot is not yet latched. When the slot changes, it resets the latch state and disposes the old event.\n\nThe score is preserved before the slot change. A time jump from slot 0 to slot 1 correctly scores the old event first. Calling `latchSlot` without stepping the event first is intentional, capturing the live result. The exact number of steps per 1/6-second advance still needs verification.\n\nThe 1/6-second advance equals exactly 20 fixed steps, and `hub.time()` returns the same constant `ms` across all of them. This confirms the test faithfully reproduces the bug scenario where local time never advances during the frame. I still need to verify whether the test actually holds `ms` constant and whether the deal logic picks plates.\n\nThe test logic is safe from double-scoring. When the frame lands exactly at 56 seconds, the first step scores the event and sets the latch flag. The next step sees the latch and only displays results. When the frame lands slightly before 56 seconds, the event steps through all 20 fixed updates. If it finishes during that window, it latches once. The following frame then simply shows results without pushing again.\n\nSlot changes during latched states reset the latch flag correctly. Jumps from an earlier slot to a later one score the in-progress event once before starting the new slot. A jump from the intro phase into the scoring window returns early because no event exists, so nothing is scored.\n\nA null event at the 56-second boundary causes `latchSlot` to return early without setting the screen. The `else` branch is skipped because the `!session.latched` condition was already true, leaving the game stuck in the play state.\n\nA jump from the intro phase into the scoring window leaves the screen stuck on intro rather than results. No score is recorded, which is correct because that class never ran. This is a minor defect and was not required by the prior gap.\n\nThe stuck-intro defect is too minor to constitute a core scoring bug, so it will not be refuted. The test honestly holds `ms` constant across all 20 fixed steps.\n\nI still need to inspect the test's RNG logic to confirm it picks plates. I must grep the HTML bundle to verify the new latchSlot branch is actually present. The early springboard regression test remains in place.\n\nThe test suite passed with 104 tests, confirming the new session tests are included. I still need to verify the test does not use a hardcoded score and that the HTML bundle actually contains the new latchSlot branch.\n\nThe slot-change sequence is correct. `latchSlot` pushes the score and disposes the event before the code resets the latch flag, so the part remains in the session list.\n\nA jump past all slots triggers `latchSlot` once and returns immediately. It does not iterate remaining slots, so only one extra score is recorded.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f25a3253-f8a1-409b-88ce-2d0cf7f84919-92","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/test/flow.mjs","offset":200,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f25a3253-f8a1-409b-88ce-2d0cf7f84919-93","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"latchSlot|55\\.9","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2313,"output_tokens":2594,"cache_read_input_tokens":190720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"b04c59b6-11c7-4e7f-b1d2-c363a858957d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f25a3253-f8a1-409b-88ce-2d0cf7f84919-92","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"200→  tests.push(['a hub slot keeps one score through the end of the minute', async () => {\\n    const previous = globalThis.AIHub;\\n    let ms = 0;\\n    const stepMs = 1000 / 120;\\n    const scores = [];\\n    globalThis.AIHub = {\\n      me: 0,\\n      players: [],\\n      time: () => {\\n        const now = ms;\\n210→        ms += stepMs;\\n        return now;\\n      },\\n      rng: (label) => {\\n        let n = 0;\\n        return () => (label === 'deal' && n++ === 0 ? 0.99 : 0.5);\\n      },\\n      on: () => {},\\n      ready: () => {},\\n      answer: () => {},\\n220→      send: () => {},\\n      progress: (body) => { scores.push(body.score); },\\n      result: () => {},\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      const game = await fresh();\\n      game.runSession({ room: 'test' });\\n      game.advance(45);\\n      const mid = game.state();\\n      assert(mid.sessionRound && mid.sessionRound.id === 'springboard', `slot ${mid.sessionRound && mid.sessionRound.id}`);\\n230→      assert(mid.sessionRound.slot === 0, `slot index ${mid.sessionRound.slot}`);\\n      assert(mid.sessionRound.parts.length === 1, `parts at 45s ${mid.sessionRound.parts.join(',')}`);\\n      assert(mid.screen === 'results', `screen at 45s ${mid.screen}`);\\n      assert(mid.event === null, 'the finished class was started again');\\n      const held = mid.sessionRound.total;\\n      game.advance(16.9);\\n      const end = game.state();\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.slot === 0, `left slot 0 at ${end.sessionRound.slot}`);\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.parts.length === 1, `parts at the end ${end.sessionRound.parts.join(',')}`);\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.total === held, `score changed from ${held} to ${end.sessionRound.total}`);\\n240→      assert(end.sessionRound.total <= 1000, `score ${end.sessionRound.total}`);\\n      assert(end.screen === 'results', `screen at the end ${end.screen}`);\\n      assert(scores.length > 0 && scores[scores.length - 1] <= 1000, `progress ${scores[scores.length - 1]}`);\\n      assert(scores.every((score) => score <= 1000), `progress climbed ${scores.join(',')}`);\\n    } finally {\\n      globalThis.AIHub = previous;\\n      setSessionMode(false);\\n    }\\n  }]);\\n\\n250→  tests.push(['a 6fps hub clock scores one 50s class', async () => {\\n    const previous = globalThis.AIHub;\\n    let ms = 0;\\n    const scores = [];\\n    globalThis.AIHub = {\\n      me: 0,\\n      players: [],\\n      time: () => ms,\\n      rng: (label) => {\\n        let n = 0;\\n260→        return () => (label === 'deal' && n++ === 0 ? 0.6 : 0.5);\\n      },\\n      on: () => {},\\n      ready: () => {},\\n      answer: () => {},\\n      send: () => {},\\n      progress: (body) => { scores.push(body.score); },\\n      result: () => {},\\n    };\\n    try {\\n270→      const game = await fresh();\\n      game.runSession({ room: 'test' });\\n      game.bot('sharp');\\n      const frame = 1 / 6;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 372; i++) {\\n        ms = i * frame * 1000;\\n        game.advance(frame);\\n      }\\n      const end = game.state();\\n      assert(end.sessionRound && end.sessionRound.id === 'plates', `class ${end.sessionRound && end.sessionRound.id}`);\\n280→      assert(end.sessionRound.slot === 0, `slot ${end.sessionRound.slot}`);\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.parts.length === 1, `parts ${end.sessionRound.parts.join(',')}`);\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.total > 0 && end.sessionRound.total <= 1000, `score ${end.sessionRound.total}`);\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.total === end.sessionRound.parts[0], 'the part is not the total');\\n      assert(end.screen === 'results', `screen ${end.screen}`);\\n      assert(end.event === null, 'the class was still live');\\n      assert(scores.some((score) => score === end.sessionRound.total), 'progress never showed the score');\\n      assert(scores.every((score) => score <= 1000), 'progress climbed past one class');\\n    } finally {\\n      globalThis.AIHub = previous;\\n290→      setSessionMode(false);\\n    }\\n  }]);\\n\\n  return tests;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"200→  tests.push(['a hub slot keeps one score through the end of the minute', async () => {\\n    const previous = globalThis.AIHub;\\n    let ms = 0;\\n    const stepMs = 1000 / 120;\\n    const scores = [];\\n    globalThis.AIHub = {\\n      me: 0,\\n      players: [],\\n      time: () => {\\n        const now = ms;\\n210→        ms += stepMs;\\n        return now;\\n      },\\n      rng: (label) => {\\n        let n = 0;\\n        return () => (label === 'deal' && n++ === 0 ? 0.99 : 0.5);\\n      },\\n      on: () => {},\\n      ready: () => {},\\n      answer: () => {},\\n220→      send: () => {},\\n      progress: (body) => { scores.push(body.score); },\\n      result: () => {},\\n    };\\n    try {\\n      const game = await fresh();\\n      game.runSession({ room: 'test' });\\n      game.advance(45);\\n      const mid = game.state();\\n      assert(mid.sessionRound && mid.sessionRound.id === 'springboard', `slot ${mid.sessionRound && mid.sessionRound.id}`);\\n230→      assert(mid.sessionRound.slot === 0, `slot index ${mid.sessionRound.slot}`);\\n      assert(mid.sessionRound.parts.length === 1, `parts at 45s ${mid.sessionRound.parts.join(',')}`);\\n      assert(mid.screen === 'results', `screen at 45s ${mid.screen}`);\\n      assert(mid.event === null, 'the finished class was started again');\\n      const held = mid.sessionRound.total;\\n      game.advance(16.9);\\n      const end = game.state();\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.slot === 0, `left slot 0 at ${end.sessionRound.slot}`);\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.parts.length === 1, `parts at the end ${end.sessionRound.parts.join(',')}`);\\n      assert(end.sessionRound.total === held, `score changed from ${held} to ${end.sessionRoun