le causes include a mismatched internal clock, the play period not starting\n\nThe 55.9-second latch precisely at local time six, or sessionConfig threshold is harmless duration not aligning at 6fps because the with accumulated fixed steps. frame rate skips that window entirely. If an event finishes early, the code latches and disposes it, then correctly waits for local time to reach 56 before showing results.\n\nI suspect the test might pass only because the event internally\n\nI checked whether  sets done at fifty seconds during local`session.latched` is 55.833, not because missing from the session the >=56 boundary logic object. It defaults to undefined, which is falsy, so the early-return guard in `latchSlot` works. If that is true, removing the else branch would still let the test pass, so the original bug would remain undetected. I need to verify whether plates reaches its done condition before local hits 56, and check what happens if the else branch is removed. still works correctly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b1d8c85-a20a-40ba-a322-d088f6d71cdc-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"sessionConfig|done|duration|50","glob":"**/events/{plates,fruitHat,stepClass,base}.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b1d8c85-a20a-40ba-a322-d088f6d71cdc-13","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"sessionConfig|function startEvent|session:","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6b1d8c85-a20a-40ba-a322-d088f6d71cdc-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","offset":560,"limit":140}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6613,"output_tokens":2317,"cache_read_input_tokens":35328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"3ee038fa-c579-494a-8432-e468e204aa6e"}
