{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_562","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe `latchSlot()` call sits immediately after `stepEvent(dt, snaps)` and `session.playT += dt`, so an event that sets `event.done` during its own step latches in the same frame regardless of local time. This means the 6fps test would pass even if plates finished early, because the director would latch via `event.done` inside the play branch before the new `local >= 56` fallback could run. I am now re-reading the gap report to understand why the skeptic observed empty parts.\n\nThe gap report confirms the three events never set `event.done` beforeThe latch fix exists only in director.js, the window closes, so the only scoring window is `[55.9, 56)`. At 6fps that interval is skipped entirely. If an event finished at 50 seconds of internal time before local reached 55.9, it would have latched via `event.done` inside the play branch and avoided the empty-parts bug. The old code apparently did not auto-complete those events early. not in the HTML bundle.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-62724a3b-fb43-4d35-9442-81cd3adc6137-16","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"done|sessionConfig|duration|50","glob":"**/events/{plates.js,base.js,fruitHat.js,stepClass.js}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-62724a3b-fb43-4d35-9442-81cd3adc6137-17","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"sessionConfig|duration|playSec|50","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1160,"output_tokens":5388,"cache_read_input_tokens":41600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"599c973d-1bbc-4ab6-be19-2d8646401757"}
