{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_570","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bundle contains the fix.stepCores increments the simulation time at the start of each frame.\n\nThe test logic is sound. The play window spans exactly 50 seconds, so the done flag is set at t=50.\n\nPlates sets `done` once the accumulated time reaches its duration. After 6000 steps at 1/120, the simulation should reach roughly 50 seconds. The old code latches when that threshold is crossed. In `sessionFixed`, `startEvent` and `stepEvent`\n\nThe old code would execute in the same still pass the plates step. test. The event completes itself and sets done on the last step, so latchSlot fires before the jump. The prior 6fps failure likely had a different cause.\n\nThe 6000-step simulation spans 300 frames at 20 steps per frame. The implementer satisfied the prior gap by advancing AIHub.time() in roughly 1/6-second increments and keeping slot 0 within the required bounds. The outcome is therefore met even if plates self-completes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bd2a6292-7332-4c21-b71a-d44c1cec1719-30","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"FIXED_DT","glob":"**/config.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bd2a6292-7332-4c21-b71a-d44c1cec1719-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/events/base.js","offset":90,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1305,"output_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":57600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"09043440-828f-4cae-83a5-a07778a77c9e"}
