not latched_by_done and not latched_by_559:\\n                latched_by_559=True\\n                print(\\\"55.9 latch at\\\", i, local)\\n            play_steps += 1\\n        else:\\n            if not (latched_by_done or latched_by_559 or latched_by_56):\\n                latched_by_56=True\\n                print(\\\">=56 latch at frame\\\", i, \\\"local\\\", local, \\\"event_t\\\", t_event)\\n            break\\nprint(\\\"play_steps\\\", play_steps, \\\"event_t\\\", t_event)\\nprint(\\\"flags\\\", latched_by_done, latched_by_559, latched_by_56)\\nPY\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Simulate 6fps latch timing against plates duration\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9%2Fwork/01a1ab10-2efc-7451-8078-53db9914afa2/terminal/call-befc6fec-4746-4c46-8c83-cba27798994e-32.log\",\"total_bytes\":201}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"ba7e1e8d-b3d9-4263-a59f-debc1ab7e555"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_573","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" jump past the 55.9–56 threshold before the simulation advances.This is the smoking gun for test honesty and fix correctness.\n\nThe 30-step cap lets the simulation keep up at 6fps, so the hub and simulation stay aligned. At a slower frame rate, however, the simulation lags behind the hub clock. The event can reach its duration while local time has already crossed 56 seconds, leaving done unset. In that case, the >=56 latch is essential to capture the partial result. The skeptic's report of empty parts at 6fps suggests the simulation may have been running slower than expected.\n\nThe simulation and hub clocks should finish together at 50 seconds if they start aligned. The bug likely occurs when the event starts after the intro window, or when floating-point drift causes the simulation to lag slightly behind the hub clock. I will\n\nThe test hits a floating-point simulate exact float values for both clocks boundary where 6000×(1/120) to verify this. evaluates to roughly 49.999999999997804, which is below the 50-second threshold. This forces `event.done` to stay false and forces the event to rely solely on the `latchSlot()` path at local time 56. The old code would have failed this exact boundary case, while the new code passes\n\nA concrete simulation it. The test also verifies loop was written to that aliveTime accumulates test the exact float properly over the ~50-second behavior. It steps through 372 frames at window.\n\nThe log shows 104  6fps, accumulating fixed deltas and checking whether the event finishes before local time crosses the 55.9–56 window.passed and 0 failed. I should verify this test is actually counted among those 104, since the runner only prints","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c56c5cad-dae2-4e38-85f5-ce1f6e413144-22","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function startEvent|function stepEvent","glob":"**/director.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c56c5cad-dae2-4e38-85f5-ce1f6e413144-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js","offset":650,"limit":90}}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7031,"output_tokens":1513,"cache_read_input_tokens":51584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"f48c1704-3aec-440d-a03e-cf382b0a0cd8"}
