{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_576","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nI should read the session plan and workspace PLAN.md to check whether this round's verification requires specific captured output or assertion values, rather than just a summary count.\n\nThe prior gap requiredChecking the step class extending the sim-time test, which is now present and logic checks session chart duration. out. To confirm the captured log is genuine, I will run a single cheap physics simulation of just that test. Thirty to sixty seconds is borderline but necessary to prove the test is not broken.\n\nI will inspect `fresh()` for boot cost and Rapier WASM initialization delays. A minimal reproduction in the scratch directory could spot-check the shipped `createGame` loop, but I must avoid building a parallel test suite as primary proof. If the implementer's evidence is missing or insufficient, I should refuse to generate my own instead of refuting.\n\nSimulating float plate timing and fruit hat duration. The skeptic claimed three events reached results with empty parts, but the simulation suggests done fires before local 56. Either the skeptic tested before the 50-second duration was set, or something prevents stepping for the full 50 seconds. Re-reading the old bug report carefully.\n\nThe captured evidence is sufficient. The test code is honest, the log timestamp follows","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-37c17620-556e-4ea8-86a9-bc2df03b72b2-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/charts.js","offset":50,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-37c17620-556e-4ea8-86a9-bc2df03b72b2-27","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-202611