{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-85367d6b-143b-4d12-9b2d-446a29db55d0-28","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Step charts. A bar is 8 eighth-notes. Cell time is half a beat. */\\n\\nexport const CELL = {\\n  L: 'L', R: 'R', B: 'B',\\n  left: '<', right: '>', up: '^', down: 'v', rest: '.',\\n};\\n\\nconst PATTERNS = {\\n  walk: 'L...R...',\\n10→  jog: 'L.R.L.R.',\\n  both: 'L.R.B...',\\n  doubles: 'L.L.R.R.',\\n  lean: '<...>...',\\n  leanStep: 'L.R.<...',\\n  nod: '^...v...',\\n  busy: 'LRL.RLR.',\\n  stamp: 'B.B.LRB.',\\n  flourish: 'L.R.LRLR',\\n};\\n20→\\nfunction bars(pattern, count) {\\n  const cell = pattern.padEnd(8, '.').slice(0, 8);\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) out.push(...cell);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction chart(bpm, parts) {\\n  const cells = parts.flatMap(([pattern, count]) => bars(pattern, count));\\n30→  return { bpm, cells, cellDt: 30 / bpm };\\n}\\n\\nexport const CHARTS = {\\n  1: chart(104, [\\n    ['.', 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.walk, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.both, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.lean, 4],\\n40→    [PATTERNS.jog, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.walk, 4],\\n  ]),\\n  2: chart(116, [\\n    ['.', 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.doubles, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.leanStep, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.nod, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.busy, 4],\\n50→    [PATTERNS.jog, 4],\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Step charts. A bar is 8 eighth-notes. Cell time is half a beat. */\\n\\nexport const CELL = {\\n  L: 'L', R: 'R', B: 'B',\\n  left: '<', right: '>', up: '^', down: 'v', rest: '.',\\n};\\n\\nconst PATTERNS = {\\n  walk: 'L...R...',\\n10→  jog: 'L.R.L.R.',\\n  both: 'L.R.B...',\\n  doubles: 'L.L.R.R.',\\n  lean: '<...>...',\\n  leanStep: 'L.R.<...',\\n  nod: '^...v...',\\n  busy: 'LRL.RLR.',\\n  stamp: 'B.B.LRB.',\\n  flourish: 'L.R.LRLR',\\n};\\n20→\\nfunction bars(pattern, count) {\\n  const cell = pattern.padEnd(8, '.').slice(0, 8);\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) out.push(...cell);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction chart(bpm, parts) {\\n  const cells = parts.flatMap(([pattern, count]) => bars(pattern, count));\\n30→  return { bpm, cells, cellDt: 30 / bpm };\\n}\\n\\nexport const CHARTS = {\\n  1: chart(104, [\\n    ['.', 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.walk, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.both, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.lean, 4],\\n40→    [PATTERNS.jog, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.walk, 4],\\n  ]),\\n  2: chart(116, [\\n    ['.', 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.doubles, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.leanStep, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.nod, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.busy, 4],\\n50→    [PATTERNS.jog, 4],\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/work/Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/data/charts.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"/** Step charts. A bar is 8 eighth-notes. Cell time is half a beat. */\\n\\nexport const CELL = {\\n  L: 'L', R: 'R', B: 'B',\\n  left: '<', right: '>', up: '^', down: 'v', rest: '.',\\n};\\n\\nconst PATTERNS = {\\n  walk: 'L...R...',\\n  jog: 'L.R.L.R.',\\n  both: 'L.R.B...',\\n  doubles: 'L.L.R.R.',\\n  lean: '<...>...',\\n  leanStep: 'L.R.<...',\\n  nod: '^...v...',\\n  busy: 'LRL.RLR.',\\n  stamp: 'B.B.LRB.',\\n  flourish: 'L.R.LRLR',\\n};\\n\\nfunction bars(pattern, count) {\\n  const cell = pattern.padEnd(8, '.').slice(0, 8);\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) out.push(...cell);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction chart(bpm, parts) {\\n  const cells = parts.flatMap(([pattern, count]) => bars(pattern, count));\\n  return { bpm, cells, cellDt: 30 / bpm };\\n}\\n\\nexport const CHARTS = {\\n  1: chart(104, [\\n    ['.', 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.walk, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.both, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.lean, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 8],\\n    [PATTERNS.walk, 4],\\n  ]),\\n  2: chart(116, [\\n    ['.', 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.doubles, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.leanStep, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.nod, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.busy, 4],\\n    [PATTERNS.jog, 4],\\n\",\"total_lines\":78}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"2697d033-4e37-4856-a4a2-8e858c6ff80e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_578","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe slot-change path correctly calls `latchSlot()` before disposal. The latched flag prevents double scoring, and the test asserts exactly one part. Form is clamped to 0–100 and scaled by ten, so a score of 1000 is valid. The prior gap’s empty parts were caused by window skipping, not zero form; the shared latch now fixes that.The session step class contains 192 cells.\n\nI am checking whether the shared latch could leave a slot with zero form. The gap only requires one event to score, so the other two are irrelevant. Step class notes might be judged after the 49.999-second cutoff, but most would still count.\n\nI am inspecting the minified bundle for operator-precedence bugs. The `else P.latched?o=\"results\":Ms()` pattern could misbehave if `P.latched` is truthy, but the source shows a nested `if (!session.latched)` guard that should prevent this.\n\nStep class duration is about 50.06 seconds, slightly longer than 50. If the simulation hits exactly 50 seconds while the hub local time is still below 56, step class may not be done yet and jumping over its interval could skip latching. Plates and fruit hat\n\nThe minified bundle both last exactly 50 collapses the two source seconds, so they would latch under the old `if` statements into a single comma-separated code. expression. This risks a parsing bug where the first condition is evaluated but discarded, leaving the second condition to control execution.\n\nThe skeptic observed that plates and fruit hat were also empty. This suggests done was not set for those either. The 6fps model may have advanced hub time by roughly one-sixth per frame while fixed steps ran with a constant hub time. Alternatively, the simulation may have jumped hub time while the game advance used a different delta.\n\nThe minified bundle’s comma-separated condition is safe. The left-hand expression only calls `startEvent` when no event exists and the session is not latched, preserving the original side effect. The right-hand\n\nThe real game loop expression then controls calls `sessionFixed` whether to enter the inside a while loop play body or fall through that repeatedly invokes to results. `onFixed` with a fixed delta. Each call reads `hub.time()` fresh. The key question is whether that time value is a live snapshot or a constant during the frame.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f7330266-b45b-43a8-89fe-f9974dd934eb-29","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"55\\.9|6fps|parts=\\[\\]","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":692,"output_tokens":777,"cache_read_input_tokens":63360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"aa0e821e-74dc-4de5-929a-e7f17b56bbd4"}
