d. The latched flag is in the built HTML.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"The 6fps scoring gap is fixed.\\\\n\\\\n`latchSlot` in `src/game/director.js` records one `round(form*10)`, sets `session.latched`, and disposes the world. It runs when the class sets `done`, when `local >= 55.9`, when `local >= 56` (the branch that used to only change the screen), when the slot index changes, and when the round ends. A later step in the same window sees `latched` and does not start or score the class again.\\\\n\\\\nReplay with `AIHub.time()` stepped by 1/6s and held still across that frame's fixed steps, deal forced to Plate Spinners, sharp bot: slot 0 ends with `parts: [1000]`, `total: 1000`, `event: null`, screen `results`. A clock jump from 55.0s to 56.2s while the class is still live latches a single part instead of leaving `parts: []`. The new flow test drives that 6fps loop through `runSession` and requires one part with `0 < total <= 1000`. `test-full.log` reports `104 passed, 0 failed`. The built HTML contains the latch.\\\"\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-classifier-cfc5772a1498-2-skeptic-0.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"`session.latched` in `sessionFixed` stops a second `startEvent` after a part is pushed. Springboard, which finishes well before 50s, keeps one part through the end of slot 0. That matches the new flow test and a 6fps replay (one part, 47).\"},{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"The push itself is still gated by `event.done || local >= 55.9`, and that check sits only in the `local < 56` branch (`director.js` around 830 and 841). When `local >= 56` the code sets the results screen and does not read `event.result`. The window is 0.1s wide. This machine's software WebGPU path is about 6fps, so `AIHub.time()` jumps by ~1/6s between frames and stays put while that frame's fixed steps run. From a session start at 0, those stamps go 55.833s then 56.000s and never land in [55.9, 56).\"},{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"Replay of that loop, deal forced to one class: Plate Spinners, Fruit Hat, and Step Class all finish slot 0 with `parts: []`, `total: 0`, screen `results`, event time still ~50. The same Plate Spinners run at 60fps latches a single part of 35, because a frame does fall on 55.9. A 50s class must not score 0 just because no frame sampled a 100ms band.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-verdict-cfc5772a1498-1-0.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"A hub slot scores and disposes the event while local time is still under 56s, then the next fixed step sees event===null and starts a new one. Poses (33s), Cairn (~42s), Log Reps (40s) and Springboard (3 dives) finish inside the 50s play window and are scored again; once local is in [55.9, 56) every 1/120 step starts a fresh world and pushes another round(form*10). Latch one part per slot and hold results until local>=56. A sim-time session with AIHub.time() must show one part and score<=1000 at the end of slot 0.\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"sessionFixed replay, rng deal=0 (slot 0 = Poses): progress score 0 at t=0, 257 at t=39, 11576 at t=56 (one slot must be a single round(form*10), at most 1000). Same 55.9 latch is in the built HTML.\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"Hub session scoring restarts the class and banks it many times.\\\\n\\\\n`sessionFixed` in `src/game/director.js` treats `local < 56` as \\\\\\\"still playing\\\\\\\". When the event sets `done`, or when `local >= 55.9`, it pushes `round(form*10)`, disposes the world, and sets `event = null`. The next `fixed` step is still inside that window, so `if (!event) startEvent(...)` builds a new world and the same branch scores it again.\\\\n\\\\nPLAN.md §12 says each of the three slots is 6s intro, 50s play, 6s results, and contributes one `round(form × 10)`. Several session events end early: Poses tier 1 is `3 * (3 + 8) = 33s`, Cairn tier 1 is about `1.2 + 6*5.5 + 8 = 42s`, Log Reps is `8 * 5 = 40s` at the default tempo, and Springboard sets `done` after three dives. Those completions fall while `local < 56`.\\\\n\\\\nSpot-check: manual `createGame`, `runSession`, `AIHub.rng` returning 0 so slot 0 is Poses, clock advanced `1/120` s per fixed step. Progress score was 0 at t=0, 257 at t=39 (first Poses end [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-classifier-cfc5772a1498-2.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"  - bug · Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js:841 — A slot still scores only while local is inside [55.9, 56) or the event already set done. The local>=56 branch only switches to results. At 6fps (hub time jumps ~1/6s and stays put across that frame's fixed steps) Plate Spinners, Fruit Hat, and Step Class reach results with parts=[] and total 0. Score the live event once on any exit from the play window, including local>=56 and a slot change. Extend the sim-time test so AIHub.time() advances in ~1/6s frames, constant during the frame's steps, and slot 0 of a 50s class still has one part with 0<total<=1000.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-classifier-cfc5772a1498-3-skeptic-0.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"The 6fps scoring gap is fixed.\"},{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"`latchSlot` in `src/game/director.js` records one `round(form*10)`, sets `session.latched`, and disposes the world. It runs when the class sets `done`, when `local >= 55.9`, when `local >= 56` (the branch that used to only change the screen), when the slot index changes, and when the round ends. A later step in the same window sees `latched` and does not start or score the class again.\"},{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"Replay with `AIHub.time()` stepped by 1/6s and held still across that frame's fixed steps, deal forced to Plate Spinners, sharp bot: slot 0 ends with `parts: [1000]`, `total: 1000`, `event: null`, screen `results`. A clock jump from 55.0s to 56.2s while the class is still live latches a single part instead of leaving `parts: []`. The new flow test drives that 6fps loop through `runSession` and requires one part with `0 < total <= 1000`. `test-full.log` reports `104 passed, 0 failed`. The built HTML contains the latch.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-verdict-cfc5772a1498-2-0.json\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"A slot still scores only while local is inside [55.9, 56) or the event already set done. The local>=56 branch only switches to results. At 6fps (hub time jumps ~1/6s and stays put across that frame's fixed steps) Plate Spinners, Fruit Hat, and Step Class reach results with parts=[] and total 0. Score the live event once on any exit from the play window, including local>=56 and a slot change. Extend the sim-time test so AIHub.time() advances in ~1/6s frames, constant during the frame's steps, and slot 0 of a 50s class still has one part with 0<total<=1000.\\\"\"},{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"6fps frame replay of sessionFixed: plates/fruitHat/stepClass end slot 0 at total 0 (et~50, screen results, parts []); the same plates run at 60fps latches one part (35). Springboard still latches once (47) because it ends early. test-full.log 103 passed only steps the clock by 1/120, which always hits [55.9, 56).\\\",\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"The double-score latch holds for a class that ends early. It still drops the score for a class that lasts the whole slot.\\\\n\\\\n`session.latched` in `sessionFixed` stops a second `startEvent` after a part is pushed. Springboard, which finishes well before 50s, keeps one part through the end of slot 0. That matches the new flow test and a 6fps replay (one part, 47).\\\\n\\\\nThe push itself is still gated by `event.done || local >= 55.9`, and that check sits only in the `local < 56` branch (`director.js` around 830 and 841). When `local >= 56` the code sets the results screen and does not read `event.result`. The window is 0.1s wide. This machine's software WebGPU path is about 6fps, so `AIHub.time()` jumps by ~1/6s between frames and stays put while that frame's fixed steps run. From a session start at 0, those stamps go 55.833s then 56.000s and never land in [55.9, 56).\\\\n\\\\nReplay of that loop, deal forced to one class: Plate Spinners, Fruit Hat, and Step Class all finish slot  [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-classifier-cfc5772a1498-1.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":8,\"content\":\"  - bug · Level Best-Wii Fit-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-231317/src/game/director.js:812 — A hub slot scores and disposes the event while local time is still under 56s, then the next fixed step sees event===null and starts a new one. Poses (33s), Cairn (~42s), Log Reps (40s) and Springboard (3 dives) finish inside the 50s play window and are scored again; once local is in [55.9, 56) every 1/120 step starts a fresh world and pushes another round(form*10). Latch one part per slot and hold results until local>=56. A sim-time session with AIHub.time() must show one part and score<=1000 at the end of slot 0.\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-classifier-cfc5772a1498-1-skeptic-0.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"`sessionFixed` in `src/game/director.js` treats `local < 56` as \\\"still playing\\\". When the event sets `done`, or when `local >= 55.9`, it pushes `round(form*10)`, disposes the world, and sets `event = null`. The next `fixed` step is still inside that window, so `if (!event) startEvent(...)` builds a new world and the same branch scores it again.\"},{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"Spot-check: manual `createGame`, `runSession`, `AIHub.rng` returning 0 so slot 0 is Poses, clock advanced `1/120` s per fixed step. Progress score was 0 at t=0, 257 at t=39 (first Poses ended), then 11576 at t=56. One slot cannot exceed 1000. The same `55.9` latch is in the bundled HTML. The harness still passes because it does not check the score magnitude.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"f75804d1-0854-4e54-ae71-7071e25f2090"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_579","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A prior goal verdict already marks the gap as fixed and not refuted.\n\nThe progress-update timing is correct. The first progress is sent immediately because lastProgress starts at -1, and the next update fires roughly one second later. This ensures the final score reaches the hub before the loop ends.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-12087695-bee1-416e-9b1e-2716051d362d-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"tests\\.push\\(","glob":"**/test/*.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-12087695-bee1-416e-9b1e-2716051d362d-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"return \\[","glob":"**/test/browser.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":743,"output_tokens":2424,"cache_read_input_tokens":60032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa57-1af6-7b91-b0b8-da8c4d991b66","uuid":"b62c1203-7d1f-4ec3-beb7-0c721d9b0ac3"}
