{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_590","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" the assignment, not the function call.\n\nThe prior gap is genuinely fixed. Now searching for a new demonstrable defect.\n\nThe `Ms()` function pushes a rounded `form` value into `P.parts`. A zero result would fail the sharp-plates test, but the total must exceed zero. The slot-change path also avoids double-disposing the event because `latchSlot` already nulls it.\n\nA new defect is found. When jumping slots while not latched, `latchSlot` nulls the event and resets latched. If the next step hits local>=56, `Ms()` returns early because `h` is null and never sets the screen to results. The display stays on whatever frame was last drawn.\n\nThe suspected defect is not a real bug. When jumping slots into the results window, `latchSlot` first scores the previous slot and sets the screen to results. The subsequent early return in the new slot's step leaves that results screen unchanged, so the display remains correct.\n\nA hidden tab jump into a skipped slot's results window would leave the screen on intro. This is an edge case, not the prior gap. At 6fps it cannot be demonstrated.\n\nThe score remains zero during the entire play until the final latch. The test only checks that the final total matches the expected value, so this behavior is acceptable.\n\nThe progress update fires after the final latch, so the total is included in the test output. All 104 tests passed with zero failures. The objective is not refuted.\n\nThe new test is not skipped or placed after a return in the test file. The test code sets the sharp bot before running the session, and the first deal produces plates.\n\nThe deal RNG is sourced directly from the hub, not the local session. The final verdict will be \"Not Refuted\" with an empty findings array.\n\nThe 6fps test halts at t=61.833 while still in slot 0, asserting exactly one part. This final check is being reviewed to confirm the fix holds.\n\nThe 6fps test halts at t=61.833 while still in slot 0, so it cannot catch a double-score when entering slot 1. The prior round's double-score gap was already fixed by the latched flag. A separate test checks that one score persists through the end of the minute; its clock increments every time() call by 1/120 rather than 6fps, and after advance(45) plus advance(16.9) the total reaches roughly 61.9 seconds, still inside slot 0.\n\nThe 6fps test never reaches slot 1, so it cannot catch a double-score at the boundary. The prior double-count gap was already fixed in an earlier round, and the current objective is to avoid re-litigating that resolved issue. A new concern is whether the new else branch could reintroduce double scoring when an event sets done while local time is near the 55.9-second threshold.\n\nThe latched flag prevents double scoring at slot boundaries. When an event finishes near the 55.9-second threshold, the single if-condition still fires latchSlot exactly once. The new else branch does not reintroduce a regression.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The 6fps window skip is closed in source and in the bundle, and the new sim-time test is what would fail without that branch. I'll record the verdict."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7dc011ac-beb6-4e0d-b1ed-46330deea1d2-37","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-verdict-cfc5772a1498-3-2.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"director.js:847 latches on local>=56; flow.mjs 6fps loop skips [55.9,56) with event.t just under 50 so done stays false; test-full.log is 104 passed, 0 failed; the same branch is in the bundled HTML.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"The 6fps scoring gap is fixed.\\n\\n`latchSlot` (`src/game/director.js:781`) records one `round(form*10)` and sets `session.latched`. `sessionFixed` calls it when the class sets `done`, when `local >= 55.9` (`:844`), when `local >= 56` (`:847`), on a slot change (`:819`), and when the round ends (`:813`). A later step in that window sees `latched` and does not start or score the class again.\\n\\nA hub clock stepped by 1/6s from t=0 lands on local 55.833 then exactly 56, so it never samples [55.9, 56). Six thousand steps of 1/120 leave event time at 49.9999999999978, so Plate Spinners' `t >= 50` done flag stays false and only the `local >= 56` branch can score. `test/flow.mjs:250` drives that loop through `runSession` (deal 0.6 selects Plate Spinners, sharp bot, time held constant for each frame's steps) and requires one part with `0 < total <= 1000`. `implementer/test-full.log` is `104 passed, 0 failed`. The bundled HTML has the same `else latched ? results : latch` branch.\\n\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7dc011ac-beb6-4e0d-b1ed-46330deea1d2-38","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-231317__x29b4d9/tmp/grok-goal-cfc5772a1498/goal-classifier-cfc5772a1498-3-skeptic-2.md","content":"The 6fps scoring gap is fixed.\n\n`latchSlot` (`src/game/director.js:781`) records one `round(form*10)` and sets `session.latched`. `sessionFixed` calls it when the class sets `done`, when `local >= 55.9` (`:844`), when `local >= 56` (`:847`), on a slot change (`:819`), and when the round ends (`:813`). A later step in that window sees `latched` and does not start or score the class again.\n\nA hub clock stepped by 1/6s from t=0 lands on local 55.833 then exactly 56, so it never samples [55.9, 56). Six thousand steps of 1/120 leave event time at 49.9999999999978, so Plate Spinners' `t >= 50` done flag stays false and only the `local >= 56` branch can score. `test/flow.mjs:250` drives that loop through `runSession` (deal 0.6 selects Plate Spinners, sharp bot, time held constant for each frame's steps) and requires one part with